window.FWN_UNDEAD_LEGION_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_UNDEAD_LEGION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1101,"title":"Chapter 1101: I’m Death’s Heir [1]","paragraphs":["BOOOOOOOOOOM!!","A chain of explosions engulfed the chimera. Towering pillars of pink fire rose into the heavens, momentarily overwhelming even the endless freezing rain.","The chimera roared as several bone plates shattered beneath the relentless bombardment. Yet it showed no intention of retreating.","Instead, it charged directly through the exploding blossoms. Its barbed skeletal tail lashed forward like a colossal spear.","The serpent flowed through the air with astonishing elegance. Its body bent around the incoming strike by the narrowest margin before another wave of flaming flowers materialized around the chimera, preparing to bloom once more.","However, while the undead clashed fiercely across the battlefield, their masters had their own battle to fight.","Varek suddenly swung his bone staff. A circular object no larger than a palm appeared between his fingers before he casually tossed it into the air.","Michael's eyes immediately narrowed.","\"A treasure?\"","The moment the disk reached its highest point, intricate runes covering its surface lit up.","Click! Click! Click!","The single disk instantly separated into seven identical smaller disks.","Each floated into a different position around Varek before beginning to rotate at tremendous speed.","The next moment, seven brilliant beams erupted simultaneously.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","The rays shot across the battlefield from different angles, cutting through the freezing rain with astonishing precision.","Michael instinctively prepared to teleport.","Then his vision suddenly went black. Everything disappeared.","Michael recognized the feeling instantly.","\"...Is this Blind Curse?\"","It was one of the curse spells he himself possessed.","Unfortunately for Varek, the darkness lasted for less than the blink of an eye. Michael's vision instantly returned.","Without the slightest hesitation, space distorted around him and his figure vanished. The seven beams crossed through the exact location where he had been standing only a fraction of a second earlier.","BOOM!","The frozen mountain behind him was pierced clean through. Several more explosions echoed as the remaining beams carved enormous trenches across the battlefield.","Across the battlefield, Varek frowned.","\"...What?\"","His eyes narrowed in confusion. The timing had been perfect. He had intentionally synchronized the Blind Curse with the attack from the Seven-Ray Disk so that his opponent wouldn't have enough time to react.","Had the curse failed?","Impossible. He had clearly seen it activate.","\"...Was his resistance that high?\"","For the first time, genuine surprise appeared in Varek's eyes.","Meanwhile, Michael looked equally puzzled, though for an entirely different reason.","\"...Am I fighting a fake necromancer?\"","His expression became rather strange.","A necromancer's greatest strengths were usually undead, curses, soul arts, battlefield control, and long-term attrition. Yet why did this Level 100 necromancer's spells feel like they had been cast by someone at Level 40?","Though it had certainly come as a surprise to be attacked with a curse from such a distance and so silently, the actual effect had been embarrassingly weak.","\"Ahh.\"","Suddenly Michael laughed in self mock and shook his head at his own oversight.","\"What was I even thinking? Even if I set aside my curiosity about how others fight, when it comes to death-related arts, who can actually match me?\"","He couldn't help but laugh at himself.","Who was he?","He was Death's Heir!","Even if he has previously being necromancer, the era for Michael to learn how to fight like one had long passed.","In the same element, when facing him in death-related arts, unless someone was perhaps two full ranks above him, they wouldn't be able to do much to him.","Even if they were, how much would that truly change his advantage over death? At most the gap would be limited.","He, Michael, was already someone who had forcefully reclaimed a life from the universe's own hands. The way he was currently fighting truly didn't befit him, nor did it show any respect toward his class.","\"Being cautious and wary of potential loss isn't bad, but it seems to be making me dull. This is not good.\"","\"While overwhelming advantage won't exactly sharpen my resourcefulness or help me realize the full potential of my strength, since that requires genuine pressure, this situation is also my advantage.\"","\"Whatever issues might come from fighting more openly, the future me will handle them. I shouldn't be so stiff.\"","Michael felt a rare moment of clarity wash over him.","Varek suddenly heard a sigh drifting across the battlefield. It was soft. Yet somehow it reached his ears clearly through the howling rain and roaring collisions. A chill crawled up his spine.","His gaze snapped toward Michael.","\"What is he planning?\"","The next instant, Varek's expression changed.","The connection between him and his undead suddenly trembled.","On the surface nothing seemed to happen, but an experienced necromancer and master of soul arts could immediately feel that his connection with his undead had weakened.","Though it was only slightly, for a necromancer, that slight disturbance was enough to feel like a blade pressed against the throat.","\"How?!\"","Across the battlefield, Michael's eyes had turned a deeper shade of green.","His gaze swept across the skeletal dragon, the wyvern, and the bone chimera. He had always wondered how the near-absolute domination over creatures of death granted by his class would work against undead that didn't belong to him.","Now he finally had the chance to test it.","Using the range provided by Death's Ground, which currently had Varek's undead within it, Michael immediately felt something.","A sort of connection. Thin. But undeniably there. When he tried to connect deeper with it, however, there was a barrier blocking him. No, not one. Two barriers.","A quick look revealed what they were. One came from Varek, the undead's master. The other came from the undead creature's own instinctive will. The latter was much weaker than the former.","Michael wasn't too surprised. Though he was still Rank Three, there were probably not many Rank Four awakeners with a soul stronger than his.","And with his class advantage added on top of that, if these undead had been ownerless, they might have already fallen under his control.","The thought made Michael pause. Then his eyes lit up slightly.","Wait. Didn't that mean that if he found wild undead in the future, as long as they weren't Rank Five or above, he might be able to directly suppress and control them without any of the usual process?","Wasn't that basically cheating?"]},{"number":1102,"title":"Chapter 1102: I’m Death’s Heir [2]","paragraphs":["Michael's excitement quietly grew. Instead of continuing to spread his will across all three undead at once, he immediately changed his approach. Since three targets created too much resistance, he would take one first.","His gaze locked onto the skeletal dragon fighting with his High Drake. By this point Varek had also moved toward the center of the battlefield, much like Michael.","The green light in Michael's eyes deepened. Death's Ground pulsed again with his consciousness infused into it, but this time all the pressure gathered toward a single point.","The skeletal dragon.","Varek's expression changed instantly.","\"What?!\"","The connection between him and the skeletal dragon began weakening at a terrifying speed. It wasn't a slight tremble anymore.","It was as though an invisible hand had grabbed the bond between master and undead and was tearing it apart strand by strand.","Varek immediately poured more soul power into the connection. The crown-shaped mark above the skeletal dragon's head flickered violently.","For a moment, the dragon's soul flames burned brighter.","Then they dimmed.","Varek's pupils contracted.","The undead creature's own resistance was pathetically weak in comparison. It existed, but it was more like an instinctive rejection rather than true defiance.","This made Michael immediately understand that near-absolute domination didn't necessarily mean instant obedience.","If the target was powerful enough or already bound to another master, resistance would still exist, even if it was ultimately futile.","The skeletal dragon's movements suddenly stopped.","Varek's face turned ugly.","The next instant, the soul flames inside the skeletal dragon's eyes changed direction. They no longer looked toward Michael.","They looked toward Varek.","Seeing this, Varek was in utter disbelief.","\"No...\"","The skeletal dragon opened its jaws. Pale-green flames gathered deep within its throat.","Varek's expression twisted.","\"You dare!\"","ROOOOOOOAR!!","A torrent of deathly dragon breath erupted toward its former master. The freezing rain evaporated instantly.","Varek raised his bone staff in fury, and layers of bone shields erupted before him one after another.","BOOOOOOM!!","The dragon breath smashed into the shields. One layer shattered. Then another. Then another.","Varek was forced backward through the air, his robes whipping violently in the shockwave as his face turned darker than the sky above.","Michael watched from afar with a bright smile.","Taking one undead hadn't satisfied him at all.","This worked perfectly!","Before this, he had been frustrated at being unable to snatch the Epic Grade wand from that Rank Three angel.","At the time, as the timer on his plan drew increasingly close, his intentions and actions had been very direct.","Using only his physical body, he had ruthlessly beaten the female angel who had wanted his life black and blue, but unfortunately whenever he reached out to grab the wand she refused to release it, placing it into her storage space and only taking it out again once she had created enough distance to cast spells.","That match had ended with a massive fireball that failed to put down the angel's remarkable regenerative abilities, causing him to fall short of snatching the treasure.","Now that he could finally get his hands on something worthwhile in the Origin Battlefield, how could he, Michael Norman, settle for just one?","What he wanted was not just one of the undead before him, or even two, but all three.","In fact, if the opponent had even more Level 100 undead to show, Michael wanted those as well.","As if answering his wish, Varek had already summoned four more undead while defending himself, and all four were still at Level 100.","The opponent appeared to be an undead specialist, Michael judged, but he wasn't particularly concerned.","In the brief window he had, he had already moved to seize control of a second undead, the wyvern.","Varek cursed loudly. The sound was swallowed by the freezing rain, but the fury in it was unmistakable.","Another of his undead had had actually been stolen again?","As an experienced necromancer, Varek immediately understood that for some reason, dark arts seemed to be completely useless against this young man. No, worse than useless.","Against Michael, they were like toys. But that only made it more absurd, because Michael was still only Rank Three. Only Level 75.","With a level like that, why were his methods this terrifying?","Varek's face twisted with rage, humiliation, and disbelief.","For a brief moment, he wanted to pour everything he had into crushing Michael, even if it meant risking serious injury. Then his reason returned.","This was no longer a battle worth continuing. The environment favored both of them, but Michael's methods directly countered the very foundation of Varek's combat system.","If the fight dragged on, more of his undead might be stolen. That was unacceptable.","Varek gritted his teeth and raised his staff. The bone chimera, along with the newly summoned undead that had yet to fully enter the battle, were immediately recalled. Their bodies collapsed into streams of light before vanishing.","Michael's eyes widened slightly.","\"Wait...\"","He had only just begun. Before he could make another move, Varek's presence faded away entirely.","Michael's expression changed. The battlefield fell silent. The freezing rain continued to fall.","Michael remained standing in the Deathfrost Rainlands, his expression filled with confusion and dissatisfaction.","\"...That's it?\"","He looked toward the skeletal dragon he had just stolen. Then at the empty space where Varek had disappeared. His lips twitched.","\"I wasn't done yet.\"","Unfortunately, the Origin Will clearly didn't care whether he was done or not. Several panels appeared before him at the same time.","[Ranking Challenge Concluded]","[Winner: Michael Norman]","[Victory Method: Opponent Surrender]","[Defender Victory Confirmed]","[Current Rank Maintained: 198]","[Match Record Updated]","[Matches: 1]","[Victories: 1]","[Defeats: 0]","[Challenge Protection Progress: 1/3]","[Two additional successful defenses required to activate monthly challenge protection] Michael stared at the panels for a moment. Then he sighed.","At least there was something gained. His gaze shifted toward the skeletal dragon as wyvern. The soul flames in their eyes flickered quietly, waiting for his command.","Michael's mood improved slightly.","\"Well... I suppose this counts as compensation.\""]},{"number":1103,"title":"Chapter 1103: Engraving [1]","paragraphs":["Michael had barely finished speaking when another notification appeared. His attention immediately shifted back to the floating panels.","[Battlefield Arena Closing]","[The ranking arena will remain active for 02 Hours 59 Minutes 41 Seconds] [Participants may continue exploring the battlefield until the countdown reaches zero] [When the timer expires, all remaining participants will be returned to their previous location within the Origin Battlefield] Michael blinked in surprise.","\"...Returned?\"","After a match ended, the arena didn't immediately collapse.","\"So that's another function...\"","It seemed the Origin Battlefield was revealing its rules little by little instead of explaining everything at once. Michael then patiently waited for another panel to appear, but after a full minute, nothing happened.","\"...\"","The silence became almost awkward.","Finally, Michael's face darkened.","\"...That's it?\"","He looked around the empty battlefield as though expecting another panel to suddenly appear, but was still met with nothing.","Michael's eyebrow twitched.","\"So someone lower-ranked can challenge me whenever they want, and after I beat the person who came looking for trouble I get nothing?\"","Silence answered him.","Michael looked toward the gray sky.","\"Origin Battlefield, you're unbelievably stingy.\"","His lips twitched. The only reward he had obtained was maintaining the rank he already possessed. Not even moving up. Just not moving down.","Michael clicked his tongue.","\"So I waste my mana, spend my time, reveal part of my abilities, and all I get is keeping what I already had.\"","He suddenly understood why the challenge system allowed participants to refuse three times every month.","\"If this is the reward for successfully defending, then anyone with a brain would refuse challenges unless they were forced to accept.","The challenger risks little. The defender risks everything. If the challenger wins, they steal your ranking. If they lose, they lose almost nothing if they play smart.\"","\"...What kind of unfair system is this?\"","Michael folded his arms. Of course, he knew there had to be a reason. Otherwise, no one would willingly defend their position.","Perhaps the true value lay entirely in the monthly ranking rewards. If those rewards were extraordinary enough, then protecting one's position would naturally become worthwhile.","Even so, he still couldn't help muttering,","\"...You could've at least given me a participation reward.\"","The empty battlefield remained as silent as ever, completely ignoring his complaint.","Michael waited another few seconds before finally giving up.","\"...Fine.\"","If there were no rewards, then there were no rewards. His gaze naturally shifted toward the two undead floating quietly nearby. A smile slowly spread across his face.","\"...At least you two were worth the effort.\"","With a wave of his hand, both undead drifted toward him obediently. Michael activated Detect.","[Bone Dragon]","Level: 100","Grade: Extraordinary ★★★","[Bone Wyvern]","Level: 100","Grade: Extraordinary ★★★","Michael nodded in satisfaction.","\"Peak Rank Four...\"","Though he possessed thousands of Rank Four undead, the vast majority were ordinary Rank Fours. Only a single one of his undead had truly reached the peak of Rank Four before today. Even those close to that level were extremely few.","Yet now, thanks to one extraordinarily generous person, he suddenly possessed two more.","His smile widened.","\"And they're both from the Bone series.\"","That pleased him even more. Before today, despite commanding thousands of undead, he hadn't owned a single high-grade bone-type undead.","His legion consisted mostly of corpses that had retained flesh, or bodies capable of taking a human shape after advancing to Rank Three.","Michael slowly walked around the enormous Bone Dragon, inspecting every section of its body. Its bones possessed a metallic sheen.","Every joint was engraved with naturally formed runes that continuously gathered Death Energy from the surroundings. Its soul fire burned steadily without the slightest sign of instability.","The wyvern wasn't much worse. Although smaller than the dragon, its wings were exceptionally broad and its bones considerably lighter.","\"...Not bad.\"","Michael became increasingly satisfied the more he looked. These weren't ordinary summons. They had obviously been cultivated carefully over many years.","Varek had likely invested an enormous amount of resources into raising them to this level.","Even their foundation was stronger than his undead High Drake's base stats, though that couldn't be helped given the difference in accumulated time.","In any case, these two now belonged to him.","Michael chuckled.","\"I suppose I should thank him.\"","If Varek hadn't been so unwilling to accept someone ranked above him, these two powerful undead would never have fallen into his hands.","Thinking about the expression Varek would probably have after returning to the Origin Battlefield made Michael's smile grow even brighter.","\"I wonder if he'll challenge me again.\"","After a brief pause, he shook his head.","\"...Hopefully.\"","After all, there might still be several more valuable undead waiting inside that generous necromancer's collection.","Michael's eyes lingered on the Bone Dragon and Bone Wyvern for another moment before a thought suddenly crossed his mind.","\"...I still have almost three hours.\"","He slowly looked around the endless Deathfrost Rainlands. The battlefield was enormous. More importantly, it was filled with death.","A slow smile spread across his face.","\"...This really is a wonderful place.\"","Such an opportunity wasn't something he intended to waste. Especially now that he had obtained two new peak Rank Four undead.","Michael immediately thought of one of the core abilities granted by his Death Heir class.","Engraving.","Unlike ordinary summoning skills, Engraving wasn't merely a method of storing undead. It absorbed the very essence of a dead creature, preserving its existence within Michael himself.","As long as an engraved undead remained intact, Michael could call it forth whenever he wished.","Even if its temporary body was destroyed, its engraved essence would remain unharmed. It was, without question, one of the greatest methods for keeping the best of his legion and giving them terrifying survivability.","At Rank Three, Michael possessed only twenty engraving slots. And every single one of them was currently occupied.","Naturally, none of those twenty were weak. Even so, that didn't mean some couldn't be replaced. If something stronger appeared, then weaker engraved undead would simply have to make room."]},{"number":1104,"title":"Chapter 1104: Engraving [2]","paragraphs":["There were three methods for clearing occupied slots.","The first was if the engraved undead died. However, this was extraordinarily difficult. Once engraved, an undead's constitution fundamentally changed.","Whenever one was pushed close to destruction, it would instinctively retreat into its engraving to recover.","Of course, that recovery wasn't free. It continuously consumed Michael's energy alongside large quantities of physical materials suitable for reconstructing a new body. But as long as he could afford the cost, an engraved undead was incredibly difficult to eliminate permanently.","The second method was to release the engraving.","By consuming an enormous quantity of energy, along with blood and suitable materials, monster blood worked particularly well, Michael could reconstruct a physical body for the engraved undead, returning their relationship to its previous state before the engraving.","Once the process was complete, the engraving slot would immediately become vacant. Naturally, the resource consumption was astonishing.","The third method was simply erasing the engraved creature, causing it to fade away entirely. Once the remnant link completely dispersed, the engraving slot would naturally become empty.","It was simple, but unbelievably wasteful. Even someone in Michael's position, with thousands of undead, couldn't help but feel it was a loss when dealing with a Rank Four subject.","Fortunately, before entering the arena he had happened to hunt a strong monster.","Knowing he had limited time, Michael used the ape's corpse to create bodies for two undead currently occupying his engraving slots, freeing them through the second method.","The process left Michael noticeably drained. Releasing two engraved undead from their slots and reconstructing bodies for them was not a small matter.","Even with the ape corpse as material, the energy consumption was still heavy.","However, the smile on Michael's face did not weaken. The Deathfrost Rainlands quickly proved its worth.","Dense energy continuously entered his body, and with his own monstrous recovery speed, Michael's condition improved at a visible rate.","Before long, he had recovered enough to begin the next step.","\"Now then...\"","Michael's gaze shifted toward the Bone Dragon and Bone Wyvern.","The first thing he needed to do was simple. Create contract space.","With a thought, Michael's consciousness entered the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion. Inside that legendary-grade treasure, thousands of undead remained stored in perfect silence.","He casually selected two random Rank Three undead and severed the contracts between them.","Michael wasn't worried about them causing trouble. They were currently inside his own world.","Even if they regained a little freedom, they were still trapped within the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion.","Besides, with the terrifying undead stationed there, two ordinary Rank Three undead couldn't create any real disturbance.","The moment the two contracts were cut, two empty contract slots opened. Michael immediately turned his attention back to the Bone Dragon and Bone Wyvern and contracted them as well.","However, the process was so smooth that Michael himself was left in disbelief.","\"...That easy?\"","He had just contracted two Level 100 peak Rank Four undead while only being Level 75.","Even with the undead already suppressed under his domination, this ease was still ridiculous.","Michael couldn't help but sigh again at the advantage of his class.","Death Heir.","Against creatures of death, the authority it provided was simply unreasonable.","After the contracts stabilized, Michael wasted no time.","\"Let me start engraving.\"","Compared to contracting them, Engraving retained the difficulty it should have possessed when dealing with powerful undead. The Bone Dragon and Bone Wyvern were Level 100 peak Rank Four existences.","Even though Michael had already contracted them, engraving their essence into himself was still far from effortless.","Fortunately, the environment was perfect. The Deathfrost Rainlands continuously supplied dense Death Energy and Yin Cold Energy, reducing much of the burden.","The two undead also offered no resistance, allowing the process to proceed far more smoothly than it otherwise would have.","The moment the process ended, Michael felt his body grow heavier, but also stronger. The passive benefits from the new engravings flowed through him, filling him with a dense, stable power.","For a brief moment, a thought appeared in his mind.","\"Could I... handle a Rank Five undead now?\"","With his current accumulation, evolving more than one undead to Rank Five was not impossible. But Michael soon shook his head.","Rank Five beings were called Demigods for a reason.","From that realm onward, supernatural beings truly began touching divinity. And he was still only Rank Three. If a Rank Five undead broke free from his control, Michael had no confidence it wouldn't immediately turn on him.","Still, he hadn't given up on the idea. His current stats already surpassed many Rank Four awakeners.","Once he polished himself further, strengthened his soul again, and relied on the full advantage of his Death Heir class, perhaps the risk would become acceptable.","Michael exhaled slowly.","\"That's for later.\"","With nothing else left to do inside the arena, he opened the exit option. The Deathfrost Rainlands blurred around him. A moment later, Michael disappeared.","The surrounding scenery dissolved into streaks of light before the entire world twisted. A moment later, Michael felt solid ground beneath his feet once again.","The familiar mountain range where he had accepted Varek's challenge reappeared around him exactly as he had left it.","The shattered rocks, the lingering traces of battle from earlier, and even the direction of the cold wind remained unchanged.","\"...Back.\"","Michael slowly looked around. Nothing had changed. He had truly returned to the exact location where he had accepted the challenge.","Realization dawned on him almost immediately.","\"...Just another hidden trap.\"","His expression became somewhat strange. He had initially assumed participants would return to a random location after leaving a ranking arena.","Instead, the Origin Battlefield returned everyone to their previous position. At first glance, it seemed perfectly reasonable. But after thinking about it for only a moment, \"If someone knew where I was before accepting a challenge...\"","\"...they could simply remain here.\"","The moment the battle ended, regardless of whether he won or lost, he would reappear in exactly the same place."]},{"number":1105,"title":"Chapter 1105: Terrifying World","paragraphs":["That was practically inviting an ambush. The ranking arena itself was safe enough, but the moment one stepped outside, that protection vanished.","Michael rubbed his chin thoughtfully.","Perhaps in the future he would see schemes like someone deliberately challenging an opponent, losing on purpose, and then immediately notifying allies waiting outside.","Or perhaps several people could simply watch someone disappear into a ranking battle before surrounding the area where they had vanished.","The instant that person returned, they would be greeted by an ambush instead of an empty battlefield.","Michael clicked his tongue.","\"The Origin Battlefield really likes hidden rules.\"","Almost every new function it revealed seemed harmless on the surface. Yet many of them concealed another danger.","If one wasn't careful, a small oversight today could easily become the cause of death tomorrow.","Fortunately, Michael currently didn't have any enemies capable of organizing something like that.","At least none that he knew of. The angel girl had probably survived their previous encounter, but she neither knew his identity nor possessed enough influence to arrange an ambush so quickly.","As for Varek, Michael doubted the necromancer was even in the same region as him. And even if he were, the fellow probably wouldn't dare confront him again.","The thought almost made him laugh.","Still, just because he was safe today didn't mean he would always be safe.","\"I'll have to remember this.\"","From now on, before accepting any ranking challenge, he would first ensure his surroundings were suitable. If necessary, he could even deliberately move to an isolated location before responding.","The longer Michael remained inside the Origin Battlefield, the more he realized that surviving here required far more than simply possessing overwhelming strength.","After finally having some uninterrupted time to himself, Michael truly began exploring the Fourth Layer. There was no need to rush.","He only needed to survive a little over forty-eight more hours before the temporary stay granted by the Origin Battlefield ended and he would be returned home.","With that thought in mind, Michael became considerably more restrained.","The previous battle against Varek had reminded him that while he could contend with ordinary peak Rank Four awakeners, there were still countless unknown monsters lurking within this place.","His current objective wasn't to become famous. It was to return alive.","Of course, it would also be ideal if he came across some wild, formidably strong undead along the way.","The following hours passed quietly. Michael traveled through mountain ranges, abandoned plains, frozen valleys, and forests filled with all manner of creatures.","Occasionally he would stop to hunt monsters guarding treasures, gradually learning things Lily and her companion had discovered much earlier.","But it couldn't be helped. He had been chased by hundreds of awakeners within seconds of entering the Fourth Layer.","Fortunately, for the next two days nothing truly dangerous happened to him, and his knowledge of the Origin Battlefield continued to grow.","Like Lily and Timi, Michael had also come across Level 2 regions in the Fourth Layer, though the situation there wasn't as dramatic as what they had encountered in the Zeroth Layer.","The only notable changes were that treasures appeared more frequently, monsters were stronger and more often approaching the late stages of Rank Four, and all consistently graded as Three-Star Extraordinary.","As for a Level 3 region, Michael had yet to encounter one.","However, on his second day, with only a few hours remaining before the return, he encountered something unexpected.","The heavens split apart.","BOOOOOOM!","Five enormous pillars of light descended from the sky almost simultaneously. Even from a great distance, Michael could feel astonishing waves of energy radiating outward.","\"Another treasure descent...\"","He wasn't surprised to see it. If anything, he had half expected it.","His eyes swept across the five descending beams. The central pillar was by far the brightest.","Even before anyone approached it, Michael could already tell that whatever treasure rested there was almost certainly the finest among the five.","Based on his earlier experience, he suspected it was comparable to, if not better than, his incense.","However, that probably also meant it was a problem.","Michael's perception spread outward. One. Three. Seven. Ten. Powerful auras began rushing toward the descending treasures from every direction.","Within moments, Michael had already sensed close to twenty peak Rank Four awakeners converging on the brightest pillar alone.","His lips twitched.","\"...I'll pass.\"","He wasn't stupid. The previous treasure descent had already taught him enough.","The strongest treasure always attracted the strongest competitors. And right now, Michael had absolutely no intention of throwing himself into the middle of nearly twenty Level 100 peak Rank Four awakeners.","Even if he believed he could survive s, there was no guarantee he could actually leave with the treasure without losing some of his undead.","More importantly, he only had a few hours remaining before returning home. There was no reason to gamble everything now.","Instead, his gaze shifted toward one of the dimmer pillars far from the center.","\"...That one looks much quieter.\"","Compared to the battlefield surrounding the strongest treasure, only three powerful auras seemed to be heading toward this location. With a faint smile, space distorted around him.","Whoosh!","His figure disappeared, leaving only drifting mist behind as he calmly headed toward a treasure that, while perhaps not the greatest, had a far higher chance of actually ending up in his hands.","Chasing the treasures, Michael found that his earlier speculation had been completely correct. In the future, every battle over these descending treasures would become unimaginably bloody.","What he hadn't expected was for it to happen so soon.","It seemed that while he had been playing things safe and exploring other parts of the Fourth Layer, similar treasure descents had already occurred elsewhere.","The news had spread rapidly across the Origin Battlefield, drawing powerful awakeners from every direction whenever another treasure appeared.","However, what truly caught Michael off guard wasn't the competition surrounding the treasures.","It was something else entirely. Something that sent a chill down his spine.","[You have killed a Level 82 Half-Elf]","[You have received **** Experience Points!]","Michael froze.","\"...Experience?\"","This was the first intelligent lifeform he had personally killed since entering the Origin Battlefield. Yet somehow, something that had never occurred since the appearance of awakeners in the universe had happened here.","He had gained experience points from killing an intelligent race.","If intelligent races awarded experience, then the Origin Battlefield wasn't merely encouraging conflict. It was rewarding slaughter.","This was indeed the true world created for awakeners alone."]},{"number":1106,"title":"Chapter 1106: Power","paragraphs":["The mountain range had long since fallen silent.","More than forty awakeners stood scattered across the shattered peaks, none of them daring to move. Their eyes were fixed upon the young man floating calmly in the evening sky, filled with pure, undisguised fear.","Michael hovered high above them, his expression as indifferent as ever. His pale skin reflected the fading sunlight, while his handsome features seemed almost ethereal beneath the evening glow. His emerald-green eyes shone faintly, carrying neither excitement nor anger. Only indifference.","In one hand, he held a treasure whose brilliant radiance was rapidly fading, signaling that the Origin Battlefield's tracking effect had already been completed.","Beside him, a headless corpse slowly tumbled from the sky. Blood rained onto the broken mountains below.","But the youth himself wasn't the only source of everyone's fear. It was what surrounded him.","Undead.","They were everywhere, surrounding the youth. Some might not have recognized them at first glance, but they were surely undead.","Then again, was there anything that represented the beauty of death more fittingly than undead?","Some towered over the mountains like moving fortresses. Others floated silently through the air. Each possessed a different appearance, and each radiated a terrifying aura.","Most importantly, there were simply too many. The undead outnumbered the gathered awakeners by more than two to one.","Although the majority of Michael's Rank Four undead were only in the early stages of Rank Four and lacked the combat techniques, treasures, and experience possessed by intelligent races, quantity had a quality of its own.","Two ordinary Rank Four undead working together were more than capable of matching an experienced awakener. Even if they couldn't kill them, stalling was more than enough.","The current situation looked as though a long and brutal battle had already taken place. In reality, barely a minute had passed.","The reason these awakeners appeared so miserable wasn't because they had fought for a long time. It was because they had been completely overwhelmed by Michael's legion.","Only a short while earlier, the treasure's previous holder had been fleeing desperately through the mountain range.","Nearly fifty Rank Four awakeners had chased after him without pause, gradually cornering him from every direction. Realizing he would be caught sooner or later, the man made a decisive choice and threw the treasure into the crowd.","The glowing orb shot across the battlefield like a meteor. Everyone abandoned the fleeing awakener and lunged toward the treasure simultaneously.","Yet just before anyone reached it, a figure appeared seemingly out of nowhere and snatched it.","Naturally, that figure was Michael.","Unlike everyone else, he hadn't rushed forward the moment the treasure descended. Instead, he had hidden himself from the very beginning, patiently observing the situation while waiting for the treasure's protective light to weaken to a level he found acceptable.","The instant it reached that point, he moved.","Of course, Michael had never intended to face nearly fifty Rank Four awakeners by himself. But compared to the first incident, no one here seemed capable of threatening him with a genuine loss among his undead.","Still, to be safe, Michael summoned a hundred relatively strong undead from the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion. This was double the number of awakeners pursuing him.","Seeing such a terrifying legion descend upon the battlefield, Michael had naturally expected the others to retreat. After all, there wasn't a single peak Rank Four awakener among them.","Things didn't proceed as he expected.","Although the expressions on every awakener's face changed drastically and fear became visible in many of their eyes, not a single one fled. Instead, they continued attacking.","Michael was confused at first. Surely, to have reached this stage, they weren't idiots.","The only thing he could think of was that if they were willing to fight despite such overwhelming odds, the value of these descending treasures had already spread throughout the Fourth Layer, and no one wanted to surrender one so easily, even if the odds looked hopeless.","This was precisely why Michael was so cautious about fighting these veterans.","Fortunately, he was the stronger party. His undead immediately surrounded the awakeners, completely suppressing them through sheer numerical superiority.","The battlefield quickly descended into chaos, with many awakeners barely holding their limbs together.","Michael had assumed they would soon lose the will to fight after being beaten senseless and was wondering whether to summon more undead or deploy one of his engravings, when one awakener suddenly broke through a gap in the encirclement and charged at him directly.","He accelerated explosively, his spear wreathed in ice magic and shining with blinding light as he shot toward Michael like a bolt of lightning.","Unfortunately, he had severely overestimated himself.","Caught by surprise, Michael's body simply moved on instinct. His fist descended.","BOOOOM!!","The air exploded. The mountains trembled. The entire sky seemed to distort around the single punch.","The awakener's spear shattered into countless fragments before the fist continued onward without losing any momentum. His protective treasure exploded. His armor caved inward. His body collapsed instantly. The upper half simply disappeared.","Blood and shattered flesh erupted into the air before raining across the mountains.","Absolute silence filled the range. Every remaining awakener froze. Their pupils trembled as they stared at the young man in the sky.","Until now, they had believed the terrifying undead legion was the greatest threat. Now they realized the legion wasn't protecting Michael. Michael was leading it.","And judging from that single punch, the young man himself might very well be even more terrifying than the monsters currently surrounding them.","Cold sweat streamed down countless faces.","Only then did they realize that Michael had never personally targeted any of them. If he had been bloodthirsty from the start, many of them would already be among the corpses lying across the shattered mountains.","The realization filled everyone with lingering fear.","Ironically, what they didn't understand was that if they hadn't continued resisting so desperately, or if that awakener hadn't attacked and forced Michael's hand before he had time to consider adding more numbers to the encirclement, half of them would be dead now."]},{"number":1107,"title":"Chapter 1107: Building, Where The Pillar Stood [1]","paragraphs":["Michael stared at the experience panel before him in disbelief.","When had it become possible to gain experience from killing other intelligent races outside of monsters? However, after the initial surprise, and after linking it to the uniqueness of the Origin Battlefield, he stopped dwelling on it.","Though only a few months had passed, he was no longer the Michael who recoiled at whatever uncomfortable thoughts might surface. He had already killed people before, and all of them had been enemies who came at him first.","As long as he continued operating within that boundary, it didn't matter whether they granted experience points or not.","In any case, thanks to a certain cursed title, Michael wasn't particularly interested in experience points, especially since at his maxed level any he gained would simply be wasted.","That was, of course, a different matter for his undead.","It was foreseeable that in the future, all awakeners in the Origin Battlefield, Michael included, would become far less forgiving toward opponents once this reality spread.","Michael didn't have long to sink into his thoughts, however. Much to his surprise, the awakeners who had been fighting so energetically moments ago had now fled into the distance.","\"...\"","\"They don't want the treasure anymore? I thought they'd put up a bit more of a fight before giving up. Strange.\"","Wondering why they had fled even faster than they had originally chased the treasure, he turned to look down at the object resting quietly in his palm.","It was surprisingly small. Roughly the size of an adult's fist. The treasure resembled a perfectly spherical metal orb forged from an unknown silver-black alloy.","Its surface was covered in countless crimson runes that intertwined with one another, forming an intricate network across the entire sphere.","Every few seconds, one of the runes pulsed faintly before falling silent again.","Even without Detect, Michael could feel the terrifying destructive energy sleeping within it.","\"...Surely it's not a bomb, right?\"","With a thought, Michael activated Detect. Immediately, a panel appeared before him.","[Rune Annihilation Sphere] Grade: One-Star Epic Description: A disposable treasure created by compressing an enormous quantity of destructive energy within a runic shell.","Once activated, the sphere detonates after a brief delay, releasing catastrophic force over a wide area. Effects: Releases a devastating explosion equivalent to the full-force magic attack of a Peak Rank Four powerhouse.","The explosion ignores most forms of ordinary elemental resistance. Effective destruction radius scales with the surrounding environment. Restrictions: Single Use. Cannot be interrupted once activation is complete.","\"Heavens, it really is a bomb!!!\"","Michael flinched slightly and immediately threw the treasure into his storage space. Only then did he calm down somewhat.","\"Another good harvest. Although it's only a One-Star Epic treasure, even for me it can serve as another trump card.\" He suspected the same would be true for many Level 100 awakeners.","\"But its grade feels a little low for something with this much destructive power.\"","According to the description, the Rune Annihilation Sphere could unleash an attack comparable to the standard full-powered magic attack of a Peak Rank Four powerhouse.","That wasn't weak by any stretch of the imagination. If it was comparable to the dragon breath of the undead High Drake, it might even be better than that. But it was only a One-Star Epic treasure.","\"It must be because it's disposable.\"","That was the only explanation that made sense. Permanent treasures naturally possessed far greater long-term value than something that could only be used once.","No matter how terrifying a single attack was, once it exploded, it was gone forever. If this treasure could be reused repeatedly, Michael had little doubt its grade would be far higher.","Aside from the treasure's type and grade, Michael had also learned a few more things about descending treasures. His eyes unconsciously drifted toward the sky.","\"This treasure only came from one of the weaker beams of light, and it was still an Epic-grade treasure. Does that mean all five descending treasures were Epic-grade? The only difference is probably their value within the Epic grade itself.\"","The brighter the descending light, the more valuable the treasure hidden inside. Michael found the theory increasingly reasonable.","His first descent had rewarded him with the Three-Star Epic Incense of Enlightenment, so extraordinarily useful that even now he considered it one of the greatest treasures he possessed.","This second descent had only involved one of the weaker lights, yet it still contained a One-Star Epic treasure capable of threatening peak Rank Four awakeners.","Both of them were also consumables.","Michael couldn't help but wonder if this was simply his luck, or if this was how descending treasures normally worked.","\"I really want another treasure like the Incense of Enlightenment. If I manage to obtain one or two more from the brightest descent, I should be able to determine whether that first Incense was merely coincidence, or whether the greatest descending treasure is always something on an entirely different level.\"","As his thoughts wandered, he recalled his undead back into his spatial world and continued exploring.","More time passed.","What Michael hadn't expected was that just four hours before his departure, he would come across a special location in the Origin Battlefield.","\"Is this a building? What's a building doing in the Origin Battlefield?\"","The Land of Origin had been vast beyond imagination.","The Origin Battlefield was no different. Mountains, valleys, forests, swamps, deserts, frozen wastelands, volcanic regions, the Fourth Layer alone contained environments that looked as though they belonged to entirely different worlds stitched together by some incomprehensible force.","Over the past two days, Michael had gradually discovered another pattern. The Origin Battlefield wasn't simply divided into layers. It was also divided into regions.","Each region possessed a numerical designation.","Level 1. Level 2. Level 3. The higher the regional level, the richer the resources became.","Naturally, the danger increased alongside them.","Fortunately, Michael had also noticed another rule. The Origin Battlefield appeared to maintain an astonishing degree of balance. This was only the Fourth Layer."]},{"number":1108,"title":"Chapter 1108: Building, Where The Pillar Stood [2]","paragraphs":["By all indications, Rank Five creatures simply shouldn't exist here. Otherwise, the Fourth Layer would become an impossible death trap for Rank Four awakeners.","Even so, Michael didn't allow himself to become careless.","Just because there shouldn't be Rank Five monsters didn't mean there couldn't be something equally troublesome.","With that thought, Michael had activated his stealth ability before entering the newly discovered Level 3 region.","The moment he crossed its invisible boundary, Michael immediately sensed the difference. The density of energy rose dramatically.","Even the vitality of the surrounding vegetation became noticeably richer. The ancient trees growing here towered several hundred meters into the sky. Their trunks were thicker than castle walls, and the air itself carried a faint oppressive pressure.","\"...As expected.\"","The higher the region, the more extraordinary everything became.","Michael carefully advanced deeper. For nearly ten minutes, nothing happened. Then Michael suddenly stopped.","\"...Hm?\"","His sharp senses picked up movement.","\"A hundred creatures in one place?\"","His expression became thoughtful. The strange thing wasn't merely the number. It was that every aura belonged to the same species.","Thinking a monster nest was nearby, curiosity followed caution. Instead of retreating, Michael concealed himself even further before silently approaching.","But the further he advanced, the denser the monster population became.","The creatures he saw were large wolf-like beings covered in dark gray scales instead of fur. Their eyes burned with crimson light while jagged bone spikes protruded from their backs.","Every single one possessed strength at least comparable to an early Rank Four monster. Yet there were hundreds. Perhaps close to a thousand.","\"This is no ordinary nest. Could it be related to the Origin Battlefield itself? This region is a newly discovered Level 3 for me, so perhaps it's not surprising that things are different here...\"","Michael had encountered monster groups before. But never on this scale. It didn't resemble a hunting pack. It resembled an organized colony. The monsters weren't wandering randomly.","Many continuously moved toward a single direction before returning moments later, almost like workers performing assigned tasks.","\"...What are they guarding?\"","Michael's curiosity deepened. Keeping his breathing perfectly steady, he slipped between the countless monsters without disturbing even a single one. Minutes passed. The nest became increasingly dense.","Eventually he reached the center, and what he saw there made him even more shocked.","\"Epic Grade Level 100 monsters? And there are four of them?\"","Michael narrowed his eyes as his heart beat rapidly in his chest.","\"...That's strange. But why does it look like they're defending something?\"","He turned to look around and observed that at the very center stood a structure. It rose nearly thirty meters high, resembling an ancient stone tower weathered by countless years. Its surface was covered in mysterious black runes that pulsed rhythmically, almost like a beating heart. Countless cracks spread across its walls, while thick chains extended from its foundation deep into the earth, disappearing beneath the surrounding stone.","Michael's expression slowly became serious.","\"...What exactly is this thing?\"","To be honest, Michael already had a fairly good idea. From Level 1 to Level 2 regions, monster nests frequently contained treasures. It wasn't guaranteed.","Some nests offered nothing beyond the monsters themselves, but a lucky nest could still provide valuable corpses, rare raw materials, and a generous amount of experience.","If the creature ruling the nest was powerful enough, it could also produce a Treasure Orb after death. In other cases, the monsters gathered resources naturally over many years and stored them within their dwellings.","Regardless of which situation applied, monster nests were rarely without value. Michael was willing to bet the lives of his enemies that the enormous colony before him followed the same pattern.","The strange tower was either a treasure itself, or it concealed something extremely valuable.","Unfortunately, though the possible treasure was right in front of him, Michael didn't dare act rashly.","The four creatures standing before him were all Epic Grade Level 100.","Michael remained hidden, his entire presence suppressed as his glowing green eyes carefully studied the nest's center.","Surrounding the ancient tower were four enormous figures. Despite their differences, they all clearly belonged to the same species.","The first possessed three massive heads, each with a different pair of glowing crimson eyes. Its body stretched nearly twenty meters long, while dark metallic scales covered its limbs and back instead of fur. Thin streams of scarlet flames escaped from its three mouths with every breath.","The second was noticeably bulkier. It stood on four colossal legs with broad shoulders and an exceptionally muscular frame. Thick black bone plates naturally covered its neck, chest, and spine, giving it the appearance of wearing heavy natural armor.","The third was the fastest-looking of the four. Its body was lean and streamlined, with long powerful limbs built for explosive bursts of speed.","Two pairs of black feathered wings rested neatly against its sides, while razor-sharp bone blades extended from its forelegs like natural weapons. Even standing still, faint gusts of wind continuously swirled around its body.","The final wolf was by far the largest. Its dark silver fur shimmered faintly beneath the dim light, while dozens of jagged bone spikes protruded from its shoulders and back.","A heavy black mist drifted endlessly around its body, obscuring its paws and making it seem as though it floated above the ground.","Of the four, its aura was the calmest, yet also the most oppressive. Even the surrounding monsters unconsciously kept a greater distance from it.","Michael's expression became increasingly solemn.","For the first time, Michael finally understood what his enemies must have felt whenever they faced his strongest undead.","What stood before him wasn't simply a group of four Level 100 creatures. It was more like four different forces of nature wearing physical forms.","If Michael had never encountered Epic Grade creatures before, he might not have fully understood the danger.","Unfortunately, he was very familiar with them. At the same level, Epic Grade creatures were almost unrivaled except by their peers. Their attributes, bloodlines, skills, and natural abilities all surpassed lower-grade creatures by a frightening margin.","This held true across all ranks, but starting from Epic Grade, the difference began to become genuinely ridiculous.","These were precisely the type of creatures Michael would have expected the Origin Battlefield to reject from the Fourth Layer. Yet here they were.","Perhaps they had been weakened in some manner, or their abilities restricted. Or perhaps they were simply what the Origin Battlefield considered to be the extreme threshold of Rank Four."]},{"number":1109,"title":"Chapter 1109: Intruders [1] (Edited!!!!)","paragraphs":["If Michael had never seen the treasure, he wouldn't have cared. That was normal. After all, how could someone desire something they didn't even know existed?","Unfortunately, Michael had already seen it. Now that he had, simply turning around and pretending the tower didn't exist was almost impossible.","Even if he left this place, the image of the tower would remain somewhere in the back of his mind.","Michael couldn't help but find the current situation somewhat amusing. Before entering the Origin Battlefield, he had wanted absolutely nothing to do with this place.","His reluctance and dislike to this unfamiliar realm was mostly thanks to his cousin. But now, after spending close to three days here, Michael had to admit that he didn't need to be forced to come back. He would return willingly.","Perhaps it was the same for most awakeners who experienced this place.","The Origin Battlefield was obviously dangerous. One mistake could easily lead to disaster. However, danger wasn't the only thing present here. There were also extraordinary opportunities.","The Origin Battlefield was currently a place where an awakener at his stage could experience rapid growth. Perhaps this would change in the future, but for now it was undoubtedly one of the greatest lands of opportunity for awakeners at his level.","In a strange way, it even coincided with Michael's original intention of traveling through the void. Why had he wanted to explore it in the first place?","Even if all its resources were eventually consumed, just the occasional treasure descent alone was worth returning for. The Incense of Enlightenment was already the perfect example.","Now, another mysterious treasure was sitting directly in front of him.","For all Michael knew, it might have nothing to do with Law comprehension or his advancement to Rank Four. But did that really matter?","The fact that four Epic Grade Level 100 monsters and close to a thousand other Rank Four creatures were guarding it already said enough.","Whatever was inside that tower, or whatever the tower itself was, it was special. And Michael wanted it.","\"...This is a huge problem. If only it could be carried away. I'm confident in my speed, but this seems rooted to the ground. And what if I can't even store it? This is so troublesome...\"","Michael carefully observed the four Epic Grade wolves. The three-headed wolf remained lying near the eastern side of the tower.","The enormous armored wolf guarded the west, while the winged wolf and the silver-furred wolf occupied the remaining directions.","Michael continued observing them from a distance, his mind rapidly considering several possibilities.","Could he lure them away?","Even if he managed to draw one or two away from the tower, the remaining creatures would still be a problem. There were also nearly a thousand other monsters surrounding the area.","Could he summon his undead and force his way through?","Though it was a bit reckless and there was a high chance of multiple casualties, dealing with the four using all his cards should be more than doable. However, the main thing causing his hesitation was the value of the treasure.","It was obviously extremely valuable, but it would be deeply painful if he lost one of his primary undead by over something he that might just end up not being worth such a loss.","Just as he was wondering whether to temporarily retreat and return with a better plan, something unexpected happened.","The largest wolf suddenly raised its head. Its dark silver eyes slowly swept across the surroundings. Then it spoke in a strange language, one completely unfamiliar to Michael.","Fortunately, thanks to his status as an awakener and the built-in translation that came with it, the meaning naturally appeared within his mind.","\"If the one hiding is done hiding, come out.\"","\"...\"","Michael's heart sank. For a brief moment his body trembled before he managed to control himself and remained still.","\"...They found me?\"","How? Michael couldn't understand. The four creatures were indeed Epic Grade. Their senses were undoubtedly far superior to those of their ordinary peers.","However, Michael had confidence in his stealth. It was already a powerful ability by itself, and with the passive blessing of his class, all of Michael's abilities associated with darkness and death became even more potent.","Michael's eyes narrowed slightly.","\"...Is it bluffing?\"","It was possible. Perhaps the creature had merely sensed something unusual and suspected an intruder was nearby without knowing Michael's exact position. If that was the case, moving now would only confirm his presence.","Michael remained silent.","Several seconds passed.","The enormous wolf remained still. Its expression was difficult to read since it had a monster's face, and Michael didn't dare hold his gaze on it for too long. But he could almost feel its patience gradually disappearing.","The largest wolf spoke again.","\"I will not repeat myself after this.\"","The dark mist surrounding its body suddenly became denser.","\"Come out.\"","Michael's expression grew grim. This time the wolf began slowly moving its body.","\"...Damn.\"","But Michael still didn't move. His muscles were tensed. Mana silently circulated throughout his body while his spatial abilities prepared to activate at the slightest sign of danger.","He was ready to run. There was no shame in retreating. He could always return later.","Michael was just about to move when he felt a disturbance in another location.","\"...Hm?\"","Michael stopped.","Several meters away from him, the void suddenly rippled. The surrounding space twisted violently before four figures stepped out of nowhere. Michael stared in silent shock.","\"Even with Wisdom State active, how did I sense nothing?\"","It was obvious the newcomers were not simple. But discovering that the wolf hadn't been addressing him gave Michael an indescribable sense of relief.","The four figures that emerged from the void were all humanoid, though most appeared non human.","The first was nearly three meters tall. His skin resembled cracked stone, with faint golden light leaking from the gaps across his muscular body. A massive black hammer rested against his shoulder."]},{"number":1110,"title":"Chapter 1110: Intruders [2] (Edited!!!!)","paragraphs":["Beside the stone skinned man stood a slender woman with pale blue skin. Six transparent wings extended from her back, and long silver hair reached her waist. Her eyes possessed no pupils, only a uniform white glow.","The third figure was covered entirely in crimson armor. Not a single part of their body was visible.","The final person appeared the most ordinary. He was an old man.","A human, at least Michael thought so.","The man wore simple gray robes and held a wooden staff in one hand. His white hair was tied behind his head while a faint smile rested on his wrinkled face.","Michael's eyes immediately narrowed.","\"A mage? Is he the reason I couldn't sense them before?\"","That was Michael's first thought, before he carefully tried to gauge their levels without being discovered.","They were all Level 100.","With such a powerful team comprising four individuals at that level, Michael could have bet the lives of his enemies that they were here for the same treasure. In fact, they had probably been aware of it before him.","The stone-skinned man laughed loudly.","\"So you noticed us.\"","His voice boomed across the area. The other three Epic Grade wolves had by now also sensed the intruders and risen to their feet.","Michael remained hidden throughout all of this. He no longer had any intention of leaving immediately.","Even if he couldn't get the treasure today, the situation unfolding before him was too interesting to abandon.","He wanted to gather as much information as possible before departing.","The silver wolf had already proven that the four Epic Grade wolves were beyond the ordinary monsters of the Origin Battlefield, creatures who didn't simply act on instinct.","He wondered, though, why none of them had taken a humanoid form.","Perhaps it was because they had never seen one. After all, the Origin Battlefield had been inactive for who knew how many years.","The winged woman glanced around.","\"We meant no disrespect.\"","The silver wolf's expression didn't change.","\"Leave.\"","It only uttered a single word.","The stone-skinned man's smile disappeared. The crimson-armored figure remained silent. The old man lightly tapped his wooden staff against the ground.","\"We merely wish to inspect the tower.\"","\"No.\"","The wolf's response was immediate.","The old man's smile widened slightly.","\"Then perhaps we can trade.\"","\"No.\"","\"...You haven't even heard our offer.\"","\"I do not care.\"","Michael almost laughed in his hiding spot.","He liked this wolf.","'Yes! No one should be able to touch or even look at my treasure!'","The old man's smile finally weakened.","Meanwhile, the stone-skinned awakener lowered the massive hammer from his shoulder.","Boom!","The moment its head touched the ground, cracks spread across the surrounding stone.","\"Old man, I told you talking wouldn't work.\"","The winged woman frowned.","\"Don't be reckless.\"","\"Reckless?\" The stone-skinned man grinned. \"There are four of them.\" He pointed toward the Epic Grade wolves. \"And four of us.\"","Michael's expression became strange. Though the four awakeners were clearly powerful, evident from their levels, taking on an Epic Grade creature one on one at the same level would be more than difficult.","Were these four somehow special compared to other Level 100 awakeners?","'If only I knew their names I could check their rankings on the Origin Battlefield leaderboard.'","Also, was that really how they were counting? Did the nearly one thousand Rank Four monsters surrounding the area suddenly become decorations?","Michael genuinely couldn't understand where the stone-skinned man's confidence came from.","The silver wolf stared at him. Then, strangely, it sighed.","\"You strange outsiders who appeared out of nowhere are always the same.\"","Its massive body straightened to its full height. The other three Epic Grade wolves immediately followed.","Scarlet flames poured from the three-headed wolf's mouths.","The armored wolf's bone plates expanded with several loud cracks.","The winged wolf spread its four wings, and the surrounding wind instantly became violent.","Finally, the black mist around the silver wolf surged outward.","\"One final time.\"","Its voice echoed throughout the nest.","\"Leave.\"","The four awakeners didn't move.","Michael's eyes gradually brightened.","\"...Fight. Please fight.\"","He almost said it aloud. The situation couldn't have developed any better. If both sides fought, Michael didn't need to defeat the four Epic Grade creatures by himself.","He didn't even need to lure them away. Someone else would do all of that for him. All he had to do was wait for the perfect opportunity.","Michael felt a very slight pang of guilt. Only very slight, of course. After all, he hadn't asked these people to come here.","If they wanted to risk their lives fighting four Epic Grade monsters, who was Michael to stop them? He was merely an innocent bystander.","The crimson-armored figure finally moved. A low voice emerged from beneath the helmet.","\"Are you truly not afraid for the treasure you are defending? What if we destroy it?\"","The threat was subtle, but everyone present understood it. Even Michael narrowed his eyes slightly, though he didn't believe the four would actually risk destroying the treasure.","There was also the separate question of whether they even had the power to do so.","The silver wolf, however, merely snorted.","\"I do not care.\"","Its response was so casual that even the four awakeners fell silent for a moment.","The old mage's expression became thoughtful. Then, without warning, he raised his staff. Mana erupted.","The spell was short, yet the power compressed into it was enough to make every instinct in Michael's body scream.","A brilliant beam of concentrated energy shot directly toward the ancient tower.","Before it could touch the stone, a transparent barrier suddenly appeared. The spell struck it head-on. Michael expected an explosion.","Instead, the barrier didn't even ripple. The terrifying attack disappeared against its surface as though it had never existed.","Silence followed.","Michael stared at the tower with a solemn expression. The same was true of the other four awakeners.","\"...\"","The mage slowly lowered his staff. His thoughtful expression deepened.","The silver wolf merely watched him.","\"I told you to leave.\""]},{"number":1111,"title":"Chapter 1111: Let’s Fight [1]","paragraphs":["The atmosphere became increasingly tense.","The stone-skinned man tightened his grip around his hammer. The winged woman's six transparent wings slowly spread behind her.","The crimson-armored figure lowered their body slightly, while the old mage's fingers remained wrapped firmly around his wooden staff.","Across from them, the four wolves were equally prepared. A battle could erupt at any moment.","Michael's earlier excitement had already faded considerably. More importantly, if the battle became too destructive, there was no guarantee his stealth would remain effective.","'I should move back a little.'","Michael carefully studied his surroundings. He needed to create some distance without attracting attention. His stealth abilities were powerful, but they didn't make him nonexistent. If he moved too quickly or accidentally disturbed the surrounding energy, any one of these Level 100 beings might notice him.","Michael had just decided on a route when the silver wolf suddenly spoke.","\"Since you refuse to leave...\" Its glowing eyes slowly swept across the surroundings. \"...why don't the others hiding nearby come out as well?\"","Michael's heart sank.","'Damn.'","For a moment, he genuinely thought he had been discovered. His consciousness instantly connected with the engraving of the Undead High Drake.","The slightest thought was all he needed, and it would appear. Perhaps because of the heightened tension surrounding him, Michael almost summoned it immediately.","However, at the final moment, he stopped himself.","'Wait.'","Michael forced his body to remain perfectly still. His heartbeat slowed. If the wolf had truly discovered him, why hadn't it looked in his direction? More importantly, it had said others.","Michael waited.","One second. Two. Three.","Nothing happened.","The silver wolf's eyes became colder.","\"Must I drag you out?\"","Whoosh!","A brilliant golden light suddenly erupted from the distant forest. Michael's pupils contracted.","A figure rose into the sky. Six white wings spread behind him, each feather glowing with dense energy. His hair flowed freely behind him, while an ornate wand remained tightly held in one hand.","Michael's eyes widened.","'Him?!'","How could he not recognize him? The Rank Four angel. The same man who had chased him for his treasure alongside two other Level 100 awakeners shortly after entering the Fourth Layer.","Michael's expression immediately became strange.","'What kind of coincidence is this?'","However, before he could properly process Lord Seraphiel's appearance, the temperature suddenly increased.","FWOOSH!","Scarlet flames erupted from another section of the forest. The flames spiraled into the sky before gradually gathering into a humanoid figure.","A middle-aged man with a bare upper body stepped out from the sea of fire. Long crimson hair rested against his shoulders, while a pair of enormous wings formed entirely from scarlet flames burned behind him.","Michael's heart skipped again.","'The phoenix too?!'","His expression almost collapsed. He recognized this person as well. These two were precisely among the people who had caused him the most trouble after he first entered the Fourth Layer.","The angel. And the phoenix.","Michael stared at them silently.","'This world is too small.'","No. The Fourth Layer was enormous. That made the situation even stranger. He had spent almost three days wandering randomly, only to encounter two people he already knew in the first Level 3 region he entered.","Fortunately, neither seemed to have noticed him.","The phoenix's expression was noticeably ugly as he stared at the silver wolf. The angel, on the other hand, appeared far calmer.","\"So you noticed us too.\"","The silver wolf snorted.","\"You outsiders are terrible at hiding.\"","Michael's expression became slightly offended.","'Don't include me.'","He was still hidden. That alone proved his stealth was clearly on another level entirely.","The stone-skinned man looked toward the two newcomers and frowned.","\"More people?\"","The old mage's eyes narrowed slightly. Unlike his companion, he appeared to recognize something.","\"Celestial race...\" His gaze then shifted toward the crimson-haired young man. \"...and Phoenix Clan.\"","The angel ignored him. His eyes remained fixed on the tower. The phoenix glanced at the four Epic Grade wolves before turning toward the angel.","\"Still want to try?\"","The angel remained silent for several seconds. Then he slowly nodded.","\"Yes.\"","Michael's eyes brightened.","The silver wolf's expression, however, became colder.","\"Six.\" Black mist spread further across the ground. \"Six outsiders who cannot understand a simple word.\"","The three-headed wolf growled. The armored wolf lowered its enormous body. The four-winged wolf vanished.","BOOOOM!!","The ground suddenly exploded. The stone-skinned man's expression changed drastically as a black blur appeared directly before him.","CLANG!","His massive hammer rose just in time. A bone blade collided against its surface. The resulting shockwave tore through the forest for several kilometers.","The battle had begun.","Michael remained perfectly still. Yet beneath his concealment, a smile slowly spread across his face.","'Six against four...'","His gaze moved toward the ancient tower. Then toward the nearly one thousand wolves surrounding it. Finally, he looked at the angel.","Michael's smile widened. It seemed leaving the Origin Battlefield soon was no longer an option. Not that he was complaining. All he wanted them to do was fight, and he would clean up afterward.","For the first time since becoming a supernatural, Michael was playing the role of the fisherman. Well. Perhaps it was the second time.","AWOOOOOOOOOOO!","His amusement lasted exactly three seconds before the four wolves howled simultaneously.","The sound erupted from four directions at once. It wasn't merely loud.","The combined howl carried an almost physical force, spreading through the ancient forest in visible waves. Leaves tore from branches. Loose stones trembled. Even the clouds above the dark sky seemed to scatter beneath the sound.","Everyone's expression changed, including Michael's.","Hearing the howl, they all remembered the nearly one thousand Rank Four monsters outside.","RUMBLE!","The earth began to shake. Michael's perception immediately caught hundreds of auras changing direction at once. The wolves that had previously been scattered throughout the enormous nest were moving, and they were all coming here fast.","Michael's smile vanished.","'Time to go.'","The four Epic Grade wolves hadn't actually needed to howl to alert their subordinates. With the scale of the battle that had just erupted, the other wolves would have discovered the intruders sooner or later. The howl had simply accelerated the process considerably.","Everyone's expression grew ugly. There were six powerful awakeners here against four Epic Grade wolves, and nearly a thousand Rank Four monsters rapidly approaching.","The numbers suddenly didn't look very favorable. They hadn't even had time to properly isolate the area, and it seemed the four wolves had already accounted for that.","Michael carefully began retreating.","'Good luck.'","His fisherman career had ended before it could properly begin. He hadn't even caught a single fish.","Just as it seemed everyone was preparing to retreat, the old mage suddenly spoke."]},{"number":1112,"title":"Chapter 1112: Let’s Fight [2]","paragraphs":["\"Wait.\"","The stone-skinned man blocked another strike from the armored wolf before roaring, \"Old man, if you have something to say, say it quickly!\"","\"We have to deal with these four first.\" The old mage raised his staff.","The winged woman's pupil-less eyes turned toward him.","\"Together?\"","\"For now. We may not be of one mind, but our objective is clearly similar. The specifics can be discussed later.\"","The old man smiled faintly. His gaze briefly swept across the angel and the phoenix.","The angel's expression remained indifferent. However, he didn't reject the suggestion. The phoenix frowned.","\"And the wolves outside?\"","\"Leave them to me.\"","The old mage's answer was immediate, delivered through Wide Voice Transmission so quickly that not a second had passed.","Michael stopped retreating and decided to observe further. The closest monster, though fast, would still take roughly seven seconds to arrive. With his skills and abilities, escape was still more than feasible. He had only paused because of the old mage's transmission.","Wide Voice Transmission. It was a relatively common communication technique among high-ranking supernaturals. Unlike ordinary voice transmission, which formed a direct connection between two specific individuals, Wide Voice Transmission was indiscriminate.","Once activated, the user selected a specific range. Anyone within that range capable of receiving energy-based communication would hear it. More importantly, they could choose to tap into the temporary channel and respond. It was almost like creating a small, temporary room for conversation.","Ordinary voice transmission was different. It required a target. The sender had to locate the person they wished to contact, lock onto their presence, and then establish a connection. If Michael was hidden, an ordinary voice transmission couldn't reach him without discovering him first.","Wide Voice Transmission didn't care. It simply spread a communication channel throughout a designated area. Due to its function, it wasn't a sensory ability. This meant the old mage hadn't actually located Michael. Michael had simply been standing within the range of the technique.","Naturally, Michael had no intention of tapping into the channel and responding. Doing so would immediately announce his presence to everyone within range.","The only reason he had stopped in the first place was the confidence in the old mage's voice.","'What?'","Leave nearly one thousand Rank Four monsters to him? Michael's eyes narrowed. Was this old man secretly a necromancer too?","The thought had barely surfaced when the mage reached into his robe and threw out five metallic disks.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Four disks immediately shot in different directions. One flew east. One west. The remaining two separated toward the north and south.","They moved so quickly that Michael barely tracked them before they disappeared into the distant forest.","The fifth disk fell directly beneath the old mage.","Clink.","The moment it touched the ground, space twisted. A dark circular opening rapidly formed above the disk.","Michael's expression changed.","'A portal?'","It certainly looked like one.","\"That is our escape route,\" the old mage said.","The stone-skinned man's battle will immediately returned.","\"Hahaha! I knew bringing you was the correct choice!\"","The old mage ignored him.","Meanwhile, Michael suddenly sensed something else. His head snapped upward. Far in the distance, four faint lights appeared.","The disks the old man had thrown out in different directions had stopped. Thin black lines erupted from each one, shooting into the sky before rapidly connecting.","East to north. North to west. West to south. South to east.","A gigantic square formed in the air. Michael's pupils contracted as black energy began pouring downward from its edges like curtains.","'A barrier!'","The old man had never planned to fight nearly one thousand Rank Four wolves. He was planning to seal them outside.","Michael immediately understood. And his expression immediately turned ugly.","After all, he was also inside.","'Damn.'","Michael no longer cared about watching the battle. The barrier was descending rapidly. Once it completely formed, he had no idea whether he would be able to escape using his own abilities.","He wasn't opposed to a fight, but he wanted the option to retreat if needed.","Michael hated gambling against unknown magic, especially magic created by a Level 100 mage powerful enough to conceal four peak Rank Four awakeners from his perception.","'I need to get outside the range first.'","Without hesitation, Michael moved.","Whoosh!","His concealed figure shot toward the nearest edge of the forming barrier. The sudden movement immediately disturbed the surrounding energy.","Ten heads turned almost simultaneously.","Michael felt their gazes lock onto him. His concealment collapsed. His pale figure appeared in the open.","The stone-skinned man's eyes widened. The pale-blue-skinned woman froze. The crimson-armored figure actually turned away from the wolf they had been fighting.","The old mage's calm expression disappeared for the first time.","There had been another person here the entire time?!","The silver wolf's glowing eyes narrowed. Clearly, even it hadn't detected Michael.","However, the most dramatic reactions came from two people.","Lord Seraphiel's expression changed.","The phoenix's eyes widened.","\"You!\"","Michael glanced toward them while still moving.","\"...\"","For a moment, he considered pretending not to know them. Then he smiled. A bright, friendly smile. The kind one gave an old friend they hadn't seen in years.","\"Hello.\"","The phoenix's face darkened instantly.","\"You bastard!\"","Michael accelerated.","BOOOOM!","The ground beneath him shattered. The black barrier was already less than a hundred meters from touching the earth. Fifty meters. Thirty. Twenty.","Michael's body blurred.","Ten!","WHOOSH!","He passed beneath the descending barrier at the final moment.","BOOOOOOM!","Black energy struck the earth behind him. The entire Level 3 region trembled.","Michael stopped several kilometers away and slowly turned around. A gigantic black barrier now covered the ancient tower, the four Epic Grade wolves, and the six awakeners.","Outside it, hundreds of wolves were arriving. Their furious roars shook the forest.","Michael stared silently.","\"...\"","Then he looked at the phoenix through the dark barrier. The phoenix was also staring at him. Even from this distance, Michael could practically feel the hatred radiating from the man's eyes.","Michael raised one hand.","He waved.","The phoenix's flames exploded.","\"YOU!\"","Unfortunately, the barrier swallowed whatever else he shouted.","Michael's smile widened.","'What a nice reunion.'","Still, his amusement quickly faded as he considered the old mage.","That had been close. If he had hesitated for another second, he would currently be trapped inside with six Level 100 awakeners and four Epic Grade wolves.","AWOOOO!","His thoughts were interrupted. He slowly turned his head.","Nearly one thousand wolves had gathered around the black barrier. And several of them were looking directly at him.","Michael's expression stiffened.","\"...\"","The wolves stared. Michael stared back. A few seconds passed.","Michael smiled awkwardly.","\"I'm not with them.\"","Growl...","Hundreds of crimson eyes gradually turned toward him.","Michael's smile disappeared.","\"...You don't believe me?\"","The first wolf lunged.","Michael vanished.","BOOOOM!","The ground where he had stood erupted. Far in the distance, Michael's furious voice echoed across the forest.","\"SINCE YOU WANT A FIGHT, LET'S FIGHT!\"","Hundreds of wolves rushed at him.","Michael spread both arms wide in midair as two thousand humanoid figures materialized behind him, casting a colossal shadow over everything below."]},{"number":1113,"title":"Chapter 1113: Battle [1]","paragraphs":["Whether it was the ten figures inside the rapidly darkening barrier or the nearly one thousand wolves rushing toward Michael, everyone was stunned by the sight before them.","For a brief moment, their minds simply failed to comprehend what they were seeing.","One second ago, the sky behind Michael had been empty. The next, nearly two thousand figures had appeared in midair out of nowhere, filling the sky.","Humanoid figures of different heights, builds, and appearances floated behind Michael in complete silence, their green eyes collectively glowing in the darkness and creating an eerie, suffocating sight.","The figures inside the barrier went through a wave of complicated emotions. If that human youth had been trapped in the barrier with them, would they have come out unscathed?","What they didn't know was that Michael had simply been unlucky to lack enough peak Rank Four undead.","If he had possessed more, he would have had his undead match both the quality and quantity of those inside the barrier and dealt with them first. But he didn't, and being trapped in that space would have also meant being targeted by those monsters in an enclosed area.","Even with a large number of undead, the restricted space would have worked against him as well.","Of course, neither side knew the other's thoughts or the realizations that followed.","The phoenix stared outside the barrier with an increasingly ugly expression. Suddenly, his previous pursuit of Michael felt considerably more dangerous in hindsight.","If Michael had summoned all of these undead back then, the phoenix's expression darkened further.","Fortunately, or perhaps unfortunately, none of them had time to dwell on it.","The wolves outside were equally stunned. Their charge visibly slowed. Hundreds of crimson eyes stared upward at the enormous army filling the sky.","Michael noticed this. A faint smile appeared on his face.","'Finally scared?'","Nearly two thousand Rank Four undead. Even if most of them were only in the early stages of Rank Four, numbers like this should have been enough to make anyone reconsider their decisions.","Unfortunately, instead of retreating, their roars became even louder.","AWOOOOOOOO!","The air exploded as hundreds of enormous bodies charged even more fiercely than before.","\"...\"","Michael's smile disappeared.","\"What is wrong with all of you?\"","Did no one in the Origin Battlefield understand the concept of retreat? However, Michael had already summoned his undead. There was no longer any reason to back down.","His emerald eyes became cold.","\"Attack.\"","The moment the command left his mouth, two thousand pairs of green eyes moved simultaneously. Then their bodies began to change.","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","The sound of shifting bones filled the sky. The humanoid appearances maintained by many of Michael's undead collapsed one after another.","Massive bodies expanded violently in midair.","In only a few seconds, the army of humanoid figures disappeared. In its place stood a legion of monsters.","With their true forms unleashed, dense Death Energy immediately flooded the surroundings.","Unlike the undead of other necromancers or wild undead, whose Death Energy often carried a filthy, decaying presence that clung to the skin like rotting mud and filled the air with an uncomfortable sensation of corruption, his undead were nothing like that.","The Death Energy surrounding them was dense. Pure. Almost frighteningly so. There was no disgusting feeling of filth. Only a bone-deep, soul-chilling cold.","Two thousand monsters filled the sky. The sight was horrifying. Yet the transformation wasn't over. Hints of red appeared in their eyes.","[Berserk]","A skill Michael had specifically selected for widespread Memory Infusion. He had encountered many useful skills since becoming an awakener, but Berserk remained one of the most suitable abilities for undead.","For living beings, the skill possessed obvious dangers and costs. Physical strain. Muscle damage. Loss of rationality. In extreme cases, permanent injuries. But undead didn't care about torn muscles.","They didn't fear pain, or have to worry about life energy or physique the way the living did. The primary cost of Berserk when adapted to their bodies was simply energy. As long as sufficient energy remained, they could maintain the enhanced state.","That was why Michael, who had finally had more time to himself over the past three months, had spent a considerable amount of it using Memory Infusion to spread the skill throughout his legion.","The results were now obvious.","BOOOOOOM!","Nearly two thousand Rank Four auras erupted simultaneously. The sky shook.","In terms of levels, Michael's undead were at a disadvantage. The wolves living within this Level 3 region had clearly existed for an extremely long time.","Their average level sat somewhere between Level 85 and Level 90. Meanwhile, many of Michael's undead had only recently entered Rank Four.","If even someone like Lily with all her foundation could only push herself to the early levels of Rank Four, what more could be said about ordinary undead?","Under normal circumstances, the difference in accumulated strength would have been painfully obvious, and the losses would have been severe. But Berserk violently narrowed that gap.","\"Kill them.\"","Michael pointed forward.","The legion moved.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!","Two armies collided. The first impact devastated the forest.","Ancient trees hundreds of meters tall shattered beneath enormous bodies. Mountains trembled as wolves were thrown through stone, while flying undead crashed from the sky with monsters biting into their limbs.","A scaled wolf tore the throat from one undead. The undead didn't even react. Its claws wrapped around the wolf's body. A second undead descended.","BOOM!","The wolf disappeared beneath them.","Elsewhere, seven wolves surrounded an enormous giant undead. The giant roared. Its green-red eyes burned violently as it grabbed one wolf by the hind legs and smashed it into another.","The entire region descended into complete chaos.","Michael floated above it all, his eyes continuously moving across the battlefield. However, his attention didn't remain on the larger battle for long. His eyes soon locked onto five particular wolves.","It turned out the four wolves inside the black barrier weren't the only Level 100 monsters here."]},{"number":1114,"title":"Chapter 1114: Battle [2]","paragraphs":["These five were also Level 100, though fortunately none were Epic Grade. All five were Three-Star Extraordinary.","The five wolves had already chosen their opponents. Or more accurately, they and Michael's undead had chosen each other the moment both sides were revealed.","Facing the five wolves were the Undead High Drake, the Bone Dragon, and the Bone Wyvern.","Two wolves attacked the Undead High Drake, one went against the Bone Dragon, and the remaining two targeted the Bone Wyvern.","At first, the arrangement seemed slightly odd.","The Undead High Drake was the strongest of the three.","Two wolves attacking it made sense, since a single Level 100 Three-Star Extraordinary monster wouldn't be able to stall it for long, let alone defeat it.","Even if one generously assumed some tiny possibility of victory existed, the High Drake would tear its opponent apart before that possibility could become reality.","BOOOOOOM!","A deafening explosion shook the sky. The Undead High Drake's enormous claws collided with the first wolf, forcing its massive body downward.","Before the High Drake could follow up, the second wolf appeared above its head. Its jaws opened and a compressed sphere of gray energy formed.","BOOOOM!","The attack struck the High Drake directly. Its enormous body tilted in the air. The first wolf immediately recovered and lunged again.","Michael watched silently. Noting that the High Drake wasn't in any immediate danger, his gaze shifted.","On another end was the Bone Dragon. Only slightly inferior to the Undead High Drake, the fact that it had once served as Varek's main undead was enough to prove its strength.","Its foundation was genuinely astonishing, having been cultivated over countless years. Yet only one wolf had gone to stop it.","If the wolves were assigning opponents purely by strength, the Bone Dragon should have received two enemies as well. Instead, only one had been sent.","ROOOOOAR!","The Bone Wyvern released a furious roar as two wolves attacked it simultaneously. One tore through the sky from above while the other rushed beneath its enormous body.","The Bone Wyvern twisted. Its skeletal tail struck the first wolf.","BOOOOM!","The wolf was sent flying. However, the second had already reached its left wing.","CRACK!","Powerful jaws closed around the bone. The Bone Wyvern violently rolled through the sky, dragging the wolf with it.","Michael's expression slowly changed.","\"Oh.\"","He now understood. Even the monsters within this nest, aside from the four special ones, possessed better-than-average intelligence and solid battle sense.","From their formation, it was obvious they weren't randomly choosing opponents.","The Undead High Drake was clearly the greatest threat, so two wolves restrained it.","The Bone Dragon was slightly weaker, but its defensive ability was absurd. Sending two wolves after it might not yield a quick result. So they only sent one, enough to keep it occupied, then concentrated on the Bone Wyvern, the assumed weakest of the three.","The Bone Wyvern wasn't weak. It was after all a Level 100 Three-Star Extraordinary undead. But compared to the Undead High Drake and Bone Dragon, it was the most vulnerable of the three. The wolves had noticed and acted accordingly.","If Michael read the situation correctly, the plan was for two wolves to hold down the Undead High Drake, one to stall the Bone Dragon, and the remaining two to concentrate their strength on the Bone Wyvern and destroy it as quickly as possible.","Once it fell, those two would free up, and three could then surround either the Bone Dragon or the High Drake before concentrating all five to finish the last one.","The strategy was simple. But also very efficient.","However, it was far from enough to leave Michael helpless. He had solutions. Several, in fact.","Michael's gaze briefly shifted toward another part of the battlefield. Two enormous serpentine figures were currently tearing through the wolf army. One was engulfed in blue flames.","Every movement of its enormous body left streaks of azure fire across the battlefield. Wolves that approached too carelessly were swallowed by the flames before being struck aside by its tail. The other was surrounded by soft pink fire.","Beautiful flower-shaped flames continuously blossomed around it before detonating among groups of wolves.","The two ancestors of the Black Serpent Empire were causing absolute mayhem.","Michael only needed to call them back. Although both were still some distance from the true peak of Rank Four, they had already reached Level 98.","More importantly, both were powerfull undead with excellent foundations. Defeating a Level 100 alone might be difficult, but defeating one wasn't necessary. They only needed to break the wolves' formation.","Once one wolf was removed from the equation, the Bone Wyvern's situation would immediately improve.","That was one solution.","There was another.","Beginning.","Although Beginning was only Level 96, it had a foundation comparable to an Epic Grade creature. At the same level, Epic Grade creatures were nearly unrivaled.","Even while four levels lower, Beginning was more than capable of fighting a Level 100 Three-Star Extraordinary monster. In fact, if Beginning managed to trigger its ability and burst forth with greater strength, there was a very real possibility it could defeat the wolf entirely.","But the problem also lay with Beginning's Law of Brutal Rebirth. The stronger Beginning became, the more troublesome activating the Law became.","It needed injury. And as Beginning continued growing stronger, ordinary attacks naturally became less capable of causing enough damage, since it needed to be pushed to the brink of death.","Of course, this wasn't truly an issue since Beginning could injure itself, though that method was less effective. Still, the more significant problem was different.","As his opponents grew stronger, Michael had increasingly come to dislike the idea of using Beginning's burst state against powerful enemies.","Perhaps it was because Beginning had accompanied him for so long. Or perhaps it was simply because Beginning was too precious.","Michael didn't like combat styles that depended on recklessly throwing something valuable into danger.","He much preferred dominating battles or having the freedom to maneuver however he wished against similarly leveled opponents."]},{"number":1115,"title":"Chapter 1115: Battle [3]","paragraphs":["Beginning's law was almost designed to always put it in direct conflict with the most powerful enemies present. And at his current level, one mistake was sometimes enough to turn a situation desperate.","The Black Serpent Emperor was a perfect example, since Beginning had nearly tasted true death during that battle, though part of that could also be blamed on Beginning's own tendencies given its law.","Michael continued observing the five wolves. Several breaths passed. His expression gradually relaxed.","\"They aren't that strong.\"","At least, not in the way intelligent Rank Four awakeners were strong.","Their physical abilities were excellent. Their energy reserves were dense. Their instincts were sharp. Their coordination was surprisingly impressive. But their methods were limited, straightforward in a way that made them easier to read and counter.","If these five had been awakeners instead, the battle would have been considerably tougher. It was precisely because of this that Michael hadn't deployed Beginning and had instead relied primarily on the High Drake, whose durability was effectively armor plating.","Even if something happened to it, it would simply become evolution material for Lucky when it eventually advanced to Rank Five.","Watching the wolves fight for a while was enough for Michael to roughly understand their full range of abilities.","With this level of opposition, there was an enormous margin for error even if he used Beginning. His concern slowly faded.","\"Compared to fighting awakeners...\"","His lips curled slightly.","\"Monsters really are easier.\"","The Bone Wyvern was struck again.","BOOOOOOM!","Its skeletal body crashed through an ancient mountain. Before the two wolves could pursue, blue flames suddenly exploded between them.","FWOOSH!","One of the Black Serpent ancestors appeared. Its enormous body twisted through the sky before its burning tail swept horizontally.","BANG!","The nearest wolf was struck directly across the face. Its massive body was pushed back. The second Black Serpent ancestor followed almost immediately. Pink flowers bloomed. The flaming blossoms completely surrounded the same wolf before detonating together.","BOOOOOOOOM!","Pink flames consumed the sky. The two serpent ancestors immediately concentrated on a single Level 100 wolf.","Their objective wasn't to kill it, only to restrain it. With two Level 98 Three-Star Extraordinary undead working together under Berserk, that was more than achievable.","The Bone Wyvern was now left facing a single opponent. The original formation had been broken.","Michael's consciousness moved. Within the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion, a huge figure opened its eyes.","The air beside Michael distorted.","Beginning appeared. Its enormous body descended from above like a falling mountain. Its green eyes immediately locked onto one of the Level 100 wolves.","Michael observed the wolf for another second. He had already seen enough. There was sufficient room for error.","Even if Beginning fought recklessly, the possibility of something immediately fatal occurring was extremely low.","More importantly, Michael's gaze drifted toward the black barrier.","The barrier wouldn't last forever. Inside were four Level 100 Epic Grade wolves. Six powerful Level 100 awakeners. And a treasure whose value was still completely unknown.","No matter which side emerged victorious, the situation after the barrier came down would almost certainly become even more chaotic.","Michael needed to prepare.","He smiled faintly.","\"Beginning.\"","The giant tilted its head slightly.","Michael pointed toward one of the Level 100 wolves.","\"Go.\"","Beginning moved.","BOOOOOOM!","The ground exploded. Its massive figure crossed the battlefield in an instant. The Level 100 wolf reacted quickly. Its dark claws shone with metallic light as it swung forward.","Beginning didn't dodge. Its body simply grew bigger.","BANG!","The claws struck directly against its chest. Five enormous wounds opened. Green acidic blood sprayed through the air.","Michael's eyebrow twitched.","\"...You didn't have to take that directly.\"","Beginning's wounds began closing. The wolf instinctively stepped backward upon seeing this.","Michael stared silently. Then sighed.","\"Well...\"","Perhaps worrying about Beginning fighting recklessly had always been somewhat pointless. Beginning itself clearly had no such concerns.","BOOM!","Its fist descended. The Level 100 wolf crossed both forelimbs and was driven straight into the ground, injuring several undead and fellow monsters along the way.","CRACK!!!","The earth split apart. Beginning descended rapidly and punched again.","BOOM!","Again. BOOM!","Again. BOOOOOOM!","The wolf was steadily driven deeper into the earth.","Michael's eyes slowly widened.","\"Why does it look stronger than before?\"","He was genuinely surprised. The wolf was no weakling, and yet Beginning was dominating it in a way that even surprised Michael, who had watched Beginning fight many times.","Wait. Was it that the wolves simply weren't as strong as he'd assumed, or was it that the Undead High Drake had always been the outlier, making everything else seem weaker by comparison?","Michael had actually never seen the full extent of the High Drake's power. The times it had fought personally alongside him had always been against awakeners, where its strength hadn't looked particularly dominant in context.","And against other undead in sparring, Michael had always made sure not to cross certain limits.","Unfortunately, since it wasn't a monster, Michael couldn't see its grade the way he could for others. All he knew was that it probably didn't qualify as Epic Grade even if such a category applied to it.","Michael glanced once more toward the black barrier. Anticipation gradually appeared in his eyes.","\"Good.\"","Let Beginning warm up now. When that barrier came down, Michael had a feeling the true battle would finally begin.","As for why he was so certain the barrier would eventually fall, it was because he had already used his senses to probe it earlier and confirmed that the energy maintaining it was finite, likely drawn from that thrown disk.","This was also why Michael wanted the battle outside to conclude quickly. Once it was over, he could have his undead concentrate on the barrier simultaneously and potentially hasten its collapse.","As for himself, all he needed to do was stay hidden and conserve his energy.","It seemed that lacking sufficient individual power had, ironically, made him a more careful and methodical necromancer.","But a fake one still."]},{"number":1116,"title":"Chapter 1116: Awareness And Correction [1]","paragraphs":["The situation surrounding the five Level 100 wolves changed almost immediately after Beginning entered the battlefield.","Originally, the wolves had possessed a clear advantage in how they divided themselves. Two restrained the Undead High Drake, one occupied the Bone Dragon, and two concentrated on the Bone Wyvern.","Their intention had been to destroy the weakest target first, then gradually use the freed-up numbers to overwhelm the remaining two. It was a perfectly reasonable strategy.","Unfortunately, Michael had broken their arrangement before it could produce any meaningful result.","The arrival of the two Black Serpent ancestors had drawn away one of the wolves attacking the Bone Wyvern. Now Beginning had entered as well.","The battlefield was reorganized instantly.","The Undead High Drake still faced two Level 100 wolves. The Bone Dragon remained against one. The Bone Wyvern fought one. And Beginning had directly taken the last.","Of course, the distribution was far from equal.","ROOOOOAR!!","The Undead High Drake swept one enormous wing sideways.","BOOOOOOM!","The first wolf was struck across the body and thrown through several mountains. The second immediately appeared above the drake. Its claws descended.","CLANG!","Sparks exploded. The claws carved shallow marks across the High Drake's scales but failed to penetrate deeply. The Undead High Drake twisted violently. Its tail moved.","BANG!","The wolf barely crossed its forelimbs before the strike sent it tumbling through the sky.","Even with two Level 100 Three-Star Extraordinary monsters attacking together, the High Drake showed no signs of being overwhelmed. At most, they were successfully restraining it.","Michael watched for a moment before shifting his attention.","The Bone Dragon's fight was much simpler. It and the opposing wolf had practically entered a contest of durability.","BOOM!","The wolf's claws struck the dragon's ribs. Several bone fragments flew. The Bone Dragon ignored the damage completely. Its enormous jaws closed around the wolf's shoulder.","CRACK!","The wolf howled. Its hind claws immediately tore into the Bone Dragon's chest. More bones shattered. Neither retreated.","Michael's expression became slightly strange.","\"...Idiots.\"","He wasn't even sure which one he was referring to. Fortunately, the Bone Dragon had enough energy to continuously nourish itself, and several tiny cracks were already beginning to repair.","The Bone Wyvern's battle was more dangerous. Although it now only faced one wolf, its previous injuries hadn't disappeared. One wing had several visible fractures and its left side was covered in claw marks.","The wolf had clearly noticed this, as every attack targeted the injured areas. But without another wolf supporting it, the Bone Wyvern could finally fight properly.","The Bone Wyvern's wings suddenly folded.","Whoosh!","The skeletal figure dropped. The wolf followed immediately. Just before reaching the ground, the Bone Wyvern spread its wings.","The skeletal figure dropped. The wolf followed immediately. Just before reaching the ground, the Bone Wyvern spread its wings.","BOOOOOOM!","The sudden change in direction created a violent burst of wind. Its body shot horizontally. The wolf missed. The Wyvern's barbed tail swung backward.","CRACK!","Several spikes pierced the wolf's side. The wolf roared and bit down on the tail. The Bone Wyvern twisted. Both creatures crashed into the forest.","Compared to these three battles, Beginning's fight was almost absurd.","Michael had specifically ordered it not to act recklessly. That meant no intentionally allowing itself to be heavily injured just to trigger increasingly violent bursts of Brutal Rebirth. No deliberately ignoring fatal attacks. No using its body as though it were a disposable weapon. For once, Beginning was fighting with its full strength normally. Or at least, what the undead considered normal.","BOOOOOOM!","Beginning's fist collided against the wolf's skull. The massive beast crashed downward. Beginning followed. The wolf twisted in the air and opened its jaws. Gray energy erupted.","BOOM!","The attack struck Beginning directly in the chest. Its enormous body was pushed backward several hundred meters. The energy disappeared. Large sections of Beginning's chest had been torn apart.","Beginning looked down at its injury before returning its gaze to its opponent.","The wolf immediately moved again. Its claws descended. Beginning could have dodged. Yet it only shifted slightly. The claws that should have torn across its neck instead struck its shoulder. Flesh exploded.","CRACK!","Michael's eyebrow twitched.","\"...Beginning. I said don't be reckless.\"","Still hidden in the void to avoid attracting attention and conserve energy for the battle ahead, Michael communicated mentally with his undead.","Beginning slowly turned back toward the wolf. This time, it dodged.","Completely.","Whoosh!","The wolf's claws passed through empty space. Michael nodded in satisfaction.","Then Beginning grabbed the wolf's hind leg.","BOOOOOOM!","It smashed the creature into the ground. Again. BOOM! Again. BOOM!","The situation looked remarkably familiar. Michael's expression became strange. Perhaps Beginning simply enjoyed smashing things into the ground.","However, despite Michael's command, Beginning wasn't completely abandoning the advantage granted by its Law. That was something Michael also agreed with. Abandoning it entirely would have been foolish. Michael had merely changed the degree.","Attacks that posed genuine danger were avoided. Attacks that would cause excessive damage were blocked. But roughly seventy percent of the wolf's ordinary attacks, Beginning simply absorbed.","BANG!","A claw struck its ribs. Beginning punched the wolf. BOOM! The wolf's tail smashed into Beginning's leg. Beginning grabbed the tail. CRACK! The wolf bit into Beginning's forearm. Beginning drove its knee into the creature's stomach.","BOOOOOOM!","Every injury Beginning received gradually accumulated. Cuts. Fractures. Torn flesh. And with every injury, its aura slowly, steadily grew.","However, the transformation wasn't explosive yet, as Beginning wasn't desperately seeking death.","Michael watched Beginning for a few more breaths before finally pulling his attention away to the much larger battlefield.","At first glance, it was an absolute mess. Mountains continuously collapsed. Ancient trees were torn apart. Flames, poison, lightning, ice, and dozens of other strange abilities erupted in every direction.","One could hardly find an untouched section of land anymore, and this was even after many had confined themselves within the domains of opposing creatures.","Michael silently observed for several seconds. Then his expression gradually became strange.","\"...Have I been too cautious?\"","As a result of almost exclusively fighting stronger opponents the more powerful he became, Michael had unknowingly started evaluating every situation from the most pessimistic angle possible.","But now, looking at the battlefield beneath him, he couldn't help but wonder if his caution had gradually begun turning into underestimating himself."]},{"number":1117,"title":"Chapter 1117: Awareness And Correction [2]","paragraphs":["The battle had not lasted particularly long. Yet Michael had already lost slightly more than twenty Rank Four undead.","It hurt, but it wasn't enough to visibly affect him or significantly strain his soul. In comparison, the wolves had suffered far greater losses, and their casualties were continuing to rise rapidly.","Michael's eyes narrowed.","\"Was I really this strong already?\"","He genuinely began reconsidering his recent decisions.","Naturally, Michael knew he possessed many powerful undead. Beginning. Lily. Wisdom. Jester. Lucky. Prince. Spartan. The Undead High Drake. Several others.","These were all existences Michael considered genuinely exceptional. But perhaps because these undead constantly occupied his attention, he had unconsciously overlooked the rest of his legion.","Michael possessed slightly more than three hundred Epic Grade undead. Many of these were survivors of Michael's expedition into Hell.","This meant that most of their growth had come almost entirely from Michael's evolutions, which had only raised them to Three-Star Extraordinary Grade before they entered Rank Four.","This was different from the corpses Michael had obtained from the academy.","Although the creatures themselves might not have been particularly powerful while alive, the academy specifically only stored corpses with good foundations, which had ultimately served as materials for Michael to fill his contract slots. Because these creatures had already been well developed while alive, the effects of Michael's evolution were far more pronounced on them.","It was reminiscent of when Michael had first begun understanding his talent. Back then, he had noticed that undead with higher levels before evolving usually progressed further in terms of levels after evolution as well.","A better foundation naturally produced better results.","Of course, another reason they progressed so well was Michael's blood. As Michael grew stronger, his blood itself gradually became an increasingly extraordinary evolutionary material.","When used during evolution, it further strengthened his undead and improved their foundations. Because of this, even among undead of the same grade and star level, Michael's undead were considerably stronger, and their prowess could be compared to creatures a full star above them within the same grade.","Of course, no matter how powerful the foundation, there was always a ceiling. This was why Michael still only had close to two thousand Rank Four undead and not four thousand.","The other Rank Three undead were all Three-Star Extraordinary Grade creatures, and Michael could not afford to evolve all of them at once, choosing to continue saving up instead.","In any case, more than three hundred Epic Grade creatures was a terrifying quantity. Unfortunately, their levels weren't particularly impressive. The problem remained the same. Their foundations were insufficient for more rapid growth.","Beginning and Lily were both technically Three-Star Extraordinary creatures before their current developments. Yet could ordinary Three-Star Extraordinary monsters truly be compared to them? Obviously not.","Michael had invested an absurd amount of resources into both, and together with what they had taken without permission, their foundations had been repeatedly strengthened.","Most importantly, both possessed powerful Laws that gave them paths of further progression. Even before reaching Epic Grade, both had already possessed foundations capable of competing with creatures of that level.","The same applied to Wisdom, Jester, and several others. They were anomalies.","Michael's three hundred Epic Grade undead weren't like that. Most had reached their current grade through Infinite Evolution. But evolution couldn't magically create thousands of years of accumulation, nor could it provide the rare opportunities and resources that beings like Beginning had continuously received.","Wisdom was perhaps the clearest example. Its foundation was excellent.","Among Michael's undead, Wisdom had been one of the most carefully developed. Yet after evolving into Rank Four several months ago, it had only reached Level 80. Level 80.","That was merely the beginning stages of Rank Four. If Wisdom, with all its accumulated foundation, had only progressed that far, what could Michael expect from ordinary Epic Grade undead that relied almost entirely on evolution?","Many were still in the low eighties. Some had barely passed Level 80. A few remained just above the threshold of Rank Four.","The stronger one becomes, the harder progressing gets.","Fortunately, evolution remained the fastest shortcut Michael possessed. Though it couldn't replace accumulation completely, it could violently raise an undead's potential and foundation, allowing future progress that would otherwise be impossible.","Michael's gaze settled on one section of the battlefield. An","Epic Grade undead resembling a six-legged black lion was surrounded by three wolves. Its level was only 82.","The lowest wolf attacking it was Level 87. The highest was Level 91. By level alone, the difference was obvious. Yet the black lion wasn't losing. It was being pushed hard, certainly, but only almost.","Michael stared at all this in contemplation.","\"...Right.\"","He had truly been paying too much attention to levels recently and had forgotten his own foundation.","\"...I've really been too cautious. Do I need to start fighting more boldly?\"","Of course, his caution against Level 100 awakeners was still entirely justified.","Varek alone had demonstrated how troublesome an experienced peak Rank Four could be.","The angel and phoenix had been no different.","Monsters were different. Most fought with what they possessed naturally. What Michael saw was usually what he got. Their hidden methods were limited.","That drastically reduced the uncertainty.","Michael's lips slowly curled upward.","\"Perhaps I should separate the two in my mind.\"","He had been treating Rank Four monsters and Rank Four awakeners with almost the same degree of caution.","That was the mistake.","An experienced Level 90 awakener could potentially be more troublesome than a Level 100 monster. Not necessarily stronger. But far more dangerous to underestimate.","The battlefield beneath Michael suddenly shook.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!","A massive explosion swallowed several wolves. When the smoke cleared, an Epic Grade undead stood at the center. Its entire body resembled a tree made from black metal. Countless branches extended from its back. Several wolves had been impaled.","Michael blinked.","\"...When did I get that one?\"","He genuinely couldn't remember. There were too many undead now. That was perhaps another reason he had underestimated his legion.","Once the number reached thousands, individual achievements became difficult to track. His main undead remained memorable because Michael constantly interacted with them."]},{"number":1118,"title":"Chapter 1118: Awareness And Correction [3]","paragraphs":["Michael suddenly felt slightly guilty.","\"I should probably inspect everyone properly after returning.\"","Three hundred Epic Grade undead. He couldn't keep treating them as ordinary soldiers simply because they weren't Beginning or Lily.","Of course, if he ever needed to fully release them in the future, he had to make sure the enemies he faced didn't survive to spread the information.","Three or five Epic Grade monsters could be dismissed as luck. Revealing hundreds would paint a permanent target on his back.","In any case, the presence of those hundreds of Epic Grade undead made one thing increasingly obvious.","The battle was approaching its end. Perhaps not within the next few seconds, but the direction of the battlefield had already become irreversible.","The wolves were powerful. Their average level was higher, and their coordination was impressive for monsters.","But Michael's legion possessed almost twice their numbers, hundreds of Epic Grade existences, and the advantage of Berserk.","More importantly, every wolf that died made the situation worse for the remaining ones.","BOOOOOOM!","The six-legged black lion finally broke free from the three wolves surrounding it. One of its six legs was twisted unnaturally.","Several sections of its body had been torn open. Yet its green-red eyes remained bright.","Its enormous mouth opened as it gathered energy between its jaws.","The three wolves immediately separated, but one was slightly too slow.","A black sphere disappeared into its chest. The wolf froze. For a moment, nothing seemed to happen.","Then black branches erupted from inside its body.","PUCHI! PUCHI! PUCHI!","Dozens of metallic branches tore through flesh and scales.","The wolf collapsed. The two remaining wolves didn't even have time to react.","Five Rank Four undead descended on one. And Four attacked the other.","The black lion joined the first group.","BOOOOOOM!","Less than ten seconds later, another wolf died.","The freed undead immediately separated. Some rushed toward the nearest battles while Others responded to Michael's commands and began surrounding wolves that had already suffered severe injuries.","The effect continued spreading.","Michael's eyes flashed continuously as he monitored his legion.","He had stopped counting his own losses for the moment. Not because he didn't care. Every destroyed undead still caused a painful ache in his soul through the severed contract. But his losses had become increasingly few compared to the wolves.","Right now, his attention had gradually shifted toward something else entirely.","Hundreds of enormous wolf corpses were scattered throughout the Level 3 region. Some were completely destroyed. Others had lost limbs. A few had been crushed beyond recognition. But many were relatively complete.","After several recent realizations about himself, Michael had started forcing himself to think more creatively.","He had a bad habit. Whenever he obtained something, he liked keeping it. But the stronger and faster he grew, he couldn't deny that times had arrived where letting go was the correct choice.","Even things that had clearly fallen behind his current strength were often left untouched because Michael subconsciously believed they might become useful later.","This wasn't necessarily wrong. The problem was that his situation had changed. Michael was no longer the Rank One necromancer who needed every single undead he could get his hands on.","Michael's expression became increasingly thoughtful. His consciousness briefly entered the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion.","Thousands of undead appeared within his perception. Many of his Rank Three undead were Three-Star Extraordinary Grade creatures.","They weren't weak But Michael looked back at the battlefield and saw a Level 89 wolf corpse crash into the remains of a mountain. Its body was almost completely intact. Only its neck had been broken.","Michael looked back at his contracts.","\"...\"","\"Why am I keeping all of you?\"","The question sounded cruel.","Michael rubbed his chin in his hiding spot as his emerald eyes gradually brightened.","\"If I break the contracts...\"","Normally, breaking an undead contract meant losing control of the undead. For most necromancers, that was an obvious problem.","An uncontrolled undead could become hostile or escape. Depending on its intelligence, it might even remember its former master and seek revenge.","But Michael wasn't an ordinary necromancer. His class had already fundamentally altered his relationship with his undead. The ones he created remained his regardless of the contract. Even those he hadn't personally created could come under his influence.","The contract was important as it established a deeper connection for him to use his talent on them, but thanks to recent changes in his talent, he no longer needed a soul connection to evolve a creature.","Michael slowly smiled.","\"...I've been wasting contract slots.\"","The realization struck harder than expected. He had always known that his undead remained under his control even outside the contract system.","He had used this characteristic before. Yet he had never seriously considered deliberately reorganizing his contracts on a large scale.","Why? Because there had never been a need.","Before obtaining the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion, maintaining enormous numbers of uncontracted undead would have been troublesome.","Before reaching Rank Three, high-ranking corpses hadn't exactly been falling into his hands every day, and the cost for evolving a creature to Rank Three could still be managed given his limited contract slots.","Michael also hadn't been at Rank Three for long.","This was the rank where he had reached the peak at an absurd speed and was already preparing to advance again. Before this point, Michael hadn't fully understood the extent of his authority over undead creatures.","BOOOOOOM!","Another violent explosion tore through the ruined surroundings. Michael's eyes immediately shifted.","Just as the battle involving the hundreds of ordinary wolves was rapidly approaching its conclusion, the five troublesome Level 100 wolves were finally reaching their limits as well.","And the first battle to end was, unsurprisingly, Beginning's.","AWOOOO!","The Level 100 wolf released a furious howl. Its entire body was covered in injuries. One eye had already been destroyed.","Several ribs had visibly collapsed inward, while its right forelimb bent at an unnatural angle. Yet the wolf still charged forward."]},{"number":1119,"title":"Chapter 1119: Battle Conclusion [1]","paragraphs":["This was another strange thing Michael had noticed about the Level 3 region.","The wolves here were somehow unwilling to retreat, even when facing certain death. Michael could only attribute it to the special nature of whatever lay within the barrier.","Gray energy gathered around the wolf's remaining claws. The surrounding air split apart beneath the pressure.","Beginning stood opposite it. Its condition didn't look much better, at least visually. Large chunks of flesh were missing from its torso. Green acidic blood continuously dripped onto the earth.","Sssssss!","The ground dissolved wherever the blood landed. Yet Beginning's aura, though it hadn't reached a first-stage burst, was considerably stronger than when the battle had started.","The wolf seemed to sense this as well. Its remaining crimson eye carried a faint trace of unease.","Unfortunately, it was already too late.","BOOOOOOM!","The wolf's body disappeared. Beginning's head turned. Its fist rose. The wolf appeared directly before it. Claws descended. Beginning shifted.","Whoosh!","The attack barely missed its neck. At the same moment, Beginning's fist struck the wolf's lower jaw.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!","The wolf's enormous head snapped upward. Several teeth shattered. Before its body could be thrown away, Beginning's other hand closed around its throat.","CRACK!","The wolf struggled violently. Its claws tore across Beginning's chest. Beginning ignored the attack. Its grip tightened. The wolf's claws struck again.","PUCHI!","Flesh exploded. Beginning's green eyes remained fixed on it. Then its knee rose.","BOOOOOOM!","The wolf's abdomen collapsed inward. Its entire body folded. Beginning released its throat before both hands grabbed the creature's head.","Michael's expression changed.","\"Beginning, wait. The corpse...\"","CRAAAAACK!","The wolf's neck twisted. Its massive body immediately went limp.","\"...\"","Beginning released it. BOOM! The corpse struck the earth.","Michael stared silently. Beginning looked toward Michael's hiding space. Their gazes somehow met despite Michael still being concealed.","\"...At least the body is complete.\"","Michael sighed. He couldn't really complain. The head was still attached. More importantly, Beginning had actually listened to his earlier instructions throughout the battle.","It hadn't recklessly pushed Brutal Rebirth to its extreme or deliberately placed itself one step from death. It had simply fought. And won. Against a Level 100 creature while only being Level 96.","\"Beginning really is getting ridiculous.\"","It hadn't even triggered the truly terrifying stages of its Law.","If Beginning had fought with the same recklessness it displayed against the Black Serpent Emperor, Michael suspected the battle would have ended much earlier.","\"Good.\"","Beginning immediately turned toward another battlefield, this one involving the two Black Serpent ancestors. The Level 100 wolf fighting them had clearly been having a miserable time.","FWOOSH!","Blue flames covered the sky.","The first Black Serpent ancestor twisted through the inferno. Its enormous tail descended.","The wolf dodged.","Before the wolf could properly regain its footing mid-air, hundreds of pink flowers appeared around its body.","Hundreds.","The wolf's crimson eyes contracted as pink flames swallowed it.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!","AWOOOO!","The wolf erupted from the explosion. Large sections of its scales had been burned black. Its jaws opened.","A gray beam shot toward the second Black Serpent ancestor.","The serpent's enormous body twisted, but the attack tore through a section of its tail. Yet before the wolf could capitalize on the injury, the first ancestor appeared. Its jaws closed around the wolf's neck.","CRUNCH!","The wolf roared. Its claws immediately tore into the serpent's body. The first ancestor refused to release it.","The second Black Serpent ancestor moved. Pink flowers bloomed around its head as it appeared to be charging a very powerful attack.","Michael's eyes narrowed in his hiding space and he hurriedly spoke.","\"Don't destroy the body.\"","The second ancestor paused upon hearing this. The flowers disappeared.","It was at this moment that Beginning arrived.","BOOOOOOM!","Its fist struck the wolf directly in the side. The enormous creature was ripped from the Black Serpent ancestor's jaws and sent tumbling across the battlefield.","Beginning followed, and the two serpent ancestors followed his lead.","The wolf had barely risen when three enormous shadows covered it.","\"...\"","For some reason, Michael almost felt sorry for it.","The wolf howled furiously, only to receive a punch on its head from directly above.","BOOOOOOM!","Its head struck the earth. A blue-flamed tail wrapped around its hind legs.","The first Black Serpent ancestor pulled and the wolf's body was stretched across the ground.","The second ancestor descended and pinned one of its forelimbs beneath its body.","Beginning raised its fist.","Michael immediately spoke.","\"Please leave a complete body!\"","Beginning's fist changed direction.","BOOOOOOM!","The wolf's neck collapsed. Its body twitched. Beginning punched again.","BOOM!","The movement stopped.","Michael stared at the relatively complete corpse.","\"...Excellent.\"","Two Level 100 corpses now in hand.","The three undead didn't linger and immediately charged toward the Bone Wyvern, which was the closest ongoing battle.","The Level 100 wolf fighting it had gained a considerable advantage.","The Bone Wyvern's earlier injuries had become increasingly problematic. Its left wing was now almost completely broken, and several sections of its skeletal body had been shattered.","The wolf had also suffered injuries, but nothing comparable.","AWOOOO!","The wolf lunged. Its claws descended toward the Bone Wyvern's damaged wing. The Bone Wyvern twisted, but it was too slow.","CRACK!","The wing nearly shattered. The Bone Wyvern lost balance. Its enormous skeletal body began to fall. The wolf immediately followed. Its jaws opened as energy gathered.","BOOOOOOM!","Beginning crashed into the wolf from the side. The gathered energy exploded harmlessly into the distance.","The wolf was thrown away. It twisted in midair when blue flames erupted beneath it. The first Black Serpent ancestor emerged. Its head struck the wolf's stomach.","BOOOOOOM!","The wolf flew upward, but it had barely gone far when pink flowers appeared above it.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","The flowers exploded around the wolf's limbs, and the detonations tore apart scales and flesh.","The wolf howled in agony, its etes turning red in pain when a massive hand grabbed its throat in midair and rapidly carried it down.","BOOOOOOM!"]},{"number":1120,"title":"Chapter 1120: Battle Conclusion [2]","paragraphs":["Both crashed into the earth. The wolf struggled to free itself, but Beginning's knee pressed against its chest, pinning it down. One hand remained around its throat. The other rose.","The wolf's head struck the ground.","BOOM! Again. BOOM!","Michael's eyelids twitched.","\"...Beginning. Finish it cleanly.\"","The fist stopped. Beginning stared at the wolf. Its hand tightened.","CRACK!","The wolf's neck broke.","Three Level 100 corpses now.","This time all undead targets converged on the wolf fighting the Bone Dragon. With five undead ganging up on it, the wolf that had initially been holding its own did not die a peaceful death.","In the distance, the two remaining Level 100 wolves were still fighting the Undead High Drake when they noticed that their fellow wolves had all fallen.","The Undead High Drake stood between the two with its enormous wings spread wide.","Compared to the two before it, it was in relatively good condition.","The two wolves had fought it together from the beginning, and after all of that, the High Drake was merely injured.","With Beginning and the others joining the Undead High Drake, the two remaining wolves did not die well, though to Michael's satisfaction their bodies were relatively intact.","At this point, the larger battle had already entered its final stages.","The outcome was no longer in question.","Scattered packs of wolves continued resisting across the destroyed Level 3 region, but the terrifying momentum they had possessed at the beginning was gone.","Every few seconds, another wolf fell, freeing several undead to join another battle.","Michael watched all of this from his hiding space. Then he finally stepped out. His pale figure silently emerged into the open. There was no longer much reason to remain hidden.","The ordinary wolves were nearly finished, the five Level 100 monsters had already died, and the beings inside the black barrier couldn't see what was happening outside anyway.","Michael looked around.","\"...What a mess.\"","Calling the surrounding area a forest would have been generous.","The ancient trees that had once towered hundreds of meters into the sky were either uprooted, shattered, or burning. Entire mountains had collapsed.","Enormous craters covered the earth, while countless domains had permanently altered sections of the terrain.","One area had become a frozen wasteland. Another was filled with black flames.","Farther away, purple poisonous mist clung to the remains of several mountains.","Everywhere Michael looked were corpses, not limited to the wolves, with about thirty belonging to his legion as well.","Even with an aching feeling in his soul from the losses, Michael's eyes immediately brightened.","He had work to do.","Without wasting time, Michael had his undead gather the scattered corpses and placed them all within the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion's spatial world.","After finishing the collection, he looked toward his legion.","\"...Everyone.\"","Thousands of green-red eyes turned to gaze at him.","Michael pointed toward the black barrier.","\"Let's bring this thing down.\"","Immediately, close to two thousand gathered around the barrier. Michael gave his command.","\"Attack!\"","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!","The world exploded. Nearly two thousand Rank Four undead unleashed their attacks simultaneously.","Flames. Ice. Lightning. Poison. Countless abilities crossed the destroyed region.","For a moment, the entire sky disappeared beneath energy. Then everything struck the barrier.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!!","The explosion was deafening. The earth beneath Michael's feet collapsed. Mountains that had survived the previous battle finally shattered.","A colossal mushroom-shaped cloud of dust and energy rose into the sky.","Michael's robes violently fluttered. His long hair was thrown backward.","His emerald eyes stared directly ahead, fixed on the trembling barrier.","Michael's eyes brightened, and he had his undead, all except a few, continue attacking without rest.","This continued for a while until a thin crack finally appeared on the surface.","Seeing this, Michael pointed at the crack and had his legion concentrate their attacks there.","\"Concentrate everything on that point!\"","The legion reacted instantly.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","Nearly two thousand attacks converged on a single point, causing the crack to expand.","Thin fractures spread from the original crack.","Within seconds, a gigantic network of cracks covered the black surface.","The barrier looked like glass struck by an enormous hammer.","Michael didn't let the undead stop their barrage, and for a while, the sky was filled with colors.","Awakeners who had initially been drawn by the noise fled, though a few still remained at a distance; they were curious, but they did not dare to come too close.","Finally, after several rounds of attacks, the black barrier distorted and shattered.","KACHA!","Countless black fragments exploded outward before dissolving into particles of black energy.","Michael's expression immediately became even more solemn.","The first thing he saw was destruction.","\"...\"","The interior of the barrier was completely ruined.","The land Michael remembered from before the barrier formed had ceased to exist.","Enormous trenches crossed the ground.","Several craters were so deep that Michael couldn't immediately see their bottoms.","Scarlet flames burned across one section of the battlefield, while violent winds continued circling another.","Golden feathers were scattered everywhere.","Michael even saw pieces of shattered crimson armor embedded in the earth.","However...","The tower remained unchanged.","Michael's gaze briefly moved toward it.","The ancient structure stood silently at the center of everything.","Not a single additional crack had appeared on its surface.","\"...Ridiculous.\"","Ten Level 100 beings had fought around it, yet the tower looked exactly the same.","Michael's curiosity toward whatever existed inside it increased considerably.","However, he didn't allow himself to become distracted.","His emerald eyes immediately moved toward the four Epic Grade wolves.","They were still alive, but compared to the energetic state Michael had once seen them in, the four were in terrible shape.","The three-headed wolf was missing one of its heads. Several sections of its scaled body were burned black.","Of the remaining two heads, one eye had been destroyed while the other head's jaw hung unnaturally to the side, slowly healing on its own.","The armored wolf wasn't much better.","Nearly half of the bone armor covering its enormous body had been shattered.","Several broken bone plates protruded from its flesh."]},{"number":1121,"title":"Chapter 1121: Strange Fragments","paragraphs":["The four-winged wolf now possessed only two wings.","Countless wounds covered its body, while one enormous gash extended from its neck to its abdomen.","Then there was the silver wolf.","Michael's expression became slightly more serious.","It was still standing.","Of the four...","It appeared to be in the best condition.","Of course, \"best\" was relative.","A large section of silver fur on its left side had disappeared.","The flesh beneath had been burned almost completely black, and one ear was missing.","A deep wound crossed its face and continued down its chest.","Black mist still surrounded it, but compared to the terrifying ocean of darkness Michael had seen earlier...","It was pitifully thin.","However, only these four remained within the boundary of the shattered barrier.","\"...Where are the others?\"","The six awakeners were obviously gone, assuming they hadn't died.","Michael's perception swept across the ruined battlefield and discovered nothing.","His eyes moved toward the position where the old mage's portal had previously existed.","The disk was gone, and the portal was gone as well.","\"They escaped?\"","Michael's expression became thoughtful.","That was the most likely explanation.","The old mage had explicitly created an escape route before the battle began.","Perhaps the six awakeners had realized they couldn't defeat the four Epic Grade wolves without suffering unacceptable losses.","Or perhaps they had suffered serious injuries, or maybe their temporary alliance had started falling apart.","Michael had no idea, and frankly, he didn't care.","His eyes remained on the four wolves.","A smile appeared on his face.","\"This is perfect.\"","The four Epic Grade wolves had survived.","However...","They were injured and far from their peak.","Michael couldn't have asked for a better result.","AWOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO!","The silver wolf raised its head.","Its howl shook the ruined region.","The other three followed.","AWOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO!","Four howls overlapped.","Despite their injuries and their exhaustion...","Their auras began rising.","Michael's expression changed slightly.","\"Oh?\"","The wolves weren't surrendering even after seeing the forces gathered beside him.","Not that he had expected them to.","The nearly one thousand monsters outside had already demonstrated the strange determination possessed by the creatures of this nest.","They would fight until death.","Michael's expression gradually became cold.","\"Fine.\"","His energy stirred, and the air around Michael darkened.","His emerald eyes glowed.","[Death Ground]","Immediately...","Michael's face paled.","\"...!\"","He gritted his teeth.","Even though he had used Death Ground several times before, the burden of simultaneously strengthening such an enormous number of undead was still ridiculous.","But the effect remained as good as before.","The already dense aura of his undead suddenly multiplied.","Michael took a breath and pointed at the ground below.","\"Bombard them.\"","The silver wolf's eyes contracted.","Michael had absolutely no intention of allowing four Level 100 Epic Grade monsters time to recover or display their full abilities.","The legion attacked without hesitation.","The sky changed.","Hundreds of diverse attacks illuminated the darkness.","There were countless strange abilities Michael couldn't even immediately identify.","The four wolves stared upward in shock as they watched the sky descend upon them. They wanted to teleport, but with hundreds of undead locking down the surrounding void with their collective prowess, they were left with limited options.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The world became white.","The overwhelming bombardment continued for several breaths.","The brightness became so intense that even Michael had to narrow his eyes.","Finally, he raised one hand to signal a stop.","\"Stop.\"","The command spread through the legion, and almost instantly, the attacks ceased.","The sudden silence was deafening.","Only the distant rumbling of collapsing terrain remained.","Michael stared downward; or at least, he stared at where the ground had once been.","\"...\"","The area had already been destroyed beyond recognition before the bombardment.","Now it was far worse.","There was practically no ground left beneath the tower.","Only an enormous abyss stretched in every direction, its depth impossible to measure through the dense smoke and lingering energy.","At the center of all this destruction...","The tower remained standing.","Michael's eyelids twitched.","More accurately, the circular stone platform beneath the tower remained standing.","The platform floated above the abyss as though the destruction surrounding it had nothing to do with it.","Not a single crack had appeared, and the tower was exactly the same.","Immediately after, his attention quickly moved away from it.","\"The wolves...\"","Michael's eyes swept across the ruined landscape and found nothing.","His expression became slightly strange.","\"Did they die? But why did I not receive a notification?\"","He had expected them to die, believing that even Level 100 Epic Grade monsters couldn't casually survive the concentrated attacks of nearly two thousand Rank Four undead while already severely injured.","Though it would be a shame if their bodies were lost, there was no need to take more losses and face another grueling battle.","Spreading his senses wide, Michael suddenly noticed something.","\"There.\"","Michael's gaze locked onto four locations surrounding the tower.","At first glance, there was nothing unusual.","Only fading energy.","But gradually...","Four faint silhouettes became visible.","The silhouettes were shaped like wolves.","Or more accurately...","They were the remains of the four wolves.","Their bodies had become almost transparent.","Particles of multicolored light escaped from their bodies, and countless colors mixed together.","\"What is this?\"","The wolves disappeared even faster.","Within seconds, their enormous bodies had completely vanished. In their place...","Four strange fragments remained.","Each was roughly the size of Michael's palm.","Color continuously flowed across their surfaces.","Michael watched silently.","\"So this is why they gave no experience?\"","That was his first thought.","Perhaps the four wolves weren't ordinary creatures. Maybe they had been created by the Origin Battlefield specifically to guard the tower, or perhaps their existence was directly connected to whatever was inside.","Michael didn't know, and he cautiously continued observing as the fragments floated peacefully.","Only after having an undead reach out and hold one of them for a few seconds with nothing happening did Michael let his guard down.","\"Bring it,\" Michael commanded.","Taking the item from his undead, Michael examined the fragment."]},{"number":1122,"title":"Chapter 1122: Universal Cornerstone [1]","paragraphs":["The instant the fragment touched his palm, a strange warmth spread across his fingers.","The other three fragments suddenly trembled, and all three shot toward him.","Before he or his undead could react, the fragments came to a halt right in front of him.","\"Wait.\"","Michael calmed his undead and continued observing the strange phenomenon.","The three fragments hovered around the first, then slowly drew toward one another as multicolored light flooded the surroundings.","Michael instinctively tightened his grip around the first fragment, but the object slipped through his fingers like liquid.","\"What?\"","It floated upward, and the four pieces collided.","There was no explosion or violent reaction.","They simply merged.","Michael watched without blinking; the process lasted only several seconds.","When the light finally faded, a single object floated before him.","It was spherical.","No larger than a human head.","Its surface resembled translucent crystal, but countless colors flowed within it like rivers of light.","Michael's expression became serious.","\"...Interesting.\"","He extended one hand.","The merged object slowly descended into his palm.","It was almost weightless.","Michael immediately activated Detect, and a panel appeared.","[Key to the Universal Cornerstone] [Grade: Legendary]","There was no description, only the name of the item and its grade. Though its use could already be guessed from the name, the moment the panel appeared, Michael's gaze fixated entirely on the grade. His hands, holding the treasure, trembled slightly.","Compared to his expectation that anything he got from this nest would at most be a three-star Epic Grade, this was a Legendary Grade item!","Then again, it made sense.","To reach this level, one not only had to get through nearly a thousand Rank Four creatures, but they also had to deal with peak Rank Four Epic Grade monsters.","Michael unconsciously tightened his fingers around the strange sphere before hurriedly loosening them again.","\"Legendary...\"","Michael's gaze immediately shifted toward the ancient tower.","Or pillar.","After seeing the entire surrounding land destroyed while the structure remained completely untouched, Michael knew the answer was obviously there.","\"If this is a Key, then it could only be for one thing.\"","Michael looked down at the colorful sphere, then at the tower, and his body moved.","WHOOSH!","He crossed the enormous abyss in an instant.","The remnants of the previous energy storm still filled the surroundings, but they were of no harm to Michael.","Within seconds, Michael landed on the circular platform.","Tap.","His feet touched ancient stone.","After a brief hesitation, Michael started walking toward the pillar, only to be forced to a stop as a transparent surface appeared directly before him.","Holding the treasure in one hand, Michael's eyes lit up with curiosity, and he sent a punch at the barrier.","BOOOOOOM!","Unfortunately, the platform remained silent, and the barrier didn't even shake.","Michael slowly lowered his fist.","\"Of course.\"","Michael wasn't surprised.","After everything that had happened, it would have been stranger if he could simply walk into the tower.","Michael looked down at the colorful sphere in his hand, then back at the barrier.","\"Key,\" he repeated, looking around the platform for anything that resembled a keyhole for the sphere in his hands.","Michael took another step closer to the barrier, and the sphere trembled.","This time, the colors flowing inside it accelerated.","Michael's eyes brightened.","\"So I was right.\"","He moved the sphere closer, and the barrier immediately reacted.","BZZZZZZZT!","Countless ripples spread across its surface, and the sphere disappeared completely into the barrier.","The runes covering the ancient structure lit up simultaneously.","Michael's eyes widened.","THUMP!","The entire Origin Battlefield seemed to shake, but the vibration was coming from beneath the pillar.","The barrier before Michael changed.","Color appeared at its center.","A tiny point at first.","Then it expanded, as countless colors spread across the transparent barrier like veins.","Michael slowly stepped backward. His emerald eyes remained fixed on the pillar.","The colorful lines continued spreading, and within seconds, the entire barrier had transformed.","Then...","KACHA!","A crack appeared, then another, and another, until...","The transparent barrier began shattering.","THUUUUUUUUM!!!","A loud sound came from the pillar.","Michael's long hair flew backward, and his robes snapped violently.","The violent force spreading from the pillar gradually weakened.","Michael remained where he stood, his emerald eyes fixed on the ancient structure.","The transparent barrier was gone.","Nothing now separated him from the pillar.","After waiting several seconds and sensing no immediate danger, Michael stepped forward. Beginning and the Undead High Drake followed closely behind him, while the remaining undead surrounded the platform, prepared to react at the slightest change.","The closer Michael moved, the more imposing the structure became.","From a distance, it had resembled an ancient tower, but with no windows or any other entrances.","\"Detect.\"","A translucent panel appeared.","[Universal Cornerstone]","[Level: 1]","[Grade: Legendary]","[Status: Unclaimed]","[Description: A foundational structure created and maintained by the Origin Will. A Universal Cornerstone serves as a territorial anchor, checkpoint, trade hub, and point of expansion across connected realms.] Michael's expression changed.","The panel continued expanding.","[Primary Effect: Regional Dominion]","[Upon claiming the Universal Cornerstone, the owner will gain authority over the surrounding Level 3 Region] [The Level 3 Region will be recognized as the owner's territory within the Origin Battlefield] [The owner may perceive major disturbances occurring within the territory] [The owner may influence entry permissions, establish restricted zones, and activate available territorial defenses] Michael stared at the lines in shock.","\"The entire region?\"","[Primary Effect: Origin Checkpoint]","[The Universal Cornerstone may serve as a fixed checkpoint within the Origin Battlefield] [The owner may designate this location as a return point] [Future entries into the Origin Battlefield may begin from this checkpoint, provided the required conditions are satisfied] [Using this cornerstone, one may take partial control of the other cornerstones in lower layers and gain even more functions] [Primary Effect: Sub-Territory Creation]","[The Universal Cornerstone may establish subsidiary territorial anchors within connected worlds, including the Land of Origin. Through the cornerstone, any permitted intelligent lifeform may enter the origin battlefield] Michael's breathing slowed.","\"Anywhere in the universe? Including the Land of Origin?\"","Does this mean anyone, even non-awakeners, could enter the Origin Battlefield?"]},{"number":1123,"title":"Chapter 1123: Universal Cornerstone [2]","paragraphs":["\"Does this mean anyone, even non-awakeners, could enter the Origin Battlefield?\"","It was a terrifying thought. One that Michael wanted to instinctively disbelieve, but couldn't help thinking about more deeply the moment it took root. However, the only way he could confirm or debunk it was to claim the treasure.","A lot had been explained, and though the words were easy enough to understand, grasping what they actually meant and signified required something more. The thought remained in Michael's mind for several seconds.","He looked up at the towering pillar.","\"How do I claim you?\"","The Universal Cornerstone remained silent. No panel appeared. No voice answered.","Michael waited several seconds before his gaze moved toward its dark stone surface. The most direct method was usually the correct one. He slowly raised his right hand and placed his palm against the pillar.","The stone was warm. Strangely warm. It almost felt alive.","Michael hesitated briefly before circulating his mana. A thin stream of energy flowed from his palm and entered the Universal Cornerstone.","For the first second, nothing happened.","Then the pillar reacted.","THUMP!","The runes covering its surface lit up simultaneously. Michael's expression changed. Before he could withdraw his hand, a tremendous suction force erupted from within the pillar.","His mana began pouring into it and the Universal Cornerstone swallowed his energy like a bottomless abyss.","Michael's eyes widened.","\"What the...\"","His mana reserves rapidly decreased. The speed of the consumption was enough to make any ordinary Rank Three awakener panic. However, Michael's energy reserves had long exceeded what should have been possible for his rank.","Even then, Michael remained prepared to forcefully sever the connection if the drain approached a dangerous level.","Fortunately, it never did. The suction weakened after consuming slightly less than half of his available mana.","Michael exhaled slowly.","\"That was expensive.\"","THUUUUM!","The pillar pulsed. A wave of invisible energy spread from the platform.","The change began with the mana in the air.","The already dense energy within the Level 3 Region suddenly increased.","Mana surged from beneath the platform and spread in every direction like an invisible tide.","The concentration rapidly doubled and continued rising.","Michael's emerald eyes widened slightly.","However, that wasn't the most astonishing change.","The destroyed region began repairing itself.","RUMBLE!","Far below the floating platform, shattered earth moved. Countless pieces of stone rose from the abyss. Mountains that had been reduced to rubble reassembled themselves.","Cracks sealed and enormous craters were filled with earth.","Burning forests vanished beneath waves of multicolored light before healthy vegetation grew in their place.","Ancient trees erupted from the ground one after another, reaching hundreds of meters into the sky within seconds.","Even the sections of land permanently altered by the previous battle began returning to their original state.","Michael stared in silent shock.","This isn't something a Level 100 mage could even accomplish. As expected of a legendary-grade item.","The restoration didn't merely return the region to how it had been before the battle. It improved it.","Putting aside the denser mana, the region contained even greater vitality than before.","Within minutes, the Level 3 Region looked as though no battle had ever occurred. It looked even better than when Michael had first entered it.","\"...Legendary.\"","The Universal Cornerstone pulsed again. Several translucent panels appeared before him.","[Universal Cornerstone successfully activated]","[Ownership recognition in progress]","[Michael Norman has been recognized as the provisional master of 'unnamed' Level 3 Territory] [Territory Authority Established]","[Current Territory Level: 1]","[Current Territory Condition: Normal]","[Current Territory Owner: Michael Norman]","Michael's gaze sharpened at the word provisional. Another panel appeared immediately.","[Ownership Rules]","[The Universal Cornerstone is bound to the owner's living essence]","[If the owner dies, ownership will be terminated]","[Upon termination of ownership, the territory will return to an Unclaimed state] [The Key to the Universal Cornerstone will reform after a designated period] Michael rubbed his chin.","\"So the territory can't be inherited automatically.\"","At least not at its current level. The next notifications continued.","[Territorial Authority is strongest within the boundaries of the claimed domain] [Certain functions of the Universal Cornerstone cannot be activated outside the main territory] [Territory development will unlock additional remote authority]","[Universal Trade Hub is currently locked]","[Requirement: Complete initial territory registration]","[Origin Checkpoint has been unlocked] [Regional Perception has been unlocked] [Basic Entry Management has been unlocked]","[Basic Territorial Restoration has been unlocked]","Michael's eyes moved rapidly across every line. Some notifications confirmed things he had already guessed. Others he only understood now.","All together, the functions made this place an almost perfect base within the Origin Battlefield, and if what he suspected was true, its significance might extend beyond the battlefield itself.","A final panel slowly formed.","[An official name is required to complete territory registration]","[Please name your domain]","Michael paused. His gaze moved away from the panel and swept across the restored region.","Ancient mountains surrounded the distant horizon and dense forests stretched beneath him.","The Universal Cornerstone towered at the center of everything, silently releasing waves of energy.","Michael's expression gradually became thoughtful.","\"A name...\"","The Level 3 Region had originally carried a name, but after he claimed it, it had reverted to unnamed. That made sense, given that naming it was required to complete registration.","It didn't take long for Michael to find a suitable one.","Thanks to a certain undead, when it came to naming a territory, only one name came to mind.","\"The Eternal Crown.\"","The name left his lips without hesitation. It was the same name carried by the empire under his control within the Land of Origin.","The Eternal Crown Empire.","Although his authority over that empire had developed in rather unexpected fashion, it remained the first true force he could call his own outside his undead legion.","Now, standing before what might become another territory in a place as significant as the Origin Battlefield, the same name felt strangely appropriate.","Michael didn't know what this territory would eventually become, but if the Universal Cornerstone truly possessed all the functions previously revealed, then its future influence might spread far beyond this Level 3 Region."]},{"number":1124,"title":"Chapter 1124: Universal Achievement","paragraphs":["The moment Michael confirmed the name, the Universal Cornerstone reacted.","THUUUUM!","The countless runes covering the pillar shone brighter.","A wave of multicolored light erupted from its surface and spread across the entire restored region.","Every mountain, river, forest, and valley was briefly covered in a thin layer of light. The sensation was strange, like something settling into place around him.","At the same time, the panels floating before him changed.","[Territory registration completed]","[The unnamed Level 3 Territory has been officially registered]","[Territory Name: Eternal Crown]","[Territory Classification: Level 1 Domain]","[Domain Master: Michael Norman]","[Universal Cornerstone ownership finalized]","[Provisional ownership has been upgraded to complete ownership]","Michael's eyes paused on the new classification.","\"Level 1 Domain...\"","The previous panel had referred to the area as a Level 3 Region. Now that registration had been completed, it had become a domain. The difference was probably more than cosmetic.","\"So an unclaimed Level 3 is still just another region, but a claimed one becomes a domain? I wonder if there'll be other tiers in the future.\"","At the same moment, an enormous amount of information entered his perception. Not everything within the Level 3 Region, or rather the Level 1 Domain, but enough to leave him briefly stunned.","He could sense the general condition of the land. The flow of mana beneath the mountains. The location of the Universal Cornerstone. The boundaries separating the Eternal Crown from the neighboring regions.","He could even vaguely sense the foreign presences still lingering near the domain's edges.","Several awakeners who had remained at a distance to observe the battle were still there, some leaving quietly while others tried to move closer to locations his undead were stationed.","Michael couldn't see their faces or determine their exact races through the domain alone, but their movements appeared in his mind like faint disturbances across a still lake.","\"So this is Regional Perception.\"","It wasn't omniscience. Far from it. But within the Eternal Crown, concealing an enormous army or causing a major disturbance without him noticing would be incredibly difficult.","Of course, the burden it placed on his mind was significant, so it was obvious he would only be able to use it sparingly in the near future.","Regardless, Michael's interest deepened.","He was just about to examine the Universal Cornerstone's functions properly when another panel appeared.","However, this one was different. It immediately radiated a brightness Michael had only seen during major announcements from the Origin Will.","Michael's expression immediately became serious.","[Universal Announcement]","[Congratulations to Michael Norman of Aurora]","[Michael Norman has become the first participant in the universe to claim a Universal Cornerstone] [Michael Norman has successfully established the first recognized domain within the Origin Battlefield] [Domain Name: Eternal Crown]","[Domain Level: 1]","[This achievement has activated the Universal Territory System]","Michael's face stiffened.","\"...What?\"","The announcement continued before he could react.","[Universal Cornerstones may now be discovered and claimed throughout the Origin Battlefield] [Qualified participants may establish domains by defeating territorial guardians and obtaining the corresponding Universal Cornerstone Key] [The establishment of a domain grants influence within the Origin Battlefield] [Additional territory-related functions have been unlocked]","[The first domain master will receive a unique achievement reward]","Michael barely registered the final sentence. His eyes remained fixed on the first few lines.","Michael Norman. Aurora. Eternal Crown.","The Origin Will had exposed all three. There was no alias. No hidden identification. No option to conceal his realm. His real name had just been announced to every participant in the Origin Battlefield.","Michael slowly looked around the peaceful region.","\"...You couldn't have asked me first?\"","The Origin Battlefield remained silent.","Michael's eyelid twitched.","He had only just finished thinking about how dangerous it would be to reveal hundreds of Epic Grade undead.","Now the Origin Will had publicly informed the entire universe that he possessed the first domain. Even if the announcement hadn't explained every function, the words Universal Cornerstone and first recognized domain were enough to attract serious attention.","Those who understood the significance, if any, would immediately become interested. Those who didn't would become curious.","And from even his brief time in the Origin Battlefield, he had already learned that curiosity here had a tendency to turn into greed remarkably quickly.","Michael rubbed his forehead.","\"So much for remaining low-key.\"","Only a few hours remained before he returned home. He had originally planned to spend them quietly examining the Universal Cornerstone's functions before leaving without drawing further attention.","That plan was now looking considerably more complicated. But he would have to return to Aurora first before deciding his next steps.","Fortunately, all awakeners were currently in their respective layers, and when the time came to leave, they would all depart simultaneously.","Michael glanced toward the restored forest surrounding the Universal Cornerstone.","Regardless of whether the announcement had exposed him, ownership had already been finalized.","This place was his. If others wanted it, they would have to come and take it from him. And the longer they waited, the harder that would become.","Michael's emerald eyes gradually became colder.","His caution remained, but the realization he had gained during the recent battles hadn't faded.","He was not weak. He possessed nearly two thousand Rank Four undead, and hundreds were Epic Grade.","He had Beginning, the Undead High Drake, the Bone Dragon, the Bone Wyvern, and many others.","Anyone treating him as an easy target because of his Level 75 would learn the same lesson Varek had learned.","Michael looked back at the announcement. The final line remained.","[Achievement Reward Pending]","[Please complete the Universal Cornerstone tutorial to receive your reward] Michael's expression became strange.","\"Of course.\"","Even after announcing his identity to the entire universe, the Origin Will still couldn't simply hand him the reward.","He sighed and placed his palm against the Universal Cornerstone once more.","\"Fine. Show me exactly what my new domain can do.\"","As Michael prepared himself to unravel the mysteries of the universal cornerstone, the news the origin will broadcasted to all awakeners left them with varying reactions."]},{"number":1125,"title":"Chapter 1125: Rank 4","paragraphs":["Just as Michael had expected, the notification had been shared with every awakener in the universe. The ones with the biggest reactions were the ones who knew his name.","In a region far away from Michael's location, a middle-aged man guarded by two skeleton knights in very expensive armor stared at the panel that had appeared before him.","He didn't even pay attention to the treasure he had just snatched from a hundred awakeners. It seemed to have lost all its brilliance.","Though Michael had stolen two of his most powerful undead, Varek remained a formidable awakener even among the thousands present in the Fourth Layer. It was simply his own fault for challenging someone like Michael.","\"Though I don't know what this Universal Cornerstone is, for this freak to be connected to it, and for the Origin Will to broadcast it to an unrelated person like me, it must be something very unique.\"","It was the same thought many others shared, though most didn't know Michael on a personal level. The majority of awakeners in the Fourth Layer knew only that the announcement referred to someone with a high ranking on the leaderboard who, for some reason, was in the Fourth Layer despite being Rank Three.","Those in other layers assumed it was someone at a higher rank, while those at higher ranks assumed the same or believed it was someone below them.","That was the case for those unfamiliar with Michael. For those who knew him personally, the reaction was considerably more pronounced.","In another location within the Fourth Layer, Director Lin stood atop a mountain peak alongside two old men, all three staring at the night sky.","\"I knew that boy wouldn't be able to keep a low profile no matter how hard he tried,\" Director Lin said in a complaining voice, though the other two could clearly hear the worry hidden beneath it.","The old man standing beside her snorted.","\"I knew the boy was a freak.\"","The third old man nodded in agreement.","\"A complete freak. When his name first appeared on the rankings, I honestly didn't want to believe it was him.\"","\"Neither did I,\" Director Lin admitted.","At first, all three had wanted to believe it was merely someone sharing the same name. After all, the universe was unimaginably vast.","The odds of another Michael Norman existing somewhere weren't impossible. But the coincidence was simply too ridiculous.","Director Lin rubbed her forehead.","\"Now look at him going wild again. Not even two days later, he has done something even more outrageous than ranking alongside hundreds of Level 100 awakeners at Level 75.\"","The three fell silent.","The first participant in the universe to establish a domain. The first to claim a Universal Cornerstone. The one who had activated an entirely new system for every awakener in existence.","Even without knowing what a Universal Cornerstone truly represented, they understood one thing. If the Origin Will personally announced it, then it was unquestionably one of the greatest opportunities in the universe.","None of them had imagined they would be connected to such a figure.","\"If the Origin Battlefield hadn't forced him to reveal himself...\" one of the old men muttered, \"...I don't think we'd ever have realized just how abnormal that child truly is.\"","Director Lin smiled bitterly.","\"He kept surprising us. Every time we thought we'd seen his limit.\" Her voice became heavier. \"Unfortunately, the tallest tree always attracts the strongest wind. Michael's situation inside Aurora was already delicate enough. Now he has extended it to the entire universe.\"","The two old men couldn't refute that. Before this, if the Origin Battlefield hadn't forcibly gathered all awakeners, Michael would have been wandering the void somewhere, keeping his presence in Aurora minimal.","But with the announcement now revealing Michael's real name and his home realm, every ambitious organization or individual in the universe knew exactly where to begin searching.","Fortunately, only a few minutes remained before they would all be returned home. There would be time to prepare then.","\"Once we're back, we need to see him immediately.\"","Director Lin laughed despite herself.","\"Although I'm not sure he'll actually listen to us anymore.\"","The two old men looked toward her.","\"What do you mean?\"","Director Lin spread her hands helplessly.","\"Think about it. He's ridiculously strong. To be honest, the only people I feel could still meaningfully advise him now would be Director Arven, the Dean, or the Vice Dean.\"","The atmosphere instantly became awkward.","\"...\"","Director Lin realized what she had just said.","\"...Right.\"","She had accidentally mentioned the three people currently giving all of them headaches.","The Dean and Vice Dean were understandable. Both had left Aurora to deal with matters so significant that even the academy directors hadn't been informed of the details. Director Arven, on the other hand, was a different matter entirely.","The tallest old man let out a long sigh.","\"That man is just as troublesome as Michael.\"","The others couldn't help agreeing.","Before entering the Origin Battlefield, everyone in Aurora had known Arven was powerful. Exceptionally powerful.","He had long been recognized as the Rank Four awakener closest to reaching the Demigod Realm, even if others had crossed over before him. But knowing someone was powerful and witnessing exactly how powerful they truly were remained two entirely different things.","Director Lin looked toward another floating panel. The Rank Four Leaderboard. There, near the very top, one name remained firmly planted.","Rank 4: Arven","Director Lin's mouth twitched. She was still coming to terms with the fact that her fellow director was the fourth strongest Rank Four being in the entire universe.","The words sounded absurd even forming in her mind. Aurora wasn't considered a weak realm, but neither was it among the ancient overlords of the universe. Yet somehow, their academy alone currently possessed two individuals capable of shaking the entire Origin Battlefield.","One was a Rank Three who had placed among Rank Fours and then established the first domain in existence. The other had entered the Fourth Layer on the very first day and immediately climbed into the top ten.","Not only had Arven failed to fall afterward, he had climbed even higher.","Now he was fourth.","The three directors exchanged complicated looks.","The tallest of the three was the first to break the silence.","\"We shouldn't think about all this now.\" His calm voice immediately pulled the others back to reality. \"There are still a few minutes before we're forced out of the Origin Battlefield. Let's wait until we return.\"","Director Lin slowly nodded. He was right. Worrying here accomplished nothing. Once they returned to Aurora, they could finally assess the situation properly.","The second old man sighed.","\"Besides, our concerns don't end with Michael and Arven.\"","His expression gradually became solemn.","Among the directors from the academy who had entered the Origin Battlefield, they had distributed communication means beforehand to remain in contact if possible. Unfortunately, reality had been cruel.","\"So far, only the three of us have successfully established contact.\""]},{"number":1126,"title":"Chapter 1126: Mad Genius","paragraphs":["Director Lin's expression darkened. That was the part worrying her the most. Communication inside the Origin Battlefield was unbelievably difficult.","The fact that the three of them had managed to communicate at all was because they had fortunately appeared relatively close to one another after entering the Fourth Layer.","Everything else was met with silence.","\"We still haven't heard from Director Arven.\"","\"And naturally, we haven't heard from Michael either.\"","The tallest old man nodded.","\"Those two aren't my greatest concern. They're both still alive.\"","The rankings themselves proved that much. In fact, they were probably doing far better than anyone had expected. What truly worried him were the others.","Meanwhile, as the leaders of the academy concerned themselves with so many things, in the second layer of the Origin Battlefield, a youth with flames visible around his fists was blowing apart sections of a mountain with his bare hands.","If Michael were here, he would have recognized him. But the impression he'd carried of Brian from a year ago, when they had both awakened, was nothing like what stood before anyone who could have seen him now.","The genius of that time, the one who had carried himself with an air of obvious superiority while others around him largely agreed, now looked like a deranged man.","BOOOOOOM!","Brian's fists slammed into the mountainside again. An enormous section of rock collapsed, tumbling thousands of meters before exploding into countless fragments. Yet he didn't stop.","Wind gathered around his body. Fire followed immediately afterward. The two different elemental energies intertwined around both fists rather than rejecting one another.","Crimson flames spiraled together with emerald wind currents, forming violent vortexes that distorted the surrounding air.","BOOOOOOOM!","The flames burned the shattered stone to molten liquid while the compressed wind blasted everything apart before the magma could even cool.","The destructive combination was both beautiful and terrifying. Any ordinary Rank Three monster struck by those fists would likely be reduced to ash instantly.","Brian paid no attention to the destruction surrounding him. His breathing was ragged.","\"...Why...\"","Another punch.","BOOOOOOOM!","\"...Why is it always Michael?\"","His voice was almost a growl. Fragments of burning stone rained across the mountain as Brian lowered his fists. His crimson eyes were bloodshot. The announcement still floated before him.","Michael Norman.","Again. Always Michael Norman.","Brian clenched his fists until his knuckles turned white. His thoughts drifted back over a year. Back to the day they had awakened. Both of them had succeeded at eighteen. Their final opportunity.","At first, Michael had been nothing special. Just another ordinary student who had barely managed to awaken before the deadline.","Brian vaguely remembered another classmate awakening alongside Michael that day. A girl. He couldn't even remember her name. She had been that insignificant. Michael had seemed no different.","At least, that was what Brian had believed.","Only Mira, another of his classmates, could be said to have a future walking alongside him. Not only did she possess a special class, she was blessed with a terrifyingly powerful talent.","However, for some reasons Brian still couldn't understand, she had always gravitated toward Michael and never paid him much attention, despite how clearly he had made his interest known.","Why Michael? Michael back then had been ordinary. Brian possessed multiple classes. His talent was superior. His future should have been brighter. He should have been the center of attention.","At first, fueled partly by that superiority complex, Brian had dismissed Michael despite his jealousy. Perhaps Michael had simply gotten lucky once or twice.","But as time passed, the distance between them failed to grow. Instead, Michael continued matching his pace. Every breakthrough. Every achievement. Every improvement. Brian would hear Michael's name again.","Then the impossible happened.","Michael stopped merely matching him. He surpassed him completely. The difference widened so rapidly that Brian suddenly realized they were no longer competing on the same track.","Michael had already entered an entirely different world.","Even so, Brian had refused to surrender.","Speed meant nothing. History was filled with geniuses who had shone brilliantly before fading away. Many had awakened extraordinary talents only to encounter bottlenecks lasting decades. Some never overcame them.","Brian had always believed Michael would become one of those people, especially given the way he constantly provoked stronger enemies and made enemies everywhere. Sooner or later, someone would kill him.","Even if that never happened, his growth had to stop eventually. Everyone had limits. When Michael finally reached his, Brian believed he would catch up, surpass him, and personally crush him.","That belief had sustained him for months.","But now Brian looked at the announcement again. His expression twisted.","\"What...\"","\"...is this?\"","The Origin Will itself had announced Michael's achievement. The first in the universe. Brian's breathing became uneven once more.","\"...Why?\"","\"Why is he still becoming more brilliant?\"","He had expected Michael's legend to end. Instead, it was growing larger. Larger than Aurora. Larger than the Land of Origin. Now it had spread across the entire universe.","Brian slowly lowered his head. For the first time since entering the Origin Battlefield, a thought he had desperately tried to suppress many times resurfaced.","\"What if...\"","His lips trembled.","\"...I can never catch him?\"","The thought lasted only an instant. Immediately afterward, his eyes filled with madness.","\"No.\"","BOOOOOOOOOOM!","His flaming fist obliterated what remained of the mountain's peak.","\"I refuse.\"","\"I'll become stronger. No matter what. I'll surpass him. Even if...\"","Brian's voice became almost a whisper.","\"...I have to sacrifice everything to do it.\"","Brian wasn't the only one affected by Michael's brilliance.","In a cave, sitting cross-legged, Rynne stared at the notification before her as her heart ached for reasons she couldn't quite name. Her eyes remained fixed on a single line.","Congratulations to Michael Norman of Aurora.","\"...\"","For a long while, she said nothing.","Unlike Brian, she didn't hate Michael. Never had. If anything, Michael was one of the few people around her age whom she genuinely acknowledged.","Someone worthy of being called a rival.","\"...Grandma.\"","She remembered something her grandmother had told her months ago, after she had taken Michael, who had been looking for business opportunities, to meet her."]},{"number":1127,"title":"Chapter 1127: He’s The Most Special In Our World","paragraphs":["Rynne lowered her gaze. She could still remember the old woman's expression after Michael had left.","It hadn't been surprise. Nor admiration. It had been contemplation. Almost reverence. Then her grandmother had looked at her and calmly spoken words Rynne hadn't understood at the time.","\"That young man... He may be the most special person in our realm.\"","At the time, Rynne had simply assumed her grandmother had been impressed. Michael's growth was extraordinary, and his strength exceeded what should have been possible.","Naturally, someone like that would attract praise. So she hadn't thought much about it.","Now she slowly looked back toward the panel floating before her.","The Origin Will itself had acknowledged him. It had announced his achievement to the entire universe. Her grandmother's words suddenly carried an entirely different weight.","\"...Perhaps...\"","\"...you already knew.\"","Rynne smiled bitterly. Her grandmother's eyes had always been frighteningly accurate. If even she had regarded Michael as the most special person in Aurora months ago, then perhaps she had noticed something Rynne had overlooked.","Rynne lowered her head. A complicated feeling spread through her chest. It wasn't hatred. Far from it. It was disappointment. Not toward Michael. Toward herself.","\"I...\"","\"...might never surpass him.\"","Those words were difficult to admit. Rynne had always possessed confidence in herself. She had trained harder than almost everyone around her.","She possessed exceptional talent. Exceptional comprehension. Exceptional resources. Even when Michael repeatedly performed miracles, she had believed she could eventually catch him.","Maybe not immediately. Maybe not in a year. But someday.","Now that confidence wavered.","The distance between them no longer felt measurable. It felt fundamental.","She quietly laughed at herself.","\"So this...\"","\"...is what defeat feels like.\"","The words echoed softly inside the cave. Yet strangely, rather than discouraging her, they brought clarity.","Rynne had never been someone who retreated simply because another person was more talented. If anything, it only strengthened her determination.","She looked once more toward Michael's name.","\"What exactly...\"","\"...did you do?\"","The Origin Will wasn't an entity that casually acknowledged individuals. What kind of feat, what kind of impossible achievement, could make even the Origin Will recognize someone by name?","Rynne slowly closed her eyes.","\"It truly must be something beyond imagination.\"","When she opened them again, the trace of disappointment had already faded. In its place remained only determination.","\"I may never surpass you...\"","She smiled softly.","\"But that doesn't mean I'll stop chasing your back.\"","After gathering herself, she turned to look at the leaderboard of the second layer. Her rank was 68. It wasn't a bad placement, but if she truly wanted to chase Michael, she still had so much to do.","Among the list of one thousand, there were a few other names she saw were from Aurora.","One named Brian was at rank 112 and another named Mira was at rank 534. She wondered whether she would encounter either of them here or back in the real world.","Compared to everyone who knew Michael and found themselves shaken, Lily, his cousin, seemed barely affected by the panel that had appeared before her.","Unlike others who had first doubted whether it was actually him, she had immediately started wondering what interesting thing her cousin had managed to do this time.","The other reason she couldn't focus on her cousin's achievements aside from her ignorance was that she and Timi were currently running for their lives.","\"Move!\"","Timi suddenly shouted.","The two immediately changed direction.","BOOOOOOM!!","An enormous pillar of ice slammed into the ground behind them. The impact froze everything within hundreds of meters. Trees instantly became crystalline sculptures before shattering into glittering fragments. The frozen ground cracked under the overwhelming force.","Lily didn't even look back.","\"He's still chasing us!\"","\"You think I can't tell?\" Timi replied while sprinting beside her.","Both of them tightly held identical radiant treasures. The light surrounding the objects had already begun fading, making it obvious they wouldn't remain active for much longer.","Behind them, a furious roar echoed throughout the forest.","\"STOP RUNNING!!\"","The earth trembled. A gigantic blue dragon burst through countless ancient trees.","Although still juvenile, its body stretched nearly twenty meters from head to tail. Sapphire scales shimmered beneath the sky while enormous wings beat violently, sending freezing winds across the forest.","Its voice didn't sound childish, closer to a teenager's.","\"I SAID STOP!\"","The dragon inhaled deeply. The surrounding temperature instantly plummeted.","WHOOOOOSH!!","A terrifying torrent of freezing breath swept through the forest. Everything in its path froze solid.","Lily grabbed Timi's sleeve.","\"Jump!\"","The two split apart. The icy breath blasted between them, freezing an entire hill into crystal before the frozen mass shattered under its own weight.","CRAAAAACK!","Lily landed lightly before glancing backward with a grin.","\"You missed again!\"","The dragon's eyes widened.","\"I DID NOT MISS!\"","\"You absolutely did.\"","Timi nodded seriously while continuing to run.","\"That one wasn't even close.\"","\"...It was close!\"","Lily laughed.","\"If that's what you call close, your eyesight must be worse than your aim.\"","The dragon's nostrils released icy mist.","\"I'LL FREEZE BOTH OF YOU!\"","Another blast erupted. Neither Lily nor Timi bothered defending. They simply accelerated. The freezing breath passed harmlessly behind them.","Lily laughed louder.","\"Too slow!\"","Timi looked over his shoulder.","\"I think your wings are just for decoration.\"","The dragon almost stumbled mid-flight.","\"My wings are magnificent!\"","\"They're average,\" Timi replied with a perfectly serious face.","\"They're huge!\"","\"They're average... for a dragon.\"","\"They're above average!\"","Lily glanced at Timi.","\"Do you think so?\"","Timi pretended to consider it carefully.","\"I've definitely seen bigger.\"","\"I HAVE NOT!\"","The dragon roared so loudly the surrounding mountains echoed. Its scales glowed brighter as frost spread through the air.","\"I'M GOING TO EAT BOTH OF YOU!\"","Lily couldn't stop laughing. The juvenile dragon nearly exploded from rage.","\"YOU TWO ARE THE WORST HUMANS I'VE EVER MET!\"","Without slowing down, Lily and Timi looked at each other before bursting into laughter again.","Behind them, the furious juvenile dragon beat its wings even harder, roaring as it relentlessly continued the chase, completely unaware that the two humans had long since stopped seeing it as an enemy and had instead turned the pursuit into their own source of entertainment."]},{"number":1128,"title":"Chapter 1128: Funtions","paragraphs":["In the fourth layer of the origin battlefield.","Communicating with the Universal Cornerstone again gave Michael more information.","The first was territory management.","Through it, Michael was able to learn that the entire Level 3 Region contained a total of one registered individual and approximately three thousand four hundred unregistered creatures.","There was no map available at Level One, but Michael didn't need one to know that the majority of those three thousand four hundred belonged to his undead, with the remainder likely being the awakeners lurking near the domain's edges.","Whether ordinary monsters were also included among the unregistered count would require his own investigation to confirm.","The next function under territory management was registration. According to the Universal Cornerstone, when individuals registered, roles could be assigned to them.","At Level One, there were three types of registered individuals.","The first was Commoners. This offered no benefits beyond being recognizable by the Universal Cornerstone within its territory and being able to access certain functions like the trade hub.","The second was the Privileged. These were similar to Commoners except they could interact with the Universal Cornerstone in additional ways beyond what ordinary residents could.","To Michael, they felt closest to staff.","The third was Registered Lords. These were individuals who, like Michael, had claimed a Cornerstone of their own but had chosen to become his subjects.","This granted them almost no visible benefit and functioned more as a formal confirmation of submission.","Of course, there were likely benefits he couldn't see yet. The information mentioned that Registered Lords would have their Cornerstone linked to his.","Perhaps that meant they would share in certain effects, or freeload from him in some fashion. As for the specifics, he could only wait for a future version of himself to figure it out.","The next registered individual was himself. It was through this entry that Michael understood how his identity as the Cornerstone's owner could be lost, aside from its destruction or his death.","The final method was voluntarily passing ownership to someone else.","Territory management wasn't limited to these functions, but many options remained greyed out. Only time would reveal what else awaited him.","The next function that caught Michael's attention was the Trade Hub.","According to the information provided by the Origin Will, this function allowed trading with the Origin Will itself.","\"Trade with the Origin Will?\"","Michael frowned in confusion.","It didn't really make sense on the surface.","To many in the universe, the Origin Will was simply the name of a system with established rules. Something like a base intelligence that only performed specific tasks and resolved problems.","But after many encounters with it, Michael knew this enigmatic system possessed intelligence no lower than any intelligent being in the universe, and was likely the most supreme existence of all.","And the Universal Cornerstone was claiming he could trade with such a figure.","\"Is it referring to the system or the will itself? Surely even legendary-grade treasures have limits.\"","Regardless of his doubts, Michael was filled with anticipation.","A panel immediately appeared before him.","[Buy] [Sell]","After a brief hesitation, Michael decided to try the sell function first.","\"Best to save the best for last.\"","As those words left his mouth and he made his selection, the panels dissolved. Instead, a strange object slowly materialized from the Universal Cornerstone.","It resembled a table, though not a normal one supported by legs. It was a perfectly smooth rectangular platform of translucent crystal that simply floated before him at about waist height.","Countless tiny runes flowed beneath its surface like rivers of light.","The moment it fully formed, information entered Michael's mind.","Trade Table. Anything placed upon it would be evaluated before an offer was made.","Michael's curiosity immediately grew.","\"So that's how it works.\"","The process was remarkably straightforward. Place an item on the Trade Table and it would be evaluated. If the owner agreed with the offered value, the trade would be completed immediately.","No bargaining. No negotiations. Just a direct exchange.","\"...Quite simple.\"","Michael looked around before opening his storage. Among the numerous resources he had collected throughout the Origin Battlefield, he selected something of relatively low value.","A Two-Star Rare Grade medicinal herb. Although considered valuable, he had harvested several identical ones throughout his travels. Selling one wouldn't affect him in the slightest.","He gently placed the herb onto the floating platform. The instant it touched the crystal surface, the entire table lit up.","Golden runes spread beneath the herb before converging into a translucent panel.","[Item Evaluation Complete]","Name: Frostleaf Grass","Grade: Rare","Evaluation: ★★","Condition: Excellent","Primary Uses:","Can be refined into intermediate recovery potions.","A common ingredient for frost-aspect medicines.","Can be consumed directly to permanently strengthen resistance against low temperatures to a minor degree.","\"So it even analyzes the item.\"","Michael quietly read through the information. His attention quickly shifted toward the bottom of the panel where another line had appeared.","Estimated Value Origin Points: 239","Would you like to proceed with the transaction?","[Yes] [No]","\"Origin Points...\"","Michael frowned slightly.","It was obvious this was some form of currency, but unfortunately the Universal Cornerstone didn't provide any further explanation. It merely displayed the amount the herb was worth.","Michael sighed helplessly, then looked toward another detail on the panel.","Evaluation: ★★","Unlike the seven universal grades he currently knew, this evaluation appeared to follow an entirely different system using only stars.","Was it grading quality? Rarity among items of the same grade? Usefulness to the Origin Will? Or perhaps overall value?","Michael had a feeling it was most likely the last, but without a way to confirm, he couldn't jump to conclusions.","However, running more tests in the future would inevitably reveal more.","Looking back at the herb resting peacefully on the floating platform, Michael didn't hesitate for long.","Two hundred and thirty-nine Origin Points didn't sound like much, but the herb itself wasn't particularly valuable to him either.","More importantly, he wanted to understand how the Trade Hub truly functioned. The only way to learn was through experience."]},{"number":1129,"title":"Chapter 1129: Might Be Too Hot To Handle","paragraphs":["Michael reached forward.","\"I accept.\"","His finger lightly pressed the [Yes] panel. The floating platform emitted a soft hum. The Frostleaf Grass slowly dissolved into countless tiny particles of light before disappearing completely.","At almost the same moment, another translucent panel materialized before him.","Transaction Successful","Item Sold: Frostleaf Grass","Origin Points Received: 239","Current Balance: 239 Origin Points","\"So that's it.\"","Michael looked around instinctively but found nothing unusual.","\"It really was sold...\"","After a brief moment of thought, he dismissed the matter. The information simply wasn't available to him yet. With the selling process complete, his attention naturally shifted toward the other option.","\"Buy.\"","The moment he selected it, the Trade Table transformed. The previous interface dissolved before an entirely new one appeared.","[Trade Hub]","Origin Point Balance: 239","[Available Goods]","Universal Goods","Knowledge","Equipment","Resources","Skills","Unique Goods","Michael selected Universal Goods first.","Rows upon rows of items immediately appeared before him causing his eyes to widened.","\"So many...\"","The list was enormous. However, after scrolling for a while, he noticed something.","Every item displayed was rated between one and four stars. Nothing higher appeared.","Perhaps a Level One Universal Cornerstone simply wasn't permitted to trade for higher-rated goods.","In any case, Michael wasn't too disappointed. Even the first few pages already contained enough treasures to leave him stunned.","His gaze landed on one particular item.","Basic Elven Language","Evaluation: ★★★★","Price: 68,600 Origin Points","Michael couldn't help gasping.","\"...Language?\"","One could directly purchase a language? His curiosity immediately overwhelmed him. He opened the description.","Basic Elven Language Grants complete mastery over the spoken and written fundamentals of the Elven language.","Michael stared silently for several seconds.","\"So knowledge itself can be traded...\"","This alone completely overturned his expectations of the Trade Hub. He quickly continued browsing.","One item after another appeared before him.","Rare Grade herbs. Rare Grade ores. Extraordinary Grade monster materials. Extraordinary Grade weapons. Extraordinary Grade cultivation resources. Extraordinary Grade spell scrolls.","There were simply too many treasures.","Yet as Michael's gaze shifted toward their prices, the excitement on his face slowly stiffened.","Tens of thousands. Hundreds of thousands. Some even reaching Millions.","Michael's eyelids twitched.","\"...I'm so poor.\"","There was simply no other way to describe it. His entire fortune consisted of a mere two hundred and thirty-nine Origin Points. Compared to the prices displayed before him, he might as well have been penniless.","Michael smiled bitterly before closing the Universal Goods section.","\"Let's look somewhere more realistic.\"","His attention shifted toward the final category.","Unique Goods.","According to the information provided by the Universal Cornerstone, these goods were exclusive to Universal Cornerstones based on their level. Michael selected the category.","The list before him immediately shrank to only a handful of items. But the very first entry caused his breathing to stop.","Basic Class Scroll","Evaluation: ★★★★★★★★★★","Price: 5,000,000","Description: Grants the user one random Basic Class at the cost of any existing foundation. No age limit.","Origin Points Unique Item Exclusive to Level One Universal Cornerstones.","Michael's pupils contracted.","\"A... class scroll?\"","For several moments, he simply stared at the panel. His heartbeat accelerated.","Every awakener in the universe, including those who had awakened naturally, could be said to have done so through pure luck.","Even two powerful awakeners coming together to have a child didn't guarantee the child would awaken in the future.","No one truly understood the conditions behind it.","Talent could be inherited from parents and Bloodlines could influence potential. But awakening itself remained one of the greatest mysteries.","Yet now, a single scroll could grant someone a class.","Didn't that mean...","\"This is practically a guaranteed awakening...\"","Michael muttered in disbelief. Anyone without a class could potentially become an awakener simply by using this scroll. Its value was impossible to estimate.","No wonder it had received a ten-star evaluation. It also seemed the star evaluation system was more complex than he had initially imagined, since one would expect such an opportunity to be considered close to priceless.","In any case, if five million Origin Points was roughly equivalent to more than twenty thousand Rare Grade herbs, Michael doubted any great power would hesitate to purchase one if given the opportunity.","Suppressing his shock, he continued scrolling down the list. There were only four additional class scrolls.","Knight Class Scroll","Evaluation: ★★★★★★★★★★","Price: 7,000,000 Origin Points","Mage Class Scroll","Evaluation: ★★★★★★★★★★","Price: 12,000,000 Origin Points","Hunter Class Scroll","Evaluation: ★★★★★★★★★★","Price: 6,000,000 Origin Points","Archer Class Scroll","Evaluation: ★★★★★★★★★★","Price: 5,500,000 Origin Points","Michael's eyes lingered on the Mage Class Scroll. It was the most expensive among the specialized classes.","Considering how powerful mages often became in the later stages of cultivation and awakening, the pricing wasn't entirely surprising.","Michael slowly leaned back, unable to hide the amazement in his eyes.","\"So these... are the exclusive goods of a Level One Universal Cornerstone.\"","Class scrolls. The mere existence of such treasures was enough to shake the foundation of countless worlds.","And yet they were only the exclusive items available at the lowest possible level of a Universal Cornerstone.","Michael suddenly found himself wondering what unimaginable treasures awaited him if he ever upgraded it to Level Two.","Suddenely an incredible chill ran up his spine.","\"Heavens, I am so cooked.\"","It was only now that the full weight of his situation settled on him.","If anyone leadned what the Universal Cornerstone was capable of, they wouldn't wait before knocking on his door with very unreasonable requests.","\"I don't even think they need to know what it can do. Just knowing I have something valuable enough to be announced will be enough.\"","Michael couldn't help feeling a trace of anxiety, though he wasn't frightened.","Given the Universal Cornerstone's value, several ideas he had originally planned to pursue only after some time now felt like they needed to be pushed forward immediately."]},{"number":1130,"title":"Chapter 1130: Temple","paragraphs":["With less than five minutes remaining before he could leave the Origin Battlefield, Michael wanted to set up some last-minute defenses around the Universal Cornerstone.","Though he hadn't encountered any life-threatening incidents, and had even been bold enough at times to accept ranking challenges, he still wasn't quite used to this dog-eat-dog world.","Better to return home for a bit and handle a few things before coming back.","Of course, he wouldn't leave this place unguarded.","But before all that, there was one more thing to address.","His reward.","After going through the Universal Cornerstone's functions, a new panel appeared before him.","[Reward Distributed]","Congratulations. Reward Successfully Claimed.","Obtained: Awakening Temple Blueprint","Michael blinked and exclaimed in surprise.","\"A blueprint?!\"","His eyes immediately lit up.","\"Finally, I can see what the Structure function is for.\"","Under Territory Management, there had always been a greyed-out section labeled Structures. According to the Universal Cornerstone, structures created through it were buildings or constructs with magical effects.","Unfortunately, the Trade Hub had contained no blueprints when he checked it earlier. Originally, Michael had assumed he would need to upgrade the Universal Cornerstone before acquiring one.","Structures required blueprints. Without a blueprint, there was nothing to construct.","Michael couldn't help smiling.","\"This saves me quite a bit of time.\"","He had expected this function to remain unavailable for quite a while. Instead, the Origin Will had directly rewarded him with his first blueprint.","Awakening Temple Blueprint.","Unfortunately, there was no description of what the Awakening Temple would actually do. Fortunately, there was one additional line beneath it.","Special Notice The first structure constructed using this blueprint will require no additional construction cost.","Michael's brows rose.","\"No cost?\"","Based on the information he had received regarding structures, every blueprint normally required something before the Universal Cornerstone could manifest it.","The stronger the structure, the greater the cost.","However, this reward completely bypassed that requirement. His first Awakening Temple would be built entirely free of charge.","Michael couldn't help nodding.","\"The Origin Will really does reward pioneers.\"","If he had to guess, the reward wasn't merely the blueprint itself. It also included a one-time exemption from the construction cost.","Otherwise, with his current balance of only two hundred and thirty-nine Origin Points, there was a strong chance he wouldn't have been able to build it even if he possessed the blueprint.","Curiosity immediately overwhelmed him. Without hesitation, Michael opened the Structures section beneath Territory Management.","This time, the previously greyed-out interface illuminated.","Structures Available Blueprints: Awakening Temple ×1","Only a single blueprint rested inside the empty interface. Michael reached out and selected it. Immediately, the Universal Cornerstone began processing.","A panel appeared before him. Unlike the previous ones, this panel didn't contain words alone. It displayed a complete projection of his territory.","A bird's-eye view of the entire Level 3 Region unfolded before him. Mountains, forests, rivers, plains, and valleys were all represented in remarkable detail.","At the very center stood the Universal Cornerstone, shining like a miniature sun. A small golden marker pulsed above it.","Then another notification appeared.","\"So I can choose where it will be built. Quite convenient.\"","[Structure Placement]","Please select the construction location for: Awakening Temple Michael studied the map for a few moments. Although the territory was enormous, he had no intention of constructing anything far away for now.","Since the Universal Cornerstone was the absolute core of his territory, keeping the Awakening Temple nearby was undoubtedly the safest decision.","Without much hesitation, Michael reached out and tapped a location roughly three hundred meters from the Universal Cornerstone.","Immediately, the selected location began glowing.","Location Confirmed.","Another notification followed before Michael could do anything else.","Special Reward Detected.","First Structure Construction Reward Applied.","Construction Cost: Waived.","Construction Time: Reduced to Maximum.","Estimated Construction Time: Instantaneous.","Michael's eyebrows rose.","\"Instantaneous?\"","The moment the final word appeared, the map vanished.","BOOOOOOM!","The Universal Cornerstone suddenly released a dazzling pillar of golden light that shot into the sky. The entire territory trembled.","Mana from every direction surged toward the selected location like countless glowing rivers. The surrounding air distorted as the earth rumbled.","Then an even brighter light erupted. Michael instinctively narrowed his eyes. For several seconds, his vision was consumed by nothing but radiant white.","The light continued growing stronger before suddenly collapsing inward.","Silence followed.","Michael slowly opened his eyes.","Standing where there had once been empty ground was a building.","It wasn't particularly large. The structure resembled a pristine white temple fashioned from flawless crystal and pale stone.","Elegant pillars supported its entrance while intricate golden runes covered every surface, glowing faintly with a sacred brilliance.","Despite its modest size, an indescribable aura surrounded it. It wasn't oppressive. Nor was it majestic in the conventional sense. Instead, it inspired instinctive reverence.","A gentle stream of pure mana continuously flowed between the Awakening Temple and the Universal Cornerstone, forming an invisible connection that linked the two together.","Almost immediately, another panel appeared before him.","Structure Successfully Constructed.","Awakening Temple Status: Active","A translucent panel simultaneously unfolded before him.","Awakening Temple Status: Active","Building Level: Level 1","Structure Function: Allows classless intelligent lifeforms to undergo the Trial of Awakening. Those who successfully complete the trial will awaken a class.","Michael's breathing paused.","\"...What?\"","He reread the panel. His eyes gradually widened.","\"This is just like a Class Scroll, except...\"","The difference was enormous.","A Basic Class Scroll was a consumable. Once used, it disappeared forever.","This was an entire structure. A permanent one. Anyone who met the requirements could enter it. If they passed the trial, they would awaken.","Michael couldn't suppress the excitement rising inside him.","\"So as long as the temple remains... people can continue awakening.\"","This was fundamentally different from consuming a priceless treasure. It was an establishment.","One capable of continuously producing awakeners.","Compared to the Class Scroll, Michael felt this building was even more valuable, at least in terms of long-term influence.","He quickly continued reading.","Unfortunately, his excitement gradually settled.","\"As expected... there really is a catch.\"","Several additional lines slowly appeared beneath the previous description.","Awakening Temple Origin Energy: 100%","Michael wasn't disappointed. If anything, this made far more sense. A structure capable of granting classes without any restrictions would have been absurd.","\"But what's with this Origin Energy? Even the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion requires it. Is it something all treasures at the legendary grade level need?\"","It did seem to be the case.","In any case, even if he couldn't actively gather the energy right now since he didn't yet understand what it was, having a full tank of it was good news.","All he needed to know was the consumption rate per use.","Would it cost more than one percent to awaken someone, or less?","That was yet another thing only the future would answer."]},{"number":1131,"title":"Chapter 1131: Temple [2]","paragraphs":["Michael closed the panel before turning his attention toward the temple itself. A second later he appeared directly at its entrance.","\"If I'm going to use this in the future, I should at least see what's inside.\"","Without hesitation, he ascended the broad staircase leading to the entrance.","Each step was carved from flawless white crystal that reflected the surrounding light without a single imperfection.","Delicate golden veins ran naturally through every slab, pulsing faintly as though the temple itself possessed a heartbeat.","The massive entrance stood nearly fifteen meters tall.","Rather than ordinary doors, two enormous crystal gates stood open, their surfaces engraved with countless runes that continuously shifted and rearranged themselves. Every rune radiated a gentle golden glow.","Towering pillars flanked the entrance. Each was thick enough that dozens of people would struggle to wrap their arms around it. They rose high into the sky before curving gracefully into elaborate arches.","Intricate carvings covered every inch of their surfaces. Warriors clashing against terrifying beasts. Scholars studying mysterious tomes. Dragons soaring among stars.","Although the carvings were motionless, Michael could almost swear they were alive. Every figure possessed astonishing detail, as though frozen in the middle of a single moment in history.","Above the entrance rested a circular golden emblem nearly five meters across. Within it was an unfamiliar symbol resembling an eye surrounded by countless concentric rings.","Simply looking at it caused Michael's soul to tremble slightly, and he quickly withdrew his gaze.","Whatever that symbol represented, if it represented anything at all, was clearly beyond his current level of understanding.","Taking a slow breath, Michael stepped through the entrance.","The instant he crossed the doorway, his footsteps unconsciously came to a halt.","\"...It's bigger.\"","From the outside, the Awakening Temple had appeared no larger than a heavy-sized chapel. Yet the space before him resembled the interior of a palace hall.","The ceiling stretched nearly a hundred meters overhead, disappearing into soft golden clouds that drifted lazily beneath an invisible sky.","Countless crystal chandeliers floated freely in the air without chains or supports, each resembling blooming flowers carved from condensed light. They illuminated the hall with a warm radiance that neither dazzled the eyes nor cast harsh shadows.","The hall itself extended for hundreds of meters. Rows of magnificent white pillars lined both sides, each one wider than an ancient tree and engraved with flowing golden runes that continuously shimmered beneath their polished surfaces.","The floor was fashioned from mirror-like white jade interwoven with intricate golden lines that formed an enormous magic formation spanning the entire temple.","Every few seconds, the formation emitted a soft pulse before fading once more, almost like the breathing of a living creature.","The air was extraordinarily pure. Every breath Michael took filled his body with refreshing energy. His accumulated fatigue seemed to melt away, while his mind became noticeably calmer and clearer.","Not a single speck of dust could be found anywhere in the temple.","The temple was immersed in absolute silence. Yet rather than feeling empty, it felt sacred.","Michael slowly turned around. The entrance remained exactly where it should have been, and nothing appeared abnormal. Yet the interior was undeniably dozens of times larger than the building he had seen from outside.","He smiled faintly.","\"Definitely some use of void magic. I wonder when Wisdom and I would reach such a level.\"","This was different from a domain, even if a domain was also another dimension in itself.","The complexity of what the temple had achieved compared to a domain seemed to gap the latter in comparison across many levels.","Though Michael hadn't created a domain himself, he was almost always surrounded by those who had, so he had some frame of reference.","Suppressing his curiosity, Michael continued walking forward.","The enormous hall was surprisingly empty.","There were no chairs. No decorations. No murals. Only two gigantic statues stood proudly at the far end of the temple.","The statue on the left depicted an imposing warrior clad in layered armor.","Unlike ordinary knights, numerous weapons were strapped across the warrior's body.","A sword rested at his waist. A spear was slung across his back. A battle axe hung from one side. Several daggers lined his belt. It was as though every conventional weapon could be wielded by him.","Standing opposite him was another statue. A mage. The figure wore long flowing robes. A beautifully crafted wand rested within one hand while the other held an ancient scroll covered in unfamiliar runes.","Both statues radiated an indescribable pressure. Yet strangely, their faces remained blurry. No matter how hard Michael tried to focus, their appearances refused to become clear.","It was almost as though some mysterious force prevented anyone from seeing them.","Beneath each statue floated a circular blue vortex. The portals rotated slowly in complete silence.","Thanks to the information that had entered his mind earlier, Michael immediately understood their purpose.","\"The two awakening paths.\"","The warrior represented the Physical Path.","Those who entered that portal would undergo physical trials. If successful, they would awaken a physical-oriented class. Knight. Warrior. Assassin. Guardian. Hunter. Or countless other possibilities.","Everything depended on the individual's performance during the trial. The better they performed, the stronger the class they obtained.","Outstanding performances could even reward additional gifts, like Traits, which in Michael's opinion were practically talents.","Although not identical, traits could significantly strengthen an awakener just as a talent would. Some enhanced physical ability, like Lily's. Others increased affinity toward certain weapons. Some even improved comprehension or granted passive abilities.","For many awakeners, acquiring an excellent trait could determine their standing among peers.","Michael then looked toward the second portal.","The Magical Path. Its principles were nearly identical. Those who entered would face trials centered around magic.","Successful challengers would awaken mage-type classes, while exceptional performers likewise had a chance of obtaining powerful traits.","\"This really does reward ability.\"","There was no favoritism or guaranteed outcome. The temple merely provided the opportunity. What one obtained depended entirely upon oneself."]},{"number":1132,"title":"Chapter 1132: Clone Registration","paragraphs":["Of course, for something like this, not everything was sunshine.","The first trial offered by the Awakening Temple was completely safe. Regardless of whether one succeeded or failed, their life would never be endangered. Failure simply meant leaving empty-handed.","However, any subsequent attempt was different. Not only would it consume considerably more Origin Energy, it also carried genuine danger, including the possibility of death.","Those who challenged the trial a second time would no longer receive the temple's protection. Failure could very well cost them their lives.","Michael slowly nodded.","\"Fair enough.\"","If repeated attempts carried no consequences, people would simply challenge the temple over and over until they eventually succeeded.","This limitation prevented exactly that. More importantly, it preserved the value of awakening itself.","His gaze swept across the spacious hall one final time. Then another realization struck him.","\"So that's why registration exists.\"","Earlier, he hadn't fully understood why individuals needed to be registered under his Universal Cornerstone. Now he did. Only registered individuals could receive the benefits provided by structures within the territory.","Even the lowest status, Commoner, was sufficient. Without becoming at least a registered commoner, no one could use the Awakening Temple.","In other words, every special building the Universal Cornerstone created would likely require some form of registration before granting its benefits.","\"It seems becoming part of the territory isn't just symbolic.\"","It was a genuine prerequisite.","Unfortunately, after another careful inspection, Michael discovered that the Level One Awakening Temple contained nothing else.","Its sole purpose at its current level was to provide the Trial of Awakening. Simple. Yet unimaginably valuable.","Michael observed the temple for several more seconds before turning around and walking toward the entrance.","There were less than three minutes remaining before he would be forced to leave the Origin Battlefield. He still had a few final arrangements to make.","As for what protections he could leave behind, Michael wasn't particularly worried. Now that the Universal Cornerstone had been claimed, it possessed its own defensive measures.","According to the information it had provided, the territory was protected by a defensive barrier centered around the Universal Cornerstone itself. Its strength depended entirely on energy, specifically the mana accumulated within the Cornerstone.","As long as sufficient mana remained, the barrier could withstand any attack directed at it.","Michael didn't doubt the claim too much. After all, if even a Level One Universal Cornerstone possessed abilities capable of producing structures like the Awakening Temple and allowing direct trade with the Origin Will, a defensive barrier capable of resisting attacks wasn't difficult to believe.","However, every defense had its limit. Once the stored mana was exhausted, the barrier would disappear.","After that, whatever happened would happen. Michael had no intention of relying entirely on a single defensive mechanism. Barriers were meant to buy time. Not solve every problem.","To prevent the worst-case scenario, Michael decided leaving several undead behind was the safest option. Even if someone somehow slipped past the barrier, or waited until its energy had been exhausted, they would still need to face Rank Four undead guarding the territory.","One should never underestimate awakeners. The universe contained countless bizarre classes with equally bizarre traits.","Even Michael himself possessed more than one method of bypassing what ordinary people considered impossible.","Who knew what equally troublesome abilities another awakener might possess?","\"It never hurts to be cautious.\"","Many of the undead around him silently dispersed. Some hid beneath the earth. Others concealed themselves within nearby forests. Several took to the skies.","The remainder stationed themselves around both the Universal Cornerstone and the Awakening Temple.","From the surface, the territory appeared almost deserted. Yet Michael knew that countless pairs of eyes were now watching every direction.","\"That should do.\"","He nodded in satisfaction. Still, he wasn't completely satisfied. Physical protection alone wasn't enough. What if something unexpected happened while he was in the real world? He couldn't constantly travel back and forth every time he wanted to inspect his territory. That would be far too inconvenient.","\"It would be nice if I could manage things remotely...\"","Fortunately, he already had a solution. Though he could enter the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion, that didn't mean he couldn't bring something out of it.","With a thought, a figure appeared before him. It was his other body, the one created in the Land of Origin.","Upon seeing it, the first thing Michael tried was to have his other body directly enter through his origin body and bypass needing to use the treasure portal entrance. It didn't work.","A single glance at the situation told him immediately that the Origin Battlefield was responsible for the restriction.","As for whether this would change after the forced entry session ended and awakeners were granted more freedom, he would have to test it again in the future.","In any case, with his other body present, Michael could use his undead more effectively from within the Land of Origin.","If those guarding the territory needed reinforcements, the other body could simply provide them by bringing out more undead from the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion.","Michael's gaze shifted toward the timer floating at the corner of his vision.","Less than two minutes remained.","\"I should hurry.\"","His attention immediately turned toward his second body. Since bringing it out from the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion was possible, there was no reason not to make full use of it.","With that thought, Michael opened the registration interface of the Universal Cornerstone.","Assign Registration","Status","Commoner","Privileged","Michael didn't hesitate.","\"Privileged.\"","The moment he confirmed his choice, golden light descended from the Universal Cornerstone and enveloped his second body.","A second later, another notification appeared.","Registration Successful.","Registered Individual: Michael Norman (Clone) Status: Privileged (Highest Authority Level)","For a brief moment, Michael held his breath. Then he immediately attempted to access the Universal Cornerstone through his second body.","A second later, another notification appeared.","Registration Successful.","Registered Individual: Michael Norman (Clone) Status: Privileged (Highest Authority Level)","For a brief moment, Michael held his breath. Then he immediately attempted to access the Universal Cornerstone through his second body.","The Territory Management interface appeared instantly. The Trade Hub. Structures. Registration. Everything.","His second body possessed exactly the same authority as his original.","\"It worked!\""]},{"number":1133,"title":"Chapter 1133: Return","paragraphs":["A satisfied smile appeared on Michael's face.","\"This is even better than I expected.\"","Just as Michael finished confirming everything, another series of panels suddenly appeared before every awakener within the Origin Battlefield.","The Tutorial Phase has officially ended. Origin Battlefield Restrictions Updated.","A second notification followed immediately.","From this point onward, awakeners may freely enter and leave the Origin Battlefield.","Current accumulated participation requirements will remain in effect.","Failure to satisfy the required participation time before the designated deadline may result in penalties determined by the Origin Battlefield.","\"So the forced schedule is finally over.\"","Michael quietly nodded. Although awakeners now possessed the freedom to leave whenever they wished, they couldn't simply ignore the Origin Battlefield altogether.","The Origin Will had clearly established a minimum participation quota. Exactly what the penalties were remained unknown. Michael had no intention of finding out.","The timer in the corner of his vision finally reached zero.","Before he could react, his body gradually became translucent. The surrounding scenery blurred. The brilliant white temple. The Universal Cornerstone. His undead. Everything slowly faded from sight.","Only his second body remained standing where he was, calmly watching the original disappear.","The next instant, Michael felt a brief sensation of weightlessness. His vision darkened.","Then light returned. The familiar scent of home entered his nose. The quiet hum of an air conditioner replaced the distant sounds of the Origin Battlefield.","Michael blinked at the sudden change.","\"Cousin!\"","Not far away, seated on the couch, Lily, who had also just returned, immediately turned toward him.","Compared to Michael, who looked almost exactly as he had before entering the Origin Battlefield, Lily looked considerably more disheveled.","Her clothes were covered in dirt and dust. Several dried leaves clung to her hair, while faint streaks of dried mud covered her exposed arms and cheeks.","Fortunately, the armor covering most of her body remained spotless. Not a single scratch could be found on it.","A quick glance confirmed what his senses had already suspected. Lily had no hidden injuries and simply appeared very disheveled.","Only after confirming all of that did he finally relax.","However, something else immediately caught his attention. His brows furrowed.","\"...Where are your beasts?\"","The two tamed monsters Lily had entered the Origin Battlefield with were nowhere to be seen. Lily scratched the back of her head awkwardly.","\"I released them.\"","Michael blinked in surprise.","\"You what?\"","She quickly waved both hands.","\"I broke the contracts.\"","\"...Why?\"","Michael's expression became thoughtful.","Lily shrugged helplessly.","\"They weren't strong enough. They helped at first, but after I entered the deeper areas, they would've only become burdens.\"","She lowered her voice slightly. \"If I had kept forcing them to follow me, they would've died. So before that happened, I broke the contracts.\"","Michael silently looked at her for a moment. Then he nodded.","\"I would've done the same.\"","There was no blame in his voice. If he didn't have his talent and wasn't a necromancer, if the beasts lacked the strength to survive, forcibly keeping the contracts would only have resulted in needless deaths without them even serving as cannon fodder.","Michael was actually quite pleased by Lily's judgment. She hadn't stubbornly clung to sentiment or confused morals. She had made the correct decision. That alone showed considerable maturity.","Still, something felt off.","Michael narrowed his eyes. Lily's strength wasn't weak. With her talent, trait, and equipment, ordinary monsters shouldn't have pushed her to such an extent.","Unless...","\"You met someone powerful?\"","The moment he asked, Lily's eyes lit up. She clapped her hands together excitedly.","\"Oh! I almost forgot to tell you!\"","Michael waited quietly.","\"There weren't many, but I did meet some really strong people.\" She gestured animatedly as she spoke. \"I don't even think they were normal.\"","\"For example...\" She pointed at herself. \"I was literally being chased by a dragon before I got dragged back here.\"","Michael stared at her.","\"...A dragon?\"","\"Yep!\" She nodded enthusiastically. \"A huge blue one! It kept yelling that it was going to eat us.\"","\"'Us?'\"","\"Me and another guy.\"","Lily couldn't help laughing as she remembered.","\"It was actually pretty funny.\"","Michael's eyelid twitched.","\"...Funny?\"","\"Yeah. He kept teasing the dragon.\" She mimicked the conversation while trying not to laugh, then burst into laughter. \"The dragon became so angry its face practically turned blue.\"","Michael remained silent.","\"...It already was blue.\"","Lily paused for a second.","\"...That's true.\"","The two looked at each other. Then Lily laughed even harder.","\"It was hilarious! It kept roaring that it was going to eat both of us while we just kept running.\"","Michael couldn't help shaking his head. Only his cousin could describe being chased by a dragon as a funny experience.","Still, his attention settled on something else.","\"There was another human capable of escaping a dragon...\"","That was considerably more important than the dragon itself. If Lily's description was accurate, that unknown awakener wasn't ordinary.","Michael remained silent for a few seconds. Then his expression became serious.","\"Lily.\"","His tone immediately caused her smile to fade.","\"What?\"","Michael looked directly into her eyes.","\"If something like that happens again, be careful around other awakeners.\"","Lily blinked.","\"The dragon guy?\"","\"Not just him.\" Michael slowly shook his head. \"Everyone.\"","He walked over and sat on the couch opposite her.","\"The Origin Battlefield isn't Aurora. It isn't a school. It isn't somewhere people have to obey laws. There, strength is the law.\"","Lily quietly listened.","Michael continued calmly.","\"Some people may genuinely cooperate. Others may save you. But many will smile while thinking about how to use you. They'll pretend to be friends. They'll pretend to be allies. They'll help you once or twice just so you'll lower your guard. And when the opportunity comes, they'll stab you in the back.\"","Lily's cheerful expression gradually disappeared. Then Michael said something that made her expression turn strange.","\"Especially men.\"","Lily tilted her head.","\"Huh?\""]},{"number":1134,"title":"Chapter 1134: Very Familiar Name","paragraphs":["Michael nodded.","\"I'm serious. If you're alone and you meet a man who seems overly friendly, don't assume he has good intentions. Some might. But many won't. They may have ulterior motives. They may want your equipment. Your resources. Or something even worse.\"","His voice remained calm throughout. He wasn't trying to frighten her. He was simply stating a reality.","\"The stronger you become, the more people like that you'll encounter.\"","Lily was silent for a while before asking softly,","\"So... you don't trust anyone?\"","Michael thought about the question.","\"I trust people. But trust isn't free. It's earned. And even after someone earns it, I'll still leave myself a way out.\" He smiled faintly. \"Being cautious isn't the same as being paranoid.\"","Lily slowly nodded.","\"I understand.\"","After a brief pause, she puffed out her cheeks.","\"But that guy really didn't seem bad.\"","Michael chuckled.","\"I'm not saying he was a bad person. He might genuinely be a decent guy. I'm saying you shouldn't decide that after meeting him once.\"","He leaned back against the sofa. Lily lowered her head in thought.","\"I'll remember that.\"","\"Good.\"","Michael nodded in satisfaction. After all, Lily's talent and equipment made her an attractive target.","She might not realize it herself, but there would undoubtedly be people who saw her as an easy opportunity because of her relatively trusting personality.","If she learned to be cautious now, it would save her from many unnecessary dangers in the future.","Michael remained thoughtful for a moment before another question surfaced in his mind.","\"Lily.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"How was your time in the First Layer?\"","Lily blinked.","\"The First Layer?\"","She looked at him with obvious confusion.","\"Cousin... I think you're mistaken.\"","Michael frowned.","\"Mistaken?\"","\"I stayed in the Zeroth Layer the entire time.\"","\"...What?\"","This time, it was Michael's turn to be confused.","\"The Zeroth Layer?\"","Lily nodded matter-of-factly.","\"Yeah. I never went anywhere else.\"","Michael fell silent.","That didn't make sense. Based on everything Lily had just described, her experiences were completely inconsistent with what he expected from the Zeroth Layer.","A dragon and a powerful awakener capable of escaping one. Those weren't things Level Ten awakeners should normally be surrounded with.","The Zeroth Layer was supposed to be the beginner's region. Its monsters shouldn't have been anywhere near that strong.","Then why had Lily experienced something completely different?","His brows gradually furrowed. Moments later, a realization flashed through his mind.","\"...I see.\"","Lily tilted her head.","\"What?\"","Michael leaned back slightly.","\"I was making an assumption.\"","He had been thinking the Zeroth Layer worked the same way the higher layers did. But that wasn't necessarily true. His thoughts rapidly connected one clue after another.","Due to the awakening ceremonies being synchronized across many realms, Lily definitely wasn't the only person who had been dragged into the Origin Battlefield just after awakening.","Some of those newly awakened individuals would naturally possess extraordinary talents. Others would come from powerful races, or might even be descendants of terrifying experts, with no time to advance before being pulled in.","Second-generation heirs. Individuals born with advantages far beyond ordinary supernaturals.","When those people entered the Origin Battlefield, the Zeroth Layer wouldn't simply contain ordinary beginners anymore. Its average strength would naturally increase.","\"No...\"","Michael corrected himself internally.","\"Not the average. The upper limit.\"","His eyes slowly widened.","\"So that's how it works.\"","He had always wondered why he had been transferred out of the Third Layer so suddenly. Originally, he believed it was simply because he had grown too strong.","Now he realized the explanation was more precise.","It wasn't strength alone. It was balance. The Origin Battlefield maintained a certain equilibrium within each layer.","Every layer possessed an upper threshold of strength that it could reasonably accommodate. Once someone exceeded that threshold by too great a margin, the Origin Battlefield would push them upward.","It was not as a punishment but to restore equilibrium. This would explain why a reward is given. Or more specifically a consolation.","Michael had done exactly what the origin battlefield will guard against.","With thousands of Rank Four undead, multiple Epic Grade subordinates, a Legendary Grade treasure, and combat power that vastly exceeded everyone else in the Third Layer, he hadn't merely surpassed the strongest inhabitants. He had completely shattered the balance of that layer.","Remaining there would have been unfair to everyone else.","\"So that's why I was transferred.\"","Everything suddenly became much clearer.","Lily, however, was different. Although she was remarkably powerful for a newly awakened individual, she couldn't be overwhelmingly stronger than every other genius present in the Zeroth Layer.","There were others, perhaps many others, with absurd backgrounds that surpassed even the advantages he had given her. As a result, the overall upper threshold of the Zeroth Layer had risen considerably.","Lily hadn't broken its balance. Therefore, the Origin Battlefield had seen no reason to move her elsewhere.","Michael exhaled slowly.","\"The Origin Battlefield system is far more stable than I gave it credit for.\"","Lily's situation, however, made Michael even more curious about who had been with her. Based on her descriptions, they had spent more time together than just being pursued by a dragon.","Since the curiosity was already spiked, Michael didn't hold it back and asked immediately.","Contrary to his expectation that the person would be from a powerful race, it was actually a human. It wasn't that Michael was looking down on humans, but in the early stages they truly weren't the strongest race around.","For a human to match Lily in the Zeroth Layer was already noteworthy.","\"That's not all. This person is also from a new world. Their world has only had awakeners for at most two to three months.\"","This made Michael even more shocked. He wasn't unfamiliar with the concept of a new world, but how could someone from one, a human no less, who had only recently awakened, match Lily in capability?","Michael found it difficult to believe. He suspected the person Lily had spoken with might have been hiding somethings.","\"Where did he say he came from?\"","The question had left Michael's mouth almost subconsciously. Even if a name was given, there was no way he would recognize it.","Or so he thought.","He was very mistaken.","\"His name is Timi, and he says he came from a world called Earth.\""]},{"number":1135,"title":"Chapter 1135: Time Difference","paragraphs":["Earth.","It was a very familiar term that was slowly becoming unfamiliar to Michael the longer he stayed in this world.","One might say it had only been a year, too soon for that to happen, but in actuality it extended closer to two years. Michael had lived two identities during that period. One in Aurora, and the other in the Land of Origin.","Because he had never had much of a life on Earth, his impression of it wasn't particularly warm. Not once had he ever thought of gaining power so he could return to his old world. He hadn't even been certain his old world and this one existed in the same universe.","Yet upon hearing of a realm named Earth, and one that was a new world at that, a suspicious thought couldn't help but take root in his mind.","Michael's reaction to the familiar term produced a visible change in his usually calm demeanor, making Lily curious.","\"Do you know this realm, cousin?\" she asked with clear expectation.","To Lily, though she didn't see her cousin as some omnipotent being, he was still the first supernatural she had ever been close to and by far the most powerful and unique person she knew.","Knowing of a new world called Earth might have seemed like a stretch to others, but to Lily it didn't feel impossible when she thought of her cousin.","However, just as Michael was about to respond and ask more questions, he paused. Both he and Lily turned toward the door at the same moment.","\"Seems like they're back,\" Michael muttered. With their senses, the two had naturally detected Aunt Mia and Jester approaching outside.","\"That's great! I was starting to think we'd need to visit her at the restaurant.\"","When the two had arrived back earlier and taken stock of their surroundings, the first thing each of them had done was spread their senses throughout the house.","Only after confirming it was empty had they begun talking amongst themselves. As for Aunt Mia's absence, it wasn't an immediate concern since Jester wasn't present either.","Lily stretched her arms above her head and looked around the room.","\"I wonder how long we've been away,\" she murmured, her eyes trailing over the furniture. \"The living room doesn't look much different than before.\"","\"It's only been a day,\" Michael answered smoothly.","Lily blinked in complete shock.","\"I was just joking with that question! What do you mean, one day?\"","Michael didn't answer.","Unlike other awakeners who had already entered the Land of Origin and could access a second body unaffected by the Origin Battlefield, Lily had been unlucky.","Being summoned a mere day after her awakening had given her no time to prepare for anything. Michael and many other awakeners, through the use of their dual bodies, had long since discovered the time difference between the Origin Battlefield and the real world.","It was a ratio of three to one. Time within the Origin Battlefield flowed three times faster than in the material world.","That was why, even after spending three full days inside, they had returned to Aurora at noon, just twenty-four hours after their initial disappearance.","Thinking about it now, Michael couldn't help but feel that the Origin Battlefield truly was the greatest cultivation ground an awakener could ever ask for.","It was simply too bloody. Life and death accompanied nearly every opportunity. Yet perhaps that was precisely why it would produce true experts.","Those who survived would inevitably become stronger. No amount of ordinary training could compare to constantly risking one's life against powerful monsters and awakeners from countless worlds.","Then there was the difference in time flow. Taking advantage of that alone would already be an unimaginable opportunity. An awakener could spend three months training while only one month passed in the material world.","At lower ranks, that advantage was already terrifying.","Michael's thoughts then drifted toward the Universal Cornerstone and its functions. A terrifying thought slowly surfaced.","If every sufficiently powerful awakener eventually established a territory, and every territory continued growing, then perhaps the Origin Battlefield wasn't merely a battlefield.","It was laying the foundation for an entirely new civilization. Or perhaps a new era in the universe itself.","Michael unconsciously exhaled.","\"...What exactly is the Origin Will trying to create?\"","No answer came. Only more questions.","Click.","The sound of the front door unlocking interrupted his thoughts. The door slowly swung inward.","Two familiar figures entered.","Jester stepped inside first. Its face remained as expressionless as ever. There wasn't the slightest change in its demeanor. Clearly, it had already sensed Michael and Lily's return long before opening the door.","Although Jester was technically an undead creature, it was strangely easy to forget that fact. Its intelligence had reached such an astonishing level that interacting with it felt no different from interacting with an ordinary person.","Only its unnaturally calm expression and flawless obedience occasionally reminded Michael of its true nature.","Behind it, Aunt Mia stepped into the house carrying several shopping bags.","The moment she looked toward the living room, she froze. Her eyes widened. The bags in her hands nearly slipped to the floor.","\"Michael?\"","\"Lily?\"","She blinked repeatedly as though questioning whether she was hallucinating.","\"Didn't you say you'd be gone for a long time?\"","Michael smiled faintly.","\"I did, but we managed to come back earlier than expected.\"","Aunt Mia hurried over without another word. Unlike Lily, whose appearance immediately suggested she had gone through something difficult, Michael looked only slightly tired.","To Aunt Mia, seeing Michael in such a state wasn't particularly surprising. Ever since he had awakened, she had unconsciously begun viewing him as someone almost invincible.","If anything, her confidence in him was even greater than Lily's. Though so too did her worries grow the more exceptional her nephew seemed to become.","Lily, on the other hand, was a different story. Aunt Mia's heart tightened the moment she saw the dirt covering her daughter's face and clothes.","The shopping bags were hastily placed on the floor."]},{"number":1136,"title":"Chapter 1136: Approaching Troubles","paragraphs":["\"My goodness...\"","Without waiting for either of them to react, Aunt Mia grabbed both Michael and Lily by the shoulders and pulled them closer.","\"Let me see.\"","She first held Lily's cheeks between both hands, turning her face from side to side.","\"Are you hurt? Did anything happen? Does anything hurt?\"","Before Lily could answer, Aunt Mia was already checking her arms. Then her shoulders. Then her forehead. Only after confirming there wasn't a visible wound anywhere did she hurriedly turn toward Michael.","\"And you.\"","She gently held his face as well.","\"Are you injured anywhere?\"","Michael felt the familiar warmth coming from her hands. For a brief moment, he simply enjoyed it.","Though he had only been a supernatural for barely more than a year and had grown so powerful, reality had shown him that this world of swords and magic wasn't a peaceful place.","This simple concern from his aunt felt strangely comforting.","\"I'm fine, Aunt.\" He smiled reassuringly. \"Not even a scratch.\"","Only then did Aunt Mia let out a relieved sigh.","Lily, meanwhile, puffed out her cheeks.","\"Mom... I'm not a child anymore. You don't have to keep checking my face like that.\"","Aunt Mia immediately pinched one of her cheeks.","\"You'll always be my child.\"","Lily groaned.","\"Moooom...\"","Michael couldn't help smiling at the scene.","Aunt Mia finally released Lily before looking between the two once more, as though still trying to reassure herself they were truly safe.","Michael then asked,","\"You came back earlier than usual.\"","Normally, at this time Aunt Mia would still be at her restaurant.","Aunt Mia smiled awkwardly.","\"I couldn't focus.\" Her expression softened. \"After the two of you disappeared, I kept worrying. No matter what I tried to do, I couldn't stop thinking about it. So I decided to close early.\"","She shook her head helplessly.","Before Michael could respond, Jester spoke in its calm, emotionless voice.","\"I concluded that continuing to work would have been detrimental to Aunt Mia's health, so I suggested that we return home. I also recommended getting some ingredients so that food would be available upon your and Lily's return.\"","Aunt Mia laughed softly.","\"I didn't actually think you'd come back this soon.\"","Michael glanced sideways at Jester. The undead stood motionless, its expression unchanged. However, Michael's eyes narrowed almost imperceptibly.","Did it... use its Law?","Jester possessed a very unique law. Thanks to its evolution a few months ago pushing it into Rank Four, its understanding of that law had grown considerably stronger.","Predicting an approximate time of arrival didn't seem entirely impossible.","Almost as though sensing Michael's gaze, Jester calmly turned its head toward him. The two stared at each other for a brief second.","Jester remained perfectly expressionless. Michael likewise said nothing. Whether it truly had used its Law or had simply made a logical deduction, he couldn't tell. Nor did he ask.","Michael eventually looked away. As long as Jester continued protecting Aunt Mia while he was away, he had no complaints.","In truth, although his second body remained on standby in case of emergencies, Michael had deliberately kept it hidden from everyone. The current period was simply too sensitive.","For the first time in history, every awakener across the universe had simultaneously been transported into another world.","During such a period, if his clone were suddenly seen moving around Aurora while everyone knew Michael himself should have been gone, it would only create unnecessary complications from those looking to exploit the situation.","The fewer people who knew, the better.","At present, only Jester knew that his second body remained active outside the Origin Battlefield. Even Aunt Mia had been kept completely in the dark.","The same applied to those secretly watching over the apartment. Michael had sensed them the moment he returned.","There weren't many. A small number belonged to the academy. The rest were individuals specifically assigned by the Federation to watch over his family because of him. Though the public statement was protection, Michael knew the Federation's interest in him was far from purely selfless.","After everything Michael had accomplished over the past year, his importance had risen to a level where the academy and several influential figures, many he had yet to even meet, were unwilling to underestimate him.","With the recent matter of the Universal Cornerstone, he could already foresee a wave of visitors arriving soon. He needed to start making preparations.","But compared to what was coming immediately, Michael was more wary of what would follow once other people began claiming Cornerstones of their own.","Unless someone possessed means similar to his, Michael was almost certain a single individual couldn't claim a Universal Cornerstone alone. A strong force, or multiple forces working together, would likely be necessary.","Even so, it probably wouldn't take long. When enough awakeners began to understand what a Universal Cornerstone was truly capable of, that was when the real battle over ownership would begin.","\"You two should sit down.\"","Aunt Mia suddenly remembered the shopping bags still sitting on the floor. \"You've only just come back. You must be starving.\"","Without waiting for an answer, she bent to pick them up again.","\"I'll make lunch.\"","Lily's eyes immediately lit up.","\"I'm starving!\" She rubbed her stomach dramatically.","Aunt Mia laughed as Michael chuckled quietly beside her.","Jester calmly stepped forward.","\"Let me assist.\"","Aunt Mia instinctively shook her head.","\"There's no need. I can manage.\"","However, Jester had already taken several of the heavier bags from her hands.","\"It will be faster.\"","Aunt Mia hesitated before smiling helplessly.","\"...Alright.\"","The two walked toward the kitchen together.","Watching the scene, Michael couldn't help but feel a sense of peace. The house hadn't changed. The familiar atmosphere remained exactly the same.","For just a brief moment, the bloody battles of the Origin Battlefield felt unimaginably distant.","But only for a moment.","Michael's gaze unconsciously drifted toward the window. Beyond those peaceful streets, the world had already changed.","Millions, perhaps billions, of awakeners had returned today carrying experiences similar to his own.","Starting from today, the world would never be the same again.","This was only the beginning."]},{"number":1137,"title":"Chapter 1137: Who Is Michael Norman?","paragraphs":["Just as Michael had expected, the moment awakeners across the universe returned to their respective worlds and had enough time to settle their thoughts, three names rapidly spread through countless realms.","Michael Norman. Aurora Realm. Universal Cornerstone.","For the overwhelming majority of awakeners, these three names were completely unfamiliar. Yet that only made them more important.","One had to remember that this wasn't an ordinary incident.","For the first time in recorded history, even Demigods had been forcibly dragged into an unfamiliar world. That fact alone was enough to shake the foundations of countless civilizations.","Many of those Demigods had entered confident in their own strength. Some never returned. Even beings standing at the peak of their worlds had died within the Origin Battlefield.","When one's own life became uncertain, every piece of information became priceless.","Contrary to what many mortals believed, the stronger a supernatural became, the more they feared death.","After spending centuries, sometimes millennia, climbing toward the peak, who would willingly throw everything away? It was precisely because they had so much to lose that powerful beings valued their lives even more.","Naturally, when the Origin Will itself suddenly announced a single individual's name before every awakener throughout the universe, ignoring it became impossible.","Compared to Michael Norman himself, most people were actually more interested in something else.","The Universal Cornerstone. What exactly was it? Why had the Origin Will specifically announced its acquisition?","Could it be the reason everyone had been dragged into the Origin Battlefield? Or perhaps it was merely connected to that reason.","In truth, very few cared whether it was directly responsible or not. At such a sensitive moment, anything acknowledged by the Origin Will immediately became the center of attention.","If the Origin Will had announced it, then it had to matter.","Powerful organizations and forces immediately began gathering information. Even secluded experts who had ignored worldly affairs for centuries were forced to emerge from isolation.","Though they didn't know who Michael Norman was or what the Universal Cornerstone was, the Origin Will had left one clue.","Aurora.","Compared to finding a single individual, finding a realm was considerably easier. And fortunately for many, Aurora turned out to be a realm whose name had already been slowly spreading across the universe, making it even simpler to locate.","Deep within Aurora, hidden behind layers of spatial barriers invisible to the outside world, lay an enormous independent secret realm.","It was the true headquarters of the Aurora Federation.","Suspended high above an endless sea of drifting clouds floated a landmass spanning hundreds of kilometers.","The entire island possessed a distinctly futuristic appearance. Countless silver-white buildings stretched across the floating land, their smooth metallic surfaces reflecting sunlight like polished mirrors.","Towering skyscrapers reached into the sky, connected by transparent bridges that seemed to hang unsupported in midair.","Streams of blue energy flowed beneath crystal roads instead of conventional power lines.","Vehicles without wheels silently glided through the air along predetermined routes, leaving behind trails of pale light before disappearing between enormous buildings.","Above the city, hundreds of floating platforms orbited like miniature satellites.","Some served as docking stations for aircraft. Others housed defensive weapons capable of threatening even high-ranking supernaturals.","Occasionally, massive warships several kilometers long slowly cruised through the sky. Their hulls were forged from rare alloys while thousands of runes continuously shimmered beneath their armored exteriors.","They resembled a fusion of magic and technology. Neither completely one nor the other. Rather, both had become inseparable.","Surrounding the entire floating island was an enormous translucent barrier. Its surface remained invisible most of the time.","Only when sunlight from the realm struck it from certain angles would faint ripples become visible, revealing the countless overlapping defensive formations protecting one of the Federation's most important locations.","This was Aurora's greatest fortress. Its final sanctuary and command center. The heart of the Federation.","At the very center of the island stood the tallest structure.","A magnificent tower over two thousand meters high pierced the clouds. Unlike the surrounding buildings, this tower appeared almost entirely crystalline.","Its surface resembled transparent glass, yet within it flowed rivers of golden light that continuously circulated from the base to the summit.","The closer one approached, the greater the invisible pressure became.","At the tower's peak, a circular conference hall overlooked the entirety of the floating city. The walls were fashioned entirely from transparent crystal, allowing one to observe every corner of the secret realm.","Normally, this place remained nearly empty. Only when matters concerning the entirety of Aurora arose would the highest authorities gather here.","Today, every seat was occupied.","The atmosphere was unprecedentedly solemn. No one spoke. The silence itself seemed heavy.","Many of the figures seated around the enormous circular table possessed auras so overwhelming that the surrounding space subtly distorted around them.","Some appeared middle-aged. Others looked like ordinary old men and women. One looked no older than sixteen. But appearances meant very little at their level. Each represented one of Aurora's greatest powers.","Above the center of the conference table floated a massive holographic projection. One name remained suspended in the air.","Michael Norman.","After a long period of silence, an elderly man with silver hair finally broke it.","\"Everyone.\"","The elderly man sat at the head of the circular table. His silver hair was neatly combed behind him, while his aged face carried neither joy nor anger. He simply sat there quietly. Yet the moment one looked at him, an indescribable pressure naturally arose.","This was the Chairman of the Aurora Federation. One of the strongest experts in the entire Aurora Realm.","To his left and right sat six individuals each. Together with him, there were exactly thirteen people inside the conference hall.","The old man slowly opened his eyes. His calm gaze swept across everyone present before finally stopping on the holographic words floating above the conference table.","\"Recently...\" His aged voice echoed throughout the silent chamber. \"...something concerning the entire universe, as we know it, has occurred.\""]},{"number":1138,"title":"Chapter 1138: Intentions","paragraphs":["As those words fell, whether consciously or unconsciously, every single person in the room turned toward one individual.","An old man sat three seats away from the Chairman.","His complexion was unusually pale. His right sleeve hung empty. One arm was missing.","His expression remained indifferent despite the numerous gazes directed toward him.","The old man continued calmly.","\"The Origin Battlefield. The Universal Cornerstone. The disappearance of several awakeners in the world. Any one of these matters should have been enough to occupy the universe's complete attention for years.\"","He paused briefly.","\"But for some reason...\" His gaze slowly shifted toward the floating name. \"...that matter, which initially concerned the entire universe, has now become concentrated upon our heads.\"","The Chairman lightly waved his hand. The holographic words suspended above the table immediately disappeared.","In their place, a three-dimensional image slowly materialized.","A young man with black hair and calm eyes appeared above the conference table. He looked no older than twenty.","The image slowly rotated.","The Chairman's gaze never left it.","\"This...\" He said quietly. \"...is Michael Norman.\"","However, no one present showed the slightest surprise upon seeing Michael's image. Not because they lacked curiosity. Nor because they underestimated him.","Aside from every person seated within this room having already received a briefing before the meeting officially began, this was far from the first time they had heard the name Michael Norman.","The atmosphere remained heavy as everyone's eyes rested upon the projection.","The Chairman slowly continued.","\"I believe everyone here is already aware that this young man has made numerous contributions to Aurora over the past year.\"","Several people nodded.","\"Michael Norman advanced at a speed that completely exceeded our expectations. Initially, we simply believed we had discovered another talented genius on the level of a holy child.\" His expression became complicated. \"Now, I'm no longer certain the word genius is sufficient to describe him.\"","No one refuted those words.","The first time Michael Norman had been revealed to these people was months ago, during an incident gone wrong in Hell that ultimately exposed a carefully orchestrated scheme by the Demonic Faction.","If their plan had succeeded, such a blow would have shaken the Federation's foundation for a long time. Fortunately, the outcome had been completely overturned.","The Demonic Faction's plans had collapsed before they could be realized.","The Federation emerged from what should have been one of its greatest disasters with losses that were almost negligible.","The individual responsible for that miraculous outcome was the young man whose image now floated above the conference table.","Yet despite the immense contribution he had made, the Federation had failed to handle the aftermath properly.","Distrust, political interests, and unnecessary scrutiny had overshadowed the gratitude he should have received, leaving a stain on what should have been a mutually beneficial relationship.","A burly middle-aged man sitting near the end of the table suddenly let out a cold snort.","\"I knew this brat would become a problem one day.\"","Several people frowned, but he continued regardless.","\"We should have forcefully brought him under the Federation's control back then. If we had done that, we wouldn't be sitting here discussing this situation.\"","Silence followed his words for a brief moment. Then an elegant woman seated opposite him shook her head.","\"And it is precisely because of that attitude that our current situation is so delicate.\"","She looked directly at him.","\"If our relationship with Michael Norman had remained favorable, this meeting wouldn't even be necessary. We could have simply invited him here, explained the situation, and asked about the Universal Cornerstone. Considering everything, he is a child of Aurora like us and has loved ones here. I doubt he would have refused.\"","Her voice remained calm. The burly man's expression darkened. Before he could respond, another elderly man slowly spoke.","\"Why should we concern ourselves with the thoughts of a mere brat?\"","His gaze swept across everyone present.","\"When the interests of the entire realm are involved, personal feelings become insignificant.\" He looked toward the Chairman.","\"My suggestion is simple. Issue a mandatory summons. Order Michael Norman to appear before this council immediately. He will explain everything he knows about the Universal Cornerstone. As a citizen of Aurora, he has that obligation.\"","Several people frowned. The elegant woman looked visibly displeased. Before she could respond, another voice rang out.","\"Oh?\"","The speaker was a white-haired old man who had remained silent until now. He looked toward the elderly man with an amused smile.","\"So why weren't you this bold when Arven was here months ago?\"","The conference room instantly fell silent.","The old man's smile widened slightly.","\"If I remember correctly, when Michael returned from Hell, Arven personally came to see you. We all know how that ended.\" He leaned back in his chair. \"So, did you dare walk over and snatch that youth from under Arven's nose?\"","The elderly man's expression immediately stiffened. He remained silent.","The white-haired old man chuckled.","\"I thought not.\"","Everyone present understood exactly what he meant. Arven was not merely another Rank Four expert. He was one of Aurora's most powerful combatants.","More importantly, that obviously sick-in-the head man had openly demonstrated his intention to protect Michael. Trying to forcefully take Michael away in front of Arven at that time would have been no different from openly challenging him.","No one in that room had been willing to take that step. Those who weren't afraid of Arven personally were concerned about the more powerful figures behind him, and had no desire to invite that trouble.","The white-haired old man slowly shook his head.","\"Though I don't agree with your forceful tone, I do believe we should indeed summon the boy for a meeting and have him explain the situation. You should all know that several realms are currently on their way here, and we would like to have some answers ready since some of them are our allies.\"","Upon hearing those words, many of the people present nodded.","As for whether their agreement aligned with the old man's intended meaning, only they themselves knew."]},{"number":1139,"title":"Chapter 1139: Visit","paragraphs":["Though Michael had expected visitors to arrive sooner or later, he hadn't expected the first ones to appear barely two hours after his return to Aurora.","Fortunately, he had long since prepared for such a possibility.","Immediately after settling down, Michael had done a little persuasion work with his family and succeeded, with Jester taking the lead.","At this very moment, Aunt Mia, Lily, and Jester were no longer inside the apartment. Michael had quietly sent all three into the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion.","After everything he had experienced over the past year, Michael had learned one lesson better than most.","Never underestimate a supernatural. Confidence and carelessness were two entirely different things.","Before any potential conflict could arise, he had already ensured that the two people he cared about most in this world were somewhere no ordinary means could reach.","As for himself, he wasn't particularly worried. Michael had absolute confidence in his own ability to survive.","As long as the one pursuing him wasn't a Demigod, he believed himself to be within a relatively safe range.","Even if a Demigod truly decided to make a move, they would first have to catch him.","A faint smile appeared on Michael's face. Over the past several months, he had quietly left spatial portals throughout Aurora. Combined with Wisdom's spatial abilities, his escape methods had long since reached an astonishing level.","If Michael truly decided to disappear, even the entire Federation would likely have to mobilize all of its forces just to begin searching for him.","Whether they could actually find him was another matter entirely.","Inside the apartment, Michael calmly poured himself a cup of tea before taking a slow sip. His expression remained relaxed.","He wasn't afraid of the Federation. Nor did he intend to become their enemy. At least, not unless they forced him into that position.","Compared to worrying, he was more curious about who would arrive first. The Federation. The Academy. Or perhaps someone from beyond Aurora.","Just then, a gentle ripple spread through the apartment's defensive formation. This was something he and Jester had created months ago for security reasons, given the watchful eyes outside.","Beyond its defensive features, the formation also had the ability to create illusions and launch attacks, though those functions were relatively weak. Its greatest purpose was to act as a radar for supernaturals in the vicinity.","Michael slowly opened his eyes.","\"They're here.\"","His spiritual sense quietly spread outward. Outside the apartment building, four figures had appeared seemingly out of nowhere. To his surprise, he could immediately recognize all four.","Turning to look at an undead beside him in its humanoid form, Michael gave a quiet order.","\"Go open the door for our guests.\"","Outside the apartment, Director Lin turned her head toward the elderly man standing beside her and smiled.","\"So the Federation really came.\"","The old man wore a perfectly tailored black suit. Despite appearing no different from an ordinary elderly gentleman, the faint pressure surrounding him revealed he was anything but ordinary.","Standing beside him, Teacher Brian smiled politely.","\"Director.\"","Director Lin returned the greeting with a nod before her eyes shifted toward the old man. Teacher Brian spoke first.","\"Allow me to introduce him. This is General Caelum.\"","Director Lin smiled.","\"So it's General Caelum.\" She then gestured toward the woman standing quietly beside her. \"And this is Instructor Yara.\"","The beautiful woman gave a slight nod. General Caelum acknowledged her with the same courtesy before falling silent once more.","Director Lin suddenly laughed.","\"I have to admit, General, I'm a little surprised.\" Her tone carried a hint of teasing.","\"Shouldn't the Federation be drowning in work right now? The whole universe is practically knocking on Aurora's door.\" She tilted her head. \"So what brings the Federation all the way here?\"","General Caelum's expression remained unchanged.","\"The affairs of the Federation... have no relation to outsiders.\"","Director Lin blinked. Then she placed a hand over her chest with an exaggerated look of grievance.","\"Outsider?\" She smiled helplessly. \"General Caelum, your words really hurt. I was born in Aurora. I grew up in Aurora.\" She sighed dramatically. \"And yet you call me an outsider. I think you've broken my heart.\"","General Caelum merely looked at her. His expression did not change in the slightest. He simply ignored the complaint as though he hadn't heard a single word.","Seeing that she had failed to provoke even the slightest reaction, Director Lin clicked her tongue in disappointment.","\"You Federation folks are boring as ever.\"","Neither continued the topic. Standing behind the two Rank Four supernaturals, neither Brian nor Instructor Yara uttered a single word. They were already accustomed to scenes like this.","The Awakener Academies and the Federation had maintained a complicated relationship for centuries.","Although both ultimately served Aurora, their philosophies differed greatly.","The Federation valued centralized authority and stability.","The Academy valued freedom and nurturing exceptional individuals.","Because of that, their senior figures rarely missed an opportunity to exchange subtle barbs whenever they met.","Fortunately, this much was practically routine. No one genuinely expected the other side to become angry over a few sarcastic remarks.","Just then, the apartment door slowly opened. A figure stepped out.","The figure standing in the doorway possessed striking emerald-green eyes. Neither Teacher Brian nor General Caelum appeared surprised by that detail.","Even Director Lin merely glanced before looking away. By now, the information surrounding Michael Norman had already spread through Aurora's highest circles.","Any major organization with even a moderately competent intelligence network had discovered one recurring trait among Michael and his undead.","Green eyes.","Whenever an apparently human individual possessed those distinctive emerald irises while remaining closely associated with Michael, there was an overwhelming probability they were one of his undead. That much was no longer considered a secret.","Yet only a few meters away from the figure, the three couldn't help but feel a trace of genuine amazement. If they hadn't deliberately examined him with their spiritual senses, nothing about him suggested he was undead.","He seemed to even carry the warmth of a living person, though with a somewhat cold demeanor.","He looked alive. Completely alive.","Teacher Brian's eyes flickered slightly. He had seen intelligent undead before. He had even seen undead capable of disguising themselves as humans. But none had reached this level. It wasn't simply a disguise.","It was perfection. It resembled less a reanimated corpse and more one of those undying races like vampires, who could reproduce and lived with the warmth of life.","However, the undead itself wasn't the only matter occupying their thoughts. The image of Michael's two family members surfaced in all three of their minds.","Both possessed the same emerald-green eyes, and both had undergone obvious changes in appearance over the past several months.","Combined with everything they had learned about Michael's undead, the similarities became increasingly difficult to ignore.","Of course, no one present believed Aunt Mia and Lily had become undead. Their life force had always been genuine. They were unquestionably alive. But the resemblance was enough to raise questions.","Questions Michael himself had already anticipated. He knew perfectly well that this wasn't something he could hide forever. Nor had he truly intended to, since he already knew what others would most likely attribute it to the moment they noticed.","And he was right. Many people thought the changes in the two were the result of biological engineering. After all, biological engineering had always been one of the many branches explored by necromancers.","From enhancing physiques to repairing damaged organs to improving bloodlines, countless necromancers had studied and practiced similar techniques.","Would some people consider it disturbing? Certainly. Would others find it unacceptable that he had altered the bodies of his own family? Probably. But Michael simply didn't care.","Their opinions held no value to him. The only people whose thoughts mattered regarding that decision were Aunt Mia and Lily themselves. As for everyone else, they were outsiders.","However, it wasn't only the undead's emerald-green eyes that drew the attention of the four visitors. It was the aura surrounding him.","The undead was dressed in simple casual clothing. A black shirt. Dark trousers. Nothing about his attire was particularly remarkable. Yet his physique certainly was. He stood well over two meters tall with broad shoulders and a powerfully built frame that seemed carved from stone.","His skin possessed a healthy bronze tan. His facial features were sharp. His jawline was perfectly defined. Combined with his emerald-green eyes and calm expression, he looked like a man in his late twenties or perhaps early thirties.","A mature, handsome man.","Instructor Yara's beautiful eyes couldn't help but brighten slightly. Even Director Lin found herself taking another glance. Teacher Brian and General Caelum exchanged a subtle look.","For a brief moment, the same thought surfaced in all four of their minds.","Did Michael seriously have nothing better to do than make his combat undead this handsome?","None of them voiced the thought.","Their attention quickly shifted elsewhere. To the undead's aura. The moment their spiritual senses carefully brushed against it, the expressions of all four changed almost imperceptibly."]},{"number":1140,"title":"Chapter 1140: Intimidation [1]","paragraphs":["Danger.","An unmistakable sense of danger.","It resembled a dormant volcano. Quiet. Motionless. Yet capable of erupting at any moment.","General Caelum's eyes narrowed almost imperceptibly. Teacher Brian's breathing slowed. Even Director Lin's smile faded slightly.","Without exchanging a single word, the four reached almost the same conclusion.","This being was powerful.","Teacher Brian felt his heart grow increasingly heavy. Michael himself had already become one of Aurora's greatest geniuses.","According to their new intelligence, the world all awakeners had been forced to enter was divided into layers according to their ranks.","Officially, Michael was still a Rank Three awakener, but not only had he not remained in the Third Layer, he had entered the Fourth and ranked within the top two hundred among the thousands of awakeners gathered from across the universe.","None of them knew precisely what that rank signified, but to be stronger than dozens of peak Rank Four individuals meant Michael was far more dangerous than initially thought.","Wasn't he supposed to be a one-year-old supernatural? What was this demonic level of growth?","General Caelum remained expressionless. However, his heart couldn't help but grow heavier with every passing second.","When he had first received the order to personally visit Michael Norman on behalf of the Federation, he had refused. It wasn't because he had been afraid of Michael at the time. It was because the entire matter smelled like trouble. Nothing but trouble.","To begin with, his relationship with Michael could hardly be described as friendly. The misunderstanding surrounding the Hell operation had already left an unpleasant impression between them.","More importantly, he wanted absolutely nothing to do with the Awakener Academy Michael was enrolled in. Over the past year, it had become increasingly obvious that the Academy had every intention of protecting Michael. Especially Arven.","Just recalling that man's face made Caelum's temples ache.","Months ago, the two of them had fought inside Hell. To outsiders, it might have appeared evenly matched. Only Caelum himself knew the truth. He had never been Arven's equal. Hell had heavily suppressed the strength of higher-ranked supernaturals.","The stronger one was, the greater the suppression became. That was the only reason he had been capable of exchanging blows with Arven in the first place.","Even under such overwhelming restrictions, Arven had fought with his usual carefree smile. He even looked distracted for most of the battle. Yet Caelum had failed to gain even the slightest advantage.","If that battle had taken place inside Aurora, without Hell's suppression, Caelum didn't believe he could have lasted very long.","That man was publicly acknowledged as the strongest Rank Four combatant within the Awakener Academy, and some argued it was the same across Aurora as a whole. Whether that claim was entirely accurate or not, Caelum had absolutely no desire to verify it personally.","Which was precisely why, when the Federation decided to send someone to negotiate with Michael, he had wanted no part of it.","Unfortunately, his superior had used the argument that he had interacted with Michael Norman before and had played a role in ensuring he survived the Hell incident.","Regardless of the misunderstandings that followed, an existing connection was already there, making him one of the most suitable candidates.","Suitable?","Caelum had nearly laughed when he heard that. Suitable for what? Walking straight into the center of a political storm?","Yet orders were orders. As a General of the Federation, he could refuse once. Perhaps twice. But eventually, he still had to obey.","However, when the intelligence reports from the Origin Battlefield arrived, he regretted not trying harder to reject the order.","Each page of the report made less sense than the previous one. Officially, Michael Norman was still only a Rank Three awakener. Yet he hadn't remained in the Third Layer. He had entered the Fourth. Not only that, among the countless Rank Four awakeners gathered from innumerable realms, Michael had ranked within the top two hundred.","At first, Caelum thought there had been a mistake. To his understanding, the Fourth Layer wasn't populated by ordinary Rank Fours. Many of the strongest Rank Four awakeners in the universe had entered as well.","Veterans who had spent centuries accumulating experience. Yet Michael Norman's demonstrated combat ability was estimated to be comparable to the top ten percent of Rank Four awakeners across the known universe.","Caelum had still been managing his composure until he reached Arven's estimated standing.","Top one percent.","\"...\"","For the first time in many years, General Caelum genuinely questioned whether the Federation was intentionally trying to get him killed.","What do you mean Michael is already at that level? What do you mean Arven is even stronger?","He had almost marched straight back into his superior's office.","Sending him to negotiate with two individuals who already had reasons to dislike him, both of whom apparently stood among the most terrifying combatants in the universe, was that truly diplomacy?","Or had the Federation simply found an exceptionally polite method of arranging his funeral?","Before arriving at Michael's location, Caelum had clung to his doubts. But after seeing the enormous figure standing in the doorway, all of those thoughts vanished entirely.","Why did this undead feel as though it could contend with one of the weaker members of the Federation's Thirteen Pillars?","The thought itself sounded ridiculous. Yet the more he observed the undead, the harder it became to dismiss.","The Thirteen Pillars of the Federation were publicly recognized as the highest representatives of Aurora's Federation. They consisted of one Chairman and twelve Elders.","Across Aurora, to the moderately knowledgeable, they were often referred to as the leaders of the realm. In reality, that description wasn't entirely accurate.","Representative would have been a more fitting title.","Although the Thirteen Pillars undoubtedly stood among Aurora's strongest experts, they were far from being the only ones.","Though Aurora had only existed as a supernatural realm for four hundred years, the foundation it had managed to carve out in that time was simply extraordinary."]},{"number":1141,"title":"Chapter 1141: Intimidation [2]","paragraphs":["The various Awakener Academies alone possessed terrifying foundations. Every major academy had at least one peak Rank Four expert overseeing it, and the strongest academies possessed Demigods.","Some even had multiple, like Verdant's Edge Academy, the institution Michael attended.","Within the Federation itself, setting aside the Chairman who stood above everyone else, among the remaining twelve Pillars only four had truly crossed the boundary into the Demigod Realm.","The other eight were all peak Rank Four experts who stood only a single step away from that threshold.","Of course, this did not mean the Federation possessed only five Demigods. Far from it.","The Federation's military, hidden departments, and countless affiliated organizations still contained numerous Demigods who did not occupy seats among the Thirteen Pillars.","Likewise, the academies, the great clans, and independent factions all possessed terrifying experts of their own.","Thanks to these forces, no single power could truly claim absolute authority over the entire realm. Instead, the Federation acted as Aurora's representative to the outside world, but never its sole ruler.","The bronze-skinned undead gave the four visitors a slight nod.","\"My master is waiting.\"","Without asking whether they wished to enter, he simply turned around and walked deeper into the apartment. The four visitors exchanged brief glances before following behind him.","The apartment itself appeared surprisingly ordinary. The furnishings were simple. Everything was clean and neatly arranged.","Nothing about it reflected the status of the man who had become the center of the universe's attention.","Yet the moment they stepped into the living room, all four instinctively stopped.","Their hearts sank.","Though the Michael they were looking for was currently nowhere to be seen, the room was far from empty.","In one corner stood a towering muscular man who appeared to be in his mid-twenties.","His body seemed sculpted from steel, every muscle perfectly defined beneath a simple dark shirt. His complexion carried a faint grayish tint that was almost imperceptible unless one looked carefully.","Beside him stood a woman who possessed similar facial features, suggesting they shared some connection. Although noticeably shorter than the giant beside her, she still stood far above the height of an ordinary human.","Her physique was athletic and powerful. Compared to normal people, she was still a giant.","Neither spoke. They merely observed the newcomers with calm, almost cold emerald-green eyes.","In another corner, two more figures occupied a sofa. One was another enormous man, just as massive as the undead who had led them into the apartment, with a body built like a fortress.","Every inch of his physique radiated overwhelming physical strength, his broad shoulders and thick muscles making him appear capable of crushing steel with his bare hands.","Sitting beside him was another man.","Unlike the giant, he possessed a far more refined appearance. He looked completely human. He was tall, exceptionally handsome, with long black hair neatly resting behind his shoulders.","A pair of elegant glasses sat upon his face, and a thick book rested calmly in his hands as though the arrival of four visitors had done nothing to interrupt his reading. Without raising his head, he calmly turned another page.","The room remained silent.","Yet the expressions of the four visitors had subtly changed.","Green eyes. Every single one possessed emerald-green eyes. Which meant every single one was almost certainly one of Michael Norman's undead.","But that wasn't what caused their hearts to sink. It was the pressure. Though subtle and almost imperceptible, it was unmistakable at the level of Rank Four. All four radiated the aura of Rank Four existences.","Cold sweat slowly formed on Brian's forehead. Instructor Yara's breathing unconsciously became slower as she instinctively regulated her own aura to withstand the oppressive atmosphere.","All four were deep in thought at the sight laid before them.","Including the undead who had opened the door, that made five Rank Four presences in total. And one had to remember that Michael had only entered the supernatural world slightly over a year ago.","Looking at the silent figures occupying the room, an unsettling realization surfaced in everyone's mind.","Exactly how many Rank Four undead did Michael Norman actually possess?","Just as the four remained lost in their thoughts, the sound of approaching footsteps echoed from deeper within the apartment.","Tap. Tap. Tap.","A moment later, a familiar young man entered the living room.","It was Michael.","Like most of his undead, he wore simple casual clothes. In one hand, he carried a tray. Resting upon it were four cups and several chilled drinks.","Seeing everyone already gathered, Michael smiled apologetically.","\"Sorry for the delay. My guests arrived sooner than I expected.\"","He walked over to the center table before carefully placing the tray down. Only then did he look toward the four visitors.","\"Welcome.\"","His tone was calm. Neither overly enthusiastic nor distant. Simply polite.","After placing the cups onto the table, Michael turned his head toward two of the undead seated nearby.","\"Spartan. Ghost.\"","\"You're occupying the seats meant for our guests.\"","The handsome man with the glasses quietly closed the book in his hand. Without the slightest complaint, he rose to his feet. Beside him, the enormous muscular undead also stood up in silence. The two calmly stepped aside.","Michael then looked back toward the visitors.","\"Please. Have a seat.\"","Only then did the four slowly move. Director Lin and Instructor Yara chose the now vacated sofa, while General Caelum and Teacher Brian sat opposite them.","The room soon settled into silence once again.","Michael himself remained standing beside the center table. His calm gaze slowly swept across each of the four visitors before finally coming to rest on General Caelum.","For a brief moment, no one spoke.","The atmosphere was strangely quiet. Teacher Brian unconsciously adjusted his sitting posture. Instructor Yara quietly folded her hands on her lap.","Even Director Lin, who usually maintained her carefree smile regardless of the situation, found herself becoming noticeably more composed.","As for General Caelum, he looked at the young man standing before him while doing his best to settle the emotions stirring beneath the surface."]},{"number":1142,"title":"Chapter 1142: Attack?","paragraphs":["Though Michael's face remained completely expressionless, the scene before him left him inwardly satisfied.","For someone in his current position, to speak to others reasonably, power had to be recognized.","Michael had long understood a simple truth. A man carrying treasures coveted by others was guilty by default. Whether he had committed any crime was irrelevant. The moment others realized what he possessed or felt he possessed something incredible, someone would inevitably begin calculating how to obtain it.","Because of that, it didn't matter which organization had come knocking on his door today. As long as they approached him as a force rather than as individuals, Michael would instinctively regard them as potential enemies.","The Awakener Academy was no exception. Of course, his attitude toward the Academy wasn't nearly as guarded. He genuinely appreciated everything they had done for him over the past year. However, gratitude and trust were two entirely different things. No matter how well they had treated him, as long as they continued to view him as a junior, the balance between them would always remain unequal.","Even if their intentions were sincere and every suggestion they made was for his benefit, their position would naturally influence the way they dealt with him.","Seniors advised. Juniors listened. Seniors instructed. Juniors complied.","That relationship had existed for countless generations. There was nothing inherently wrong with it. But it was not suitable for him.","As long as they subconsciously regarded him as their student or their junior, whatever negotiations took place today would never truly place him in an advantageous position.","As for the Federation, the situation was even simpler. There wasn't much that needed to be considered.","Michael didn't regard the Federation as an enemy. At least, not yet.","Likewise, he had no intention of becoming Aurora's enemy. It was the world where Aunt Mia and Lily still lived. He had every reason to protect it if circumstances demanded.","Even so, that didn't mean he trusted the Federation. If anything, among every major organization in Aurora, together with the demonic supernaturals, they were the group he remained most guarded against.","Unlike the Academy, from Michael's perspective, the Federation would always prioritize Aurora's interests over his own. And if one day those two interests came into conflict, he had little doubt which side they would choose.","That was precisely why, from the very beginning, he had never intended to negotiate from a position of weakness. Today's meeting wasn't merely a conversation. It was a declaration to them and the others that would come after.","Though he had yet to fully utilize the universal cornerstone, Michael knew this was something that he couldn't keep alone to himself unless he was willing to hide in the land of origin with his family for a long period of time. As much as he didn't want any business to do with the federation, he had to admit that standing against the many forces in the universe, he needed their backing.","Michael allowed the silence to linger for another few seconds. Only then did his gaze shift toward the drinks resting neatly on the center table.","\"Would anyone like something to drink?\"","The four visitors almost instinctively shook their heads.","\"No.\"","\"There's no need.\"","\"We're fine.\"","Not a single person reached for the cups.","Michael wasn't surprised. He could easily tell from the atmosphere, and the five Rank Four undead silently standing around the room made it rather difficult for anyone to leisurely enjoy a drink.","Seeing their reactions, Michael didn't insist. He simply nodded before taking his own seat. His movements remained calm and unhurried.","Once seated, his gaze calmly swept across the four visitors.","\"So...\"","\"What brings everyone here today?\"","The room became silent once more.","Teacher Brian's eyelids twitched. Instructor Yara's lips almost parted before she stopped herself. Even Director Lin couldn't help narrowing her eyes slightly.","So shameless!","All four reached almost the same conclusion. After deliberately displaying enough strength to leave them thoroughly intimidated and carefully establishing exactly who held the initiative in this room, he now asked for the purpose of their visit as though he knew nothing.","It was such an obvious attempt to seize control of the conversation that none of them failed to notice it.","Unfortunately, no one pointed it out thanks to the delicate atmosphere.","Another few moments passed before General Caelum finally broke the silence.","\"I believe...\" He paused briefly. \"...it would be better if we got straight to the point.\"","His voice was deep and steady, carrying the natural authority expected of one of the Federation's Generals. Under ordinary circumstances, such a bearing alone would have been enough to recover a bit of control over the conversation.","Unfortunately, careful observation revealed an almost imperceptible slight stiffness and the faintest trace of hesitation hidden beneath his composed exterior. His tone, though only by the smallest margin, carried a subtle tremor, but it couldn't escape Michael.","Meeting Michael's calm gaze, Caelum continued.","\"On behalf of the Federation...\"","\"I've come to discuss matters concerning you and...\"","He never managed to finish the sentence.","BOOM!!","The entire apartment violently shook. The walls trembled. The windows rattled as though struck by an invisible tidal wave.","Everyone's expression changed. General Caelum's eyes snapped toward the ceiling, and Director Lin immediately rose to her feet.","At the same instant, the five undead standing throughout the living room moved as well, with Ghost silently appearing beside Michael.","An indescribably heavy pressure descended from above. It was as though the sky itself had collapsed.","The surrounding space groaned under the weight of that terrifying aura. The apartment building trembled continuously. Outside, cracks rapidly spread across the roads. Ordinary people throughout the district suddenly felt an overwhelming urge to kneel. Many collapsed to the ground without understanding why.","Inside the apartment, even General Caelum's expression became incomparably solemn.","A Demigod.","There was no doubt. Only a Demigod could release such overwhelming pressure.","Before anyone could react further, a woman's voice echoed throughout the entire city. It was cold, majestic, and filled with unconcealed killing intent.","\"Michael Norman...\"","The voice reverberated through the heavens themselves. Every being within hundreds of kilometers heard it clearly.","\"Time...\"","\"And time again...\"","\"You have ruined the plans of my people.\"","Each word seemed to carry an invisible weight, causing the surrounding air to vibrate. The killing intent became increasingly suffocating.","\"It is time you paid the price.\"","The final words had barely fallen when the clouds above abruptly split apart.","An enormous crimson magic formation slowly unfolded across the sky. Its size covered several kilometers. Scarlet runes ignited one after another.","The horrifying pressure instantly multiplied.","General Caelum's pupils constricted. Director Lin's usually carefree expression completely vanished.","Only Michael remained seated, though the anger on his face could be seen from miles away.","\"You demonic supernaturals!\" he spat out."]},{"number":1143,"title":"Chapter 1143: All Out [1]","paragraphs":["It wasn't that Michael had failed to consider the possibility of an attack. If he had, Aunt Mia and Lily would still have been inside the apartment.","The moment he returned to Aurora, Michael had already begun preparing for the worst.","Michael had expected trouble. What he had not expected was for that trouble to arrive so soon.","Barely two hours had passed since he returned from the Origin Battlefield.","Two hours.","Every awakener throughout the universe had only recently been expelled from that mysterious place.","Even if the news concerning the Universal Cornerstone had already spread beyond control, Michael had assumed that the major forces of other realms would require at least some time to gather information, prepare their people, and travel toward Aurora. Perhaps a few days. At worst, several hours. He certainly hadn't expected someone to launch an attack today.","More importantly, he had never expected the first attacker to come from Aurora's demonic supernaturals. That possibility had barely entered his calculations.","Director Lin and General Caelum were equally confused.","Several months ago, Aurora had launched a large-scale campaign against the demonic supernatural factions.","The conflict had spread across several regions and hidden realms. Countless demonic supernaturals had died. Numerous strongholds had been destroyed.","Even several of their most powerful figures had either been killed or severely injured.","Although the Federation and academies had failed to completely eliminate them, everyone had agreed that the demonic factions had suffered enough damage to remain hidden for several years. They should have been licking their wounds.","Yet one of them had now appeared openly above a major city. Not merely a common member, but a Demigod.","The crimson formation above the city continued expanding.","Scarlet light flowed between the runes like blood through veins, gradually forming a massive circular structure that covered the clouds.","The pressure descending from it became heavier by the second.","Buildings throughout the district groaned. Glass shattered. Streetlights bent under an invisible force.","The apartment's defensive formation activated automatically. Thin layers of translucent light spread across the walls and ceiling, but they flickered violently almost as soon as they appeared.","Michael's anger deepened.","His formation had never been intended to resist a Demigod. Its greatest purpose was detection. Under the direct pressure of the figure above, its defensive functions had long approached their limit.","However, Michael was not afraid.","He had failed to anticipate that an attack would come so soon, but that did not mean he had failed to prepare for one.","Before his visitors had even arrived, Michael had already begun arranging several contingencies throughout the city.","The moment the Demigod revealed herself above Aurora, a silent command spread through the spiritual connection binding him to his undead.","Across different districts, inside restaurants, near shopping centers, on rooftops, beside roads, within parks and public squares, figures who had previously appeared completely ordinary suddenly stopped whatever they were doing.","There were nearly a thousand of them. Men. Women. Young. Old. Tall. Short. Some wore formal clothing. Others wore casual shirts, jackets, or simple work uniforms.","To the ordinary people around them, they had seemed no different from any other residents of the city.","Until all of them raised their heads at the same time.","Emerald-green eyes reflected the crimson formation covering the heavens.","Then every single one raised a hand. Magic power erupted.","BOOM!","The city shook once again. Hundreds of different attacks were launched into the sky. Some were straightforward. Others twisted through the air, changing direction as they locked onto the presence above.","A thousand Rank Four auras erupted almost simultaneously.","The sky brightened. For a brief moment, the crimson formation was completely drowned beneath a sea of colors.","Every supernatural watching from within the city froze.","General Caelum stared through the shaking ceiling. Not far from him, Director Lin's eyes widened as well while Teacher Brian and Instructor Yara were left just as speechless.","Even the Demigod above seemed to pause.","No one had expected an attack to come from below. Certainly not one of this scale. One moment, the streets had appeared ordinary. The next, nearly a thousand powerful existences had revealed themselves throughout the city.","The combined pressure of their attacks tore apart the lingering clouds. The crimson formation trembled violently as countless attacks slammed into it.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Explosions spread across the heavens. Scarlet runes shattered. Several sections of the formation dimmed under the bombardment. The woman's oppressive aura flickered for the first time.","This was Michael's preparation.","He had not specifically prepared to fight a Demigod. Such an opponent had never been part of his immediate expectations.","What he had prepared for was the possibility of several powerful Rank Four experts arriving together.","If outsiders entered Aurora intending to capture him, threaten his family, or seize the Universal Cornerstone, Michael had no intention of allowing them to surround him first.","Instead, he would surround them. Then beat them into submission before they had the opportunity to act.","The undead scattered throughout the city had been concealed before the Federation representatives arrived.","Michael's original plan had been simple.","Observe every powerful visitor who approached and determine their intentions.","If they came peacefully, there would be no conflict. If they came with hostility, the entire city would become a battlefield prepared in his favor.","The only flaw was that the enemy who appeared had surpassed the level he had prepared for.","Even so, a thousand Rank Four undead were not insignificant. Even a Demigod could not completely ignore their combined assault.","Michael slowly rose from his seat. His expression remained cold, but there was no fear in his eyes.","The realization he had gained within the Origin Battlefield had changed him. His caution had not disappeared. He would never become completely reckless.","He still had too much to care about and too much to hide. But he was no longer willing to conceal every card he possessed merely because others might feel threatened by it or target him."]},{"number":1144,"title":"Chapter 1144: All Out [2]","paragraphs":["Michael controlled close to two thousand Rank Four undead. He also possessed another two thousand Rank Three undead that could still be used for reconnaissance, support, and sacrifice.","That was no longer the strength of a talented individual. It was an army. A force powerful enough to conquer many realms within the universe.","Some realms might not possess a thousand Rank Four existences even after exhausting every foundation they had accumulated over centuries. Michael alone possessed nearly twice that number.","With such strength, there was no reason for him to remain timid, no reason to pretend he was weaker than he truly was, and no reason to continue relying solely on others for protection.","He now possessed enough power to protect himself. More importantly, he possessed enough power to protect his family. That was what mattered most.","The only reason Michael still cared about maintaining a relationship with Aurora's Federation and its forces was because of the ties connecting him to this world.","Aunt Mia had lived here her entire life. Lily had friends, memories, and a future here. Their lives were rooted in Aurora. Michael could not simply abandon everything without considering what they wanted.","If he had been alone, with no one whose happiness he needed to consider, he would not have bothered negotiating with anyone. He could have entered the Origin Battlefield, established his territory, and allowed every force in Aurora to argue among themselves.","The Universal Cornerstone was his. His strength was his. His future belonged to him.","But Michael was not alone. That fact was both a weakness and the greatest reason behind his determination.","Another series of explosions shook the heavens. The crimson formation cracked further. Through the damaged sections, a figure finally became visible.","A woman stood high above the city, wrapped in flowing crimson robes. Her face was beautiful, but twisted by fury.","A barrier of condensed blood surrounded her body. Hundreds of attacks continued slamming into it. Each impact sent ripples across its surface.","The demigod earlier confidence had vanished. The killing intent remained, but now it was mixed with unmistakable astonishment.","Below, the nearly one thousand undead prepared another round of attacks. Their emerald-green eyes shone throughout the city like countless stars.","The sight caused the expressions of everyone inside the apartment to become strange.","General Caelum had believed the five Rank Four undead inside the room were already shocking. Now he understood how laughably incomplete that assumption had been.","Those five were not Michael Norman's army. They were merely the guards he had chosen to keep inside his home.","The first exchange had already revealed that the woman had not come to capture Michael. She had come to kill him.","That realization sent a chill through Michael's heart.","Not only because he feared for himself.","Even if Aunt Mia and Lily were already safe within the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion, and even if he possessed several methods of escaping before an attack landed, what frightened and angered him more was the number of people who would have died if he had failed to respond in time.","This was not an isolated location. They were in the middle of a populated city.","Millions of ordinary people lived within it. Countless families. Children. Elderly people. If that attack had fully descended, the consequences would have been unimaginable.","At least half of the city would have vanished. Depending on the true strength of the formation above, the destruction might have spread much farther.","Michael valued his own life above the lives of strangers. He valued Aunt Mia and Lily's lives even more. He also regarded his undead as his people, regardless of the fact that most of them were technically dead.","But that did not mean the lives of everyone else were worthless to him. He was not some emotionless monster. As long as his life and the lives of his family were not at immediate risk, he was not willing to stand by while millions were slaughtered.","The fear in Michael's heart rapidly transformed into fury.","This woman deserved to die.","For the first time since awakening, Michael felt a genuine ambition to step beyond the shell he had built around himself.","Until now, most of his decisions had been defensive.","Grow stronger.","Hide his most valuable abilities.","Protect his family.","Avoid unnecessary attention.","Escape when the danger became too great.","Those instincts had kept him alive. But there came a point where constant retreat only encouraged others to continue advancing.","If he fled today, what would happen tomorrow? Would he be forced to flee again the next time a powerful force appeared?","Michael refused to allow that impression to spread at the current stage he was in.","This woman had come intending to use his death as a message.","Michael decided he would use hers instead.","Her corpse would become a declaration. A warning to Aurora. A warning to the demonic factions. A warning to every foreign force already travelling toward this realm.","Michael Norman was no longer prey.","However, wanting her dead and being able to kill her were two completely different matters. Michael understood that better than anyone.","The combined attack of nearly a thousand Rank Four undead had damaged the formation and forced the woman to defend herself, but it had not caused her any meaningful injury.","Her blood barrier remained intact. Though the ripples spreading across its surface looked violent, the aura within it remained terrifyingly stable.","This was a genuine Demigod. One that stood within Aurora without suffering any form of external suppression.","The situation would have been completely different in Hell. Here, no such restriction existed. The woman possessed her complete strength.","Even a thousand Rank Four undead could not kill her through a simple bombardment. They might exhaust her, delay her, or force her to become cautious. But if Michael continued relying solely on them, the eventual result would be catastrophic.","Many of his undead would die. The city would become the battlefield. And the woman might still escape."]},{"number":1145,"title":"Chapter 1145: All Out [3]","paragraphs":["Michael had no intention of allowing that.","If he wanted to kill her, he could not depend entirely on his Rank Four forces. He needed something else.","Fortunately, the woman's actions had also exposed a weakness. She was in a hurry.","The instant she appeared, she had attempted to kill him. She did not waste time making demands or attempt to interrogate him about the Universal Cornerstone.","Michael knew she could not remain here for long.","The demonic factions might possess hidden strongholds and methods of concealing themselves from Aurora's powers, but they had never been free to act openly.","If Demigods belonging to the demonic factions could enter major cities whenever they wished, Aurora would have fallen long ago.","The fact that they remained concealed proved that Aurora's righteous powers still possessed enough strength to suppress them.","Michael estimated that he only needed to delay her. Five minutes. Perhaps ten at most. The Federation would not ignore this. Neither would the academies or any other strong forces capable of opposing this woman.","The problem was keeping her here until reinforcements arrived. A Demigod would undoubtedly possess an escape method. The moment she realized the attack had failed, she might leave.","Michael's gaze sharpened.","The blood-robed woman floated above the broken formation, staring down at the city with murderous eyes. Her barrier pulsed. The surrounding attacks were repelled simultaneously.","A crimson wave exploded outward. Hundreds of spells shattered before reaching her. Several of Michael's undead who had been flying upward to meet her were thrown backward by the resulting force, smashing through rooftops and walls.","Yet none retreated. The damaged undead rose almost immediately.","Numerous emerald-green eyes remained fixed upon the woman above.","It was at this moment that Michael revealed his trump card.","\"Law Skill...\"","\"...Echoed Bestowal.\"","The target of this skill was once again his Undead High Drake.","However, though this skill had proven itself formidable within the Origin Battlefield, it alone was far from capable of competing with a Demigod on equal footing.","But this wasn't the Origin Battlefield. This was Aurora. And thanks to a certain gift of Michael's, the effect of this skill was far stronger than anything he had demonstrated before.","[Gift]: Aurora's Child","[Description]: Ever since Aurora awakened, she has been searching for a partner to her will. Unfortunately, she has yet to find one. Still, Aurora has not given up. At certain points, she chooses individuals born within her realm as candidates to inherit her will.","[Effect]: Law effectiveness is increased by 200% within Aurora.","With this gift, the power the Undead High Drake would draw from the law skill would be far greater, and without any additional cost.","But since a Demigod was the opponent here, Michael, true to his cautious nature, went all out.","Without anyone noticing, an item appeared above Michael's left hand, hovering silently in the air.","Months ago, thanks to Jester infusing him with a skill that allowed Michael to link his soul with inanimate objects, Michael had gained the ability to use his talent on objects as well.","But aside from using it on his first spear, he hadn't linked his soul to another object since, even after using the Perfect Mastery skill ticket he had received as an advancement reward to strengthen the skill.","[Object Refinement Art {Perfect Mastery}]","Functions as both an anchor and a storage space. Infuse an item with your soul signature to bind it. This grants the ability to summon or dismiss it at will from the soul space, and allows a more comprehensive degree of control and compatibility with the item and its abilities.","Current Slot: 3/5","At Intermediate Mastery, this skill obtained from the cultivation world had only allowed for two item refinements.","At that time, Michael had used it on his now-evolved coffin of the forgotten and his now Epic Grade spear, which had not even been an Extraordinary Grade weapon back then.","Now at Perfect Mastery, Michael could refine three more items with his soul.","With such limited slots granting him the ability to evolve inanimate objects through his talent, Michael valued each one greatly.","Setting aside the two objects he had already refined in the past, one now at Legendary Grade and one at Epic Grade, Michael had also bonded his soul to a third item.","At the time he had bound his soul to it, it had only been a Three-Star Extraordinary item.","[Enhancer (Three-Star Extraordinary Grade)]","Once a One-Star Epic-Grade artifact that was partially destroyed and dropped in rank. Its effect, when activated, boosts the effectiveness of a law by at least 200%.","Duration lasts ten minutes, and with natural recovery, requires four months of cooldown.","After Michael's 'care' over the past few months, this item was considerably stronger.","[Enhancer (Three-Star Epic Grade)]","Not only did its effect duration extend to twenty minutes. Its effectiveness boost over one's law had risen to as high as 400%.","The only downside was that its cooldown had increased from four months to eight months.","Thanks to the evolution, its previous cooldown had reset entirely, making this item a usable trump card once again.","The form of the Epic Grade Enhancer was a silver orb covered in numerous mysterious runes that constantly shifted positions across its surface.","Thanks to its effect, the boost to Michael's law reached 400%.","Combined with the 200% from his gift, the total amplification reached 600%.","Even Michael himself did not know how strong his Undead High Drake would become under such conditions.","Fortunately, it was time to find out. And even better, there was an enemy present to test it on.","The moment Michael activated the skill alongside the Enhancer to empower his Undead High Drake, the bronze-skinned undead disappeared from the living room, catching the attention of the other four visitors.","But before anyone could say a word about it, or about the situation they currently found themselves in, an enormous pressure erupted throughout the city.","This time, it brought every single being to their knees, including Michael himself, who had initially been prepared."]},{"number":1146,"title":"Chapter 1146: Fake Dragon Might [1]","paragraphs":["The pressure that descended upon the city did not come from a single source. There were two.","The first felt familiar. It was from the female Demigod in the sky.","When it first arrived, the pressure had inspired awe, feeling ancient and majestic, like the arrival of a creature that naturally stood above lesser lifeforms.","This time, however, that same presence had become far more reckless and far more forceful.","There was no restraint behind it. It crashed down upon the city like an invisible ocean, forcing buildings to groan and countless beings to collapse beneath its weight.","As for the second pressure, it felt completely different.","There was no aggression behind it. It seemed to be nothing more than the natural aura released by the creature as it appeared. Yet somehow, it was just as powerful.","The two pressures overlapped. Together, they became something so oppressive that even Michael, who had mentally prepared himself, was forced down onto one knee.","General Caelum and Director Lin were in nearly the same situation, looking miserable under the sudden strain. Teacher Brian and Instructor Yara had already fallen to their knees, unable to resist.","Fortunately, Michael and the other two Rank Four experts soon caught their bearing and recovered.","But if even people like them were struggling, one could only imagine what was happening to the rest of the city.","If not for Michael's undead scattered across the streets resisting the pressure with all their strength, far more people would have died but even with all this, as the seconds ticked by, the crushing aura alone was taking lives, especially among the children.","A strained voice sounded beside Michael.","\"Is that... a dragon?\"","Michael didn't respond, his gaze fixed on the sky.","The question had come from General Caelum. His voice no longer carried its usual authority, filled instead with pure disbelief.","The ceiling of the apartment obstructed ordinary sight, but for existences at their level, such a barrier meant very little.","Their vision pierced through concrete and steel, and what they saw caused everyone to fall silent.","'Is that truly a dragon?' Even Michael couldn't help but think in shock.","Aurora had no known dragon population, so why was one here?","The sky above Brightgate City had disappeared. Something enormous had blocked the sun.","\"S-s-so h-h-huge!\" Instructor Yara exclaimed in shock.","Michael had seen giants before, including his own Undead High Drake, which normally stood around three hundred meters tall and could reach six hundred meters when empowered.","At the time, that size had seemed absurd. Yet the being now appearing above the city was far larger. Only its head had emerged through the distorted layers of space, yet that alone seemed large enough to cover the heavens.","The sunlight vanished. An enormous shadow spread across countless streets.","Dark scales covered the creature's face, each larger than a building, with thin lines of green light pulsing between them like veins of deathly fire.","Two colossal horns stretched backward into the distorted sky. Its nostrils released clouds of pale mist.","Then its eyes opened.","Two enormous emerald suns appeared, their gaze falling upon the city.","The sight filled the female demonic Demigod with immense shock and rising fear, though the dragon's killing intent quickly stirred her anger in return.","The gigantic creature looked down at her without releasing a roar.","The sheer natural pressure radiating from its existence forced cracks to appear across her blood barrier.","General Caelum stared upward in silence. Director Lin's sharp mind failed to process what she was witnessing.","The creature resembled a dragon, its majesty unmatched, yet standing beside the Demigod felt like looking at truth and illusion at the same time.","Unlike the confused supernaturals, Michael understood what was happening.","The creature above might look like a match for the Demigod in terms of rank, but it was truly just a Rank Four creature in the end.","Through Echoed Bestowal, he had copied the traits of Beginning and Lucky onto the Undead High Drake.","Combined with the six-hundred-percent boost to his law effectiveness from Aurora's Child and the Three-Star Epic Grade Enhancer, the skill had pushed far beyond the drake's original form.","Through sheer coincidence, choosing two traits aligned with draconic heritage had triggered a qualitative change, temporarily pulling the creature closer to the origin of its species.","It wasn't a permanent transformation into a true dragon, but for the next twenty minutes, those limitations didn't matter.","The enormous undead dragon lowered its head slightly, sending a violent storm sweeping across the city.","The blood-robed woman raised both hands as her barrier thickened, wrapping herself in layers of crimson armor formed from blood while six wings spread behind her.","Above the city, the undead dragon's jaws opened. A sphere of condensed green energy formed within its throat, expanding rapidly from ten meters to a hundred.","The surrounding space collapsed inward, swallowing every trace of light. The pressure released by the gathering attack caused the blood-robed woman's expression to change completely.","For the first time since arriving, fear appeared within her eyes.","At the same time, Michael's own expression changed. His pupils contracted.","Before activating Echoed Bestowal, Michael had already issued a command through his connection with his Undead High Drake to try and defeat the female Demigod, and if that proved impossible, to delay her with everything it had and most importantly force the battle away from the city.","That single instruction had been engraved into the undead before the transformation even began.","Yet something had definitely gone wrong now that he saw its actions.","Michael could still feel the connection. He could still issue commands. The Undead High Drake had not broken free from his control.","However, for some reason, there was resistance. It wasn't the undead resisting him. Rather, it was something instinctive.","Michael had experienced something vaguely similar in the Origin Battlefield when he had seized control of another Rank Four necromancer's undead.","At that time, the Bone Dragons and Bone Wyverns had instinctively resisted changing masters. However, compared to that resistance, this was entirely different."]},{"number":1147,"title":"Chapter 1147: Fake Dragon Might [2]","paragraphs":["Fortunately, the resistance wasn't enough to sever the connection. Michael still possessed control. But the attack was already close to being unleashed.","The instant Michael understood what was about to happen, he roared at the top of his lungs through the soul connection linking him to every summoned undead.","\"DEFEND THE CITY!\"","The command exploded across the city simultaneously.","Nearly one thousand Rank Four undead reacted without a moment's hesitation.","Earth-type undead tore entire sections of the ground upward, raising massive walls of compacted stone around residential districts.","Plant-type undead caused forests of enormous vines to erupt from beneath the streets, weaving themselves into dense barriers capable of absorbing searing heat.","Water-element undead summoned gigantic tidal barriers that surged upward like living walls.","Many other undead defended in their own way.","General Caelum's expression changed drastically at the sight bearing down on the city.","Without waiting for orders, he exploded into the sky. Director Lin followed immediately behind him.","Teacher Brian and Instructor Yara also moved, despite knowing their strength would barely register against what was coming.","Across Brightgate City, powerful auras awakened one after another.","Every supernatural who could still move instinctively rushed to cast whatever defensive measure they could manage, throwing up shields, barriers, and formations in a desperate scramble.","The sphere of energy within the dragon's throat reached its limit.","The gigantic head tilted directly toward the blood-robed Demigod.","Michael's heart skipped a beat.","\"No...\"","The dragon opened its jaws completely. A beam of condensed emerald destruction erupted.","The heavens split apart. Everything before the beam simply ceased to exist.","The attack was unimaginably fast.","The blood-robed Demigod's eyes widened. She immediately abandoned every thought of counterattacking.","All six wings folded before her body. Blood-like substance erupted from every pore as layer after layer of crimson barriers materialized. She even burned her own essence without hesitation.","At this stage, she could not care about the consequences. She only wanted to survive.","Unfortunately, the dragon's breath did not discriminate. It was simply too enormous.","Even though its primary target remained the Demigod, its sheer energy threatened to engulf Brightgate City.","The dragon's breath collided with the first defensive barrier of the female demigod.","The world exploded.","The emerald dragon breath pierced through the heavens with terrifying precision. It never deviated from its target.","From the moment it left the Undead High Drake's jaws until it reached the blood-robed Demigod, the beam remained locked onto her existence as though it possessed a will of its own.","Yet an attack of such magnitude could never be perfectly contained. The residual energy alone was enough to throw the entire sky into chaos.","The air ignited. Violent currents spread in every direction, heating the atmosphere to unimaginable temperatures, causing even the moisture in the air to vaporize beneath the overwhelming heat.","The surrounding space rippled violently, releasing invisible shockwaves that raced across Brightgate City.","BOOM!","The first wave reached the city. Buildings trembled. Thousands of windows shattered simultaneously.","Cars were overturned as powerful winds swept through the streets. Many ordinary people who had only just managed to stand were thrown back onto the ground once again.","The defenders immediately realized what they were facing.","\"Hold on!\"","General Caelum roared.","All supernaturals immediately strengthened their focus as they reinforced their defenses against the expanding shockwaves.","Barrier after barrier continued to appear over Brightgate City like overlapping transparent domes.","Earth walls rose around residential districts as enormous forests of vines intertwined to absorb the searing heat.","For perhaps the first time in decades, every supernatural within Brightgate City fought toward the same objective.","Protect the civilians.","But regardless of what was erected, many of the unleashed barriers could only tremble and crack.","Fortunately, together they endured.","Even then, they could not protect everyone.","Several weakened buildings collapsed after enduring repeated shockwaves that slipped through.","A few unfortunate people, already injured by the earlier pressure, failed to survive when debris buried them beneath the rubble.","Others suffered severe burns from the waves of superheated air sweeping through certain districts.","Compared to the catastrophe that should have occurred, the losses were incredibly small. But every life lost still weighed heavily upon Michael.","High above the city, the emerald dragon breath had long reached its destination.","The blood-robed Demigod screamed as every layer of crimson defense she had erected collapsed one after another beneath the concentrated attack.","Space behind her continuously fractured, creating sonic booms as the beam forced her backward across the heavens.","Seeing the city withstand the aftermath, Michael immediately issued another command through his soul connection.","The enormous undead dragon's emerald eyes shifted. It no longer gathered another dragon breath. Instead, it closed its jaws. Its colossal body blurred.","BOOM!","The heavens cracked beneath a single flap of its wings. An instant later, it appeared beside the blood-robed Demigod.","A claw larger than a mountain descended. The woman barely managed to raise both arms before the strike landed.","BOOM!","The impact shook the sky itself. She was sent hurtling thousands of meters through the air, crimson blood scattering behind her.","Before she could regain her balance, the undead dragon was already upon her again.","This time, it fought like the apex predator it had temporarily become. No more breath attacks. Only overwhelming physical force.","Each swing of its claws distorted the air around it. Each beat of its wings created hurricanes that scattered whatever could stand before it.","The female Demigod was forced into a desperate retreat. She no longer had even a moment to look toward Brightgate City.","Every ounce of her concentration was devoted to survival.","With every exchange, the battle moved farther from the city.","The immense collisions continued to fill the heavens with emerald and crimson light, but the destructive aftermath reaching Brightgate gradually weakened."]},{"number":1148,"title":"Chapter 1148: Fake Dragon Might [3]","paragraphs":["The moment the crushing pressure weighing down on the city finally lessened, countless people collapsed in relief. Many instinctively gasped for air. Others clutched their chests as though they had narrowly escaped drowning.","Children who had been crying moments earlier broke down completely, throwing themselves into the arms of their parents or the closest person they could find. Many simply sat or lay on the ground, their minds still unable to process what had just happened.","Relief swept across Brightgate City.","But almost as quickly, that relief gave way to sorrow.","Tears began appearing throughout the city. Some cried after realizing they were still alive. Others cried because the person standing beside them only moments ago no longer was.","Emergency sirens echoed continuously through the streets. Collapsed buildings had buried countless people beneath concrete and twisted steel. Smoke rose from several districts where the waves of scorching heat had ignited fires.","Throughout the city, rescue efforts began almost immediately as the Supers Association got to work.","Everywhere, voices filled the streets.","\"Help!\"","\"There's someone trapped here!\"","\"My child! Someone save my child!\"","\"We're over here!\"","The cries of grief mixed with desperate shouts for help. Many who had survived stood frozen before collapsed buildings, staring blankly at what had once been their homes.","The disaster had erased countless differences in an instant. No one cared whether the person beside them was an ordinary civilian or a supernatural. Whether they were rich or poor, known or unknown.","At that moment, everyone simply felt they were all the same miserable ants beneath the two battling above.","High above, the battle continued. Every collision between the undead dragon and the blood-robed Demigod sent another distant tremor through the heavens. Although the two combatants were rapidly moving farther away, each exchange still shook the horizon.","The crimson lights illuminated the darkening day like two miniature suns constantly colliding. Every time another explosion echoed across the sky, the people below instinctively looked upward. Fear lingered within every heart.","Michael silently watched everything unfold. His expression remained calm. Only the slight tightening of his fists betrayed the emotions hidden beneath.","This was the consequence of power. A single clash between beings standing near the pinnacle had nearly reduced one city to ruins through nothing more than the aftereffects of their battle.","The attacks themselves had never been directed at Brightgate. Yet merely standing nearby had almost become a death sentence.","If the dragon's breath had landed within the city instead...","Michael did not allow himself to finish the thought. If anything, the current situation only made his resolve sharpen further. Stronger. Stronger undead. His family stronger.","His gaze slowly swept across the devastated streets below before rising once more toward the distant battlefield.","Even now, every clash between the undead dragon and the blood-robed Demigod caused the sky to shudder.","Teacher Brian continued staring at the distant battle for several long seconds. Only after confirming that the battlefield had moved several dozen kilometers away did he slowly turn toward Michael.","\"...So.\" His voice was quieter than usual. \"What now?\"","The question broke the silence inside the apartment. No one else spoke. They all looked toward Michael.","Their expressions were complicated. Shock. Disbelief. Confusion. Curiosity. Wariness. There were simply too many questions.","How had Michael hidden nearly a thousand Rank Four undead without anyone noticing? How had he created that dragon? How strong had Michael truly become?","Did he really possess an army capable of conquering an entire realm? Was this truly the power someone who had awakened just a year ago should have?","Were other awakeners playing an entirely different game?","Countless questions filled their minds. Unfortunately, Michael had absolutely no intention of answering any of them, even if they asked. Not now. Perhaps not ever.","His emotions were anything but calm. He actually wanted to lash out. The only reason he restrained himself was because the person who had spoken was Teacher Brian.","Among everyone standing inside the apartment, Brian was one of the few people Michael genuinely respected, followed by Director Lin and Instructor Yara. Because of that, Michael swallowed the words rising to his throat.","Had it been only General Caelum standing here, that old kidnapper, Michael doubted he would have remained this restrained.","Fortunately, Brian's presence prevented him from saying something he would undoubtedly regret later.","Even so, he had neither the time nor the patience to entertain anyone. The battle was still ongoing.","The Undead High Drake had successfully forced the blood-robed Demigod away from Brightgate City, but that did not mean everything was under control.","Worried about the connection between him and the Undead High Drake now, Michael did not want to test what would happen if it went out of communication range.","The connection between him and the transformed undead still existed. It remained as clear as ever. However, it no longer felt the same.","Previously, commanding his undead had been no different from moving his own limbs.","Every thought was executed with absolute precision. Every order carried unquestionable authority. There was no hesitation, delay, or resistance whatsoever.","Now, that certainty had loosened.","Though his commands still reached the Undead High Drake without issue and the dragon still obeyed, there was an unmistakable difference. It no longer felt like he was directly moving an extension of himself.","Instead, it felt as though he was directing an immensely intelligent creature that retained its own instincts. Those instincts did not oppose him. Nor did they seek freedom. They simply existed and subtly influenced how his commands were interpreted.","It reminded Michael of Beast Tamers. Their contracted beasts remained loyal to them, yet they were still living creatures capable of making independent judgments while carrying out their master's orders.","Depending on their strength, the contract between them and their owner could even shift toward something more equal.","The transformed Undead High Drake now gave him a remarkably similar feeling.","The difference was that it was an undead. Its loyalty toward him was unquestionable.","Its might had simply risen to a level where it instinctively optimized commands according to its own judgment.","With too many unknowns, Michael could not afford to waste even another second.","Without waiting for another question, he simply informed the four that he would be back. The next instant, space distorted. His figure disappeared from the apartment without another word.","Silence immediately descended. Only the distant explosions echoing across the heavens remained.","Teacher Brian slowly lowered the hand he had subconsciously raised. General Caelum's expression became increasingly complicated as he mentally cursed every generation of whoever had suggested it was a good idea to send him here.","Director Lin and Instructor Yara continued staring at the place where Michael had vanished.","None of them attempted to follow.","Space folded.","Michael reappeared several dozen kilometers away from Brightgate City. The instant his body emerged, a violent wave of force struck him head-on.","His clothes snapped against his skin as he was pushed several meters backward through the air.","The surrounding atmosphere had become so chaotic that even maintaining his position required effort.","Before him, the sky had completely transformed. There were no clouds or sunlight.","Only endless stretches of shattered space, crimson radiance, and emerald deathly light."]},{"number":1149,"title":"Chapter 1149: Fake Dragon Might [4]","paragraphs":["The crimson light belonged to the female Demigod, and the emerald belonged to the Undead High Drake, a reflection of Lucky's flame.","Knowing that Spartan's Abyssal Flames, while undoubtedly strong, were too destructive, he had opted for Lucky's flame instead.","While not as strong when its poison property wasn't factored in, it was still considerably more potent than ordinary flames. To think that one decision alone had led to such a massive transformation.","Even with the battle already far beyond Brightgate City, the destruction left in its wake remained visible for dozens of kilometers.","Every few seconds, another thunderous collision echoed through the region and caused the world beneath Michael's feet to tremble.","With a pale face from the enormous energy consumption needed to sustain his law skill, Michael's eyes remained locked on the figure above.","The female Demigod had finally recovered from the earlier dragon breath.","Although her crimson armor was covered in cracks and one of her six wings had been almost destroyed from the Undead High Drake's relentless assault, the power radiating from her had not diminished by much.","If anything, it had become even more violent.","Blood surged around her in endless waves. The liquid did not fall toward the ground. Instead, it spread across the sky, forming a vast crimson sea that stretched for several kilometers in every direction.","Countless figures emerged from within it. Some resembled enormous beasts. Others took the form of armored warriors wielding spears, axes, and curved blades.","Each one carried an aura comparable to a powerful Rank Four existence. There were about two hundred. The instant they appeared, they rushed toward the Undead High Drake from every direction.","The sky became filled with blood-red attacks. Beams of condensed crimson energy struck the dragon's body one after another. The combined assault was enough to erase mountains.","Yet the Undead High Drake did not retreat. It simply charged forward. Its enormous body smashed directly through the blood-formed creatures.","Those struck by its chest exploded before they could even slow it down. Its wings tore apart dozens more with a single flap and Its tail swept across the crimson sea, creating a path of destruction thousands of meters wide.","The female Demigod raised a hand. The entire sea of blood responded.","A colossal palm formed above the dragon and descended with enough force to crush everything beneath it.","The Undead High Drake lifted its head. Then it rammed upward.","BOOM!","The enormous blood palm shattered. The impact scattered crimson rain across the heavens.","Before the fragments could reform, the dragon's claw tore through them and continued toward the female Demigod, who immediately forced her way through the locked void and teleported to dodge.","The claw passed through the space where she had stood and split the crimson sea apart.","A fraction of a second later, the female Demigod reappeared above the dragon's back. Six blood-red swords materialized behind her.","Every blade carried a different power.","One radiated unbearable heat.","Another caused the surrounding air to decay. Michael didn't know how that worked, but it did.","A third was covered in countless screaming faces.","The remaining three contained enormous violent energies without any distinct separate property.","All six descended at once and struck the Undead High Drake's back, creating a storm of crimson and emerald.","The explosion engulfed the dragon's entire upper body.","Michael's expression changed as worry filled his heart.","Yet when the light faded, the dragon was still there. The dark scales covering its body remained intact. There were several shallow marks across its back, but none had pierced through its defenses.","Michael, who was far below, could not see the exact situation clearly, but from his position alone he could tell the Demigod hadn't been able to truly wound his Undead High Drake.","Above, the female Demigod's expression grew increasingly ugly. She attacked again.","The crimson sea beneath her transformed into thousands of chains. They wrapped around the dragon's limbs, wings, neck, and tail.","Bright crimson symbols appeared across every link. The pressure released by them became so intense that the ground thousands of meters below began sinking.","The Undead High Drake was dragged downward. For the first time since the physical battle began, its momentum stopped.","Seeing this, the female Demigod clasped both hands together.","The chains tightened. A crimson formation appeared around the dragon's body, sealing every direction. Then the entire formation collapsed inward.","BOOM!","Everything disappeared into a sphere of pure light, forcing Michael, who was far away, to close his eyes from the stinging pain.","If it had been any ordinary person, they would surely have gone blind, if not suffered lethal brain damage.","ROAR!!!!!!","After the light faded, Michael could see his Undead High Drake forcing its way out.","Several chains still clung to its body, but they began scattering as its muscles expanded beneath its scales. Its emerald eyes remained cold as it lunged at the female Demigod.","The female Demigod barely managed to move aside before the dragon's head tore through her position.","Even then, one of its horns grazed the edge of her body. Half of the crimson armor covering her side exploded.","Blood sprayed outward.","The female demigod immediately transformed into a crimson shadow and retreated several kilometers.","The Undead High Drake followed without hesitation.","Michael watched the exchange with growing disbelief.","The Demigod was not weak. Far from it. Every attack she released possessed enough strength to kill almost any Rank Four existence instantly.","Her control over that mysterious blood was terrifying. Her speed was monstrous. Her defensive methods were numerous.","She could reshape the terrain, summon armies from blood, form weapons from blood, seal space to prevent teleportation, and recover from injuries at a frightening rate.","She was demonstrating exactly why Demigods stood above ordinary supernaturals.","Yet she still could not truly injure the Undead High Drake.","At most, her strongest attacks left shallow marks across its scales. The situation had become almost absurd.","The female Demigod was using techniques, formations, weapons, magic arts, and everything else at her disposal. Meanwhile, the Undead High Drake was fighting with nothing but its body.","It had not released another breath attack, per Michael's command, and simply relied on its claws, wings, horns, tail, jaws, and overwhelming physical strength.","Even so, the female Demigod could only maintain a standstill.","Seeing this, another thought came to Michael.","\"Hey, isn't this just a ready-made Rank Five undead material for me?\""]},{"number":1150,"title":"Chapter 1150: Another One? [1]","paragraphs":["When the Demigod had first appeared above Brightgate City, what consumed Michael was anger.","Of course, he only allowed himself that anger because he already knew he could handle a Demigod, provided she wasn't too far beyond what he had prepared for.","He hadn't expected someone of that level to come for him at all, which was precisely why he hadn't fled the moment she appeared.","However, beneath the anger of someone wanting his life lay something more calculated.","An eye for an eye.","In truth, his main purpose had never been simple revenge. It was demonstration. If it was said that Rank Three was the first true step toward being recognized as a power in the universe, then Rank Four could be called the backbone of any civilization.","Even great races like elves and star humans treated their Rank Four individuals as treasures, because not everyone could reach that level. The true measure of any civilization was not its territory or its wealth, but how many Rank Four existences it possessed and how powerful those individuals were.","Demigods were then the pillars and rulers of a realm. One-man armies. To defeat even a single Demigod through sheer numbers alone, a force would need hundreds of powerful Rank Four supernaturals working in perfect concert.","If Michael could demonstrate that he alone possessed the ability to match that level of threat, the implications would be immediate and far-reaching.","Setting aside the foreign forces already making their way toward Aurora, even the Federation and the demonic supernaturals would be forced to treat him with extreme caution. They would have to reconsider every calculation they had ever made about him.","This thought process had been born from a necessary but forceful realization. Now that he stood on a universal stage, the only language that carried real weight was power.","If he wanted to protect everything he had, everything he cared about, he could not afford to be treated as prey any longer. The moment he allowed that impression to take root, he would lose everything.","This was also why Michael believed the female Demigod had struck when she did. Rather than wait while the entire universe's attention converged on him, it was probably better to kill him now.","If she succeeded before the wider world had time to react, his death would bear no consequence. At least, that was what Michael believed her reasoning to be.","However, what Michael had not expected was for the effects of his trump card to exceed every calculation he had made.","Instead of his Undead High Drake desperately struggling to keep pace with a Demigod, it was the Demigod who was receiving a beating. A sustained, one-sided beating that grew more embarrassing for her with every passing exchange.","He knew, of course, that this wouldn't last forever, especially since he was on a time limit. Even with the Undead High Drake's current absurd defensive capability and raw physical dominance, the female Demigod was not going to simply fall.","Her recovery speed alone was a nightmare, and the moment the Enhancer's effects ran out, the balance would shift. Michael didn't think a 200% boost to the Undead High Drake would produce a massive upgrade in strength regardless.","Also, if he gave the drake freedom to use its magic and unleash another dragon breath at full force, he was genuinely more worried about the collateral damage to the surrounding region than about whether it would hurt the Demigod. She was not a stationary fighter.","The attack would certainly hurt her if it connected, but whether the undead high drake could kill her before it leveled everything else within a hundred kilometer radius was the real question.","All of this pointed toward one conclusion. The female Demigod would eventually be defeated the longer this went on. But not soon, and probably not within the time limit imposed on him.","When the Federation Demigods arrived, the finishing blow, and the prestige that came with it, would also not be his.","Michael was not happy with any of this, on the outside or within.","His heart rate began climbing.","A ready-made Rank Five undead.","His breathing, usually so controlled, became noticeably less steady.","The Federation would be here soon. That was the problem. Once they arrived, the battle would likely end.","The female Demigod would either escape or be killed by someone else. Either outcome closed the window permanently. Which meant if he wanted her, he needed to act before that window closed.","Fortunately, not all hope was lost yet.","Though the energy consumption needed to maintain his skill was high, Michael still had enough.","After all, the current power his Undead High Drake could output had largely nothing to do with him directly. The boost in strength came from his gift and the Three-Star Epic Grade Enhancer.","All he needed to do was maintain the law skill that made all of this possible.","And with his current level of achievement in law cultivation, Michael could use his law skill on two creatures simultaneously.","Yes.","With his remaining energy, Michael was planning on having one more Demigod-level combatant enter the field.","Surely that much wasn't impossible, right?","\"However, who do I choose?\"","In fact, Michael already had someone in mind.","Lucky.","Seeing the effect the Enhancer had produced in the Undead High Drake, wouldn't Lucky also undergo a dramatic transformation if he merged it with the traits of Beginning and the Undead High Drake?","Wouldn't that give him two dragons for the remaining seventeen minutes?","It was an exciting thought. But unfortunately, after a quick moment of honest reflection, Michael knew the reality would be much different.","While he might be able to produce another temporary false dragon, it would not reach the level of the Undead High Drake.","Lucky's foundation simply wasn't strong enough.","Though its dragon blood and evolution into Epic Grade had granted it more levels than others who started at the same grade, it still wasn't comparable to the Undead High Drake, a peak Rank Four creature at level 100, also carrying dragon blood.","But if not Lucky, then who?"]},{"number":1151,"title":"Chapter 1151: Another One? [2]","paragraphs":["The answer came easily.","Beginning.","After the Undead High Drake, it could be argued that Beginning was the strongest undead in Michael's legion.","He had considered the Bone Dragon first. After all, if the effects of Echoed Bestowal truly pulled creatures closer to the origin of their bloodline depending on the chosen traits, then an undead like the Bone Dragon should receive an enormous boost with Beginning's and the High Drake's traits fused to it.","However, putting aside compatibility, the Bone Dragon could not even defeat Beginning under normal circumstances, which made Michael lean heavily toward the giant.","Beginning was stronger than nearly every other undead in his legion, and its potential ceiling could easily rank among the top five. Its body was absurdly powerful. Its Law of Brutal Rebirth made it increasingly difficult to kill. Its instincts in battle were terrifying.","If any undead had the qualifications to temporarily step into the Demigod level, it was Beginning.","Michael had already placed it inside the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion before leaving the apartment. All he needed to do was summon it.","But just as he was about to, his expression became complicated and he halted.","\"Beginning is certainly the best option in terms of raw power. Unfortunately, it is also the worst option in every other way.\"","Beginning's reckless nature alone was enough to make Michael hesitate. At this point, he was almost certain that while he could still control an undead elevated to the Demigod level, that control was no longer perfect.","If the same thing happened to Beginning...","Michael's eyelid twitched.","This undead had a troubled history. Twice already, it had treated powerful opponents as nourishment for its own advancement.","The giant seemed to possess an almost instinctive desire to temper itself through overwhelming pressure, suffering, and destruction.","If Michael summoned it now and elevated it to the same temporary level as the Undead High Drake, there was no telling what it might decide to do.","The female Demigod was exactly the kind of opponent Beginning would adore.","A being capable of tearing apart its body. A source of pressure far beyond anything it had previously endured. A living opportunity to push Brutal Rebirth toward another transformation.","What if Beginning interpreted the battle as a chance to ascend? What if it deliberately allowed the female Demigod to destroy its body over and over again and attempted to use her power as nourishment?","A chill ran through Michael.","\"It has already done something similar twice. I have no reason to believe it would suddenly develop restraint now.\"","Also, regardless of the enhanced power, Beginning remained a Rank Four creature at its core. Its temporary Demigod-level strength came from borrowed power.","If it recklessly attempted to use that temporary state to force an advancement involving its essence, soul, or foundation, the consequences could be disastrous.","For a realm as sensitive as Demigod, Michael refused to gamble.","Once Michael reached this conclusion, only one choice remained.","The Bone Dragon.","Michael's gaze shifted.","While it was not the most impressive undead in his legion, only a Three-Star Extraordinary Grade creature compared to Beginning, Lucky, Spartan, Ghost, Lily, and several others with more visible potential, the Bone Dragon had once been the primary undead of another peak Rank Four necromancer.","Its grade might not seem remarkable now, but its actual foundation was far stronger than most creatures of the same grade.","Unlike Beginning, the Bone Dragon possessed only basic intelligence. If he elevated it to Demigod-level prowess, any resistance he felt should stem from something other than independent thought.","There was another advantage. It was still a dragon.","Perhaps not a true dragon in the purest sense. Its body had been assembled from countless powerful remains, with some bones not even belonging to the same species, making it more of a constructed monster than a natural race. But the draconic nature remained.","Michael's heartbeat quickened.","The Undead High Drake had transformed after receiving Beginning's and Lucky's traits. So what would happen if the Bone Dragon received the traits of Beginning and the Undead High Drake?","The thought alone made his scalp tingle.","Michael did not know what would appear. Perhaps another dragon. Perhaps something entirely different.","Whatever the result, its foundation should be sufficient to temporarily reach the same battlefield. And even if it failed to match the Undead High Drake, it only needed to help.","Two false Demigods attacking together would completely overturn the current standstill. The female Demigod was already struggling to defend herself against one.","Against two, her chances of escape would plummet, and unless she had some exceptional trump card left, she would obediently become his next undead.","Michael no longer hesitated. A thought flashed through his mind. The space behind him immediately distorted. The air became several degrees colder. A pair of blue flames lit up.","The enormous skull of the Bone Dragon slowly rose, and it looked ready to release a thunderous roar before Michael stopped it.","\"Are you crazy? You're an undead. Why are you roaring? Are you excited? Are you even supposed to feel excited?\"","\".....\"","After distancing himself, Michael wasted no time.","\"Echoed Bestowal.\"","His already pale face became noticeably whiter as the Law of Echoed Existence surged once more.","BOOM!","The Bone Dragon's skeletal frame violently shook. Its entire body expanded. Cracks spread across countless bones before immediately repairing themselves.","The aura surrounding it exploded upward. The empty eye sockets blazed several times brighter. Its ribs thickened. Its limbs became noticeably more robust. Even the countless mismatched bones making up its body seemed to instinctively reorganize themselves into a sturdier structure.","A savage aura slowly began emerging from the dragon.","BOOOOOOM!","The heavens shook.","Michael's pupils contracted.","Every bone covering the dragon suddenly emitted dazzling golden light. Countless cracks appeared across its body as the countless imperfections that had accompanied its creation until now rapidly disappeared.","Its twisted skeletal frame became increasingly harmonious.","The skull elongated, its horns growing backward in elegant curves.","The empty gaps between several bones became filled by dense death energy that behaved almost like flesh."]},{"number":1152,"title":"Chapter 1152: Another One? [3]","paragraphs":["Even its wings changed.","Previously, they had appeared assembled from countless skeletal fragments. Now every bone aligned perfectly.","The wings expanded until they rivaled mountains in size.","Its vertebrae thickened. Its tail lengthened. The flames within its eye sockets compressed before exploding into two brilliant suns of ghostly fire.","The pressure surrounding the Bone Dragon climbed without stopping.","Michael immediately felt an immense drain on his reserves. His breathing became rough.","The burden of maintaining two Echoed Bestowals simultaneously was far beyond anything he had ever attempted.","Sweat poured down his forehead. His vision blurred for an instant. But he gritted his teeth and endured.","This much he could still handle. His gaze remained fixed on the sight before him.","Unlike the Undead High Drake, which had flesh, the Bone Dragon remained a creature of death.","However, those bones no longer resembled ordinary skeletons. Each one appeared carved from flawless crystal, with ancient-looking runes naturally spread across every surface.","The surrounding death energy condensed into an enormous translucent dragon that perfectly overlapped the skeletal body.","The Bone Dragon slowly raised its head.","ROOOOOOOOAAAAAR!!","The sound rolled across hundreds of kilometers. Even the Undead High Drake paused for a fraction of a second before continuing its assault.","The blood-robed Demigod's expression finally changed completely. Her eyes shifted away from the Undead High Drake.","For the first time since the battle began, she looked toward Michael. A trace of panic appeared in her crimson eyes.","Michael had no pity for her. Not even a little. The woman had descended upon Brightgate City intending to kill him, knowing full well how many ordinary people would be caught beneath her aura alone.","Whatever happened next was simply the result of her own decision.","His gaze hardened.","\"Go.\"","The command travelled through the soul connection. The transformed Bone Dragon reacted instantly.","BOOM!","Its enormous wings spread. Unlike the Undead High Drake, whose every movement created violent hurricanes through sheer overwhelming mass, the Bone Dragon moved with a strange and almost unnatural silence.","The sky in front of it collapsed inward. A golden streak tore across the battlefield.","The female Demigod sensed the approaching danger immediately. Her expression changed. She twisted her body and raised one hand.","The vast sea of blood surrounding her surged upward, forming dozens of enormous walls between herself and the incoming Bone Dragon. Each wall was several hundred meters thick.","Bright crimson symbols covered their surfaces while countless screaming faces emerged from within the blood. The defenses were strong enough to endure attacks from powerful Rank Four supernaturals without trembling.","The Bone Dragon did not slow down.","Golden light gathered around its horns as it lowered its skull.","BOOM!","The first wall exploded. Then the second. The third. The fourth. The Bone Dragon tore through every layer without losing momentum. Blood scattered across the heavens like a crimson storm.","The female Demigod's pupils contracted. She immediately shifted through space. Her figure disappeared from her position just before the Bone Dragon's jaws snapped shut.","CLANG!","The collision between its teeth sent a metallic shockwave across the sky. Even though the attack missed, the force alone crushed the surrounding blood sea and created a circular void several kilometers wide.","The woman reappeared far above it. Before she could stabilize herself, a shadow covered her body.","The Undead High Drake had arrived. Its claw descended from above.","The female Demigod crossed all six wings before her. Crimson light surged around them.","BOOM!","The claw struck. The woman was smashed downward like a falling star. She tore through several layers of the blood sea before crashing toward the ground.","However, before she could reach it, the Bone Dragon's tail swept horizontally. The enormous skeletal tail struck her side.","CRACK!","Several sections of her crimson armor shattered. Her body changed direction instantly and was sent flying across the horizon. Blood spilled from her lips.","The Bone Dragon followed. Its wings folded tightly against its frame. Golden death energy surrounded its body as it shot after her with terrifying speed.","The female Demigod barely managed to turn before the Bone Dragon's skull rammed into her.","BOOM!","The air ruptured behind her. The impact forced her body through several kilometers of air in a single instant. Her remaining wings spread desperately as she attempted to halt her momentum.","The Undead High Drake appeared behind her. A colossal tail descended.","The Demigod's eyes widened. She vanished again. The tail struck empty space.","The ground thousands of meters below collapsed as the force travelled downward. A massive trench appeared across the landscape.","The female Demigod reappeared between the two dragons. Her breathing had become noticeably heavier. Blood streamed from the corner of her mouth.","The armor covering her torso had been reduced to cracked fragments. With the void being locked by the two dragons working in tandem, her teleportation became increasingly difficult.","As for deploying her domain, just like many of Michael's opponents before her, after exchanging blows she had come to believe he possessed abilities comparable to her own rank.","That caution had kept her domain inactive, held in reserve in case the High Drake deployed its own.","If she had deployed it instead of sitting on it, she might have glimpsed the reality of the situation and turned things around. Unfortunately for her, that caution worked entirely in Michael's favor.","She looked from the Undead High Drake to the transformed Bone Dragon. She had expected Michael to possess some hidden means, had even prepared herself for the possibility that he could temporarily resist her.","However, resisting a Demigod and summoning two creatures capable of overwhelming one were completely different matters.","The female Demigod raised both hands. The remaining blood sea surged violently.","Every drop of blood within several kilometers gathered around her.","Michael watched in shock as even creatures caught beyond the shockwaves of the battle dissolved into blood mist, drawn into her gathering power.","Her six wings opened fully. The damaged wing regrew before his eyes as blood filled the missing portions.","A crimson crown materialized above her head and the pressure surrounding her increased sharply."]},{"number":1153,"title":"Chapter 1153: Another One? [4]","paragraphs":["Michael's expression grew serious.","\"Even now she can still increase her strength. As expected of a Demigod.\"","A Demigod truly could not be underestimated.","The blood surrounding her condensed into a gigantic humanoid figure. It stood thousands of meters tall. Six wings spread from its back.","A featureless face looked down upon the two dragons while a crimson spear formed within its hands. The spear alone was longer than a mountain range.","The female Demigod stood within the center of the giant's chest. Her hands clasped together. The enormous blood avatar copied her movement.","Crimson lines spread across the heavens. The surrounding space hardened. Michael felt the spatial energy in the region become almost completely unusable.","The avatar thrust its spear forward. The weapon moved with impossible speed for something so large. The tip pierced toward the transformed Bone Dragon.","The Bone Dragon immediately crossed both wings before its body.","BOOM!","The crimson spear struck. Golden light and blood energy exploded across the sky. The Bone Dragon was pushed backward for several kilometers. Cracks appeared across the bones covering its wings.","The female Demigod's eyes flashed. The avatar twisted the spear and pressed forward, attempting to pierce through the Bone Dragon completely.","More cracks spread across its frame when the runes covering the Bone Dragon's body lit up. The cracked bones began repairing themselves as its aura seemed to grow even stronger.","The Bone Dragon unfolded its wings. The crimson spear was forced aside as its skeletal claws wrapped around the weapon. The avatar attempted to pull it free when the Bone Dragon's grip tightened and the spear snapped.","CRACK!","The female Demigod's expression changed. Before she could reform the weapon, the Undead High Drake slammed into the blood avatar from the side.","BOOOOOOM!","The enormous humanoid figure staggered. One of its six wings burst apart, bitten off a fraction of a second later by the Undead High Drake.","The High Drake continued, sinking its claws into the avatar's shoulder. Its jaws opened and bit directly into the blood construct.","The female Demigod screamed. Although the avatar was formed from mysterious means and wasn't drawn from her innate blood, it remained connected to her essence.","Damage to it affected her directly.","She hurriedly separated herself from the construct. Her true body shot upward from its chest.","The blood avatar collapsed into an enormous wave beneath her.","She had barely escaped when the Bone Dragon emerged from the crimson tide. Its golden crystal-like skull tore through the blood. One claw reached toward her.","The female Demigod waved her hand. Hundreds of blood blades appeared and struck the Bone Dragon's arm. Every blade carried enough power to split mountains.","The Bone Dragon did not retreat. The blades shattered against its bones. Several left shallow marks, but those marks repaired before the next attack could land.","Its claw continued forward.","The Demigod folded two wings around herself. The claw struck them.","CRACK!","Both wings broke. The female Demigod was flung away. She spun through the air, but her control remained exceptional. Before the Bone Dragon could pursue, she pointed toward it.","Countless droplets of blood attached to its skeleton suddenly expanded. They transformed into crimson spikes that drove inward from every direction.","The gaps between the Bone Dragon's ribs filled with sharp blood crystals. Its joints were locked. Its wings were pinned.","For the first time since entering the battlefield, its entire body stopped moving.","The female Demigod's eyes flashed with cruel satisfaction.","\"Die.\"","She clenched her fist. The blood spikes exploded.","BOOM!","The Bone Dragon disappeared inside a massive crimson detonation. Michael, watching from below, trembled with worry, followed immediately by astonishment.","A golden light appeared within the explosion. Then two enormous skeletal wings spread. The crimson energy scattered.","The Bone Dragon emerged. Several bones were damaged. Part of one horn had shattered. A portion of its chest had been blown apart. But the golden runes across its body were already glowing.","The missing sections began regrowing from condensed death energy. New bone formed over old fractures. Its broken horn extended once more.","Within seconds, nearly every injury had disappeared, and the Bone Dragon's aura grew even stronger.","The female Demigod stared.","Michael could almost understand her disbelief. If he were in her situation, he would despise fighting himself.","Both his undead had received the effects of Brutal Rebirth.","Hurting one was difficult. Keeping either injured was almost impossible. The Demigod's strength remained extraordinary, but in the end she was still only one person.","The Undead High Drake attacked again. Its wing swept across the sky. The female Demigod lowered her body and avoided it.","The Bone Dragon's jaws appeared beneath her. She twisted sideways, narrowly dodging, but a fraction of a second later a golden horn struck her shoulder.","Blood erupted and she was thrown upward where the Undead High Drake's claw was already waiting.","BOOM!","The woman was smashed back down. The Bone Dragon swung its tail.","BOOM!","She was sent sideways. The Undead High Drake struck her with its wing.","BOOM!","Before she could recover, the Bone Dragon caught her between its claws. The female Demigod released a furious scream. A violent crimson explosion erupted from her body.","The Bone Dragon's fingers were blown apart. The female demigod escaped from its grasp.","However, the moment she emerged, the Undead High Drake's skull slammed into her. Her body folded around the impact. Blood sprayed from her mouth. She was launched through the air once again.","The two dragons did not give her room to breathe. One attacked from the front. The other attacked from behind. Whenever she avoided a claw, a tail was waiting. Whenever she blocked a wing, a set of skeletal jaws appeared from another direction. Whenever she created distance, one of the dragons crossed it in an instant.","She tried to fly upward. The Undead High Drake forced her down. She attempted to descend toward the ground. The Bone Dragon intercepted her.","Michael watched silently from afar. Even he found the sight somewhat excessive. A true Demigod was being passed between two dragons like a toy.","Still, he issued no order for them to stop.","The female Demigod screamed and released another wave of blood energy. The blast forced both dragons backward, finally obtaining a moment of distance."]},{"number":1154,"title":"Chapter 1154: Down","paragraphs":["Her appearance had become miserable. Three of her wings were broken and one arm hung at an unnatural angle.","The crimson armor covering her body had almost completely disappeared. Blood covered her from head to toe.","Despite all of that, the power in her eyes remained terrifying.","Michael's expression darkened.","\"What a ridiculous recovery ability.\"","It was said Demigods had the ability to revive from a single drop of blood. How true that was, Michael didn't know, but it was obvious she possessed a ridiculous healing factor. Even after taking such a beating, she remained capable of fighting.","This was the excellence of a Demigod.","Since the power gap between him and the three fighting above was too vast, even Michael with his intelligence couldn't fully decipher their methods.","Surely the Demigod had used means only Demigods could access. Unfortunately for her, her enemies were equally ridiculous.","This was the path of the cheater.","Michael continued watching the battle from below, admist his ridiculous thoughts, as the end of the battle seemed to be fast approaching.","The Undead High Drake released another earth-shaking roar while the Bone Dragon silently lowered its crystal-like skull.","The contrast between the two dragons could not have been more obvious. Yet under Michael's continuous commands delivered through their connection, they moved with astonishing harmony.","The female Demigod sensed the danger immediately. She no longer dared exchange blows head-on. Instead, her figure dissolved into countless droplets of blood.","Every droplet scattered in a different direction before rapidly reforming into hundreds of identical crimson silhouettes.","Each clone carried nearly the same aura and each seemed to possess enough power to threaten an ordinary Rank Four expert.","The Undead High Drake ignored all of them.","Its emerald eyes remained locked onto a single target. Its instincts had already identified the genuine body.","BOOM!","The dragon's wings exploded with force. Its gigantic body vanished. The heavens cracked as it accelerated.","The female Demigod's true body immediately sensed death approaching. The hundreds of blood clones rushed forward simultaneously, sacrificing themselves without hesitation.","Each one detonated before the Undead High Drake. The continuous explosions illuminated the sky crimson.","Surviving mountains beneath the battlefield collapsed from the repeated impacts. Entire sections of forest were reduced to ash.","The Undead High Drake charged through everything.","Every explosion merely scattered against its scales and every blood clone that attempted to restrain it was crushed beneath claws capable of ripping apart the air itself.","Seeing this, the female Demigod extended her remaining functional arm. The blood sea condensed into nine enormous crimson suns, creating a distinct heat that could be felt even from a great distance.","Unlike ordinary fire, these spheres radiated terrifying corrosive energy. The nine crimson suns shot toward the Undead High Drake one after another.","BOOM! BOOM!! BOOM!!!","Each collision shook the heavens. The first exploded against the dragon's chest. The second struck its neck. The third detonated beneath one wing.","By the ninth explosion, even Michael, who had relaxed somewhat, became serious again, drawing a sharp breath.","The accumulated force had become terrifying. The emerald light surrounding the Undead High Drake flickered. Its advance finally slowed.","Then it continued forward.","The dark scales covering its body now possessed several visible cracks, and in some sections the damaged flesh underneath could be seen slowly corroding away.","Yet before the female Demigod's eyes, those cracks rapidly closed as the dragon's aura seemed to even increase.","The female Demigod gritted her teeth. She had finally managed to inflict meaningful damage, only for it to disappear within moments.","Unfortunately, while her attention remained fixed on the Undead High Drake for just a brief moment, without the slightest warning, the Bone Dragon emerged beneath her.","Its enormous skeletal wings folded inward as it rose like a spear from below. Its crystal claws reached upward.","The female Demigod instinctively crossed her remaining wings.","CLANG!","The claws collided against them. The impact resembled two worlds crashing together. The shattered remains of her damaged wings scattered across the sky. Before she could recover, the Bone Dragon's tail struck.","BOOM!","The impact sent her body spinning uncontrollably. This time, the Bone Dragon did not pursue. Instead, it opened its jaws.","The energy compressed again and again until even the surrounding space began distorting. But before it could release, the female Demigod sent a ball of condensed blood directly into its jaws. The ball exploded.","The sphere of gathered energy dispersed violently.","The female Demigod, however, had already witnessed enough. Cold sweat covered her face.","That attack, if released, would undoubtedly have rivaled the earlier dragon breath.","Her crimson eyes became incomparably cold.","The blood surrounding her body suddenly began flowing backward. Not toward her wounds, but toward her heart instead.","Every drop of blood she had spilled throughout the battle seemed to return. The scattered droplets rose from the air, pulled inward as though gravity itself had reversed for them alone.","Even the blood soaking her robes peeled away and rejoined the flow.","The shattered armor reassembled. Her broken wings rapidly regenerated. Even the arm hanging unnaturally returned to its proper position.","Within only a few breaths, she had almost completely recovered once more.","The cost, however, was obvious.","The crimson aura surrounding her had noticeably weakened. Her face had become pale. Even maintaining flight seemed slightly more difficult.","Whatever technique she had just used, it had drawn heavily from something deeper than her ordinary reserves.","The Undead High Drake descended from above. The Bone Dragon ascended from below. The female Demigod stood directly between them.","She clenched both fists. A colossal crimson barrier expanded in every direction. Its surface contained countless layered formations rotating simultaneously.","Each layer reinforced the next. Each one drew upon her remaining essence. She had abandoned offense entirely.","Of course, this wasn't because she had given up. Far away, she could sense a familiar presence.","If she could survive for even a few more seconds, she might still live through this, even if not well.","To think it would come down to this level in the end."]},{"number":1155,"title":"Chapter 1155: High Level Thief [1]","paragraphs":["The Undead High Drake's claw descended. The Bone Dragon's crystal horns pierced upward.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!","The first layer shattered. Then the second. Then the third. The barriers collapsed one after another like fragile glass. Each collapse released violent shockwaves that flattened the mountains below.","The female Demigod screamed as blood poured from every pore. She desperately pushed more power into the formations.","For one brief instant, the final barrier actually held.","The two dragons stopped. But only for a heartbeat.","Then the Undead High Drake roared. The Bone Dragon answered with a silent surge of energy. Their combined strength increased once more.","CRACK!","The last barrier finally gave way. Two colossal claws descended simultaneously. The female Demigod disappeared beneath them.","The impact distorted the heavens themselves. A circular shockwave spread across the horizon, erasing everything in its path. Even the clouds hundreds of kilometers away dispersed instantly.","When the blinding light finally faded, the female Demigod was falling. Her body tumbled helplessly through the sky.","For the first time since the battle began, she did not immediately recover.","Michael's eyes sharpened.","The opportunity had finally arrived. If his undead dealt one more overwhelming blow, she would either be knocked unconscious or killed. Either outcome worked for him.","His fingers instinctively tightened. His eyes gleamed with excitement. He was just about to give the command when his actions came to a sudden halt.","\"Young man.\"","A calm elderly voice suddenly echoed across the battlefield. It wasn't loud, yet somehow it carried clearly directly to his ear.","Michael's expression changed. His head snapped toward the source.","Far away, standing upon empty space several kilometers from the battlefield, was an elderly man with snow-white hair tied neatly behind his head.","He wore simple gray robes that looked no different from ordinary clothing.","Yet Michael's pupils contracted.","Every instinct in his body warned him.","Danger. Extreme danger.","Although the old man had restrained his aura almost perfectly, the tiny amount naturally escaping was enough to make Michael deeply uncomfortable.","Another Demigod.","\"...\"","Michael's face remained expressionless. Internally, however, he wanted to curse.","Seriously?","Wasn't it said that the stronger someone became, the rarer people of the same level were supposed to be?","Then why was it that every single time he climbed a bit in power, these supposedly legendary existences suddenly appeared one after another?","Rank Three. Rank Four. Now Demigods.","It was as though the universe had specifically chosen to direct its malice at him whenever he was involved. One Demigod trying to kill him.","Another arriving before the battle had even ended. At this rate, would Rank Five experts start appearing in groups once he advanced again?","His expression remained calm while his thoughts raced.","Friend or enemy? From the Federation, maybe? Or a demonic supernatural?","He couldn't afford to make the wrong judgment.","The elderly man looked toward Michael before shifting his gaze to the blood-robed woman still falling through the sky. His voice remained calm.","\"Young man.\"","\"I know your anger is great.\"","\"But I ask you to show mercy.\"","\"Please do not kill her.\"","Michael remained silent. His eyes never left the old man. One thought from him was all it would take for both dragons to continue their assault.","The elderly man continued.","\"I am from the Federation. I know she intended to kill you. I also understand your anger. But that woman holds far greater value alive than dead. There are many things we need to learn from her. So let us talk this through first.\"","Hearing that, Michael relaxed. Only internally.","So. Federation. That was at least better than another hidden enemy appearing. From the old man's posture and words, he didn't seem to harbor any hostility.","Still, Michael did not lower his guard. Perhaps the old man truly belonged to the Federation. Perhaps he genuinely wanted to negotiate.","Or perhaps he simply had no desire to fight two Demigod-level dragons. He could also very well be feigning goodwill to buy time.","Either explanation sounded reasonable.","But did he honestly think a few words were enough?","This was a Demigod, for crying out loud. One who had descended with the intention of killing him and had caused countless innocent deaths.","And now, just when victory was finally within reach, he was expected to simply stop?","Even if the Federation later offered compensation, could anything they provided compare to obtaining the corpse of a complete Demigod?","No. Not merely a corpse. A future Demigod undead. Its value was immeasurable. How could he possibly abandon such an opportunity simply because someone politely asked?","Wait. Wasn't this old man essentially trying to steal his loot? But what was he supposed to do now?","A thought flashed through Michael's mind. Then he made his decision.","His expression twisted. The hesitation disappeared. In its place appeared naked fury.","It was real enough that even Michael himself almost believed it.","He pointed toward the distant elderly man.","\"You demonic bastard!\"","His voice exploded across the battlefield.","\"So that's your trick? You think pretending to be from the Federation will fool me?\"","His eyes burned with killing intent.","\"You really think I'm that stupid?\"","\"DIE!\"","The elderly man's calm expression froze.","\"What?\"","At that exact moment, Michael's order reached both dragons.","The transformed Undead High Drake immediately abandoned the blood-robed Demigod. Its colossal head turned. Its emerald eyes instantly locked onto the elderly man standing far away.","The next instant—","ROOOOOOAAAR!!","The heavens shook. The dragon disappeared.","The old man's pupils shrank.","BOOOOOOM!!","A gigantic claw descended from the heavens toward him, tearing apart the surrounding space as it fell.","At the very same moment, Michael issued his second command.","\"Bone Dragon.\"","\"Finish her.\"","The Bone Dragon's loyalty remained absolute. Its enormous skeletal wings spread wide as it dived straight toward the heavily injured blood-robed Demigod like a divine executioner.","The exhausted blood-robed woman's eyes widened. The elderly Federation Demigod's composed expression changed entirely."]},{"number":1156,"title":"Chapter 1156: High Level Thief [2]","paragraphs":["Michael's plan was simple.","Play dumb.","His expression remained one of pure fury, but beneath that carefully maintained façade, his thoughts raced with frightening speed.","There was a possibility the old man was lying. There was also a possibility he was telling the truth. Michael couldn't afford to assume either.","The Federation.","Their relationship could hardly be called friendly.","At best, they were reluctant allies. A fragile understanding held together by mutual interests and, more importantly, by the existence of Aunt Mia and Lily.","Because of them, Michael had never truly considered tearing his relationship with the Federation apart. One reason was that he genuinely didn't want to make such a giant an enemy.","Also, the Federation had protected Aurora for generations. Even General Caelum, despite kidnapping him once, had never actually tried to harm him and had even saved his life.","Putting everything else aside, they deserved at least a measure of respect.","But there was another reason. A far more practical one.","He simply wasn't qualified.","Michael had no delusions about his current position. To everyone else, today's battle looked as though he possessed two Demigod-level undead capable of suppressing an actual Demigod.","Only Michael himself knew the truth. These two were on borrowed time. The moment the Enhancer's duration expired, both dragons would immediately fall back to their original level.","The Federation, however, possessed genuine Demigods.","There was an enormous difference between them that couldn't be crossed with thousands of Rank Four undead alone, especially when the Federation possessed the technology and accumulated resources of a high-tier civilization to match exactly that kind of force.","Until he possessed enough strength that the Federation itself would hesitate before provoking him, he could not honestly place himself on the same level as Aurora's greatest power.","Because of that, he needed to treat this old man carefully.","Yet he also couldn't let go now, not when one of the greatest opportunities of his life lay right before him.","A complete Demigod.","If she died here, her body would belong to him. If the corpse remained sufficiently intact, he could create the first true Rank Five undead of his legion.","The thought alone made his heart pound.","Could he negotiate with the Federation instead? Perhaps.","He could ask for a Rank Five corpse in exchange. But Michael trusted actions more than promises.","Over the past year, he had learned something about the Federation. They could indeed invest heavily in someone, but only in people they could control.","Michael had never truly been one of those people.","Even if they promised him a Demigod corpse today, what guarantee existed that they would actually hand one over tomorrow?","None.","Demigods were strategic assets. Their corpses were no less valuable. Why would the Federation willingly strengthen someone they couldn't completely command?","So no. Relying on promises was foolish, especially when certainty already lay before him.","Whatever problems came afterward, he would deal with them afterward. The future belonged to the future. Today's opportunity belonged to today.","As for the Federation's reaction to his attack, Michael felt his current actions were perfectly reasonable.","A demonic supernatural had just attempted to kill him, and when he was about to settle the matter, another Demigod appeared from nowhere claiming to be from the Federation without any proof whatsoever.","Who in their right mind would immediately believe him? Certainly not someone whose life had just been targeted.","If anything, attacking first was one of the most natural reactions imaginable.","Should the matter be investigated later, Michael could simply apologize.","\"My emotions got the better of me.\"","\"I genuinely believed he was another enemy.\"","\"He appeared in the middle of a battle without identifying himself beforehand.\"","\"My apologies, Senior.\"","Who could really blame him? Even Michael almost believed the excuse himself.","Also since the federation had to take parts of the blame for the demigod causing chaos, they shouldn't make things too difficult for him.","Meanwhile, high above, the old man's expression remained frozen.","His eyes shifted between the emerald dragon hurtling toward him and the Bone Dragon diving after the blood-robed woman.","Only now did he realize something.","This young man wasn't merely impulsive. He was terrifyingly decisive.","Of course, he wasn't aware of Michael's true thoughts.","Ironically, everything he was currently thinking was precisely what Michael wanted him to think.","Someone like this, a young genius with power who had just survived an assassination attempt, would be blinded by anger and likely incapable of calmly distinguishing friend from foe in the immediate aftermath.","It was a far more believable explanation than the truth.","The old man could understand the distrust. If their positions were reversed, he would likely react the same way.","A Demigod had appeared out of nowhere in the middle of a life-and-death battle, claiming to belong to the Federation with nothing more than a few words.","Expecting Michael to lower his guard immediately would have been absurd. The young man wasn't wrong to be suspicious.","However, understanding him and allowing him to continue were two completely different matters.","He absolutely could not permit the blood-robed woman to die here.","Not because he was some naive old man preaching mercy, and certainly not because he pitied her.","If anything, he personally wished to break every bone in her body for daring to launch an attack on innocents. But he was a Federation Demigod before he was anything else.","As a Federation pillar, emotions came second and the interests of Aurora came first.","Just as Michael had suspected, Demigods were indeed strategic assets, alive or dead.","The moment a civilization possessed more than a single Demigod, it stepped into the ranks of the universe's high-tier civilizations.","Every additional Demigod strengthened not only its military might but also its reputation, influence, and bargaining power throughout countless realms.","No civilization would casually discard such a resource, not even when that Demigod belonged to the enemy.","To ordinary people, that logic would sound ridiculous. Why preserve someone who wanted you dead?","The answer was simple.","Value."]},{"number":1157,"title":"Chapter 1157: High Level Thief [3]","paragraphs":["A living Demigod possessed immeasurable value. Even if cooperation proved impossible, there were countless other methods to extract value from them.","Demigods could become living energy sources capable of supplying unimaginably powerful artifacts for centuries. Their bodies could be transformed into battle puppets. Their blood, bones, and souls were also treasures beyond measure.","The reverse was equally true. If the demonic supernaturals ever managed to capture one of Aurora's Demigods, they would undoubtedly think the same way.","Neither side was foolish enough to casually destroy such an asset.","From an outsider's perspective, the relationship between Aurora and the demonic supernaturals was almost contradictory.","They hated one another, fought endlessly, and constantly sought to claim territory, influence, and control. Yet neither side truly wished to weaken Aurora itself beyond recovery.","A crippled Aurora would not belong to either faction. It would simply become prey for the countless powerful civilizations watching from beyond. That outcome benefited no one except outsiders.","Their conflict was one of ownership. Not annihilation.","As strange as it sounded, if a Demigod from either side fell into the other's hands alive, killing them was often considered the least profitable option.","Of course, if they died during battle despite every effort, or somewhere outside anyone's influence, then so be it.","No one could stop every death. But if they possessed the ability to prevent it, then preserving that Demigod, whether as a prisoner, a bargaining chip, an energy source, or something else entirely, almost always produced greater benefits for their civilization.","It was cold. A ruthlessly pragmatic calculation stripped of emotion.","Unfortunately, the young man standing opposite him clearly hadn't reached that stage of thinking yet.","Or perhaps he had.","After all, this was a genius necromancer.","The old man could swear with his life that nothing was more important to a necromancer than corpses. They would do anything including selling their souls for a good one.","The old man watched the Bone Dragon descend like a golden meteor toward the blood-robed woman. His eyes narrowed.","Either way, he couldn't gamble. Whether Michael acted from rage or from calculation, the result would be exactly the same.","If he did nothing, Aurora would lose a Demigod-level strategic asset and instead strengthen one of their greatest and currently most unstable factors.","That he could not allow.","The old man's eyes became resolute.","When dealing with summoners, beast tamers, necromancers, or any supernatural whose strength lay primarily in commanding others, there was one principle that remained almost universally effective.","Capture the leader.","The summoned creatures would either lose coordination, become significantly weaker, or simply stop fighting altogether.","Of course, the difficulty of doing so varied greatly depending on the individual. Still, removing the commander from the battlefield was almost always the fastest way to end a conflict.","Although he had only just arrived, the old man had observed enough. The blood-robed woman had made a fatal mistake.","If, from the very beginning, she had gone directly after Michael, the battle might never have reached this stage.","Of course, he didn't think she was stupid. Battles between high-tier individuals changed in fractions of a second.","Once the youth's undead had locked onto her, escaping to attack Michael would have become increasingly difficult. Perhaps from that moment onward she had been forced completely onto the defensive where one wrong movement would have cost her life.","Opportunities in battle were fleeting. Once missed, they rarely returned.","Which was why he intended to seize the opportunity himself.","The violent battle between three Demigod-level existences had already destabilized the first layer of the void.","Spatial ripples spread in every direction.","Countless invisible cracks silently appeared before healing again.","In an environment like this, even fighting at the edge of the destruction range would quickly influence the surrounding space, and when that happened, long-distance teleportation would become extremely dangerous.","Even short-range movement through space would have to be performed with great care.","If he wanted to act, now was the best time.","Since the young man refused to listen, he would simply stop him himself. In fact, this solution was even better.","The blood-robed woman would be captured, and so would the youth, if he valued his life. Two troublesome individuals resolved at once.","Hoping the youth wouldn't hold too much resentment afterward, the old man's body disappeared without warning.","At almost the exact same instant, Michael's expression changed.","He had only just given a command to his undead when his instincts screamed danger.","Every hair on his body stood upright. A terrifying sense of crisis engulfed him.","Without even thinking, his head snapped backward.","An old, weathered hand had somehow appeared barely inches from his face. The distance between them closed almost imperceptibly.","Five inches. Four. Three.","Michael's pupils shrank violently.","So fast.","He hadn't sensed the old man's movement at all. Not even the slightest fluctuation in space. His body couldn't react. His eyes barely managed to follow.","The old man's expression remained calm.","Just as his fingers were about to grasp Michael's shoulder, something changed. The old man's eyes widened slightly.","\"Hm?\"","The familiar sensation of gripping a human body never came. Instead, his fingers closed around something incredibly soft. Small. Warm. Covered in fur.","\"...A mouse?\"","No. A rodent.","The old man instinctively lowered his gaze. In his hand struggled an ordinary-looking rodent no larger than his palm, its tiny black eyes filled with complete confusion.","For the first time since arriving, the old man's calm expression cracked.","At the same moment, more than two hundred and fifty miles away, space distorted.","Michael suddenly appeared beside a small rock outcrop hidden within a dense forest. His breathing was uneven. Cold sweat soaked his back. His heart pounded violently inside his chest.","\"...That was close.\"","Long before this battle had even begun, Michael had already prepared for the possibility of someone bypassing his undead completely to reach him directly. Because of that, he had scattered countless insignificant creatures across the surrounding region, well outside the battlefield's destruction range.","Each one served as an anchor. The moment danger reached him, he wouldn't hesitate to use Wisdom's skill, Swap, and instantly exchange his position with one of those prepared targets.","Michael took a slow breath.","The old man's strength was indeed extraordinary.","If he had hesitated for even a fraction of a second, the creature currently holding that Demigod's attention would have been him instead."]},{"number":1158,"title":"Chapter 1158: Dead?","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, back on the battlefield, the tiny rodent never even understood what had happened.","The instant it appeared where Michael had once stood, countless terrifying auras crashed down upon its insignificant body.","The lingering pressure of two Demigod-level dragons. The blood-robed Demigod's aura. The Federation Demigod's presence. The unstable space itself.","It was simply too much.","The poor creature did not even have time to squeak. Its body burst into a cloud of blood before instantly disintegrating into ash. Not even a corpse remained.","The old man stared blankly at the empty space within his hand.","\"...\"","A spatial exchange?","His gaze became much more serious.","\"What an astonishing escape method...\"","For the first time, he felt he understood why the blood-robed woman had failed to capture this young man despite possessing overwhelming cultivation. His survival ability alone bordered on the absurd.","Unfortunately, there was no time to dwell on it.","A terrifying wave of energy erupted behind him. The old man's expression changed slightly. Without Michael's further commands, the Bone Dragon continued executing its last order.","ROOOOOOAAAAAR!!","The Bone Dragon's gigantic skeletal body descended from the heavens. Blue flames wrapped around its crystal-like claws. The surrounding sky dimmed. Even the unstable space trembled beneath the approaching pressure.","The old man sighed internally.","\"So it has come to this.\"","He gently raised one hand. There was no grand chant. No elaborate formation. Only a single drop of water appeared above his fingertip. The droplet was perfectly clear. No larger than a raindrop.","Yet the instant it appeared, the surrounding world changed.","Within only a fraction of a second, an enormous ocean had materialized above the battlefield.","The old man calmly pointed forward. The countless tons of water compressed instantly.","An ocean became a river. A river became a torrent. A torrent became a spear.","The water no longer resembled liquid.","It shone with a deep azure brilliance, compressed to such an extent that the surrounding space warped beneath its density.","Then it shot forward.","BOOOOOOM!!","The azure spear collided head-on with the Bone Dragon's descending claws. An explosion unlike any before erupted. The shockwave spread across the sky, tearing apart everything in its path.","The Bone Dragon's advance stopped completely. Its massive body was forced backward several kilometers. Several crystal-like bones along one foreleg cracked under the impact.","The old man's expression remained calm. He rotated his wrist gently. The shattered water spear exploded into countless ribbons. Each ribbon wrapped around one of the Bone Dragon's limbs like living serpents.","The dragon roared. Golden runes across its skeleton ignited.","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","One ribbon after another exploded apart.","The old man's eyebrows rose slightly.","\"What astonishing physical strength...\"","Against ordinary opponents, this single technique would have imprisoned them before they even realized what had happened. Yet this dragon simply tore through it using nothing but brute force.","The Bone Dragon spread its mountain-sized wings. The cracked bones repaired themselves almost immediately. Without hesitation, it charged again.","The old man's eyes narrowed.","\"So even that level of damage recovers almost instantly...\"","No wonder the blood-robed woman had been reduced to such a miserable state. Fighting one of these monsters was already exhausting. Facing two simultaneously, even for a Demigod, was a nightmare.","However, something had to be done.","The old man's eyes shifted away from the Bone Dragon for only a fraction of a second. Below, the Undead High Drake had already arrived above the blood-robed woman.","Its colossal body completely concealed her from view. From his current angle, he couldn't see what was happening beneath that enormous body.","But he didn't need to.","His expression changed.","\"...Not good.\"","His eyelids twitched. He could feel it. A terrifying concentration of energy was gathering around the dragon's head.","\"A dragon breath?\"","At point blank range?","His expression grew solemn.","Below, the blood-robed woman stared blankly upward. The gigantic head of the Undead High Drake filled her entire field of vision.","Its emerald eyes stared coldly at her as its jaws slowly widened. Green flames gathered between rows of enormous teeth.","One emotion after another surfaced inside her heart.","Anger. Fear. Helplessness.","The anger came first. She was a Demigod. Someone who had stood at the peak of countless beings. Reduced to such a miserable state. And not by another Demigod, but by the undead servants of a mere Rank three nineteen-year-old youth.","Every wound covering her body. Every shattered bone. Every drop of blood she had lost. All of it had been inflicted by someone whose age multiplied by twenty still wouldn't reach hers.","Her pride screamed in protest.","Then there was fear. She could clearly sense death approaching. The energy gathering within the dragon's throat made every instinct she possessed sound alarms.","She had witnessed creatures use dragon breath many times throughout her life. But never had one prepared to fire while almost touching its target.","There was nowhere to dodge. Nowhere to retreat. She would take the full force of it.","Then came the helplessness. An overwhelming feeling that no matter what she did, nothing would change.","Her cultivation was nearly exhausted. Her body had already reached its limit. Even lifting a finger required tremendous effort.","She had struggled desperately until now. Yet every attempt had ended in failure.","Then, when she had sensed a familiar aura, hope had ignited inside her chest. She hadn't expected rescue. She wasn't that naive. But as long as another Demigod arrived, she would live.","Perhaps she would spend centuries imprisoned. Perhaps she would suffer humiliation beyond imagination. It didn't matter. She would still be alive, as long as they didn't turn her into a puppet.","She hadn't sacrificed everything, hadn't crawled over mountains of corpses, simply to die here.","Life. As long as she remained alive, there would always be another opportunity. That was her belief.","Unfortunately, reality was far crueler.","Even after sensing the familiar aura, nothing had changed. The old man had indeed arrived. Yet he was now occupied by the other dragon. She could even feel violent fluctuations erupting behind her. Meaning he couldn't reach her in time.","The dragon's jaws continued opening. The terrifying energy continued condensing.","Death drew closer with every passing heartbeat."]},{"number":1159,"title":"Chapter 1159: Dragon Breath That Illuminated The Heavens","paragraphs":["The blood-robed woman slowly closed her eyes. For the first time in countless years, she felt genuine despair.","Above her, the Undead High Drake's emerald eyes glowed brighter than ever. The condensed sphere of destruction inside its mouth had already compressed to only a few meters across.","Its power, however, made the surrounding space continuously fracture before immediately healing again.","The old man's expression finally changed.","\"No!\"","Without another moment of hesitation, he abandoned all thoughts of restraining the Bone Dragon.","Saving the woman had become the absolute priority. His figure blurred. Water exploded beneath his feet.","The surrounding ocean he had created surged together once more, transforming into countless azure streams that wrapped around his body like flowing ribbons.","Every ounce of speed he possessed erupted at once. He shot toward the Undead High Drake like a streak of blue light, hoping he wasn't already too late.","The Undead High Drake paid the old man no attention whatsoever. Its emerald eyes never shifted. Its entire focus remained locked onto the blood-robed woman beneath it.","The dragon had no interest in complicated strategies. After battling her for so long, it had arrived at a very simple conclusion.","This enemy was extremely difficult to kill. Like an incredibly tough nut that refused to crack no matter how hard it was struck.","The High Drake had grown tired of it. Instead of wasting more time with claws and fangs, why not simply use the strongest attack available?","Surely, with such a sturdy body, she could survive one dragon breath.","That was the dragon's simple reasoning.","The sphere of emerald destruction within its mouth shrank further. One meter. Half a meter. Its terrifying power became even more concentrated.","The surrounding void fractured continuously under the pressure alone.","\"Stop!\"","The old man's shout echoed across the heavens. The High Drake ignored him completely.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!","A pillar of emerald dragon breath erupted downward. At such close range, there was no travel time. No opportunity to evade.","The destructive beam engulfed the blood-robed woman the instant it left the dragon's mouth.","The world turned green.","An explosion unlike anything before swallowed the battlefield. The void itself collapsed under the concentrated power. Space shattered layer after layer before desperately repairing itself.","The shockwave spread in every direction. Even hundreds of kilometers away, forests bent flat beneath the overwhelming pressure.","The old man's face darkened.","\"...Damn it!\"","He no longer cared about preserving the dragon. His hand rose. An immense torrent of compressed water condensed above his palm, carrying enough force to blast apart mountains.","If he couldn't save the woman, then at the very least he would suppress this troublesome dragon.","Just as he prepared to strike, a sense of danger exploded behind him.","His pupils contracted.","Without even turning, he instinctively twisted his body.","BOOOOOOOOM!!","A gigantic skeletal tail swept across the heavens. The Bone Dragon had arrived. Its mountain-sized tail carried terrifying momentum as it smashed toward the old man's back like a falling continent.","The old man barely managed to cross one arm behind himself. The tail struck. The impact detonated like a deployed bomb.","The surrounding air exploded into concentric rings.","The old man's figure shot across the sky like a blue comet, tearing through dozens of kilometers before finally stabilizing himself.","His sleeve had completely shattered. The arm he had used to block trembled slightly from the sheer force behind the blow.","The Bone Dragon lowered its tail before once again placing itself between the old man and the battlefield below.","Golden runes pulsed across its skeletal frame. Blue flames burned quietly within its empty eye sockets.","It made no sound and simply stared.","Behind it, the emerald radiance from the dragon breath still illuminated half the heavens. Whatever the outcome, the High Drake had already completed its attack.","The instant the dragon breath struck, the world shook. The earth itself groaned.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!","A deafening explosion echoed across the horizon. The impact drove deep into the ground beneath the battlefield. The destruction spread farther. And farther. And farther still.","More than two hundred miles away, the dense forest where Michael had hidden suddenly trembled violently.","Rumble. RUMBLE!!","The ground beneath his feet lurched sideways. Nearby trees swayed as though struck by a hurricane despite there being no wind. Loose stones rolled down the rocky slope.","Birds that had already been hiding out of fear exploded into the sky in frightened flocks.","Michael instinctively steadied himself against a nearby boulder. His pupils contracted.","\"So far away and I can still feel it?\"","Even after teleporting over two hundred and fifty miles away, the aftershocks of the collision still reached him. He slowly turned toward the distant horizon.","Although he couldn't see the battlefield itself, a blinding emerald light still illuminated the heavens. Even from this distance, it looked as though another sun had risen below.","\"...\"","Michael swallowed unconsciously. Every time he witnessed Demigod-level power, he became increasingly aware of just how absurd this realm truly was.","Even with his temporary advantages, he still wasn't truly standing at that level.","Not yet.","At the same time, back in Brightgate City, the battle had long since disappeared beyond the horizon.","Only a faint emerald and crimson glow occasionally illuminated the distant sky.","Suddenly the entire city shook.","Citizens who had only just begun calming down after the earlier attack cried out in alarm.","\"What was that?!\"","\"An earthquake?\"","\"The battle...\"","\"It has to be the battle!\"","People instinctively looked toward the distant horizon. Although they couldn't witness the fighting, the terrifying aftershocks told them enough.","Whatever was happening there had far exceeded their imagination.","Meanwhile, far above the shattered battlefield, the heavens still trembled from the collision. Gradually, the emerald radiance began to fade.","Far away, the old man stretched his senses beneath the Undead High Drake. A deep frown etched itself onto his face.","After a long breath, he disappeared. Only a single sentence remained, echoing across the ruined battlefield for miles.","\"Michael Norman, I hope our next meeting will be more peaceful.\""]},{"number":1160,"title":"Chapter 1160: Retrieving The Corpse","paragraphs":["More than two hundred and fifty miles away, Michael remained where he was. The old man's final words continued echoing in his ears.","\"Michael Norman, I hope our next meeting will be more peaceful.\"","\"...\"","His first reaction wasn't relief but suspicion.","A trap?","His eyes narrowed as he carefully observed his surroundings. After everything that had happened, he found it difficult to simply trust anyone from the Federation.","Over the past year, every interaction he had experienced with them had taught him one thing. Their morals were questionable. Not because they were necessarily evil. Michael couldn't entirely blame them. But understanding their reasoning didn't mean he trusted them.","The old man's words might genuinely be a gesture of goodwill. Or he might simply be trying to lure Michael out of hiding.","After all, the Federation Demigod had already witnessed his astonishing escape method. He could also very well be pretending to leave while watching closely.","Michael slowly shook his head.","\"No. I'll wait a bit more.\"","He remained hidden.","One minute passed. Nothing happened. Two minutes. Still nothing. Three full minutes passed. The forest remained completely silent, and there were no more terrifying fluctuations from the distance.","Only then did Michael finally lower his guard slightly.","\"...It really ended.\"","He looked toward the distant horizon.","\"I don't have much time.\"","The Enhancer. Its remaining duration was almost exhausted. His two pseudo-Demigod undead would soon return to their original strength.","Before that happened, if there was anything else that needed to be settled, he had to do it within the next few minutes.","Without another moment of hesitation, space rippled and Michael disappeared from his location.","Several moments later, Michael arrived back above the devastated battlefield. The sight before him left him momentarily speechless.","The battlefield had disappeared.","Everything within hundreds of miles had been transformed beyond recognition. Countless enormous fissures covered the earth like scars left by the wrath of the heavens. Even the air still crackled with unstable spatial fragments.","Michael silently flew lower. His eyes immediately landed upon the Undead High Drake. The enormous dragon lay inside an unbelievably large crater.","Nearby, the Bone Dragon stood guard, motionless like an ancient statue.","The old man was nowhere to be seen.","Michael's gaze swept across the surroundings several more times.","\"...He really left.\"","Despite that, Michael still didn't immediately descend. Instead, he spread his senses as far as possible. Only after several long moments without discovering anything unusual did he slowly fly downward.","He landed beside the gigantic head of the Undead High Drake. The dragon lowered its head slightly. A faint fluctuation of soul consciousness entered Michael's mind.","Michael's heartbeat quickened.","\"...Dead?\"","The High Drake confirmed once more. Its simple thoughts carried absolute certainty. It had watched the target lose every sign of life. Only then had it stopped attacking.","Michael stared at the dragon for several seconds. He trusted his undead. Still, he wasn't careless. Maintaining his vigilance, he slowly walked beneath the dragon's enormous body.","Only then did he finally see her.","The blood-robed woman's body lay at the center of the crater.","Almost everything within several hundred meters had melted into smooth, glass-like crystal from the overwhelming heat and energy. Her crimson robes had nearly vanished.","Her body was covered with horrifying burns. Countless bones protruded through blackened flesh. Even the surrounding blood aura had completely disappeared.","Most importantly, Michael could sense nothing from her.","Even so, he stopped dozens of meters away. His eyes carefully observed every detail. A Demigod was not an existence one approached carelessly until absolutely certain.","Only after confirming once more through the High Drake, and once more through his own senses, did Michael finally take another cautious step forward.","His heart began beating faster.","If she was truly dead, then lying before him was the corpse of his first Demigod victim.","Michael slowly crouched. His gaze never left the blood-robed woman's body.","Although the dragon breath had left her in a horrifying state, one thing immediately surprised him.","\"...It's still this complete?\"","Her skin had been almost completely burned away. Her robes had long since turned to ash. Large portions of flesh had been carbonized, exposing scorched bones beneath. Yet the body itself remained intact. Both arms. Both legs. The torso. Even her head. Nothing had been blown apart or reduced to dust.","A Demigod's physique truly exceeded imagination. After taking such a point-blank attack, her corpse still retained remarkable integrity.","Michael could not help taking a deep breath.","\"If this had been a Rank Four...\"","There probably wouldn't have been enough left to identify the victim.","Without wasting another second, Michael stretched out his hand.","The Mausoleum of Endless Dominion responded immediately.","A blue ripple spread beneath the corpse. Then the blood-robed woman's body slowly sank into the shadows before disappearing completely.","The moment the corpse entered the Mausoleum, Michael felt as though a tremendous burden had been lifted from his shoulders. His lips unconsciously curved upward.","His greatest harvest was finally secured.","With this he could immediately have a Rank Five undead, unlike the uncertainty he felt about evolving one of his own to that rank.","For some reason he felt it wouldn't be as simple as just raising a creature's racial grade. In any case, after reviving the female Demigod he planned to try several things he hadn't considered doing anytime soon.","Michael didn't remain distracted for long. His gaze shifted toward the Bone Dragon. The giant undead still stood vigilantly in place, blue flames quietly burning within its eye sockets.","Michael immediately waved his hand.","\"Return.\"","The Bone Dragon disappeared into the Mausoleum as well. The instant it vanished, Michael visibly relaxed.","Maintaining two Level 100 undead with his law skill simultaneously had placed an enormous burden upon him. He slowly exhaled.","\"Much better...\"","There wasn't much time remaining. He could already feel the Enhancer approaching its limit. Soon the Undead High Drake would also return to its original realm."]},{"number":1161,"title":"Chapter 1161: Clearing A Little Conscience","paragraphs":["Michael leaped lightly, landing atop the dragon's gigantic head, and placed one hand against the cold scale.","\"Let's head back.\"","The High Drake let out a low rumble. Its massive wings unfolded.","BOOM!","The enormous dragon rose into the sky before turning toward Brightgate City.","Several minutes later, the surrounding space quietly distorted. A figure stepped out as though walking through an invisible curtain.","Unlike the previous old man, this newcomer appeared much younger. He wore dark robes embroidered with unfamiliar silver patterns. His aura was completely restrained. Yet merely standing there caused the unstable space nearby to become noticeably calmer.","His eyes slowly swept across the devastated battlefield. The countless shattered mountains. The enormous craters. The lingering traces of dragon breath.","Finally, his gaze settled upon the direction Michael had departed. He clicked his tongue.","\"Tsk.\"","\"What a ruthless little fellow.\"","There wasn't much emotion in his voice. It sounded more like admiration than criticism. He lowered his gaze toward the empty crater where the Demigod's corpse had once rested.","\"...Not even the body was left behind.\"","He already knew what that meant. When it came to corpses and a necromancer, there had never been another outcome.","His gaze shifted. He looked toward the distant sky.","\"It seems Aurora has quite a few hidden powerhouses after all.\"","This tiny realm was becoming increasingly interesting.","After a moment, he smiled faintly and shook his head.","\"Forcing that boy to give up what he obtained from the Origin Will wouldn't be easy, it seems.\"","He paused. Trying to coerce such a person would likely produce the exact opposite result.","The newcomer cast one last glance toward the direction of Brightgate City. Then his figure quietly faded.","As though he had never existed. Only the devastated battlefield remained as silent proof that four Demigod-level powers had clashed there only moments before.","Michael was naturally unaware of what had taken place after he left the battlefield. At this moment, his attention was entirely focused on Brightgate City.","The Undead High Drake flew through the sky at tremendous speed. As the city gradually came into view, Michael's expression slowly became complicated.","The final battle had taken place far away from Brightgate. He had intentionally drawn the battlefield away from the city. Yet Demigod-level battles were simply too terrifying. The earlier aftershocks alone had been enough to affect everything for hundreds of miles.","From above, the consequences became painfully obvious.","Large sections of many structures had developed countless cracks. Smoke still rose from different parts of the city. Roads had split apart. Numerous houses had caved in after enduring repeated shockwaves.","People filled nearly every open street. Some were helping the injured. Others searched frantically through damaged buildings. Medical personnel and supernaturals rushed from one location to another.","Although the city had avoided complete destruction, it had still paid a heavy price.","Michael silently watched everything below.","\"...\"","A strange feeling rose inside his chest.","Objectively, none of this was his fault.","The blood-robed woman had been the one to attack Brightgate. She had been the one who forced the battle. No reasonable person could blame Michael for what had happened, since he had possessed no power to prevent any of it.","Objectively speaking, the Federation bore more responsibility for failing to contain a living, chaotic weapon without restraint.","He understood that.","Yet understanding something logically and feeling nothing emotionally were two different things. After all, if he had not been the target, this battle would never have taken place.","He couldn't save those who had already died. Not even a Demigod could casually reverse death. The dead should remain dead. Trying to violate that principle always came with a price.","However, there was still something he could do.","Michael's eyes suddenly brightened. He slowly looked beneath him. The Undead High Drake. It was temporarily standing at the threshold of Rank Five. Its control over mana had reached a level impossible for ordinary Rank Four existences.","True, the High Drake itself couldn't use healing magic. Normal undead weren't suited for that. But magic circles were different.","Magic circles relied less upon natural affinity and more upon precise construction and sufficient energy. And thanks to the countless insights he had unconsciously accumulated while cultivating, Michael possessed knowledge of an enormous number of lower-ranked healing formations.","He couldn't construct a genuine Rank Five healing array. That exceeded his current understanding. But did he really need one?","Michael immediately closed his eyes. Countless runes flashed through his mind. One healing array after another appeared before being rejected.","Finally, several different formations merged together. He continuously adjusted them. Removing unnecessary sections. Strengthening others. Expanding their area of effect.","Several minutes passed. Only then did Michael slowly open his eyes.","\"It'll do.\"","He placed one hand against the High Drake's skull. Immediately, an astonishing amount of mana surged from the dragon. The sky above Brightgate suddenly darkened.","Citizens instinctively looked upward.","\"What now?\"","\"Another attack?\"","\"Oh no...\"","Many people who had only just survived turned pale. Parents instinctively embraced their children. Even the city's defenders became tense.","Then countless emerald lines appeared across the heavens. One after another. Thousands. Tens of thousands. The lines spread outward in every direction, weaving together into an unimaginably enormous magic circle.","It continued expanding. Larger and larger. Until it completely covered Brightgate City.","Everyone stared upward in stunned silence.","\"...Is that magic?\"","\"So... large?\"","The formation rotated slowly. Its countless runes illuminated the heavens like stars.","Director Lin looked up in astonishment.","\"What is he doing...?\"","High above the city, Michael calmly extended both hands.","\"Activate.\"","BOOOOOOM!!","The enormous formation suspended above Brightgate erupted with dazzling brilliance. The High Drake's immense mana surged into every section of the magic circle.","Thousands of interconnected runes awakened one after another. For a brief moment, the entire city appeared to have gained a second sun.","The emerald radiance illuminated every street, every building, and every frightened face below.","Then the light softened.","Tiny droplets of emerald rain began descending from the heavens."]},{"number":1162,"title":"Chapter 1162: Glorious","paragraphs":["It wasn't ordinary rain.","Every single droplet was condensed life energy, purified repeatedly through the countless layers of the magic circle before finally becoming gentle enough for ordinary bodies to withstand.","Unlike violent healing spells that forcefully stimulated the body, this rain quietly nourished everything it touched.","The first droplets landed.","A middle-aged man who had collapsed against a broken wall looked down in disbelief. The deep gash across his abdomen slowly stopped bleeding.","The torn flesh visibly knitted together. The unbearable burning pain that had plagued him gradually faded until only numbness remained.","Nearby, a little girl covered in cuts instinctively reached toward her scraped knees. Before her mother could stop her, the wounds disappeared before their eyes.","\"...Mom?\"","\"They're... gone.\"","Her mother stared blankly before suddenly pulling the child tightly into her embrace, tears flowing uncontrollably.","Elsewhere, a middle-aged woman who had fractured her arm when part of her roof collapsed suddenly heard several soft cracks.","Crack... Crack...","Her bones shifted back into place. The swelling rapidly subsided. Within moments, she could move her fingers again. She flexed her hand several times in complete disbelief.","\"It... healed?\"","Not every injury disappeared completely. Severely crushed limbs remained damaged. Those missing body parts did not miraculously regrow. Yet every life-threatening wound rapidly stabilized.","Internal bleeding ceased. Damaged organs began recovering. Broken bones fused enough to prevent further deterioration.","Across the city, countless exhausted mages widened their eyes. Their nearly depleted mana reserves, drained from protecting civilians and maintaining defensive formations, slowly began recovering.","It wasn't enough to restore them completely. But it was enough to remove the terrible exhaustion weighing upon both body and soul. Many suddenly found themselves capable of casting spells once more.","However, it wasn't only the seriously injured that the rain touched.","An elderly woman trembling beneath a damaged awning suddenly froze. She slowly touched the side of her face.","For more than forty years, a long scar had stretched from her temple to her jaw after surviving a violent attack in her youth. It had never faded.","With Aurora's treatment technology she could have had surgery, but sometimes only the wealthy could afford to spend money purely on appearance.","Yet now, under the emerald rain, the scar gradually became lighter. The hardened tissue softened. Within several breaths, it disappeared completely.","\"...\"","Her wrinkled fingers continued tracing smooth skin. Tears quietly rolled down her cheeks.","Similar scenes unfolded everywhere.","Even old ailments began quietly improving.","A child who had suffered from chronic weakness since birth suddenly found breathing easier.","An elderly man whose eyesight had steadily worsened over the years blinked repeatedly before staring into the distance.","\"I can...\"","\"I can see...\"","Not perfectly. But far more clearly than before.","Across another district, a woman who had endured a persistent lung disease for years suddenly erupted into violent coughing.","Dark mucus mixed with traces of black impurities spilled onto the ground.","Several moments later, she inhaled deeply. For the first time in years, there was no pain, no tightness, no desperate struggle for air.","The emerald rain continued falling.","It wasn't omnipotent. It couldn't restore lost limbs, erase every illness, or reverse aging. And it certainly couldn't resurrect the dead. But to countless ordinary people, it was nothing short of miraculous.","Across the city, expressions of terror gradually transformed into stunned disbelief.","\"My wound...\"","\"It... it doesn't hurt anymore.\"","\"My daughter! She's breathing normally!\"","\"The bleeding stopped!\"","\"My scar... it's gone...\"","\"My back... I can stand straight again!\"","\"Look at Grandfather! He isn't coughing anymore!\"","One voice became ten. Ten became hundreds. Soon the entire city was filled with astonished cries. Many instinctively looked toward the heavens.","The giant emerald formation slowly rotated overhead. Some fell to their knees. Others clasped their hands together. Many simply stood in silence, unable to process what they had just experienced.","High above, Michael quietly observed everything.","His expression remained calm. He knew this wasn't enough. Those who had died would never return. Collapsed homes remained collapsed. Families already torn apart could not be made whole again. There were wounds no healing magic could ever mend.","But at least the living had been given another chance.","As the final streams of mana left the High Drake, the enormous magic circle gradually dissolved into countless emerald particles that drifted across the heavens like glowing stars before fading into nothingness.","Almost at the same moment, Michael felt the immense power flowing through the High Drake begin rapidly receding. The overwhelming aura that had rivaled a true Demigod steadily diminished.","The Enhancer had finally reached its limit.","Without hesitating for even a second, Michael raised his hand.","\"Return.\"","The enormous High Drake let out a low rumble before disappearing into the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion.","The moment it vanished, Michael immediately severed the connection maintained by Echoed Bestowal. An indescribable pressure disappeared from his soul.","\"...\"","Michael closed his eyes and released a long breath.","\"...Finally.\"","The last twenty minutes had been nothing but constant tension. Maintaining two pseudo-Demigod undead. Fighting a Demigod. Facing another from the Federation. Returning to retrieve the corpse. Then healing an entire city.","Every single action had pushed both his mind and body to their limits.","Fortunately, it was over. At least for now.","Michael remained floating in the sky for several seconds before slowly opening his eyes. There was still one final matter.","With a thought, hundreds of soul connections lit up within his consciousness. Scattered throughout Brightgate and the surrounding region, his Rank Four undead immediately received his command.","One after another, like countless black streams, they rose into the sky before converging toward Michael. Within moments, a vast undead legion once again assembled around him.","Only after confirming every Rank Four undead had safely returned did Michael activate the Mausoleum once more. The enormous legion disappeared batch after batch into the endless darkness. The surrounding sky gradually emptied.","Then space rippled and Michael disappeared.","A moment later, he reappeared inside his residence. His eyes instinctively swept across the room.","\"...Hm?\""]},{"number":1163,"title":"Chapter 1163: Removing Attention","paragraphs":["Michael's brows furrowed slightly.","When he had left, there had been four people. Now only three remained.","General Caelum was gone.","The brief silence didn't last long. Teacher Brian awkwardly scratched the side of his face. A faint trace of embarrassment appeared on the usually calm soldier's expression.","\"...General Caelum had to excuse himself. There were some important matters requiring his immediate attention.\"","\"...\"","Michael simply looked at him and said nothing. Yet something about Brian's expression, combined with the subtle odd looks exchanged between Director Lin and Instructor Yara, made the explanation feel somewhat forced.","Important matters.","Michael couldn't be certain. Nor did he particularly care. If anything, this arrangement suited him better. Among the Federation's higher-ranking officials, Teacher Brian was perhaps the only one Michael genuinely felt comfortable speaking with.","The others always made him feel as though every conversation concealed several hidden calculations.","Brian, at least, still felt like a teacher.","Unfortunately, Michael couldn't afford to relax.","Without the Enhancer's effect, he suddenly felt very vulnerable. If another Demigod appeared now, he had only one option. Run. And if he ran, everything he had displayed today would immediately be exposed as nothing more than a temporary bluff.","The room remained silent. Before any of the three could begin speaking, Michael raised a hand.","\"I'm afraid now isn't an appropriate time for a long conversation.\"","The three quietly nodded. No one could argue with that.","\"However...\" Michael continued. \"There is something I'd like the Federation and everyone else to know.\"","The expressions of the three immediately became serious.","Michael spoke calmly.","\"I don't know why the Origin Will issued that universal announcement. But I know what triggered it.\"","All three straightened unconsciously.","\"In the Fourth Layer of the Origin Battlefield, every Level Three Region contains a special treasure. Each one is protected by extraordinarily powerful monsters. Far stronger than the ordinary creatures inhabiting the surrounding regions. If someone defeats those guardians, they can claim the treasure.\"","He looked toward the three.","\"I suspect the treasure I obtained was one of them.\"","Silence filled the room.","After several seconds, Director Lin slowly asked,","\"You believe there are more?\"","Michael nodded.","\"I can't confirm it. But if the Fourth Layer contains more Level Three Regions, then logically the other layers should as well, if they follow the same layout. And if those regions follow similar rules, their treasures should also still exist.\"","He paused before adding one final sentence.","\"So instead of searching aimlessly, you should have your forces focus on finding Level Three Regions first. If my guess is correct, that's where the real opportunities of the Origin Battlefield are hidden.\"","The room became completely silent. The three Federation representatives looked at one another.","Although Michael had only spoken a few sentences, the strategic value of that information was enormous.","Michael, however, remained calm. There was a reason he had chosen to reveal this.","If it spread only within the Federation, that would be one thing. But he knew the Federation would never keep something like this entirely to itself. Pressure from outside would be coming soon.","And even if they managed to conceal it temporarily, they weren't capable of taking on an entire Level Three Region by themselves. They would need help from practically every organization with a Rank Four awakener in the Origin Battlefield.","In any case, eventually the information would inevitably spread beyond the Federation. That was precisely what Michael wanted.","After everything that had happened today, he really did not want to remain the sole focus of everyone's attention any longer.","The Universal Cornerstone. The Origin Will's announcement. All of it had already placed him beneath an uncomfortable spotlight.","If people believed he alone possessed opportunities from the Origin Battlefield, their eyes would naturally remain fixed on him.","But if everyone believed they could obtain similar treasures themselves, simply by exploring the Origin Battlefield and defeating its guardians, then those same eyes would gradually shift elsewhere. People would become busy chasing their own opportunities instead of chasing his.","It wasn't perfect. But it was far better than allowing himself to become the only known source of such treasures.","Besides, Michael wasn't lying. He simply hadn't confirmed everything personally. But based on everything he had observed, he estimated there was over a ninety percent chance his deduction was correct.","The remaining ten percent was simply caution. One should never speak in absolutes without proof, especially regarding something created by the Origin Will.","Director Lin slowly nodded.","\"...I understand. If this information proves correct, it will serve as valuable intelligence to a great many people.\"","Michael merely nodded in return. That was enough.","Suddenly, Instructor Yara, who had remained silent until now, spoke.","\"There is one thing I'd like to ask.\"","Michael looked toward her. She hesitated briefly before continuing.","\"The treasure... would it be possible for you to tell us exactly what it was?\" She quickly added, \"And perhaps what its function is?\"","The room became quiet once again. Teacher Brian unconsciously looked toward Michael. Director Lin did the same. No one interrupted.","Michael remained silent for several seconds.","Then he slowly shook his head.","\"I'm afraid not.\"","His refusal was polite. But absolute.","\"I've already shared what I believe can benefit everyone as a whole. As for the exact treasure and what it can or cannot do, I don't intend to discuss that.\"","There wasn't the slightest hesitation in his voice.","The atmosphere became somewhat awkward. Instructor Yara wasn't particularly surprised. Even so, a trace of disappointment flashed through her eyes. Director Lin gave a small, understanding nod.","\"I see. That was an inappropriate question.\"","Michael softly shook his head and said nothing.","Teacher Brian chuckled awkwardly.","\"It's fine to have your own secrets. In fact, I think you should consider not saying anything at all and let others figure it out themselves. It would draw fewer eyes your way.\"","He offered the advice kindly, if a little awkwardly."]},{"number":1164,"title":"Chapter 1164: Leaving","paragraphs":["Teacher Brian's words lingered in the room for a moment.","Michael simply gave a faint nod.","\"I know.\"","That was precisely why he had only revealed enough to redirect people's attention. Any more, and he would simply be replacing one problem with another.","He wasn't naïve. The Origin Will's announcement had already guaranteed that countless eyes would be fixed on him for quite some time.","There was no changing that. What he could change was the direction of those eyes.","A certain amount of mystery wasn't necessarily a bad thing. In fact, it could be useful.","If all people knew was that he had obtained something called a Universal Cornerstone, they would naturally become curious about what exactly it could do, and many would inevitably form their own guesses. But those guesses would also be restrained by the limits of their own imagination.","If his deduction proved correct, then every Level Three Region possessed its own treasure, meaning countless other Universal Cornerstones or similar treasures should still exist throughout the Origin Battlefield.","In other words, this wasn't some heaven-defying object created solely for Michael Norman. He was simply the first one to be discovered.","That subtle distinction changed everything.","People would naturally think: if someone else claims one, we'll find out sooner or later. That alone would greatly reduce the pressure focused entirely on him.","Instead of obsessing over stealing his, organizations would become far more interested in obtaining their own. Competition would shift from Michael to the Origin Battlefield itself. Exactly as he wanted.","If, however, he had opened his mouth and enthusiastically explained every function of the Universal Cornerstone, everything would have been different.","Imagine if he had revealed that it could awaken ordinary people, that it possessed countless miraculous abilities capable of changing the future of an entire civilization.","Forget curiosity and speculation. Every major power in Aurora would immediately conclude one thing.","They needed his Universal Cornerstone. Not another one. His. Whether through negotiation, pressure, or outright force.","Even if similar treasures existed elsewhere, who would willingly gamble on finding another one when they already knew where one was?","Michael had absolutely no intention of creating that situation for himself. It would be best if others across the universe started claiming Universal Cornerstones for themselves, so the heat of attention could be shared more evenly.","No one continued the discussion. The atmosphere had become noticeably lighter now that the important matters had been addressed.","Director Lin adjusted her clothes before speaking.","\"In that case, we won't disturb your rest any longer.\"","Her gaze briefly swept across Michael. Although he appeared composed, anyone paying close attention could see the exhaustion hidden beneath his calm expression.","Today's battle had undoubtedly taken a strong toll. Perhaps it had much to do with his rank, she speculated.","Instructor Yara also spoke.","\"...Thank you.\"","Michael looked at her. She continued after a brief pause.","\"For defending Brightgate.\"","Her voice carried genuine sincerity. Whether or not the battle had begun because of Michael wasn't something she cared to debate.","The fact remained that had Michael not fought, Brightgate would almost certainly have ceased to exist.","Michael merely nodded.","\"You don't need to thank me.\"","Teacher Brian stood last. His familiar smile returned.","\"Get some proper rest. You've more than earned it.\"","He hesitated before adding with a grin,","\"And try not to appear in the open for the next week at least. I'll make sure to have the Federation contact you through other means for the sake of your peace and safety.\"","A helpless smile finally appeared on Michael's face.","\"I'll do my best.\"","Brian laughed.","\"I'll hold you to that.\"","With a few final farewells, the three left together. The front door quietly closed behind them.","Click.","Silence returned to the house.","For several long seconds, Michael simply stood there without moving.","The moment he confirmed everyone had truly left, the tension supporting his body finally disappeared. He slowly walked over to a nearby chair and dropped into it.","\"...\"","He leaned back heavily. His entire body suddenly felt unbelievably tired. His mind replayed everything that had happened since entering the Origin Battlefield.","\"...What now?\"","He muttered quietly to himself. For the first time in quite a while, Michael genuinely didn't know his next step. His original plans had been completely overturned.","After sitting silently for nearly a minute, he finally looked around. Only then did he notice it properly.","The house was in miserable condition.","Long cracks stretched across several walls. The ceiling had shifted slightly from the repeated tremors. Pieces of plaster littered the floor. Even several support pillars showed obvious damage. The building still stood, but only barely.","Michael sighed.","\"...Aunt Mia isn't going to like this.\"","He could already imagine her expression. She had worked hard to make this place feel like a proper home. She had decorated it, cleaned it, and filled it with warmth. Now it looked as though it had survived a natural disaster. She would undoubtedly be upset.","Michael rubbed his forehead.","\"This is getting troublesome.\"","His eyes gradually became serious once more.","The house. Aurora. Brightgate. None of them felt safe anymore. At least not for him. Today's battle had changed too much. His identity had been exposed before multiple high-ranking existences.","Michael no longer felt comfortable remaining here without overwhelming protection.","The High Drake had reverted. The Bone Dragon was back to Rank Four. The Enhancer was on cooldown. His greatest trump cards had disappeared.","For the first time in a long while, there wasn't a single powerful undead standing beside him that made him feel secure.","That feeling made him profoundly uncomfortable.","\"...Everywhere suddenly feels too dangerous.\"","Remaining in Aurora now would simply be gambling.","Michael slowly stood.","\"There are things I can do somewhere much safer.\"","His gaze settled upon the empty space before him. With a thought, a familiar entrance appeared. A gateway leading to the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion.","Without another word, Michael stepped forward. His figure disappeared.","A second later, the portal slowly closed.","The damaged house once again fell into complete silence, its cracked walls standing as the only reminder that one of the greatest battles in Aurora's recent history had begun and ended with the young man who had just departed."]},{"number":1165,"title":"Chapter 1165: Buying Time [1]","paragraphs":["The moment Michael stepped through the portal, the atmosphere around him changed completely.","The air became cool and still. His feet landed softly upon damp grass.","Before him stretched a vast lake whose waters reflected the strange heavens overhead.","Unlike Aurora's blue skies, the Mausoleum sky was currently dark, painted with flowing streams of emerald and violet light that drifted across the heavens.","Occasionally, streaks of pale blue shimmered among them before fading into the darkness once more.","The colorful lights danced silently across the lake's surface, making the water appear almost otherworldly.","Michael stood quietly by the shore, letting the wind brush past him, calming his nerves.","A few seconds later, he slowly looked across the lake.","On the opposite bank, a lone structure stood beneath the strange sky. It resembled a modest manor one might find in a medieval era.","Constructed primarily from dark gray stone, its walls were thick and reinforced, giving it the appearance of a small fortified residence rather than a luxurious mansion.","The roof was covered with deep slate tiles that glistened faintly beneath the emerald sky. Warm golden light spilled gently from several narrow windows.","A sturdy wooden entrance stood at the front, protected by a simple stone staircase leading up to it. Low defensive walls enclosed a small courtyard where several lanterns emitted a calm blue glow.","The building wasn't large, possessing only two floors. Enough space to comfortably house a small number of people without feeling cramped.","There was nothing extravagant about it. No towering spires or elaborate decorations. Yet everything had been built with practicality in mind. Solid. Reliable. Comfortable.","Exactly the sort of place one could live in for months without complaint.","Michael's gaze softened slightly.","This was another achievement from the past several months. With such a vast world as the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion had to offer, he hadn't simply filled it with undead.","Aside from increasing the number of wild life forms this place contained, he had also constructed several facilities throughout its landscape, each one carefully positioned across different regions.","This lakeside residence happened to be one of the few structures intended primarily for living.","Michael's figure blurred. The distance of several hundred meters disappeared almost instantly. The next moment, he appeared on the opposite shore.","He walked forward at an unhurried pace. The stone path leading to the residence had been neatly laid, winding gently through patches of dark green grass and clusters of strange flowers whose pale blue petals glowed faintly beneath the night sky.","Several ancient trees surrounded the manor, their silver-gray bark reflecting the emerald light above while their dark leaves rustled softly despite the absence of any breeze.","The only sounds came from the gentle lapping of the lake against its rocky shore and the occasional distant cries of birds and frogs.","Outside of this, there was only silence. A silence that felt strangely comforting.","Michael climbed the short flight of stone steps leading to the entrance.","As he reached the heavy oak doors reinforced with black iron bands, he unconsciously relaxed further upon catching a faint sweet fragrance drifting from within.","He raised his hand.","Knock. Knock. Knock.","Several hurried footsteps sounded from the other side. A moment later, a click, and the heavy wooden door slowly swung inward.","Standing there was Lily. Her long hair had been casually tied back, and she wore simple, comfortable clothes she had brought from Aurora.","The warm light from inside the house illuminated her smiling face. Behind her stood Jester, maintaining his perfectly upright posture as always.","The two of them looked as though they had been waiting.","The moment Lily saw Michael, her smile widened.","\"You're back already.\" She stepped aside to let him enter. \"I thought you'd be gone much longer.\"","Michael paused for a brief second.","Only now did it truly register. He had entered the Mausoleum less than two hours after bringing Aunt Mia and Lily here. Outside, within those two hours, a Demigod had attacked.","An entire city had nearly been destroyed. He had fought a battle that shook hundreds of miles, claimed his first Demigod corpse, and obtained a Rank Five undead material. All before two hours had even passed.","In this supernatural world he had come to, anything could change in a matter of seconds.","Michael couldn't help smiling bitterly.","\"So much happened, and it hasn't even been half a day.\"","He muttered quietly.","Lily tilted her head.","\"Hm?\"","Michael gently shook his head.","\"Nothing.\"","He stepped inside. The warmth immediately embraced him.","Unlike the stone exterior, the interior had been carefully designed to feel welcoming. It was an unusual combination of two completely different eras.","The thick stone walls, exposed wooden beams supporting the ceiling, iron chandeliers, and broad fireplace all retained the atmosphere of an old medieval residence.","At the same time, modern comforts had been seamlessly incorporated throughout.","Soft fabric sofas surrounded a low wooden coffee table in the center of the living room. Large bookshelves occupied one wall, already holding dozens of books Michael had gradually collected over the months.","Warm crystal lamps provided steady lighting without producing smoke or soot. The dining area featured sturdy wooden furniture crafted with modern proportions, making it far more comfortable than traditional medieval designs.","Beyond it, an open kitchen contained both ordinary cookware and several modern appliances powered by battery electricity Michael had brought from Aurora.","Even the flooring reflected both styles. Smooth wooden planks covered most of the house, while darker stone tiles reinforced the areas around the fireplace and entrance.","Simple woven rugs softened the atmosphere further.","Michael slowly looked around.","Much of this place hadn't been built by him alone. His undead had done most of the physical work.","Jester had supervised almost every stage of construction, somehow displaying remarkable talent for architecture and organization despite being an undead.","The result was neither fully modern nor completely medieval.","\"...It's nice to be back.\"","Jester offered his own greeting.","\"Welcome back.\"","Those two simple words made the manor feel even warmer.","However, for Michael, the day had only truly begun. He had so many things to accomplish and so little time to accomplish them in."]},{"number":1166,"title":"Chapter 1166: Buying Time [2]","paragraphs":["Michael had barely taken a few steps into the living room before Lily caught up to him.","\"So?\"","She folded her arms.","\"What happened?\"","Michael looked at her.","\"What do you mean?\"","Lily stared at him as though he had asked the world's most obvious question.","\"You left in a hurry and came back looking so exhausted.\"","\"And you just said a lot happened.\"","She narrowed her eyes suspiciously.","\"So...\"","\"What happened?\"","Michael smiled helplessly.","\"I'll explain later.\"","Lily continued staring at him for several more seconds before finally sighing dramatically.","\"Fine.\"","Michael laughed.","Only then did Lily finally seem satisfied.","\"Good.\"","She pointed toward the kitchen.","\"Mom's cooking in the kitchen. You should go and greet her.\"","Michael nodded before walking toward the kitchen, the pleasant aroma becoming even stronger as he approached.","Stepping inside, he found Aunt Mia standing beside the kitchen counter with several freshly caught fish neatly arranged on a wooden cutting board.","She was carefully gutting another with practiced movements while two more already sizzled gently on the electric stove nearby, the quiet crackling of hot oil mixing pleasantly with the occasional hiss from the pan.","Hearing footsteps, she looked up, and the moment she saw Michael, a warm smile appeared on her face.","\"You're back.\"","Michael smiled in return.","\"I'm back.\"","For a brief moment, everything felt wonderfully normal. Then Aunt Mia's smile gradually faded as her eyes carefully studied his face, taking in the slight paleness, the tired eyes, and the faint weakness hidden beneath his usual composure.","Although he had recovered considerably after everything that had happened, his condition still wasn't something that could completely escape her. Her expression immediately became worried.","\"Michael...\"","She set the knife down.","\"Is something wrong?\"","\"You don't look well.\"","Michael knew immediately that hiding it was impossible, but there was no reason to make her worry even more, at least for now since he needed to soften the atmosphere before telling her some things. He smiled reassuringly.","\"I'm alright.\"","\"Just tired.\"","\"I've had... a rather long day.\"","Aunt Mia clearly wasn't completely convinced.","\"You should rest.\"","\"You've been working too hard lately.\"","Michael nodded obediently.","\"I will.\"","Not wanting her thoughts to remain on him, he deliberately shifted the conversation.","\"It smells really good.\"","He looked toward the fish on the stove.","\"Where did you find them?\"","Just as he expected, Aunt Mia's attention immediately shifted, and her worried expression softened into a smile once again.","\"Jester showed me.\"","She pointed toward the window overlooking the lake.","\"There were so many.\"","She laughed softly.","\"I've never seen fish so easy to catch before.\"","Then she looked around the kitchen.","\"And honestly...\"","\"I'm still amazed.\"","She slowly swept her gaze across the room.","\"You really built all this?\"","Michael nodded.","\"More or less.\"","She smiled warmly.","\"It's wonderful.\"","\"So Comfortable.\"","She gently ran her hand across the smooth wooden countertop.","\"When you said we needed to go somewhere for a little while I thought we'd be living inside some gloomy underground cave or something.\"","\"But this...\"","\"It feels like a real home.\"","Her eyes wandered toward the windows overlooking the lake.","\"The scenery is beautiful.\"","\"The air is fresh.\"","\"And it's so peaceful.\"","She smiled to herself.","\"I like it here.\"","Interestingly, she never asked how any of it worked, partly because Aunt Mia suspected many of those things were secrets Michael couldn't casually reveal.","But even more importantly, she simply wasn't interested in the mechanics; to her, it felt like anything Michael would say would sound impossibly complicated, and as long as he was safe, that was enough.","Michael found himself smiling, already knowing exactly where those fish had come from. Unlike many of the other creatures now inhabiting the Mausoleum, these particular fish had been introduced personally by him.","Over the past several months, Jester had been given enormous freedom to develop the Mausoleum. Countless plants, birds, small mammals, and even insects had been transplanted from Aurora or nurtured through the Land of Origin until entire ecosystems gradually formed.","At this point, even Michael couldn't confidently identify every species that now lived somewhere within his world unless he deliberately checked.","Jester had simply done too thorough a job.","But the fish in this land had been Michael's own idea. Back when he first began constructing this lakeside residence, he had envisioned occasionally spending a quiet afternoon fishing and had even gone as far as purchasing rods, hooks, lines, bait, folding chairs, and various fishing equipment from Aurora before transporting everything into the Mausoleum.","He remembered being strangely excited at the time, but unfortunately, reality hadn't matched the fantasy. Fishing turned out to be an exceptionally poor hobby for someone like him whose senses were far too sharp.","His perception extended beneath the water, allowing him to detect every movement of every fish within hundreds of meters. If he wanted, he could simply point at a particular fish and retrieve it instantly with telekinesis.","Waiting patiently for one to bite became almost impossible when he already knew exactly where every fish was swimming.","After trying it a handful of times, he had quietly admitted defeat, leaving the fishing rods in storage ever since while the fish themselves multiplied until they became today's meal.","The thought made Michael shake his head with an amused smile, glad that at least they hadn't gone to waste.","Michael's gaze drifted back toward the cutting board, and only now, paying closer attention, did he notice something he had overlooked: tiny puncture marks near the mouths of several fish, the unmistakable signs left behind by fishing hooks.","Michael blinked.","\"...Wait.\"","He looked at Aunt Mia.","\"You didn't catch these by yourself...\"","His eyes widened slightly.","\"...Did you?\"","Aunt Mia smiled brightly, looking almost embarrassed for a brief moment as she rubbed the back of her neck and gave a small nod.","\"I did.\"","Michael stared at her.","\"You went fishing?\"","Another nod.","\"I did.\"","Michael clicked his tongue silently, wondering why he was just finding out Aunt Mia was quite the fisher."]},{"number":1167,"title":"Chapter 1167: Buying Time [3]","paragraphs":["Aunt Mia let out a quiet laugh.","\"Jester actually offered to help but i wanted to try myself.\"","She smiled sheepishly, her expression becoming brighter than Michael had seen in years before slowly softening into something gentler carrying a trace of nostalgia as she looked through the kitchen window toward the peaceful lake outside.","\"...It's been eleven years.\"","Michael remained silent, sensing the change of mood in the atmosphere.","Aunt Mia continued quietly.","\"Eleven years since I started taking care of you.\"","Her fingers absentmindedly adjusted one of the fish lying on the cutting board.","\"And thirteen years since my husband passed away.\"","The kitchen fell quiet, with only the faint sizzling from the stove remaining as Aunt Mia smiled faintly.","\"You know...\"","\"I actually met him during a fishing trip.\"","Michael looked up.","\"I had just graduated from university and was attending a cooking academy afterward.\"","She laughed softly.","\"A few classmates invited me to spend the weekend fishing.\"","\"I almost didn't go giving so many excuses But they dragged me there anyway.\"","Her eyes gradually became distant as she recalled the past.","\"As it turned out there were actually a few cooking academies there too. That was where I meant your uncle.\"","Aunt Mia smiled to herself.","\"He was terrible.\"","\"...At fishing?\" Michael spoke slowly.","Aunt Mia nodded, unable to suppress a laugh.","\"He barely caught anything But he kept insisting he knew exactly what he was doing.\"","\"He spent more time untangling his fishing line than actually fishing.\"","Michael couldn't help laughing.","\"...That does sound like him based on the stories you told me.\"","\"It really does.\"","She chuckled.","\"By the end of the day...\"","\"I had caught more fish than he had.\"","\"He refused to accept it.\"","\"He insisted the fish were simply biased.\"","Michael laughed harder.","\"Biased?\"","\"Those were his exact words.\"","\"The fish preferred me.\"","She shook her head, still smiling at the memory.","\"He was ridiculous.\"","\"...And somehow...\"","\"I married him.\"","Silence returned, but this time it wasn't uncomfortable; it was peaceful as her smile slowly became quieter and more fragile.","\"When I saw the fishing rods here...\"","\"I couldn't help myself.\"","She glanced toward the doorway.","\"Jester offered to catch the fish for me.\"","\"But...\"","She looked back toward the lake.","\"I wanted to sit there.\"","\"Just for a little while.\"","She smiled again.","\"It felt familiar.\"","Michael finally understood that it hadn't been about catching fish, but about remembering someone and recalling a happier time.","Aunt Mia let out a slow breath.","\"I haven't gone fishing in years. I don't think I've touched a fishing rod since...\"","She stopped herself, knowing there was no need to finish the sentence because both of them already knew it had been since her husband died.","After that, life had simply become too busy, too full, and too demanding as she was left with two children to raise, facing school fees, rent, groceries, cooking, cleaning, and working to make sure neither child ever felt the absence of a parent.","Day after day, month after month, and year after year, her own hobbies had quietly disappeared somewhere along the way.","Michael remained silent as he truly thought about Aunt Mia herself—not as the dependable adult who always had everything under control, but simply as a woman who had lost the love of her life thirteen years ago.","Thinking back, he wondered when the last time she had gone out with friends or taken a vacation was, realizing the only period she had truly begun living for herself again was after he brought the family to Brightgate City, causing a tight ache in his chest.","Then Aunt Mia quietly spoke again.","\"...Michael.\"","He looked up.","Aunt Mia hesitated, her fingers unconsciously tightening around the kitchen towel in her hands before speaking very softly.","\"Are Lily and I...\"","\"...a burden to you?\"","Michael's heart skipped a beat, his expression freezing.","\"What?\"","He immediately opened his mouth.","\"Aunt—\"","But she gently shook her head before he could continue.","\"I'm not saying this because you've done anything wrong.\"","Her voice remained calm.","\"In fact...\"","\"You've done far more for us than anyone ever could.\"","She lowered her eyes.","\"You've given us a better home.\"","\"You've protected us.\"","\"You've made me younger.\"","\"You've shown us things I never thought could exist.\"","A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"But...\"","\"It also made me realize something.\"","She slowly looked at him again.","\"You seem to be carrying a lot on your shoulders. I don't know what it is but it's always like you're in a rush for something and sometimes I feel like Lily and I are part of the cause.\"","\"I've raised you for eleven years.\"","\"You don't hide your worries from me as well as you think.\"","Michael fell silent, feeling it wasn't entirely because he had inherited this body and its habits, but also because his original self was lacking in many departments.","Aunt Mia let out a quiet sigh.","\"I know we're ordinary and we can't fight or protect you.\"","\"We don't even understand half the things you talk about.\"","She forced a small smile.","\"Sometimes...\"","\"I wonder...\"","\"If Lily and I are only making your life harder.\"","Her voice became softer.","\"I don't want that.\"","\"I don't want to become chains around your feet.\"","Michael's chest tightened painfully as he reflected on how much he treasured this new life compared to his previous lonely, hospital-bound existence on Earth.","Having a mother figure like Aunt Mia, a sister figure like Lily, and if he stretched it a bit more tightly, a brother figure like Jester meant everything to him.","Aunt Mia smiled gently.","\"If we weren't here would your life be easier?\"","That was enough. Michael stepped forward, and before she could continue another word, he firmly took both of her shoulders with a grip that was resolute without being painful.","\"Aunt Mia.\"","His voice was unusually serious as she looked at him in surprise.","\"You are not a burden.\"","\"Neither is Lily.\"","\"Not now.\"","\"Not ever.\"","He didn't give her an opportunity to interrupt.","\"You are family.\"","\"Do you understand?\"","\"Family.\"","The word echoed through the quiet kitchen before Michael slowly pulled her into an embrace. For a brief moment Aunt Mia stood there in complete surprise, then she slowly relaxed as he held her tightly.","\"I only need a little more time.\"","His voice was quiet.","\"Just a little longer.\"","\"I'm almost there.\"","\"When everything settles down...\"","\"We'll go back.\"","\"We'll go back to living peacefully.\"","A faint smile appeared on his exhausted face.","\"I'll make sure of it.\"","\"No matter what happens.\"","\"I promise.\""]},{"number":1168,"title":"Chapter 1168: Evolution Candidate [1]","paragraphs":["At that moment, Michael had never been more certain of anything in his life. His old life on Earth had been lonely, spent mostly inside hospitals and empty rooms where he possessed almost nothing, whereas after arriving in this world, the original Michael's memories had gradually merged with his own until there was scarcely any difference between them.","The original Michael had truly lived while the Michael from Earth had barely been given the chance, and somewhere along the way the distinction between the two had disappeared, leaving only Michael Norman who knew he owed Aunt Mia immensely.","No matter what happened, he would protect that family at any cost.","Then Michael suddenly frowned as he felt something wrong, picking up an unusually faint fluctuation hidden within the atmosphere that Aunt Mia noticed nothing of.","Had his soul not become extraordinarily sensitive after everything that had happened, even he might have overlooked it.","Slowly turning around, Michael spotted Lily and Jester standing near the kitchen entrance, having apparently arrived some time ago.","Lily looked slightly embarrassed after realizing she had been discovered, while Jester stood perfectly still with wisps of transparent dark clouds dispersing around his body from a concealment technique.","\"...\"","Michael stared at him, his eyelids twitching.","\"...You.\"","Jester remained perfectly motionless.","\"...\"","\"What's the matter?\"","Michael narrowed his eyes.","1168 Evolution Candidate [1]","At that moment, Michael had never been more certain of anything in his life. His old life on Earth had been lonely, spent mostly inside hospitals and empty rooms where he possessed almost nothing, whereas after arriving in this world, the original Michael's memories had gradually merged with his own until there was scarcely any difference between them.","The original Michael had truly lived while the Michael from Earth had barely been given the chance, and somewhere along the way the distinction between the two had disappeared, leaving only Michael Norman who knew he owed Aunt Mia immensely.","No matter what happened, he would protect that family at any cost.","Then Michael suddenly frowned as he felt something wrong, picking up an unusually faint fluctuation hidden within the atmosphere that Aunt Mia noticed nothing of.","Had his soul not become extraordinarily sensitive after everything that had happened, even he might have overlooked it.","Slowly turning around, Michael spotted Lily and Jester standing near the kitchen entrance, having apparently arrived some time ago.","Lily looked slightly embarrassed after realizing she had been discovered, while Jester stood perfectly still with wisps of transparent dark clouds dispersing around his body from a concealment technique.","\"...\"","Michael stared at him, his eyelids twitching.","\"...You.\"","Jester remained perfectly motionless.","\"...\"","\"What's the matter?\"","Michael narrowed his eyes.","\"So you're the culprit.\"","No wonder Aunt Mia had suddenly begun voicing feelings she had buried for years. Jester's recent evolution to Rank Four as a Three-Star Epic undead had advanced his Law of Heavenly Revelation, allowing him to subtly orchestrate this entire emotional conversation.","Michael clicked his tongue.","\"Tsk.\"","He sighed mentally, realizing Jester was becoming increasingly troublesome—a terrifyingly intelligent subordinate capable of solving problems or creating entirely new ones.","Yet compared to the past, Michael found he wasn't particularly annoyed, acknowledging that perhaps this conversation had simply needed to happen.","He turned back toward Aunt Mia with his voice returning to its usual calmness.","\"I need to take care of something.\"","\"But I won't be gone long.\"","Aunt Mia nodded, and Michael smiled before looking toward Lily.","\"We still need to talk before the origin battlefield opens again.\"","\"...Okay.\"","Michael then slowly walked over to Jester, who politely inclined his head as though he hadn't just manipulated fate. Michael raised his hand and knocked his knuckles squarely on Jester's forehead.","\"...\"","Jester blinked in 'surprise'.","\"I shall interpret that as mild dissatisfaction.\"","Michael snorted.","\"You should.\"","Without saying another word, he left the manor as the door quietly closed behind him.","The next moment, his consciousness resonated with the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion, folding space and instantly transporting him to a broad stretch of rocky ground where dark elemental energy was concentrated at its highest.","Michael slowly raised a hand, sending a ripple through space that brought forth the corpse of the blood-robed Demigod, which still radiated an oppressive presence even in death.","Extending his connection to the Mausoleum, he directed an overwhelming suppressive force onto the corpse from every direction before finally stepping closer after confirming the suppression remained stable.","\"...Nothing.\"","He quietly exhaled, relieved that nothing unusual happened, though he remained vigilant knowing Demigods were notorious for their immense vitality and persistent survival traits.","Despite his caution, excitement surfaced in his eyes as he recognized this as his greatest harvest yet, eager to extract her memories before attempting a full resurrection.","Michael slowly extended his hand, letting his soul power gently reach toward the corpse.","The moment the connection formed, an invisible force erupted with a loud boom, causing his soul to tremble violently and forcing his consciousness away under a harsh backlash.","Severing the connection, he stepped backward and steadied himself, his brows knitting together.","\"...As expected.\"","His soul had barely escaped injury as the attempt failed completely due to two distinct layers of astonishing defenses protecting her memories: a natural remnant defense from her powerful soul, and an artificial lock far stronger than the first designed specifically to block memory extraction.","Even if Jester handled the task personally, it would take an enormous amount of time to dismantle those protections, and Michael couldn't afford to wait when he desperately needed power to protect his family.","He crouched beside the corpse, hovering his fingers above the blackened flesh before a deep frown appeared on his face.","\"...So that's how it is.\"","His earlier excitement faded as he confirmed that reviving this Demigod would require a specialized ritual using massive quantities of dark-element materials because the corpse was simply too powerful for ordinary resurrection methods.","Checking the resources stored throughout the Mausoleum, Michael's expression grew increasingly helpless as he realized he lacked the necessary dark-element materials, leaving him with no choice but to head to the Netherworld—a realm saturated with death where such resources were abundant.","Before entering the Netherworld, Michael turned his thoughts toward his alternative path to gaining Demigod-level power: advancing one of his existing undead through Evolution.","Although controlling a Rank Five undead at his current stage carried risks and flaws, he was now confident enough to attempt it.","Michael slowly folded his arms.","\"But the issue now is Which one?\"","Reviewing his candidates, he immediately ruled out Beginning due to the giant's overwhelming destructive instincts, and dismissed Lily for being just as reckless and prone to causing trouble.","Thinking of Jester, Michael instinctively rubbed his forehead.","\"...Definitely not.\"","Advancing Jester another entire realm made him uncertain of who would end up as whose subordinate, so he quickly set the idea aside.","Moving down the list, he passed on the Bone Dragon and High Drake, deciding it was better to keep their proven combat power intact.","As he ran out of options, a familiar figure quietly surfaced in his mind. His very first undead and oldest companion who had been with him from the start.","Lucky.","Michael slowly smiled.","\"...It's been a while.\"","Compared to the others, Lucky had gradually faded into the background as enemies grew stronger, but his foundation had been carefully tempered through selective evolutions to yield a massive potential ceiling.","There couldn't be a better candidate for attempting this new road."]},{"number":1169,"title":"Chapter 1169: Evolution Candidate [2]","paragraphs":["Michael raised a hand.","A dark tattoo suddenly appeared upon his forearm, illuminated with faint grey light. Ashes poured from the mark like an endless river before gathering several meters away.","The ashes gradually condensed. Within moments, the humanoid form became complete.","Standing before Michael was a tall young man appearing to be in his mid-twenties.","His long black hair flowed freely behind him, matching a pair of calm green eyes that carried an unusual gentleness despite his nature.","His features were refined, almost elf-like, while faint dark-green markings resembling vines spread beneath the skin around his neck before slowly fading with time.","The moment his body completely materialized, he immediately lowered himself onto one knee.","\"Master.\"","Michael gave a slight nod.","\"Stand.\"","Lucky obeyed without hesitation.","Unlike Lily's boundless enthusiasm, Beginning's silent brutality, or Jester's unsettling composure, Lucky possessed an almost tranquil temperament.","Yet the moment Lucky fully observed his surroundings, the peaceful expression on his face slowly disappeared and became slightly cold.","This wasn't directed at Michael, but at the surrounding environment.","\"...\"","Michael noticed it immediately.","One would expect an undead to feel comfortable within a place overflowing with death and darkness.","After all, this region inside the Mausoleum possessed one of the highest concentrations of dark elemental energy available.","Yet instead, Lucky looked uncomfortable.","Michael quietly smiled. Without another word, he connected his consciousness to the Mausoleum itself. Space rippled.","The surrounding rocky landscape instantly blurred before both of their figures disappeared.","The next moment, warm aurora light filtered through towering trees. A gentle breeze carried the scent of flowers.","Countless leaves rustled overhead while birds sang somewhere in the distance. A vibrant forest stretched endlessly before them.","The moment Lucky stepped onto the soft grass, his entire body visibly relaxed. The stiffness vanished. He slowly closed his eyes.","Michael found the contrast rather jarring. An undead, feeling more comfortable inside a living forest than a realm overflowing with death.","He quietly chuckled.","\"Perhaps.\" He looked at Lucky before continuing. \"You're only a monster. Not a villain.\"","Lucky opened his eyes.","\"I do not understand.\"","Michael smiled.","\"You don't need to.\"","To think that even after a year, and as a Rank Four undead, Lucky would still have its strange obsession with plants and grass.","It had only started becoming manageable once Michael engraved Lucky, giving it no choice but to remain in a passive state.","The same went for Lily. Of course, whenever he had free time he released both of them to do as they wished.","If he wasn't mistaken, Lucky seemed to have even developed more refined tastes, as it now appeared to enjoy tasting fruit. Well, it didn't have a true sense of taste, so it was more accurate to say it enjoyed the sensation.","Though given that it didn't feel much of anything unrelated to the soul, perhaps special plants that could actually be perceived were Lucky's true favorites.","For the sake of being practical, since the undead never complained, Michael had simply let it eat as much grass as it liked.","Michael shook the thought from his mind. There would be time to think about Lucky's peculiar nature later. For now, what truly mattered was whether his theory would succeed.","With a thought, a translucent panel that only he could perceive unfolded before his eyes. His gaze immediately landed on the familiar entry.","[Lucky - Undead Dire Wyvern]","Below it, another line quietly appeared.","Proceed with Evolution to Epic Grade ★★★?","To evolve an Epic Grade creature from One Star directly to Three Stars naturally required an astonishing amount of Evolution Points. Seventy-five thousand.","For Michael, it was expensive, but entirely affordable.","Among every creature currently under his command, only two had reached Three-Star Epic Grade. Wisdom and Jester.","The former wasn't an undead but his contracted beast. Jester was the only undead within the legion to have reached that level.","Michael's lips curved slightly. For all of Jester's troublesome personality, there was no denying his worth. With Lucky joining the ranks, the number of Three-Star Epic Grade creatures under him would become three.","Without the slightest hesitation, Michael made his choice. The number of Evolution Points within his panel instantly decreased.","At almost the same moment, a brilliant white light erupted beneath Lucky's feet. The light expanded at an astonishing speed, swallowing his entire figure before forming a perfectly spherical cocoon nearly five meters across.","Michael quietly observed the cocoon for several more moments. The brilliant sphere remained suspended in place, releasing rhythmic pulses.","\"...\"","After confirming that everything remained normal, Michael slowly turned around.","There was no point standing here any longer. Epic Grade evolutions weren't quick. At fastest, just over two days. At most, just over three. Lucky wouldn't emerge anytime soon.","Of course he could have remained here. The phenomena surrounding Epic Grade evolutions were extraordinarily valuable, capable of aiding one's comprehension considerably.","For someone like Michael, whose greatest bottleneck had gradually shifted toward cultivating a law domain, spending several uninterrupted days watching Lucky evolve would undoubtedly bring considerable benefits.","He silently looked back at the cocoon one last time.","\"...A shame.\"","He simply didn't have that luxury. His schedule had become completely packed.","The Origin Battlefield would reopen soon, and the Netherworld demanded immediate attention because of the Demigod corpse. Even thinking about it caused a slight headache.","Michael let out a quiet sigh.","\"I haven't even had the chance to use that treasure yet.\"","His thoughts drifted toward the Incense of Enlightenment.","Ordinarily, if the Universal Cornerstone situation hadn't happened, Michael would have immediately entered secluded cultivation the moment he obtained it.","Unfortunately, everything after acquiring it had unfolded far too quickly.","Michael rubbed the bridge of his nose.","\"...It really never stops.\"","His consciousness connected to the Mausoleum once more. The surrounding forest gradually distorted before his figure disappeared without a trace.","Silence returned.","Only the enormous cocoon remained beneath the towering trees.","Far away, within another region of the Mausoleum, Michael reappeared on a mountain range where a gigantic creature lay."]},{"number":1170,"title":"Chapter 1170: First Time In The Netherworld [1]","paragraphs":["A gigantic creature rested across the mountain peak. Its body stretched well over two hundred meters, crimson scales overlapping like forged plates of metal beneath the dim sky of the Mausoleum.","Even while lying motionless, an overwhelming aura radiated from it, causing the surrounding air to become still under its mere presence.","Yet there was something unsettling about the scene. Despite possessing such terrifying pressure, the enormous creature gave off no sensation of life whatsoever. There wasn't even the slightest fluctuation of vitality.","Of course, that was only natural. It was Michael's undead. His Undead High Drake. After exhausting itself through Echoed Bestowal, it had reverted to its original form to recover within the Mausoleum.","Echoed Bestowal itself possessed remarkably few side effects compared to abilities of similar caliber. That was one of the reasons Michael regarded it so highly.","However, few did not mean none. Whether it was the caster or the recipient, using Echoed Bestowal imposed a considerable burden.","Even undead, who normally ignored concepts such as fatigue and exhaustion, required time to recover after invoking the ability.","Michael quietly observed the enormous corpse-like creature. Compared to before the skill had been revoked, the aura leaking from its body was far less chaotic.","\"...It's stabilized.\"","Not completely, as it wasn't in a state ready for another peak battle, but enough to be usable. There was no longer any reason to leave it outside.","In fact, back in Aurora Michael could have returned it to its engraved state, but that would have required him to revoke his skill in front of everyone, revealing that his false dragon had essentially been running on borrowed power.","Michael slowly raised his right hand.","\"Return.\"","The command had barely left his lips before the High Drake's colossal body dissolved into countless streams of grey ash.","The process happened astonishingly quickly for a body so large.","The endless river of ash rapidly compressed, becoming thinner and thinner before rushing toward Michael.","The torrent circled around him several times before finally sinking beneath the skin of his left shoulder.","A new engraving slowly appeared.","Michael instinctively rolled his shoulder, adjusting to the added weight.","\"...Much better.\"","The engraving state remained one of his class greatest conveniences. Not only did it allow him to carry his strongest undead without exposing them, it also significantly increased his base power.","Unfortunately, the added weight was a constant nuisance. Without careful control, even to an outside observer, carrying him would be akin to a strong person hauling two full sacks of rice without respite.","Michael took a deep breath to calm his nerves, communicating with the Mausoleum at the same time as he called out a panel detailing the treasure's features.","[Item]: Mausoleum of Endless Dominion","[Grade]: Legendary ★","Bound to Michael Norman","[Description]: A legendary treasure born from a strange fusion. It contains a vast self-sustaining inner world.","[Effect 1]: Eternal Dominion Contains a massive internal world capable of sustaining life, death, and spiritual existence simultaneously.","The domain possesses mountains, rivers, forests, plains, and naturally regenerating mana. The owner may freely shape terrain, climate, and environmental conditions within certain limits.","Undead residing inside receive accelerated growth, recovery, and comprehension speed. Living creatures may also inhabit the domain without restriction.","[Effect 2]: Nether Gate The owner may open a gateway connecting the domain to the Netherworld. The gate can be used to travel, summon undead, or establish temporary links between both realms.","Summoned undead may be up to one rank above the owner's rank. Duration and energy consumption depend on the strength of the summoned entity.","[Effect 3]: Dominion Pulse The treasure may release a spatial shockwave. The pulse disrupts formations, barriers, domains, spatial structures, and weaker treasures while inflicting spiritual damage upon living targets. Power scales with the amount of energy supplied.","[Effect 4]: Tomb of Rebirth If the owner is killed, their soul will be anchored within the Mausoleum. After a period of recovery, the owner may resurrect within the Netherworld.","Each resurrection permanently consumes a portion of the treasure's accumulated origin energy.","Currently, the treasure can perform this function twice before becoming dormant for one hundred years.","[Effect 5]: World Seed (Sealed)","The internal domain possesses the potential to evolve into a true independent world. Growth requires vast quantities of origin energy. Current Progress: 0.01% Michael quietly read through the familiar panel.","Although he had already examined it countless times, he still found himself letting out a quiet sigh.","\"...\"","No matter how many times he looked at it, the feeling never truly disappeared. A Legendary Grade treasure really was in a class of its own.","Whether it was the enormous internal world, the ability to freely travel to the Netherworld, the terrifying Dominion Pulse, or even the unbelievable resurrection ability, every single effect could cause countless Rank Fives to fight to the death.","To think he could obtain a treasure of this level with just one million Evolution Points.","Of course, it was only because he had taken over a vast force and absorbed decades of accumulated resources that he could afford it in the first place.","Only a little over a year ago, Michael would have considered even ten thousand Evolution Points an unimaginable fortune.","At present, he controlled roughly four thousand undead capable of continuously gathering Evolution Points for him.","Without participating in any major battles or obtaining extraordinary opportunities, he estimated it would take approximately nine months to accumulate one million Evolution Points.","Nine months. For one or two Legendary Grade treasures every year.","Unfortunately, the Mausoleum wouldn't be evolving anytime soon. Not because he couldn't gather the Evolution Points, but because the evolution system itself had changed after reaching the Legendary Grade.","Unlike the previous grades, where a single evolution could directly advance from One Star to Three Stars, Legendary worked differently.","Every single star required an independent evolution, with each costing five times the previous amount. At least, he hoped it was five times and not something worse."]},{"number":1171,"title":"Chapter 1171: First Time In The Netherworld [2]","paragraphs":["Michael slowly exhaled, forcing the restless thoughts inside his mind to settle. There was no point dwelling on future evolutions.","Whether it required five million Evolution Points or fifty million, none of it would change what he had to do today.","His attention shifted toward the second effect of the Mausoleum.","Nether Gate.","Just like Hell, the Netherworld was an independent realm.","A vast world spanning areas far surpassing any ordinary realm, one that existed under its own set of rules, which could differ from universal ones at times.","Throughout countless civilizations, it had been given different names, yet every description carried one common theme.","The Land of the Dead.","It was a place where the living did not belong.","Michael's fingers unconsciously tightened.","\"...\"","If he claimed he wasn't nervous, he would only be lying to himself. His previous trip into Hell had nearly cost him everything.","Now he intended to enter an even more mysterious realm with almost no firsthand knowledge whatsoever.","Yet he had no choice. The Demigod's resurrection demanded dark-element treasures of extraordinary quality. The Netherworld possessed them in abundance.","Michael's eyes gradually became resolute.","\"What has to be done has to be done.\"","After a quiet sigh, Michael communicated his intention to the Mausoleum.","At almost the same moment, the entire mountain trembled. Space directly before him began folding inward. Unlike ordinary spatial portals, this one didn't tear.","Layer after layer of space quietly descended into impossible darkness. An enormous circular gateway gradually emerged. Its edges resembled weathered black stone engraved with ancient runes Michael couldn't recognize.","Grey flames silently burned along its circumference without producing heat. Within the center there was no light. Only endless darkness.","The darkness slowly rotated like a bottomless whirlpool. An icy aura drifted outward, carrying a profound silence.","Michael stepped forward.","The moment his body crossed the threshold, the darkness swallowed him whole.","There was no sensation of falling, no feeling of movement, no perception of time. The only thing Michael could perceive was silence.","Then his feet touched solid ground.","Michael slowly opened his eyes.","A chill immediately crept through his body. The air felt impossibly dense with energy.","Every breath carried astonishing concentrations of death-element mana, several times richer than even the Mausoleum's darkest regions.","Above him, there was no sun. No moon. No stars. Only an endless expanse of dark grey sky, where enormous rivers of pale blue light drifted silently across the heavens like ghostly auroras.","The land stretched endlessly in every direction. Black earth. Grey stone. Countless dead forests. Mountains rising in the distance like the ribs of enormous buried beasts.","Michael remained perfectly still. His senses instinctively expanded, carefully probing the unfamiliar world around him.","\"...\"","Then his brows gradually furrowed.","Something was wrong. No, wrong wasn't the correct word. Unexpected.","Contrary to everything he had anticipated, the Netherworld didn't reject him in the slightest. For a living being with, to be humble about it, one of the most powerful constitutions in his rank, that was remarkable.","Instead, it felt comfortable.","Michael slowly inhaled. The dense death-element mana entered his body naturally, flowing through his meridians without the slightest resistance.","There was no suffocating pressure, no sensation of corruption, no feeling of his life force being eroded. If anything, he felt strangely refreshed.","Michael's expression became thoughtful.","Compared to when he had first awakened over a year ago, Michael now possessed considerably more knowledge about the Netherworld, even if it wasn't extensive. Certainly not enough to be considered an expert. Just enough to understand its basic nature.","The Netherworld wasn't merely rich in death energy. It was a world whose fundamental laws favored death over life.","Every living creature entering this place would instinctively be rejected by the environment itself. Their vitality would slowly diminish. Even their souls would gradually suffer erosion if they remained for extended periods.","Naturally, creatures possessing affinity with darkness or death fared considerably better, such as necromancers, dark mages, and similar existences.","However, better did not mean unaffected. Even a Rank Four Necromancer would eventually suffer consequences. After all, they were still living beings.","Yet Michael felt absolutely nothing. If anything, every breath seemed easier than the last. The dense death-element mana surrounding him almost behaved as though it were welcoming his arrival.","\"...\"","His thoughts rapidly turned. Was it because of the Mausoleum? No. The Mausoleum merely opened the gateway. It wasn't actively protecting him. His physique?","Also unlikely. His constitution certainly granted remarkable resistance against negative energy, but it shouldn't completely negate the Netherworld's influence.","Then a realization suddenly surfaced within his mind.","\"...My class.\"","Michael's eyes widened slightly.","Death's Heir.","The title quietly echoed within his thoughts. Unlike ordinary classes obtained through awakening, Death's Heir wasn't simply an enhancement to his abilities.","It was a special class. One that fundamentally altered his relationship with the concept of death itself.","Only now, after stepping into the Netherworld, did he understand that this class went beyond simply granting dominion over the dead.","He had known this in a general sense, but he hadn't expected it to make him feel like a fish returned to water in the Netherworld itself.","\"...I see.\"","A faint smile slowly appeared on his face. It wasn't until he had changed classes that he truly began to understand how absurd special classes could be.","Michael slowly looked toward the endless grey horizon.","\"If that's the case, this expedition should be quite fruitful.\"","His confidence quietly increased.","Of course, he didn't become careless because of this discovery.","Comfort did not equal safety. This world was not an empty one. The Netherworld remained one of the most mysterious realms in existence. Even if the world itself accepted him, its inhabitants might not.","Taking one final glance at the pale blue auroras stretching across the endless sky, he chose a direction and began walking."]},{"number":1172,"title":"Chapter 1172: Natives [1]","paragraphs":["Michael continued walking for a few minutes.","The landscape remained eerily unchanged.","Every where he looked was filled with grey earth and dead forests. Not even the wind seemed willing to disturb the silence that blanketed the Netherworld.","There were also natives around, causing Michael, who had initially started to feel comfortable, a little tense.","Just as Michael was beginning to wonder whether this region was completely deserted, his footsteps gradually slowed. Several hundred meters ahead, something moved in his senses.","Click.","Clack.","Click.","The faint sound of hard objects colliding echoed through the empty wilderness. Michael's gaze sharpened as a group of skeletons slowly emerged from behind a cluster of black, leafless trees.","There were roughly twenty of them. Most stood between six and seven feet tall, their yellowish white bones carrying numerous cracks. Deep within each empty skull burned a dim blue soul flame.","\"...\"","Michael quietly observed them from a distance. Oddly enough, despite being a necromancer for over a year, this was actually the first time he had ever encountered naturally existing undead skeletons.","The realization caused a strange expression to appear on his face. It sounded almost ridiculous. His legion numbered in the thousands, yet never ordinary skeletons.","Of course, there was a reason for that. Michael couldn't really be considered a traditional necromancer.","From the very beginning, his path had diverged from that of ordinary practitioners, and even though he focused on corpses, thanks to his talent even his flesh zombies turned out different from the usual.","His first bone-derived undead had to be stolen from another necromancer. In any case, his understanding of skeleton-type undead mostly came from books rather than firsthand experience.","Michael's eyes calmly swept across the group. *Hmm, I can't sense any other presence around. So it seems these skeletons are natives?* For necromancers, there were generally two major methods of obtaining undead skeletons.","The first involved personally crafting skeletons using suitable skeletal materials before igniting them with soul fire. The second was summoning them directly from the Netherworld.","After all, if there existed one place in existence that never lacked undead, it was here. The Netherworld was the birthplace of countless naturally formed undead races.","Many necromancers throughout history had established contracts with tribes or summoned wandering undead directly from this realm instead of painstakingly creating every soldier themselves.","Michael's expression became thoughtful. The group continued marching without formation, seemingly unaware of Michael's presence.","Michael narrowed his eyes. Thanks to Death's Heir, he could vaguely perceive faint fluctuations surrounding each skeleton.","Weak. Very weak. Individually, none of them even approached Rank one.","This much wasn't surprising, as the types he could see didn't seem to be from any special race. Their race grade was probably a one star common grade creature.","Against his current strength, they posed virtually no threat.","Michael quietly watched them for a few more moments before making his decision. Since arriving in the Netherworld, this was the first truly interesting thing he had encountered.","Compared to walking around aimlessly, he wondered if he could get any information from these undead.","The concealment technique surrounding his body gradually dissipated. His aura, previously hidden, was no longer restrained.","Click!","The skeletons instantly stopped walking and their blue soul flame flickered violently.","The next moment.","Clack, clack, clack.","The entire group abruptly charged toward Michael.","Their movements were crude yet surprisingly swift, bone feet colliding against the black earth as they rushed forward.","Michael remained completely calm. His fingers subtly moved as he prepared to release a single wave of pressure enough to suppress every one of them.","However, before he could do anything, when the skeletons were forty meters away from him, they all froze simultaneously.","Before Michael could understand what was going on, without any warning, the leading skeleton dropped to the ground kneeling.","The others reacted just as quickly, throwing themselves to the ground as well.","Clack!","Clack!","One after another, all twenty skeletons prostrated themselves before him. The sudden movement was so forceful that several of them literally fell apart.","One skeleton's left arm flew a few meters away from it. Another's lower jaw detached and rolled across the ground. The third somehow managed to lose an entire leg after kneeling too quickly.","Yet none of them appeared concerned. The limbless skeleton calmly crawled toward its missing arm, picked it up, and pressed it back against the shoulder.","Click.","The bone immediately reattached as though nothing had happened. Another casually retrieved its detached jaw before fixing it beneath its skull with practiced familiarity.","Within moments, the entire group had reassembled itself. Then they returned to bowing.","\"...\"","Michael remained silent. This development had been completely unexpected.","Through his senses, Michael could faintly perceive the fluctuations within their soul flames. It was primitive, simple, instinctive. Yet hidden within it was something unexpected.","...Joy?","Michael frowned. That didn't seem right.","Undead weren't supposed to experience emotions so clearly. Even highly intelligent undead such as Jester, Beginning, or Lily didn't truly feel emotions in the same way living beings did.","They understood them and could imitate them, but genuine emotional fluctuations were extraordinarily rare.","These skeletons were just lowly rank zero creatures even goblins would disdain to ambush. Yet Michael could distinctly sense something resembling happiness. Or perhaps it was excitement.","It does seem like it, but there's also a hint of reverence.","It was difficult to describe. The feeling wasn't transmitted through expressions. After all, skeletons possessed no faces.","Instead, their soul flames themselves were fluctuating, almost as though they had encountered something they had been searching for.","Michael quietly observed them.","\"...Interesting.\"","None of the skeletons raised their heads. They simply remained prostrated before him in absolute silence.","The only sound echoing through the barren landscape was the occasional click of loose bones settling back into place.","Michael slowly stepped forward. The moment he moved, every soul flame trembled simultaneously. That strange feeling became even stronger.","\"...\"","His eyes gradually narrowed. This isn't because I'm strong...","If it were merely the difference in strength, they would have displayed instinctive obedience. Not this. This was almost worshipful reverence.","Michael's thoughts immediately drifted toward the source of everything that had been unusual since entering the Netherworld.","\"...Death's Heir.\"","The title quietly surfaced once more. Ever since arriving, the world itself had welcomed him. Now even the lowest native undead appeared to instinctively recognize something about his existence.","Michael couldn't help but wonder. Just what did the title Death's Heir actually represent in the Netherworld?","Or perhaps it wasn't the place itself that made his class even more unusual, but rather because this was his first true experience with a wild undead.","The bone dragon didn't count, as it had been stolen from its master without much resistance in a few seconds."]},{"number":1173,"title":"Chapter 1173: Natives [2]","paragraphs":["Michael suppressed his growing curiosity for the moment.","For now, the skeletons in front of him were his first real source of information in this seemingly barren world.","With a thought, he activated Detect. A series of translucent panels immediately appeared above the prostrating skeletons.","[Skeleton Patrol]","[Grade: Common ★]","[Level: 2]","...","[Skeleton Patrol]","[Grade: Common ★]","[Level: 4]","...","[Skeleton Patrol]","[Grade: Common ★]","[Level: 5]","Michael calmly examined each one. Just as he had expected, they were all One-Star Common-grade creatures.","Their levels ranged from two to five, meaning none of them had even entered Rank One.","They were weak. Extremely weak.","Even an ordinary awakened teenager who had just received a combat class could probably deal with several of them without much difficulty.","Hmmmm. As long as they had good initial training.","However, Michael barely paid attention to their levels or race. What truly caught his interest was the name displayed above every one of them.","Skeleton Patrol.","\"Patrol...\"","Michael's eyes brightened slightly. That single word told him more than their entire status panels combined.","A patrol did not wander without purpose. That meant something had assigned these skeletons a territory, or one they had assigned themselves to.","Whether they served a tribe, settlement, or some other gathering of undead, their existence strongly suggested that others were nearby.","Michael's lips curved into a faint smile.","\"That's good.\"","He had entered the Netherworld searching for dark-element resources. Although the surrounding environment was saturated with death energy, wandering aimlessly through such a vast realm would be inefficient.","Natural treasures did not simply lie everywhere waiting to be collected.","However, wherever intelligent or semi-intelligent undead gathered, there would almost certainly be resources.","Depending on their strength, the value of the resources also varied.","If these few undead were the dominant race of their settlement, whatever resources they had would most likely be scarce. But at the very least, a gathering would give him a proper direction.","Michael lowered his gaze toward the skeletons.","\"Raise your heads.\"","The skeletons immediately obeyed. Twenty skulls lifted in near-perfect unison, blue soul flames flickering inside their hollow eye sockets.","Michael attempted the simplest approach first.","\"Where did you come from?\"","Silence.","The soul flames trembled.","Michael waited.","Nothing happened.","\"Is there a settlement nearby?\"","The skeletons continued staring at him. One tilted its head. Another copied it.","Soon, nearly half of the group had their skulls leaning at different angles, as though the motion itself would help them understand.","\"...\"","Michael's eyelid twitched. He tried again, simplifying his words.","\"Others.\"","He pointed toward the skeletons.","\"More like you.\"","Then he gestured toward the surrounding wilderness.","\"Where?\"","The blue flames flickered much more intensely. A faint response finally travelled through the strange connection between them.","It was not words, nor were they proper thoughts. Only several extremely crude impressions.","\"Many. Bones. Near. Return.\"","Michael focused on the impressions, attempting to extract something clearer, but the result remained frustratingly vague.","\"There were others nearby.\"","That was all he could understand. The skeletons possessed some degree of awareness, but their intelligence was simply too low for proper communication.","Even with the advantages granted by his class, Michael could not force thoughts into minds that barely possessed them.","He sighed.","\"So you really are stupid.\"","The skeletons' soul flames continued flickering happily, apparently taking his statement as praise.","Michael stared at them for a moment.","\"...Right.\"","Expecting anything more would be pointless. Fortunately, he did not need them to explain. They only needed to show him.","Michael pointed toward the direction from which they had originally arrived.","\"Return.\"","The skeletons remained still.","Michael tried again.","\"Go back.\"","No reaction.","His brows furrowed before he adjusted the command, infusing a trace of his will into it.","\"Lead me to the others.\"","The effect was immediate. Every soul flame erupted with brighter blue light.","Clack!","The leading skeleton sprang to its feet so violently that its skull nearly flew from its spine. It quickly caught its head with both hands, twisted it back into place, and turned around.","The other skeletons rose just as eagerly. Once the group had reassembled itself, the leading skeleton faced Michael and lowered its skull respectfully. Then it began walking.","The rest followed behind it. Their previous scattered formation disappeared. This time, they arranged themselves around Michael in a loose circle, almost as though they intended to escort him rather than merely guide him.","Michael observed the formation with a strange expression. Although they were weak and barely intelligent, their reverence toward him was unmistakable.","Even now, their soul flames continued radiating that inexplicable happiness.","\"Death's Heir...\"","He quietly repeated the name of his class.","Without further delay, Michael followed the skeleton patrol deeper into the dead forest. The sound of rattling bones once again echoed through the silent wilderness.","Click.","Clack.","Click.","The march continued for several minutes without incident. The dead forest gradually became denser, its blackened trunks growing closer together.","Michael remained at the center of the loose formation while the skeleton patrol moved around him with surprising diligence.","Then, clack, clang, a different sound echoed from ahead. Unlike the light rattling of loose bones, this noise carried the unmistakable scrape of metal.","Michael's gaze shifted forward. Another group emerged from between the dead trees.","There were fewer of them, perhaps twelve in total, but they were clearly different from the first patrol. Their bones were larger and darker.","Most importantly, they were equipped. Rust-covered breastplates hung crookedly over their rib cages. Bent helmets rested unevenly upon their skulls.","Several carried chipped swords, while others wielded spears with warped iron heads. One skeleton even possessed a shield, though the shield was so badly damaged that nearly half of it was missing.","The equipment looked terrible. Some pieces were tied together with strips of leather. Others appeared to have been hammered into shape by someone who had only heard about blacksmithing through rumours.","Still, compared to the nearly bare skeletons surrounding Michael, they appeared almost elite. Their levels were also noticeably higher.","Michael activated Detect.","[Skeleton Guard]","[Grade: Common ★★]","[Level: 12]","...","[Skeleton Guard]","[Grade: Common ★★]","[Level: 11]","...","[Skeleton Guard Captain]","[Grade: Common ★★]","[Level: 15]","Michael raised an eyebrow. To think they had all entered Rank One. It was not impressive by his standards, but it confirmed that the settlement ahead possessed some form of hierarchy.","The newly arrived skeletons noticed the first patrol almost immediately. Their blue soul flames flickered. Then their attention shifted toward Michael.","For a brief moment, they froze. The guard captain raised its crooked sword.","Clang!","The others immediately spread into a crude formation. Unlike the patrol, these skeletons displayed some discipline. They lowered their weapons and charged.","Michael watched calmly.","\"So this group is more intelligent.\"","The first patrol around him made no attempt to defend him. Instead, they simply stepped aside.","The guards rushed closer.","Thirty meters.","Twenty.","Ten.","Then, just like before, their movements abruptly stopped. The guard captain's raised sword slipped from its hand.","Clang.","Its soul flame surged violently. A moment later, it dropped to both knees.","The rest followed. One after another, the armoured skeletons threw themselves onto the ground. Their battered equipment made the scene far noisier than before.","Clang!","Crash!","Clatter!","One skeleton bowed so hard that its crooked helmet flew from its skull and struck another in the back. Another lost half of its breastplate, which fell apart in three separate pieces.","The skeleton holding the broken shield accidentally planted it into the ground and snapped off what remained of its arm. It calmly picked up the detached limb, reattached it, and resumed bowing.","\"...\""]},{"number":1174,"title":"Chapter 1174: Another Outsider? [1]","paragraphs":["It was the familiar scene again. Reverence. Excitement. That strange happiness flowing through their soul flames.","Since he was expecting it, Michael wasn't surprised.","Perhaps in the land of the dead, with a title like Death's Heir, he could probably be considered royalty.","Indeed, unique classes were truly in a special category of their own.","Compared to the first patrol, the emotions from these skeletons were clearer and more organised.","The guard captain slowly lowered its skull until its forehead touched the black earth.","Michael looked down at the kneeling guards, noting the weapons in their hands.","Since the Netherworld was a realm not many ventured to or dared to venture to, there wasn't a lot of information about it, so even the knowledge of a beginner like Michael was even more lacking compared to those seniors.","While he expected natives to exist in this world, he didn't expect a civilization-type settlement like this.","However, though he was amazed, Michael focused on the most important thing. The sighting of these relatively more organized patrols showed their gathering was close.","\"Take me to your settlement.\"","The guard captain's blue soul flame blazed brightly. It rose at once, retrieved its crooked sword, and turned around.","The other guards stood as well, gathering the scattered pieces of their armour before forming two uneven lines. The original patrol moved behind Michael. The guards positioned themselves ahead.","Just like that, what had begun as a group of wandering skeletons transformed into a strange ceremonial escort. Michael walked between them, his expression thoughtful.","After walking for several more minutes, the dead forest finally began to thin. The blackened trees gradually grew farther apart, revealing a wide stretch of open land ahead. Beyond it, a settlement came into view.","Michael immediately raised a hand.","\"Stop.\"","The command spread through the strange connection between them. Every skeleton halted at once. The guards at the front froze mid-step while the weaker patrol behind him stood perfectly still, their blue soul flames quietly flickering.","Michael stepped forward until he reached the edge of the forest. Rather than approaching immediately, he remained hidden behind the last few rows of dead trees and carefully observed the settlement from afar.","It was crude. Extremely crude.","A crooked wall surrounded the entire gathering, constructed from countless bones, black stones, rusted metal plates, and pieces of wood that appeared to have been gathered from the dead forest.","The wall barely reached five meters in height. Several sections leaned dangerously to one side, looking as though a strong enough wind might collapse them.","At regular intervals, taller platforms rose above the wall. Skeletons stood upon them carrying bows made from bone and dark wood, though Michael doubted most of the weapons could survive more than a few shots.","Behind the walls were numerous buildings. Some were formed entirely from stacked bones. Others resembled huts made from black stone and rotting timber.","At the centre of the settlement stood a much larger structure, rising nearly three times higher than the surrounding buildings. It was still crude, but compared to everything else, it could almost be called a palace.","Michael narrowed his eyes.","\"That must belong to the chief.\"","Along the way, he had attempted to extract more information from the guard captain. The process had been frustrating. Although the captain was considerably more intelligent than the original patrol, communicating with it was still far from easy, unless he resorted to harvesting its soul fire for its memories. But for creatures like this, their soul fire wasn't strong, and the information he might end up getting wouldn't be satisfactory.","Michael had been forced to simplify every question into basic words, gestures, and intentions. Even then, most answers arrived as incomplete impressions.","Fortunately, after several attempts, he had managed to understand the basic structure of the settlement.","At the top stood the chief. Below the chief were the warriors. The guards escorting Michael belonged to that group. After them came the citizens. At the bottom were the militia.","The weak skeleton patrols Michael had first encountered belonged to this lowest group. They were responsible for wandering the surrounding territory, gathering basic materials, watching for threats, and serving as the settlement's first line of defence.","Or, more accurately, its expendable first line of defence. Basically, \"cannon fodder.\"","Michael glanced at the skeletons behind him. The patrols continued staring at him happily, entirely unaware of his thoughts. His expression became slightly strange.","The qualification for becoming a citizen had also caught his attention. According to the captain, a skeleton needed to be \"awake\" to become one.","Michael initially misunderstood the meaning. After further questioning, however, he realised that \"awake\" referred to intelligence.","A skeleton had to possess enough awareness to understand orders, perform specialised tasks, and communicate basic thoughts.","In other words, the citizens probably possessed intelligence similar to the guards. That suggested most of them had already entered Rank One.","Unfortunately, Michael had no idea how many skeletons lived inside the settlement. He had tried asking the captain but only received a vague impression.","But now that he was finally close by, he could estimate the exact population from where he stood. There were certainly hundreds. Perhaps more than a thousand.","Still, Michael felt no concern. Even if every skeleton inside had entered Rank One, they posed less of a threat to him than a pinch of sand thrown against a mountain.","His current strength had already reached a level where numbers alone were meaningless unless they were sufficiently powerful.","A thousand Rank One skeletons? He could suppress the entire settlement without taking a single step.","Michael folded his arms.","\"What I need to know is whether their chief is any different.\"","The settlement's organisation suggested that the chief possessed far greater intelligence than the others. Perhaps it was a stronger skeletal race, or maybe even some unusual variant native to the Netherworld.","Yet based on the strength of the guards and patrols, Michael doubted the chief could exceed Rank Two. Rank Three at the absolute highest. Nothing worth worrying about.","In fact, Michael suspected the settlement would welcome him. After all, every native undead he had encountered so far had instinctively shown him reverence."]},{"number":1175,"title":"Chapter 1175: Another Outsider? [2]","paragraphs":["Unless the chief possessed a completely different perception, there was little reason to expect hostility.","\"Perhaps I really am considered some form of royalty here.\"","The thought was absurd. Yet the evidence continued supporting it.","Michael's gaze swept across the settlement once more. Near the central building, he noticed a large stone platform covered in faint blue flames.","Several skeletons continuously carried black crystals toward it before dropping them into a pit at its centre. The crystals melted almost immediately, releasing dense waves of energy that spread across the settlement.","Michael's eyes sharpened.","\"Resources.\"","That was the true reason he had come here. The settlement might be weak, but weak did not mean useless. Even low-level undead required materials to survive, strengthen themselves, repair their bodies, and evolve.","Whatever resources they possessed might not be enough for the Demigod ritual, but they could provide Michael with clues. Perhaps they traded with stronger settlements, or perhaps they served a larger skeletal kingdom. Perhaps they even knew where richer regions could be found.","In any case, this small settlement could become his first foothold in the Netherworld.","Michael slowly lowered his hand. The guards and patrols immediately became attentive.","\"Continue.\"","The guard captain's soul flame flared. It turned toward the settlement and raised its crooked sword. The entire escort resumed moving.","As they emerged from the dead forest and entered the open land, the skeletons standing on the settlement walls quickly noticed them. Several blue soul flames flickered.","Then the watchers spotted Michael walking at the centre of the procession. For a moment, the entire wall became silent.","Michael sensed countless gazes locking onto him. Then, clang, a weapon fell from one of the watchtowers.","The skeleton that had dropped it suddenly collapsed to its knees. Another followed. Then another.","Within seconds, every skeleton upon the wall had bowed toward him.","Michael watched the sight with narrowed eyes.","\"As expected.\"","However, before he could take another step, a powerful soul fluctuation erupted from the large structure at the centre of the settlement. It was considerably stronger than anything he had sensed so far.","The doors of the central building slammed open. A towering figure emerged.","Michael's gaze immediately focused on it.","\"So that's the chief.\"","The chief was an imposing sight. It stood nearly three metres tall, towering over every other skeleton in the settlement.","Its bones were not the dull yellow-white of the patrols or guards but a deep metallic grey, with thin violet lines running across them like veins.","A long mantle made from stitched strips of black hide hung from its shoulders. Across its ribs rested several pieces of dark armour shaped far more carefully than the crooked equipment worn by the guards.","Although the armour remained crude by Michael's standards, it was clearly the finest craftsmanship this settlement possessed.","In its right hand was a long staff. Or perhaps calling it a staff was inaccurate.","The lower half resembled a heavy metal spear, ending in a sharp black point, while the upper portion split into several crooked branches that surrounded a fist-sized purple crystal.","Faint mist flowed within the crystal.","\"A hybrid weapon?\"","Michael studied it carefully. It appeared capable of functioning as both a staff and a close-combat weapon.","That alone suggested the chief was not merely a physical warrior. Perhaps it possessed some form of magical ability as well.","The towering skeleton stepped out of the central building and stopped at the top of a broad staircase overlooking the settlement. Its violet soul fire burned steadily within its hollow eye sockets.","Michael waited. Based on everything he had experienced so far, he expected the chief to kneel like the others.","However, it did not.","Instead, the skeleton tightened its grip around the strange staff and stared directly at him. The soul flame within its skull flickered once. Then a clear voice spread through the settlement.","\"Outsider.\"","Michael's expression changed. The voice was low but distinctly feminine.","\"What business do you have here?\"","\"...\"","For the first time since entering the Netherworld, Michael was genuinely caught off guard. It spoke. More importantly, it spoke in the Universal Common Tongue.","Michael's eyes narrowed slightly as he examined the towering skeleton more carefully. The fact that it possessed no flesh or vocal cords did not matter much.","There were countless methods through which powerful or intelligent undead could produce sound, whether it was creating vibrations through magic or transmitting its thoughts directly into the minds of others.","There were too many possible explanations for Michael to determine the exact method immediately.","What mattered was how did it know he was an outsider? Except for his appearance, even his living aura was almost entirely concealed.","Was it because of my appearance? If so, it seems flesh-like zombies like my undead aren't common here.","\"Interesting.\"","Michael's thoughts moved quickly. Was the skeleton similar to Li Yang?","Li Yang had been an outsider Michael summoned from the Netherworld roughly a year ago. He had not originated from this realm but had somehow become trapped within it after death. Perhaps this chief had experienced something similar. Maybe she had once lived in another world before dying and awakening here as an undead.","If so, her memories could be extremely valuable. She might know the surrounding territories, and perhaps she even knew the location of stronger undead settlements or valuable dark-element resources.","A faint trace of excitement surfaced within Michael's eyes.","From this distance, Michael could already sense the strength of her soul fire. She had not entered Rank Three. However, she was extremely close.","Peak Rank Two. Perhaps only a single opportunity separated her from advancement.","More importantly, the stability of her soul flame far surpassed that of every other skeleton in the settlement. Her intelligence was clearly no weaker than that of an ordinary person. Possibly even higher.","That alone made her far more useful than the nearly mindless patrols and barely articulate guards.","Michael stopped several dozen metres from the settlement gate. The skeletons surrounding him remained bowed, creating an unusual contrast between the chief's caution and everyone else's reverence.","His gaze moved briefly across the walls. Every skeleton continued kneeling. Even the guards who had escorted him had lowered their heads.","Only the chief remained standing.","Michael looked back at her.","\"You recognised me as an outsider.\"","It was not a question.","The violet flames within the chief's skull narrowed slightly.","\"Yes.\"","Her voice remained cautious.","\"What do you want? If you have no business here, please leave.\""]},{"number":1176,"title":"Chapter 1176: What Do You Mean By Aurora? [1]","paragraphs":["Michael's interest deepened.","\"Are you an outsider as well?\"","The chief did not answer immediately.","Michael glanced around him.","\"Should I take that as a yes?\"","The chief's grip tightened around her staff. A low pulse spread from the purple crystal. Several guards near the gate trembled, though none dared rise.","The chief's violet soul flames fixed upon Michael. Silence spread across the settlement.","Michael felt his curiosity intensify. He placed both hands behind his back.","\"I didn't come here to attack your settlement.\"","The chief remained motionless.","\"Then why have you come?\"","\"I'm searching for dark-element resources.\"","The violet flames within the chief's skull flickered.","\"What kind?\"","\"High-quality ones.\"","The chief fell silent. For the first time, the soul flame within her skull showed something resembling hesitation.","Michael noticed it immediately.","\"You know something.\"","The purple crystal at the top of her staff pulsed once. The chief slowly descended the staircase. Each step caused a metallic sound to echo through the settlement.","Clang.","Clang.","Clang.","She stopped before the gate, still several dozen metres away from Michael.","\"I know of places where such things may exist.\"","Michael's smile grew slightly.","\"Good.\"","\"However...\"","The chief tilted her skull.","\"I have no reason to give that knowledge to an outsider.\"","Michael's eyes remained calm. That was fair. Information had value, especially within a realm like the Netherworld.","\"What do you want in exchange?\"","The chief looked toward the kneeling skeletons. Then back toward Michael.","\"I want to know who you are and how you came here.\"","Michael's expression did not change.","\"That's a difficult question.\"","The violet flames narrowed.","\"Then give me a difficult answer.\"","For several seconds, the two simply stared at one another across the settlement gates. Then Michael quietly laughed, the sound fading almost as soon as it appeared.","Interesting or not, the chief appeared to have misunderstood something. She was indeed unusual. Unlike the weaker skeletons, she possessed enough intelligence, strength, and self-awareness to resist the instinctive influence of Death's Heir.","However, resistance was all it was. She had not freed herself from that influence. She was merely enduring it.","Michael could sense the tension within her soul flame and the constant effort required to remain standing before him. Every second she resisted, the violet fire inside her skull trembled more violently.","That alone proved her uniqueness. Yet uniqueness did not grant her the right to negotiate with him as an equal.","Perhaps if she had been a living being, Michael might have shown more patience. Even if she were weak, he would have acknowledged her as an independent person and treated her with a certain degree of respect.","But she was undead. No matter how open-minded Michael considered himself, some instincts were difficult to erase completely.","Undead were monsters. Intelligent monsters, perhaps. Monsters capable of loyalty, reason, preference, and even something resembling emotion. Yet still monsters.","To be honest, this was a prejudice undead races like vampires still faced throughout the wider universe. But interestingly, even they would see many undead types as monsters.","Michael's eyes gradually became colder.","\"You appear to be mistaken.\"","The violet flames inside the chief's skull narrowed.","\"About what?\"","Michael did not answer. Instead, he released a bit of his aura infused with his will and pressed down on his surroundings.","Every blue soul flame dimmed at once and the air became impossibly still.","The chief froze. Her fingers tightened around the hybrid staff.","Crack.","A fracture appeared across one of the bones in her hand. Her violet soul flames flared violently as she fought against the invisible authority descending upon her.","Michael watched calmly.","\"So you can resist.\"","The chief's body trembled. One foot slid backward. The sharp end of her staff dug into the ground as she used it to support herself.","\"You...\"","Her voice emerged strained.","\"What... are you?\"","Michael ignored the question. He strengthened his will slightly. The effect was immediate.","Boom!","The chief's knees struck the black earth. The force shattered the stones beneath her and sent several cracks spreading outward. Her staff slipped from one hand but remained gripped in the other.","The violet flames inside her skull surged wildly. She attempted to rise, but her arms shook and her spine creaked. For a brief moment, she managed to lift one knee from the ground.","Then Michael's authority pressed down once more.","Clang!","The chief collapsed completely. Both hands touched the earth. Her skull lowered despite her desperate resistance.","The surrounding skeletons remained perfectly still, their soul flames burning with even greater reverence than before.","Michael slowly approached. The distance between them disappeared one measured step at a time.","Clack.","Clack.","Clack.","The chief continued struggling. It was futile. The difference between them was not merely one of strength. This was an authority engraved into the very nature of her existence.","She could oppose Michael's mana. She could resist his soul pressure. She might even survive a casual attack from him. But resisting Death's Heir was different. It was like a flame attempting to reject the concept of heat.","Michael stopped several metres before her.","\"Raise your head.\"","The command carried his will. The chief obeyed instantly. Her skull lifted even though every movement showed her reluctance.","The violet soul flames stared directly at him. Michael examined them closely.","There was obedience. Absolute obedience. If he commanded her to release her weapon, she would do so. If he ordered her to reveal the settlement's resources, she would comply. If he told her to walk into destruction, her body would move before her will could refuse.","However, the result was not identical to the reactions of the weaker skeletons. There was no blind worship. No overwhelming joy. No complete surrender of identity.","The chief still possessed herself. Her pride remained. Her thoughts remained. Even her hostility and suspicion had not disappeared.","She simply could no longer disobey him.","Michael's eyes showed a trace of surprise.","\"...Interesting.\"","*This gives me a bit more insight into my abilities as Death's Heir.* The weaker skeletons had practically lost themselves in reverence the moment they sensed him. This chief, however, retained a distinct identity despite being placed under his absolute authority.","She did not see him as a god and did not consider herself an object created for his use. She knew who she was. She simply recognised, or had been forced to recognise, that his authority stood above her own.","Michael's curiosity deepened. With a thought, he activated Detect. A translucent panel appeared above the kneeling skeleton chief.","[Skeleton Chief]","[Grade: Epic ★★★]","[Level: 49]","\"...\"","Michael stared at the information for several seconds. Then he read it again.","Epic Grade. Three Stars. Level Forty-Nine.","What was this?"]},{"number":1177,"title":"Chapter 1177: What Do You Mean By Aurora? [2]","paragraphs":["This was the first time Michael had ever encountered an Epic-grade creature so weak.","Normally, a creature's grade reflected the strength of its race, bloodline, abilities, and potential. Even a newly born Epic-grade creature should possess a considerable advantage over ordinary beings that had to start from the bottom.","Yet this skeleton was still only Level Forty-Nine. She had not even crossed into Rank Three.","More astonishingly, she was a Three-Star Epic creature. Was this skeleton perhaps in a weakened state?","Until now, the only Three-Star Epic creatures Michael had personally seen were those under his command. Wisdom. Jester. And soon, Lucky.","Two of them possessed terrifying strength and extraordinary abilities that separated them from ordinary creatures of the same rank. Yet the skeleton before him was different. Her aura was impressive compared to the rest of the settlement, but it was nowhere near what Michael expected from a Three-Star Epic existence.","His eyes narrowed.","\"There has to be a reason.\"","Whatever the explanation was, one thing had become certain. She was special. Far more special than Michael had initially assumed.","A Three-Star Epic undead with human-level intelligence, possibly also from another world, and the ability to partially resist Death's Heir. There was no chance he would simply leave her behind.","Michael's gaze lingered on the violet soul flames within her skull. At first, he had only intended to obtain information from her. Now, his plans had changed.","He wanted her. Not merely her memories. Her entire existence.","Once he had extracted everything useful from her, he would ensure that she became part of his legion. A creature with this much potential was too valuable to abandon in a settlement filled with Common-grade skeletons.","Michael's lips curved into a faint smile.","\"You continue to surprise me.\"","The Skeleton Chief's soul flames flickered. She could clearly sense that something about his gaze had changed.","Michael allowed the silence to linger for a moment before returning to the question she had avoided.","\"Are you an outsider?\"","The Skeleton Chief's violet soul flames flickered. Her resistance had already been crushed beneath the authority of Death's Heir. Even if she wanted to remain silent, her soul could no longer reject a direct command from him. More importantly, she could not lie. This was the extent of Michael's absolute authority.","The chief lowered her skull slightly.","\"Yes.\"","Michael's eyes sharpened.","\"As expected.\"","The answer confirmed his suspicions, but it was far too vague to satisfy him.","The Skeleton Chief remained silent for a brief moment before continuing.","\"I was not born in this world. But I have become part of it.\"","Michael frowned. The answer was technically clear, yet somehow tasteless. It gave him almost nothing.","\"Elaborate.\"","The command carried a faint trace of his will.","\"In the material world, I was betrayed by someone close to me.\"","Her voice remained calm, but Michael sensed the faint disturbance spreading through her soul flame. It seemed that even after everything that had happened, the memory still affected her.","\"I had reached the final stage before advancement with my law. My soul was complete. My understanding was sufficient. I only needed to take the final step.\"","That immediately caught Michael's attention. Advancement with a law meant at least an ascension to Rank Three, and based on how she phrased it, it was most likely exactly that.","\"Unfortunately, before the final step, I was betrayed,\" the skeleton chief added, causing a solemn expression to appear on Michael's face.","Ascension was never safe, even if it only involved the first stage of laws. The moment an individual attempted to truly grasp a Law recognized by the universe into their existence, the smallest disturbance could become fatal.","Whether it was a lapse in concentration, an unstable soul, or an external attack, even an incorrect realization at the final moment could cause the entire process to collapse. Of course, moments like this weren't common, but the possibility of them happening wasn't zero.","Michael said nothing. He could imagine the scene.","At the critical moment of advancement, when she possessed almost no awareness of her surroundings, someone she trusted had attacked her. There would have been no time to defend herself. Once the process collapsed, the backlash alone would have been enough to destroy both body and soul.","The fact that she still existed meant something extraordinary had happened.","As expected, the chief shed more light on the situation.","\"Though my soul perished, one fragment remained. A sliver.\"","Michael studied the violet flames within her skull. The answer explained much. Her unusual intelligence. Her memories of another world. Perhaps even her strange grade.","\"How did it reach the Netherworld?\"","\"I do not know.\"","The response came immediately, without deception.","\"One moment, I was dying.\"","\"The next, the fragment of my soul was drifting through darkness. Then I felt this world. Perhaps it had something to do with the law I had comprehended, but the Netherworld pulled at what remained of me. Or perhaps I reached for it. I cannot remember which. I've been here for more than half a century.\"","Michael's gaze became thoughtful. A soul on the verge of complete collapse had somehow crossed the boundary between the material world and the Netherworld. Whether the realm had naturally attracted her or she had instinctively found a path here remained unclear. Either possibility was remarkable.","\"After I arrived, I was too weak to survive alone. My soul was falling apart. Every moment, another fragment disappeared. Fortunately, I found a vessel. A weak skeleton. Hidden within its soul fire, I could survive, feed myself, and grow.\"","Michael wasn't surprised and could already guess the series of events that followed.","\"Can you separate yourself from the skeleton now?\"","\"No.\"","That explained her earlier statement. She had not originated in the Netherworld, but she had become part of it.","Michael continued examining her. As for her claim of not being able to separate her soul, he believed it was her own incapacity and not an absolute fact.","In any case, this was a steal. However, he was curious about one last thing before he got back to his business.","\"What race was your origin body, and what realm did you come from?\"","\"I'm from the human race, and my realm is called Aurora, at the time of my departure.\"","\"Sorry, did you just say Aurora?\"","Michael was a bit confused and felt his high-spec body might have misheard. What sort of coincidence was this? Was this Jester's doing again?","Michael's heart raced and he couldn't stop himself from asking questions.","\"In this Aurora, does the term Federation ring a bell to you?\"","\"Ahh,\"","Though it was odd for an undead, especially a skeleton, to be very expressive, Michael could hear the surprise in her voice.","Surely this is all a coincidence, right?","\"Ahh yes, there indeed exists a Federation.\"","\"What is this Federation to your Aurora?\"","\"Somewhat of a national ruler in the grand scheme of things.\"","\"What year did you die according to your realm's calendar?\"","\"New Age year 178.\"","It was indeed half a century ago, since in Aurora it was currently the year 229 of the Federation, which had taken the reins to lead the realm on a unified front many years after the apocalypse. To be more exact, year 178 was 51 years ago.","However, it wasn't the history of Aurora that made Michael's heart feel hot, but the timing that matched.","At this point, he was absolutely sure that the undead in front of him was from the same realm."]},{"number":1178,"title":"Chapter 1178: What A Surprise","paragraphs":["Michael fell silent. The revelation had certainly been unexpected.","To think that the Netherworld would hand him someone who originated from the same world as himself. It was surprising. But only surprising.","The universe was unimaginably vast. Strange coincidences and impossible encounters happened every day somewhere across its countless realms. Compared to some of the absurdities Michael had already witnessed since awakening, this hardly qualified as the most unbelievable.","The Skeleton Chief, however, seemed to misunderstand the reason for his silence. Her violet soul flames flickered uneasily.","\"You...\"","She hesitated before speaking again.","\"...Senior.\"","Michael looked at her.","\"If you know Aurora...\"","\"...does that mean you also came from there?\"","Michael neither confirmed nor denied it.","The chief continued, her voice noticeably softer than before.","\"If that is true...\"","\"...can you take me back?\"","For the first time since their conversation began, Michael heard something resembling genuine longing. Even after more than half a century, the desire to return to the world where she had once lived had never truly disappeared.","Michael's expression remained calm. Internally, however, he found the situation rather ironic.","Take her back?","He had already decided that she would become part of his legion. Whether willingly or unwillingly, she would eventually leave the Netherworld with him.","Unlike her incapacity to leave the Netherworld, with the nether gate of his Mausoleum of Endless Dominion, traveling between Aurora and the Netherworld was little more than opening a portal. For her, leaving this realm might be nearly impossible. For him, it was merely inconvenient.","\"...It is possible,\" Michael answered truthfully.","The violet flames within the chief's skull trembled violently.","\"...Really?\"","She instinctively tried to rise but was immediately forced back into a kneeling position. This wasn't Michael's intentional action.","Michael paid little attention to it. Instead, another thought quietly surfaced in his mind.","This is troublesome.","Until now, every undead under his command had been fundamentally different. Aside from Jester, even though all of them possessed remarkably high intelligence, they were merely babies with only one year of memories. Their personalities had gradually developed after their resurrection.","Outside of their abilities, instincts, and individual preferences, there was very little true identity to speak of. They were, in many ways, perfect soldiers. Loyal. Reliable. Entirely centered around him.","This Skeleton Chief was different. She carried decades of memories that had absolutely nothing to do with Michael. With such intelligence, Michael would have to guard his secrets more carefully, even if she turned into his undead and was loyal to him.","That won't do.","He trusted his authority over undead. Completely. But trust and caution were two different things.","The Skeleton Chief was unlike any undead he had commanded before. If she were to join his legion, some precautions would have to be taken. Completely erasing her memories would be wasteful, but allowing her to retain unrestricted knowledge of his own secrets would be equally careless.","The safest solution was to seal only the memories related to him and his greatest secrets. Everything else could remain intact.","Michael nodded inwardly. That should be enough.","Only then did he look back at the kneeling Skeleton Chief. Without realizing it, her fate had already been decided. It couldn't be helped.","Though he had softened his gaze a bit after discovering she was a fellow human from the same realm as his, her value as a Three-Star Epic grade creature was too great to pass up.","The Skeleton Chief remained kneeling. Although her body could not resist his authority, her mind remained clear. That clarity allowed her to notice the way Michael's gaze had changed.","Her violet soul flames trembled faintly.","He's planning something...","At first, she had believed this mysterious existence merely wanted information. Now, she wasn't so certain anymore.","This senior undoubtedly possessed some connection to the arts of necromancy. How else could thousands of undead obey him with such unquestioning loyalty? How else could he command an authority that every undead in the settlement instinctively submitted to?","Her gaze involuntarily drifted toward the guards and citizens still kneeling throughout the settlement. Not one of them had dared move. Not one.","He commands the dead.","No, the dead obey him naturally.","That realization made her soul grow colder.","If he truly is some old necromancer monster, then what value does an undead like me, with special properties, possess?","The answer was obvious. An invaluable servant. Or an equally invaluable material.","The Skeleton Chief had survived for more than fifty years. She had no intention of ending as someone's tool.","No. I can't accept that.","Even if escape was impossible, she wanted to try one final time. Her thoughts moved rapidly.","This senior knows Aurora. He knows the Federation. Perhaps he isn't completely heartless.","If there was even the slightest chance, if she was to mention that person's name, would this senior perhaps help her?","With how talented that person was, after five decades they should be even more impressive than they were years ago, if they were still alive. In any case, if this senior did not know that person, or if they were enemies, then she would just accept her fate.","The Skeleton Chief remained silent for several moments before speaking again.","\"...Senior.\"","Michael looked at her.","\"You said... you came from Aurora.\"","\"I did.\"","\"Then...\"","The violet soul flames flickered uncertainly.","\"Do you know someone named Brian Copper?\"","Michael paused.","\"...I know two people named Brian.\"","The Skeleton Chief's soul flames brightened slightly.","\"However,\" Michael continued, \"I don't think either of them would be related to the person you're referring to.\"","The faint hope within her eyes dimmed.","\"Tell me about him.\"","\"He...\"","The Skeleton Chief seemed to hesitate, as though organizing memories she had not spoken aloud for over fifty years.","\"He specialized in fire magic.\"","Michael's brows twitched.","\"...Fire?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"He possessed exceptional talent with flames.\"","\"He was considered one of the greatest geniuses of our generation.\"","\"...\"","Michael's expression gradually became strange.","A Brian. Gifted in fire.","That description was becoming increasingly familiar. The first person who came to mind was Brian, his former classmate. The second, Teacher Brian. Both of them specialized in fire.","...Coincidence?","There were countless people named Brian. There were countless fire mages. The overlap should not have surprised him. Yet something about the timing and circumstances made him strangely uneasy.","The Skeleton Chief noticed the subtle change in his expression. Her soul flames flickered violently.","\"...Senior?\"","\"You know someone, don't you?\"","Michael did not answer immediately. Instead, he asked,","\"Can you tell me what he looked like?\"","The skeleton then requested his permission to use projection magic, which Michael allowed since this method was much better.","The Skeleton Chief slowly raised one skeletal hand. The violet crystal atop her staff emitted a soft glow. Wisps of pale spiritual light drifted into the air.","Gradually, an outline began taking shape.","A tall man. Broad shoulders. Short hair. Sharp facial features.","The image was somewhat blurred. Still, the general appearance was unmistakable.","Michael stared at it and his pupils contracted.","\"...\"","The Skeleton Chief anxiously watched his face.","\"Senior?\"","Michael did not respond. He simply continued staring at the floating figure.","The man appeared younger. His face lacked the faint wrinkles Michael remembered. His bearing was less mature. But despite those differences, there was no mistaking him.","\"...Damn it.\"","The curse escaped his lips almost instinctively.","The Skeleton Chief froze.","Michael slowly exhaled. His expression had become unusually complicated.","Teacher Brian. It's actually Teacher Brian."]},{"number":1179,"title":"Chapter 1179: His Daughter","paragraphs":["\"What's your relationship with Tea... this Brian Copper?\"","\"He is my father.\"","\"...\"","Silence. The entire settlement seemed to grow even quieter than before.","Michael slowly closed his eyes.","\"...I see.\"","Internally, he let out a long sigh. Of all people.","He had hoped the connection would be insignificant. Something he could ignore. Anything but this.","Unfortunately, reality rarely cared about what people hoped for. She just had to be Teacher Brian's daughter.","Michael rubbed the bridge of his nose. His thoughts, which had been perfectly settled only moments ago, became slightly chaotic.","It wasn't because she had once been human. That alone meant very little to him. If Aurora had been a religion-based realm and she had been its founding god, Michael would still have added her to his legion, if only for collection value.","Before hearing Brian's name, he had fully intended to make her part of his forces regardless of her identity. That decision would not have changed.","But this wasn't just anyone. This was Teacher Brian's daughter.","Michael remained expressionless, yet countless thoughts moved through his mind in rapid succession. It wasn't even respect alone that troubled him. Respect could be set aside when the benefits outweighed the sentiment. The true problem was Teacher Brian himself.","Michael couldn't deny it. Among all the people he had known, Brian was one of the few he genuinely admired, even if their relationship had never been particularly close.","Perhaps it was the way the man had carried himself, like someone who accepted the weight of being responsible for others. The very image Michael had for elders with supernatural powers, unlike a certain shameless bunch.","Or perhaps it was the impression he had left on Michael during the Woodstone City crisis, when Brian had stood as the city's protector at a time when Michael had still been too weak to make any real difference.","Michael quietly laughed at himself. How sentimental.","His expression slowly grew complicated as a different scenario took shape in his mind uninvited.","Suppose, years from now, someone discovered a being equivalent to what Lily was to him, after her destruction. And suppose that person, rather than reviving her or returning her, had instead refined her into materials, or erased her identity entirely to forge a stronger servant.","If that person later stood before Michael and offered the explanation that it had simply been the most efficient choice available, would he accept that?","No.","Not only would he refuse to accept it. That person's ending would be a miserable one.","Michael's eyes slowly lowered. Of course, Teacher Brian could never threaten him. The gap between them was too vast for that. And there was no reason Brian would ever learn the truth of what had become of his daughter, since only Michael knew. But for some reason, that thought brought him no comfort whatsoever.","Michael quietly sighed.","Perhaps this is why powerful supernaturals avoided forming too many interpersonal relationships.","The stronger one became, the longer one lived. The longer one lived, the more attachments accumulated.","Friends. Teachers. Disciples. Lovers. Family. Each relationship eventually became another chain capable of influencing one's decisions.","Michael couldn't help but smile bitterly. He had barely any meaningful relationships. Yet even that small number had already become an inconvenience.","If someone who had lived for thousands of years truly cherished hundreds of people, making completely rational decisions would become almost impossible. No wonder so many old monsters deliberately distanced themselves from others.","Whether they truly stopped caring, or simply forced themselves to.","Michael suddenly understood them a little better.","Still, he had no choice but to slowly push those thoughts aside.","Sentiment later. Business first.","His purpose for entering the Netherworld had never changed. He had come here for dark-element resources, not family reunions.","Michael gradually restrained the oppressive authority radiating from Death's Heir. The invisible pressure blanketing the settlement noticeably weakened. Although the Skeleton Chief remained kneeling, the violent trembling within her soul flame gradually subsided.","She looked at Michael with obvious confusion.","\"Let's postpone the matter of Aurora for now.\"","\"We'll discuss it another time.\"","The Skeleton Chief silently nodded.","Michael's gaze drifted toward the countless skeletons filling the settlement. Then toward the large stone platform where black crystals continuously dissolved within pale blue flames.","\"I have another question.\"","The chief waited.","\"Why keep so many skeletons?\"","His eyes swept across the settlement.","\"Surely maintaining all of them isn't merely for sentiment, right?\"","The Skeleton Chief followed his gaze. After several moments, she slowly raised one hand toward the burning platform.","\"...For my advancement.\"","Michael looked toward the flames again.","She continued.","\"The soul fire.\"","\"The skeletons.\"","She paused briefly.","\"They are all resources to sustain me.\"","Michael slowly nodded.","\"I see.\"","He didn't find it particularly disturbing, as cruelty depended on perspective. More importantly, if she truly wished to leave the Netherworld one day, remaining at Peak Rank Two was impossible. She needed to become Rank Three to even have a chance to break through the outer layers of this unique dimension.","Michael slowly nodded.","\"That won't be necessary anymore.\"","The Skeleton Chief looked up in confusion.","\"...Senior?\"","Michael's gaze swept across the settlement. Since he could freely travel between Aurora and the Netherworld using the Mausoleum's Nether Gate, there was no reason to sacrifice so many resources merely to push a single individual toward Rank Three.","His eyes lingered on the surrounding skeletons.","At this moment, Michael had already regarded everything before him as his own. The Skeleton Chief. The guards. The citizens. Even the weak militia he had first encountered. They had all quietly become part of his possessions the moment they came under the influence of Death's Heir.","He hadn't consciously thought that way before. Perhaps because even after obtaining Death's Heir, he still hadn't fully understood what the class truly represented and had repeatedly tried to estimate its limits.","Yet the deeper he explored Death's Heir, the more unreasonable it became. It wasn't merely powerful. It bordered on absurd. It was unreasonable. A class capable of making an entire race instinctively acknowledge him.","This gives me an idea."]},{"number":1180,"title":"Chapter 1180: Soul Preservation Flame","paragraphs":["His Mausoleum of Endless Dominion contained an enormous independent world. A world vast enough to sustain an entire civilization. With such a huge world, why not fill it with more undead?","Wasn't he at the perfect place in the entire universe to do that?","After all, under the influence of Death's Heir, the natives here were already no different from contracted servants in terms of obedience.","They wouldn't generate Evolution Points, but did that matter? Not really.","The Mausoleum possessed more than enough space. Food was unnecessary. Accommodation was unnecessary. Maintenance was practically nonexistent.","The undead themselves naturally absorbed energy from their surroundings. Keeping them alive required almost nothing.","Rather than allowing countless unique undead races to wander freely throughout the Netherworld, wouldn't it be more efficient to gradually relocate them into the Mausoleum? It would become a true undead civilization. A living encyclopedia of the Netherworld's countless races.","Whether for research, experiments, military reserves, or future subordinates, there were simply too many advantages.","Of course, Michael had no intention of wasting time actively hunting down every undead he encountered. That would be ridiculous. His current priorities were still the Demigod's resurrection and his own cultivation.","However, if he happened to encounter an interesting undead, or any undead at all, during his travels, there was virtually no cost to taking it with him.","Michael's gaze returned to the stone platform at the centre of the settlement.","\"What do these flames do?\"","The Skeleton Chief followed his line of sight. Without another word, she rose to her feet. Although Michael's authority still rested upon her, the crushing pressure had diminished enough for her to move normally.","The surrounding skeletons instinctively stepped aside, creating a path toward the centre of the settlement.","Clack.","Clack.","Clack.","As they approached, Michael could feel the dense fluctuations of energy becoming increasingly concentrated. The pale-blue flames burned silently within a circular pit nearly ten metres across. Skeletons continuously approached from every direction carrying rough black crystals before tossing them into the fire.","The moment each crystal entered the flames, it dissolved into pure streams of energy that spread throughout the surrounding area.","Michael stopped beside the platform.","\"So, what exactly is this?\"","The skeleton chief then went on to explain that the pale-blue flames burning at the platform's center were a survival mechanism for her. Her soul, having merged with the skeleton body, had begun adapting to the Netherworld out of necessity, but adaptation carried a cost.","The longer she remained, the more the environment rewrote her, gradually converting what had once been a human soul into something native to the realm of the dead.","Left unchecked, the process would eventually run its course entirely, leaving her memories and personality intact while hollowing out the foundation beneath them.","The flames slowed that erosion. By harvesting the Netherworld's abundant dark crystals and refining their condensed death essence through the platform, she stripped away most of the environment's natural imprint before allowing the energy to nourish and purify her soul.","Without it, she would have fully transformed years ago and become indistinguishable from any naturally born undead creature of the Netherworld. Every crystal the platform consumed bought her a little more time as the person she had once been.","Michael looked down at the dancing flames.","\"Interesting.\"","Now he seemed to understand why she had become a monster, and one with a high grade at that.","With a thought, he activated Detect. A translucent panel appeared before him.","[Soul Preservation Flame]","[Grade]: Extraordinary ★★★","[Description]: An artificially formed spiritual flame capable of refining dark and light-element energy to nourish and purify the soul.","\"...A Three-Star Extraordinary treasure.\"","His gaze lingered on the pale-blue flames dancing within the circular pit. It seems he had actually underestimated this little settlement. A Three-Star Extraordinary treasure like this was no ordinary object.","This flame possessed exactly the type of soul-nourishing properties required for resurrection rituals. Unfortunately, its power was simply too low even if its grade was higher.","If it were allowed to mature for another hundred, perhaps two hundred years, then, with one or two additional treasures of comparable quality, it might actually become sufficient to revive a Demigod.","To think such a remote skeleton settlement possessed a treasure with that much potential.","Of course, potential remained only potential. At present, the Soul Preservation Flame was still far too weak for the ritual Michael intended to perform.","Yet weak did not mean useless. A Three-Star Extraordinary treasure was still a Three-Star Extraordinary treasure. Even if it could not become the primary material, it could certainly become an auxiliary one.","Or perhaps...","Michael's eyes narrowed slightly.","Can Infinite Evolution do something with this?","The thought surfaced almost instinctively.","Michael quickly suppressed the temptation.","\"I can experiment later after leaving the Netherworld. I wonder if I can use it on that incense too.\"","Michael turned toward the Skeleton Chief.","\"I'm taking it.\"","She bowed her head without hesitation.","\"As you command.\"","There wasn't the slightest trace of reluctance. The flame had preserved her life for decades. Yet under Death's Heir, she couldn't even refuse Michael.","Michael nodded.","\"Good.\"","His consciousness immediately connected to the Mausoleum and fixated at once on one of its dark-element-rich regions. Soon, an enormous circular pit nearly fifteen metres across gradually formed.","Only after confirming the environment was suitable did he withdraw his consciousness. The preparations were complete.","Michael looked toward the Skeleton Chief.","\"Come with me.\"","She silently followed. The two walked away from the settlement while countless skeletons watched respectfully from behind.","Only after they had reached an open plain several hundred metres away did Michael stop.","He slowly crouched. His right palm rested against the black earth. Mana surged. At the same time, a faint yellow glow spread beneath his feet.","Earth-element mana. Although necromancy remained his specialty, Michael had never neglected the other elements he possessed, and even if his class did suppress them, his affinity was still higher than most.","Rumble.","The ground beneath the settlement began to tremble.","The Skeleton Chief instinctively turned around. Her violet soul flames widened.","The circular platform supporting the Soul Preservation Flame slowly separated from the surrounding earth. Cracks spread outward in every direction. Chunks of black stone detached. Entire sections of the foundation rose together as though an invisible giant had reached beneath the settlement.","Rumble!","The vibration intensified. A massive disk of earth nearly twenty metres in diameter gradually lifted into the air.","The skeletons throughout the settlement looked upward and simply watched their most sacred platform float toward the heavens.","Michael slowly raised his hand, and the enormous mass of earth ascended steadily until it hovered dozens of metres above the settlement. Even after lifting something weighing thousands of tons, Michael's breathing remained perfectly steady.","The floating platform slowly drifted toward him. The pale-blue Soul Preservation Flame continued burning undisturbed at its centre, as though nothing unusual was happening.","The Skeleton Chief stared at the spectacle in silence as she watched her most prized treasure being stolen right before her empty sockets.","\"...\"","Watching Michael do it so effortlessly, the difference between them became even clearer.","Finally, the floating platform came to a halt directly before Michael.","He slowly extended his other hand. Space rippled. A circular portal silently unfolded beside the hovering platform. Beyond it lay the vast dark landscape of the Mausoleum.","Without the slightest hesitation, Michael gently guided the entire section of earth through the portal. The moment it entered, the prepared pit within the Mausoleum welcomed it perfectly. The massive platform descended smoothly into place.","Michael smiled faintly.","\"...Much better.\""]},{"number":1181,"title":"Chapter 1181: A Bigger Future","paragraphs":["Michael withdrew his consciousness from the Mausoleum with a satisfied nod. The transfer had been flawless.","The Soul Preservation Flame now rested within one of the Mausoleum's richest death-element regions. Given enough time and sufficient nourishment, there was even a chance it would continue growing naturally.","His gaze slowly swept across the settlement. The countless skeletons still remained exactly where they had been.","With a single thought, the space behind him distorted. The entrance to the Mausoleum silently unfolded. Unlike before, the gateway remained several dozen metres wide.","Michael calmly raised one hand.","\"Enter.\"","The command spread across the entire settlement. Instantly, every skeleton moved without hesitation. They marched in orderly lines toward the portal, disappearing into the Mausoleum one after another.","The Skeleton Chief had to once again quietly watch as all her years of hard work were taken by another.","Within only a few minutes, the once lively skeleton settlement had become completely deserted. Not a single undead remained.","Michael briefly inspected the Mausoleum. The newcomers had already begun wandering through their unfamiliar surroundings before gradually settling down.","The only remaining inhabitant of the settlement now stood beside him. The Skeleton Chief.","Michael looked around the now-empty village before asking another question that had been bothering him for some time.","\"One thing still puzzles me.\"","The Skeleton Chief immediately lowered her head.","\"What is it, Senior?\"","\"The equipment you use. How did you obtain all of it?\"","He had noticed it from the very beginning. Although crude, every guard possessed weapons.","The Skeleton Chief looked toward the abandoned watchtowers and the scattered weapons lying throughout the empty settlement.","\"I made most of them.\"","This didn't surprise Michael. Given that this was someone from a much more organized civilization, using knowledge to create tools wasn't surprising.","The Skeleton Chief slowly walked toward one of the abandoned weapon racks.","\"The Netherworld is rich in death-element resources. But it also possesses ordinary resources. Although they are not always the same as those found in the material world.\"","She bent down and picked up one of the rust-covered swords lying nearby. She extended the weapon toward Michael.","\"For example... this.\"","Michael accepted the sword. At first glance, it looked utterly unimpressive.","The blade was dark reddish-brown. Its surface was covered with uneven patches resembling centuries of rust. The edge was dull, and several tiny chips lined its length. The hilt was wrapped in black leather that had long since hardened into something resembling stone.","But paying close attention to it now, Michael discovered something new.","\"Hmmm. What metal is this?\"","The Skeleton Chief answered without hesitation.","\"Rusted Metal.\"","Michael raised an eyebrow.","\"Rusted Metal?\"","\"A specialty ore from here.\"","\"Interesting.\"","Michael suppressed his curiosity for the moment and activated Detect. A translucent panel appeared before him.","[Rusted Iron Sword]","[Grade: Rare ★]","[Description: A crudely forged sword created from Rusted Metal, an ore naturally produced within the Netherworld. Though poorly refined, it possesses exceptional affinity with dark energy and greatly exceeds ordinary mortal steel in durability.] \"A One-Star Rare weapon...\"","His gaze returned to the blade. This was surprising. No, it was astonishing.","This wasn't a masterpiece forged by a grandmaster blacksmith, nor was it engraved with runes. It wasn't enchanted, and it wasn't even particularly well made. Objectively speaking, the craftsmanship was mediocre at best. The balance was imperfect. The edge uneven. Several parts of the blade had obvious impurities.","Yet it had still skipped Common grade entirely and entered the Rare rank solely because of the material itself.","Michael slowly rotated the sword beneath the dim light.","A Rare grade metal, huh.","Materials determined the upper limit of equipment almost as much as craftsmanship itself. If this same ore were refined by a skilled blacksmith, if the impurities were removed and proper forging techniques and enchantments were added, then a Three-Star Rare weapon wouldn't be impossible. Perhaps even higher.","Infusing a bit of mana into it, Michael also realised the metal itself possessed unusually high affinity with death-element mana.","Michael couldn't help but smile faintly.","\"The Netherworld really is a treasure land.\"","The more he saw, the more convinced he became. Compared to Hell, where powerful factions could at least establish footholds and repeatedly harvest valuable regions, the Netherworld was far more difficult for ordinary living beings to occupy for long periods. That naturally meant countless resources had been left untouched for absurd amounts of time.","Centuries. Perhaps millennia or eons. Even relatively ordinary materials here could possess qualities that would make realms outside fight over them.","Michael looked down at the rust-colored sword again. At present, Rusted Metal did not have much value to him personally. His strongest undead already possessed bodies that were more dangerous than most weapons, and the weaker members of his legion did not urgently need equipment.","But that would not remain true forever. His legion continued to grow, and to empower them further the importance of equipment could not be ignored.","Equipping even a portion of them with proper weapons would consume a ridiculous amount of material. And there was another reason.","The Universal Cornerstone.","Ever since obtaining it and seeing the functions connected to it, he had carried an uncomfortable feeling. The treasure had exposed him to possibilities that went far beyond the Origin Battlefield or the concept of realms entirely, whether they be separated civilizations, special dimensions, or places that had remained isolated for countless generations.","Michael had a growing suspicion that this separation would not last forever. Sooner or later, something would change. And when it did, the entire universe might be dragged into conflict.","The sub-territory function of the Universal Cornerstone stated it could be placed anywhere. If it could truly be placed anywhere, even in a place like the Land of Origin, then it seemed he might even start to worry about the empire like an actual ruler.","Michael casually tossed the sword into the Mausoleum.","\"Collecting some won't hurt.\"","The Skeleton Chief watched the sword disappear into thin air. From everything she had seen, she could tell this man with mysterious strength had a storage treasure of a significantly high grade. Knowing that this was her ticket to finally leave this forsaken place, she wanted to be more proactive and satisfy him. Perhaps he might really take her to her father.","\"Senior.\"","Michael looked at her.","\"Yes?\"","\"Would you like the dark crystals as well?\"","Michael's gaze shifted toward several broken baskets still scattered around the empty settlement. Inside them were rough black crystals similar to the ones previously fed into the Soul Preservation Flame.","He had already examined them earlier. They were useful, but not particularly impressive. In the Netherworld, crystals with that level of condensed dark energy were probably little different from ordinary stone in the material world.","Still, Michael thought for a moment.","\"Are there stronger grades?\"","The Skeleton Chief's violet soul flames flickered.","\"Yes.\""]},{"number":1182,"title":"Chapter 1182: What is Emperor Rank To Me?","paragraphs":["Michael's expression immediately became more interested.","\"How much stronger?\"","\"There are crystals with far denser concentrations of dark energy.\"","She paused.","\"One mine nearby contains much better ones.\"","\"Nearby?\"","\"Yes.\"","Michael studied her soul flame. Something felt off. There was a faint disturbance hidden beneath her otherwise steady fluctuations.","Is this resentment?","Michael's eyes narrowed slightly.","\"You don't seem particularly happy about that mine.\"","The Skeleton Chief went silent.","Michael waited. Under his authority, she couldn't avoid answering forever.","Eventually, she spoke.","\"It used to belong to me.\"","Michael's eyebrows rose.","\"Then who owns it now?\"","The violet flames inside her skull darkened.","\"Stronger monsters.\"","Michael's smile, however, didn't fade. Wasn't this what he came here for? Though common sense here might be different from the outside world, it could be said that stronger monsters defending precious treasures was a universal truth.","Perhaps by targeting these places guarded by stronger monsters, it wouldn't take long for him to gather the treasures needed to revive the Demigod as an undead. Though it couldn't be used as a main material, high-grade dark elemental crystal would function as the best auxiliary material or a source of energy. The more the better.","\"What kind?\" Michael asked.","The Skeleton Chief tightened her grip on her staff.","\"A group of Bone Hounds.\"","\"How strong, and how many?\"","\"They're five. Four at the King Rank stage and one at the Emperor stage.\"","Knowing the man came from the same world as her, to be better understood she used the names of the power system used in Aurora. King Rank correlated with a Rank Three awakener, and Emperor Rank was Rank Four.","Hearing it was only a bunch of weak monsters, Michael became even more relaxed.","Michael glanced toward the empty settlement behind them.","\"So that's where part of your resentment came from.\"","The chief did not deny it.","\"How far is the mine?\"","\"A short march for someone like you, Senior.\"","Michael turned toward the direction she had indicated and started walking.","\"Lead the way.\"","Her violet soul flames flickered.","\"To the mine? Senior, but they are at Emperor rank!\"","Michael glanced back at her.","Did she think he was weak?","In fact, the chief didn't think that at all. It was easy for the powerful to suppress weak creatures like undead skeletons, but it would be hard to make them worship that power. For one, this person not only had to be powerful, but they had to be unique in their own right.","To the Skeleton Chief, she felt Michael should be rather established at the Emperor rank, but going alone, wasn't that a bit reckless? With this being her only ticket away from this world, the Skeleton Chief didn't want anything to happen to Michael yet. It wasn't for his sake, but her own.","Michael stopped walking. For a moment, he simply looked at the Skeleton Chief.","The Skeleton Chief was already incapable of disobeying him, and he didn't need to convince her of anything. Still, if he intended to use her knowledge and cooperation during this expedition, there was no harm in letting her understand the gap between them. It might even make things easier.","Michael quietly smiled.","\"Emperor rank?\"","The Skeleton Chief's violet flames flickered.","\"Yes, Senior.\"","Michael slowly turned toward her. Then he stopped suppressing his mana.","Boom!","The change was instantaneous. An enormous wave of energy erupted from Michael's body. The surrounding ground cracked. Dust and fragments of black stone were blasted outward. The world seemed to tremble as dense mana surged into the surroundings like an invisible ocean.","The Skeleton Chief froze. Her soul flame nearly extinguished from instinctive shock.","The pressure was not directed at her, thanks to Michael deliberately shielding her. He was simply allowing his mana to exist without restraint. Yet that alone felt overwhelming.","The air around him distorted. Dark-element mana from the Netherworld itself rushed toward Michael almost instinctively, mixing with his own energy until the entire area seemed to revolve around his existence, surprising Michael himself as he realized that being in the Netherworld might actually boost his ability to a disgusting degree. This much should be expected given the dark-element-rich environment, but the sheer scale of the increase was surprising nevertheless.","It seems I might indeed be a fish in the water here.","The Skeleton Chief took several involuntary steps backward.","\"This...\"","Her voice became faint. Michael's current aura didn't resemble the Emperor-rank experts she remembered. Not even close.","Emperor-rank experts were terrifying. They could destroy cities, dominate battlefields, suppress entire armies, and rule a realm. They were respected anywhere in the universe. But both in Aurora and here, when had she ever felt so terrified by one?","Michael's energy felt terrifyingly deep. It was far too dense, and the amount was simply unreasonable.","The Skeleton Chief stared at him in stunned silence. Her thoughts became chaotic.","What rank is he? A Peak Emperor?","No. That doesn't feel right.","Someone already touching the threshold above?","Her soul fire trembled.","Could he be close to Demigod?","Then an even more absurd possibility surfaced.","Could he already be one?","The thought terrified her.","Michael watched the violent fluctuations inside her violet soul flame and almost laughed. He could more or less guess what she was thinking. After all, putting aside those magic-focused supernaturals, there were not many who could beat him in terms of mana even if they were at level 100.","After several seconds, he restrained his mana again. The terrifying pressure vanished as quickly as it had appeared. The surroundings gradually returned to normal.","The Skeleton Chief remained completely still.","Michael casually continued walking, glancing over his shoulder.","\"What is an Emperor-rank monster?\"","His expression carried genuine confusion.","\"In my eyes, they're all weak anyway.\"","The Skeleton Chief stared at his back. For several seconds, she forgot to move. Then she hurried after him.","\"Senior...\"","Her tone had changed completely. Before, there had been respect mixed with caution. Now there was something much closer to genuine awe.","Michael noticed and said nothing.","This skeleton was a little silly.","In trust he might not even need to fight and those hounds will offer their treasures including themselves to him."]},{"number":1183,"title":"Chapter 1183: Arrival","paragraphs":["Michael decided against travelling through the void.","He knew far too little about the Netherworld.","Even with the Skeleton Chief guiding him, there was no reason to take risks when he could simply observe everything from above, lest he appear in a place he could have avoided.","Michael and the Skeleton Chief rose into the air before flying in the direction of the mine.","The journey quickly became more interesting.","From above, Michael gained a much clearer picture of the surrounding region, and one thing became immediately obvious. The Netherworld truly deserved its reputation as the land of the dead.","Though spaced out, undead were everywhere.","Michael encountered ordinary skeletons similar to those he had already collected, skeletal beasts, zombies with partially preserved bodies, strange masses of rotting flesh, and even several varieties he couldn't immediately identify.","There were ghosts as well. This particularly interested him. Unlike physical undead, they appeared as translucent figures drifting through the Netherworld, their forms occasionally becoming almost invisible before materializing again.","Unfortunately, the few Michael encountered were rather weak. Most had not even entered Rank One, while the strongest ghost he found barely reached Rank Two.","Still, Michael took them. In fact, he took almost everything. Whenever an undead entered his perception, he immediately placed it into his Mausoleum.","Unranked. Rank One. Rank Two. It made little difference.","He even encountered several Rank Three undead during the journey, including a massive skeletal snake beast that had been wandering alone through a rocky valley. They all ended up inside the Mausoleum. Michael didn't discriminate much.","By the time they approached the mine, the Mausoleum had gained dozens of additional undead belonging to several different species.","The Skeleton Chief pointed toward the horizon.","\"Senior.\"","Michael followed her gaze. In the distance, the terrain had begun changing. The dead forest disappeared completely, replaced by enormous black hills and jagged cliffs stretching across the landscape. Between two of those cliffs stood a massive opening descending underground.","Even from several kilometres away, Michael could sense the concentration of dark energy surrounding it.","The Skeleton Chief's violet soul flames flickered.","\"The mine is there.\"","Michael slowed as they approached the mine. His perception swept across the black hills, then through the enormous entrance carved between the cliffs.","Michael glanced toward the Skeleton Chief.","\"They're inside?\"","\"Most likely, Senior.\"","Michael nodded, as he had expected as much. He just wanted to make sure.","Without hesitation, he descended. The Skeleton Chief followed closely behind him, landing several metres away.","\"Hmm?\"","The concentration of dark-element energy here was significantly higher than the normal atmosphere in the Netherworld.","It felt comfortable. Michael couldn't think of a better description.","The surrounding dark energy naturally flowed around his body. Some of it entered him without conscious effort before being absorbed and circulated through his mana pathways. There was no discomfort or resistance. Instead, Michael felt strangely relaxed.","His body seemed lighter, and his mana became more active.","Michael closed his eyes briefly. He suddenly remembered some of the strange records he had read back at the academy.","There had been countless stories about powerful elementalists deliberately searching for extreme environments matching their affinities. At the time, some of those stories had sounded ridiculous.","Fire Knights bathing inside pools of lava. Water Mages constructing entire temples at the bottom of oceans. Earth-element awakeners sealing themselves kilometres underground. Wind specialists living permanently above the clouds.","Michael had understood the reasoning theoretically. A suitable environment strengthened cultivation, accelerated mana recovery, improved elemental comprehension, and could even enhance certain abilities.","Understanding something intellectually, however, was completely different from experiencing it.","Now Michael understood. If an ordinary dark-element supernatural felt even a fraction of what he currently felt, they probably wouldn't want to leave.","\"This is actually quite nice.\"","The Skeleton Chief turned toward him.","\"Senior?\"","\"Nothing.\"","Michael started toward the mine. The entrance itself was enormous, easily large enough for several giant creatures to enter side by side.","The Skeleton Chief followed. The moment they crossed the threshold, the already dense dark energy increased again.","Michael's expression brightened.","Even better.","Their footsteps echoed through the cavern.","Tap.","Clack.","Tap.","Clack.","Michael's boots alternated with the Skeleton Chief's skeletal feet as they travelled deeper underground.","The tunnel gradually widened. Black crystals protruded naturally from the walls, some no larger than Michael's fingers while others were several metres long.","Faint streams of energy continuously escaped from them before dispersing into the surroundings.","Michael casually examined several as they passed. Most weren't particularly valuable, at least not individually. However, their sheer quantity was impressive.","The entire mountain seemed saturated with dark-element energy, and the deeper they travelled, the stronger that concentration became.","Michael could already understand why the Bone Hounds had taken this place. For undead creatures possessing any affinity toward darkness or death, this was practically a natural cultivation ground.","Michael stretched his shoulders.","\"This place really is comfortable.\"","The Skeleton Chief remained silent. She couldn't relate. For her, the Netherworld's energy was precisely what she had spent decades trying to prevent from completely altering her soul. For Michael, however, it was almost nourishment.","They continued deeper.","At this point there was no light in the cave. Absolute darkness swallowed the tunnel, but neither of them reacted. The Skeleton Chief was an undead whose perception had never depended entirely on ordinary vision.","Michael was even less affected. His perception spread through the surrounding cavern effortlessly, mapping the walls, crystals, passages, and energy fluctuations around him.","A light source would have been redundant, given he also had night vision.","A minute passed, and the tunnel split into five passages.","Michael stopped and looked toward the five passages.","This was convenient.","Five tunnels. Five Bone Hounds.","Considering the numbers matched perfectly, it wasn't difficult to guess what was happening.","The only question was which tunnel belonged to the Rank Four Bone Hound. He extended his perception deeper, but the abundance of strong energy in the atmosphere interfered somewhat with his senses.","He could certainly force his perception farther or use a spell, but that seemed unnecessarily troublesome.","There were only five tunnels. He would eventually check all of them anyway.","Michael casually chose the second passage from the left.","The Skeleton Chief stared at him.","\"Senior, shouldn't we determine which one contains the Emperor-rank Bone Hound first?\"","\"Why?\"","\"...\"","She suddenly remembered who she was speaking to.","\"Never mind.\""]},{"number":1184,"title":"Chapter 1184: Another Epic?","paragraphs":["Michael walked forward. The passage descended gradually. Unlike the main tunnel, the walls here were covered with enormous claw marks. Some had dug several centimetres into the stone.","Black crystals appeared increasingly frequently along the walls, although many had clearly been shattered or consumed.","Michael continued deeper for less than a minute before something entered his perception.","\"There.\"","The Skeleton Chief immediately became alert. A massive creature lay farther ahead.","Michael continued walking until the tunnel opened into a cavern. Two blue flames immediately appeared in the darkness. Then an enormous skeletal creature slowly rose.","Clack!","Bones shifted against one another. The Bone Hound stood nearly four metres tall at the shoulder. Its body resembled an enormous wolf stripped completely of flesh, although several features were clearly unnatural.","Its ribs curved outward like armor. Jagged bone spikes protruded along its spine. Its skull was disproportionately large.","The Skeleton Chief instinctively tightened her grip around her staff.","\"Senior, that's one of them.\"","Michael nodded. He had already used Detect.","[Bone Hound]","[Grade: Extraordinary ★★]","[Level: 67]","Rank Three.","The Bone Hound stared directly at Michael. Its jaws slowly opened. The Skeleton Chief prepared herself for an attack.","Instead, the blue flames within the Bone Hound's sockets suddenly contracted and its entire body froze. The next moment, the enormous creature lowered itself. Its front legs bent, and its skull touched the ground as the creature submitted without the slightest resistance.","The Skeleton Chief stared. Even after witnessing what happened at her settlement, seeing the same thing happen to a Rank Three undead remained somewhat difficult to process.","This wasn't a weak skeleton whose instincts could easily be overwhelmed. This was a King-rank undead. A creature that could have slaughtered her entire settlement almost by itself. Yet it hadn't even tried to resist.","Michael, meanwhile, looked completely unimpressed.","\"So it works exactly the same.\"","He had wondered whether stronger undead might show greater resistance. The Skeleton Chief had proven that some could retain their individuality beneath his authority, but apparently Rank Three alone wasn't enough to change much.","He had expected this already having already commanded two rank 4 undead before this. This went to show the uniqueness of the skeleton chief was not influenced by her location.","Michael approached the Bone Hound. It remained completely motionless.","\"Enter.\"","Space distorted beside it.","The Mausoleum opened and the Bone Hound immediately stood and walked through the portal.","Michael closed it afterward.","\"...\"","That was it. No battle or struggle. Michael felt strangely disappointed. He had initially thought entering the Netherworld would involve some unique situations. Instead, he had practically become a collector.","\"Just Rank Three.\"","A little tasteless.","Michael turned around.","\"Next.\"","The Skeleton Chief silently followed. They returned to the junction before entering another tunnel.","The result was almost identical. A second Bone Hound appeared.","[Bone Hound]","[Grade: Extraordinary ★★]","[Level: 71]","It sensed Michael.","It froze, then bowed seconds later.","Soon it entered the Mausoleum.","The third tunnel wasn't any different. Another effortless submission. By this point, Michael barely bothered examining it beyond checking its basic information.","\"Let's go.\"","The creature entered the Mausoleum.","They returned to the junction once again. The Skeleton Chief's violet flames flickered strangely.","These were the creatures that had forced her to abandon one of the most valuable resources she had discovered in decades. She had spent years avoiding them. Michael was collecting them like stray animals.","Neither spoke about it.","They entered the fourth tunnel. Several minutes later, they found another cavern, and another enormous skeletal creature stood within it.","The moment Michael entered, clack, its massive body immediately lowered.","Michael glanced at its information. Level Seventy-Four. Still Rank Three.","\"Another one.\"","The portal appeared. The fourth Bone Hound obediently entered.","Michael turned around. Now there was only one passage remaining. He and the Skeleton Chief returned to the central junction.","Michael's gaze settled upon the fifth tunnel. The Skeleton Chief's grip around her staff tightened. Four tunnels. Four King-rank Bone Hounds. MThere was no longer anything to guess. The last one could only belong to the Emperor-rank creature.","Michael stared into the darkness. Unlike the others, this passage was noticeably larger. The claw marks covering its walls were deeper as well. Even the concentration of dark energy flowing from within seemed slightly higher.","The Skeleton Chief stepped beside him.","\"Senior.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"That should be the Emperor.\"","Michael smiled.","\"Finally.\"","After four Rank Three creatures, perhaps this one would at least be somewhat interesting.","Without another word, Michael entered the final tunnel.","The final tunnel descended much deeper than the previous four. Michael noticed the difference almost immediately. The passage was wider, the claw marks along the walls deeper, and the dark crystals embedded within the stone were noticeably larger. More importantly, the concentration of dark energy continued to rise.","The Skeleton Chief remained several steps behind him. Despite everything Michael had shown her, she couldn't completely suppress her caution. This was an Emperor-rank undead. Rank Four.","Back in Aurora, an existence at this level would have stood near the top of an entire region, and major organizations would think carefully before provoking one unnecessarily. Yet the person ahead of her walked forward without the slightest concern.","Soon, Michael sensed something. A considerably stronger presence than the previous four.","\"There.\"","He continued forward. The tunnel eventually opened into an enormous underground chamber. Black crystals covered nearly every surface. Some rose from the ground like enormous pillars, while others hung from the ceiling like jagged teeth.","At the center of the chamber lay a massive creature. Michael immediately noticed that this Bone Hound was different from the others. It was nearly twice their size.","Its skeletal frame was much denser, with thick overlapping plates of dark bone covering its chest, shoulders, and spine. Two curved horns extended backward from its skull, while its claws had become almost metallic in appearance. Dark mist constantly drifted between its ribs.","Then two enormous blue flames ignited.","Boom!","The Bone Hound rose. Its skull lifted toward Michael.","The Skeleton Chief immediately stopped.","\"It's the Emperor.\"","Michael activated Detect.","[Bone Hound]","[Grade: Epic ★]","[Level: 83]","Michael's eyebrows rose slightly.","\"Oh?\"","Perhaps this one would actually...","Clack.","The Bone Hound lowered its head.","\"...\"","Michael stared expressionless.","Boom!","The enormous creature bent its front legs.","Its skull touched the ground. The dark mist surrounding its body dispersed, and the previously intimidating blue flames within its sockets lowered submissively."]},{"number":1185,"title":"Chapter 1185: Gathering Resources","paragraphs":["\"Hmm?\"","Michael stared at the kneeling Bone Hound and noticed a difference. A subtle one.","The Emperor-rank Bone Hound was undoubtedly submitting to him. Michael could feel that clearly through the shared connection between them with his class. If he commanded it to stand, it would stand. If he commanded it to attack the other Bone Hounds, it would attack.","If he ordered it to destroy itself, Michael suspected it would obey that as well.","Yet something about its submission felt different.","Michael studied the blue flames within its skull. Then he understood.","\"Interesting.\"","The feeling reminded him of something completely unrelated to undead. His knights back in the Land of Origin.","Whenever Michael entered the presence of those who had sworn themselves to him, their greetings carried something more than obligation. They bowed because he was their lord. But many also bowed because they genuinely wanted to. There was loyalty behind the gesture. Respect. Recognition. Perhaps even admiration.","Then there were ordinary people within his territory. They would also bow. They would address him respectfully. They would follow his laws and obey his orders. But the feeling was different.","One came from the heart. The other came from acknowledgment. *He is my lord, therefore I bow.*","That was the distinction Michael sensed now.","The weaker skeletons from the settlement had been closer to the first category. Their soul flames had practically erupted with reverence upon sensing him. Their submission hadn’t merely been forced upon them by an irresistible authority. They seemed genuinely delighted to obey him. To them, Michael’s existence itself was something worthy of worship.","The Emperor Bone Hound wasn’t like that. It acknowledged him, so it submitted. The creature still possessed enough individuality to separate obedience from devotion.","Michael slowly approached. The Bone Hound remained bowed.","\"Raise your head.\"","Its enormous skull immediately rose. The blue flames stared at Michael. There was no resistance, but neither was there the almost childlike reverence he had seen from the weaker skeletons.","This was another small insight into Death’s Heir. The class didn’t necessarily erase an undead’s personality, nor did it automatically transform every undead into a fanatic. The end result appeared to vary depending on the individual.","What Michael didn’t understand was why.","Was it strength? That seemed unlikely. He had already brought two Rank Four undead to his command. All he could tell was that the strength of an undead’s resistance did not simply depend on its strength.","If it wasn’t strength, then was it intelligence?","The Skeleton Chief was the most obvious example. Despite being weaker than the Bone Hound before him, she retained an extremely strong sense of self. Her memories, emotions, desires, fears, and ambitions were comparable to those of any living person. Death’s Heir could force her obedience, but it hadn’t transformed her into a mindless worshipper.","Then there was race. Or more specifically, grade.","Michael glanced at the information floating beside the Bone Hound.","[Grade: Epic ★]","The ordinary skeletons had mostly been Common grade. This Bone Hound was Epic. Perhaps higher-grade undead possessed stronger souls and therefore maintained more individuality under his authority.","Or perhaps both factors mattered. Intelligence. Grade. Strength. Soul quality. Maybe even the undead’s species itself.","There were too many variables.","Michael rubbed his chin.","\"This class really didn’t come with enough instructions.\"","The Skeleton Chief heard him but wisely said nothing. She didn’t even know what this senior was talking about. It’s said that old monsters tend to have mental issues. Maybe that’s why this senior seemed to love talking to himself.","Michael wasn’t particularly bothered. He had only possessed Death’s Heir for a short period. There would be plenty of opportunities to experiment. The Netherworld itself was practically the perfect testing ground. With countless undead races spread throughout this realm, sooner or later he would encounter enough variations to understand exactly how his authority worked.","For now, however, he had more important things to do.","Michael looked toward the Bone Hound.","\"Enter.\"","Space distorted. The entrance to the Mausoleum appeared beside the enormous creature. The Bone Hound immediately stood. It glanced toward the spatial opening for only a moment before walking forward without hesitation.","The massive Bone Hound disappeared into the Mausoleum and Michael closed the portal.","Five Bone Hounds. Four Rank Three. One Rank Four. All collected without throwing a single punch.","Michael couldn’t decide whether he should consider that fortunate or disappointing. Probably both.","The Skeleton Chief stared at the empty space where the Emperor Bone Hound had disappeared. Her violet flames remained unusually still.","Michael glanced at her.","\"Something wrong?\"","\"No, Senior.\"","She paused.","\"It is simply difficult to believe.\"","\"What is?\"","\"That was the creature that drove me from this mine.\"","Michael looked around the cavern.","\"And now it’s gone.\"","\"Yes.\"","The Skeleton Chief stared at him.","\"Just like that.\"","Michael shrugged.","\"Better than wasting time fighting.\"","That was the practical answer. He hadn’t entered the Netherworld looking for entertainment. He needed resources. The sooner he obtained enough materials to resurrect the Demigod, the sooner he could leave.","Michael’s attention finally shifted away from Death’s Heir and toward the cavern surrounding them. Now that he wasn’t distracted by the Bone Hound, the sheer concentration of dark-element energy became much more noticeable.","Michael inhaled slowly. Mana practically poured into his body.","Then his perception spread outward. Across the walls. Beneath the floor. Through the enormous crystal formations surrounding the chamber. His eyes gradually brightened.","The Bone Hounds were interesting. But this was what he had actually come for.","Michael walked toward the nearest crystal formation. He placed one hand against its surface.","Cold.","The dark energy contained inside was considerably denser than the crystals he had seen at the Skeleton Chief’s settlement.","Michael nodded. *This was much better.*","His perception spread farther through the cavern. Most of the larger crystals possessed roughly the same quality, while some of the smaller ones were only One-Star Rare. There were also several pockets deeper underground where the energy fluctuations seemed even stronger.","There was plenty here. Unfortunately, Michael had no intention of mining it properly. He didn’t have the equipment. More importantly, he didn’t have the time.","Michael stepped backward.","The Skeleton Chief watched him.","\"Senior?\"","Michael raised one hand.","Rumble!","The cavern shook. Cracks immediately spread across the walls.","The Skeleton Chief’s violet flames flickered violently as she looked upward.","\"Senior?\"","\"Don’t worry.\"","Michael’s mana poured into the surrounding earth.","Rumble!","An entire section of the cavern wall tore free. It wasn’t merely the exposed crystals. Stone. Ore. Crystals. Everything within an area nearly thirty metres across separated from the mountain at once.","The enormous mass floated toward Michael. Space distorted beside him. A gateway to the Mausoleum opened. Michael sent the entire thing inside.","Boom!","The massive section of rock landed within an empty region of the Mausoleum.","Michael immediately turned toward another wall.","Rumble!","Another enormous section was ripped free. Then another. And another.","There was no careful excavation. No separating valuable crystals from worthless stone. Michael simply took everything. If the crystals were embedded within several thousand tons of rock, then several thousand tons of rock would enter the Mausoleum with them.","The Skeleton Chief silently watched. The mine trembled continuously.","Boom!","Another section vanished.","Boom!","Half of a crystal-covered wall disappeared.","Boom!","A large portion of the floor was torn upward, revealing another layer of dark crystals beneath it.","Michael’s eyes brightened.","\"There’s more underneath.\"","The Skeleton Chief looked at the increasingly devastated cavern.","Rumble!","The newly exposed section disappeared as well."]},{"number":1186,"title":"Chapter 1186: Even An Undead Is Capable Of Feeling Fear","paragraphs":["Michael continued until the enormous cavern barely resembled what it had been before. Several walls had been pushed back dozens of metres. The floor had dropped considerably. Parts of the ceiling were missing.","The richest visible crystal deposits had all been transferred into the Mausoleum along with enormous quantities of surrounding rock.","Michael finally stopped.","\"That should be enough.\"","There was no point stripping the entire mountain bare. He could always return if necessary.","Michael closed the gateway and dusted his hands.","The Skeleton Chief looked around.","\"...\"","Michael turned toward her.","\"Do you know anywhere else like this?\"","\"Senior?\"","\"Places with valuable resources.\"","Michael stepped over a large crack running across the cavern floor.","\"Preferably somewhere guarded by strong undead.\"","The Skeleton Chief paused.","Michael continued.","\"Or anything unusual. Mines. Treasures. Special environments. Powerful undead territories.\"","The violet flames within her skull shifted.","\"I know several.\"","Michael smiled. If she had spent more than fifty years trapped within the Netherworld and this mine was the only valuable location she knew, then those decades would truly have been wasted.","\"Tell me.\"","The Skeleton Chief thought briefly.","\"There is a valley northeast of here.\"","\"What’s there?\"","\"Grave Flowers.\"","Michael stopped.","\"Grave Flowers?\"","\"Dark-element spiritual plants. They grow from areas where large quantities of soul energy have accumulated.\"","\"What guards them?\"","\"A Corpse Giant.\"","\"Rank?\"","\"Emperor.\"","\"Good.\"","Michael gestured for her to continue.","\"There is also a lake farther north. The water itself is poisonous to the soul, but crystals occasionally form beneath it.\"","\"What grade?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"You never collected them?\"","\"I couldn’t.\"","\"Why?\"","\"Ghosts.\"","Michael’s interest immediately increased.","\"How many?\"","\"Thousands.\"","Michael’s smile widened. That was even better than crystals, even if they were of a lower grade.","\"What else?\"","The Skeleton Chief hesitated before listing off several more, and the smile on Michael’s face couldn’t help but grow. When she was done listing everything, Michael, eager and in a hurry, immediately dashed off to these locations with her.","Over the next several days, Isabella proved far more useful than Michael had expected. With her knowledge of the surrounding region, he avoided wasting time searching blindly and moved directly between locations that possessed either valuable resources or powerful undead.","A valley filled with Grave Flowers. An underground river carrying dense energy. A ruined burial ground containing several Rare and Extraordinary-grade materials. Yes, a burial ground. Apparently some undead cultivated this way.","A lake occupied by thousands of ghosts, most of whom ended up inside the Mausoleum after Michael arrived. Several small undead territories.","One location after another was emptied. By the time Michael checked the resources accumulated within the Mausoleum, even he felt satisfied.","There was enough. More than enough.","The primary materials required for the resurrection ritual had finally been gathered, while the excess dark crystals, soul-nourishing treasures, ores, plants, and miscellaneous Netherworld materials would remain useful long after the Demigod was revived.","Without Isabella, collecting this much would have taken him at least twice as long. Perhaps longer. Michael had the strength to take whatever he encountered, but strength did not tell him where the useful things were. Her fifty years in the Netherworld had saved him an enormous amount of time.","By the third day, Michael had already decided it was time to return. Lucky’s evolution should be nearing completion. The Origin Battlefield would reopen soon. And most importantly, the Demigod’s resurrection could finally begin.","However, just as Michael prepared to end the expedition, something unexpected happened.","They found a treasure.","Michael stood at the edge of a narrow ravine, staring toward a strange tree growing alone from the black stone below. The tree was barely three metres tall. Its trunk was completely black, almost resembling charcoal, while thin silver lines pulsed beneath the bark like veins.","There were no leaves. Instead, dozens of pale-blue flames floated around its branches. Each flame gave off astonishingly pure energy.","Michael activated Detect.","[Nether Soul Tree]","[Grade: Epic ★★★]","[Description: A naturally formed spiritual tree born in regions where immense concentrations of death and soul energy overlap. Its wood, roots, and Soul Flames possess exceptional compatibility with rituals involving souls, undead evolution, resurrection, and spiritual restoration.]","Michael’s eyes lit up immediately.","\"Three-Star Epic.\"","This was easily the most valuable wild resource he had encountered during the entire expedition. More importantly, it was perfect. With this tree added to the materials already gathered, the Demigod resurrection ritual would become far more stable. Seeing its description, it would also be far more useful after that.","Michael descended into the ravine without hesitation. Isabella followed him.","\"Senior, I’ve never seen this before.\"","\"Neither have I.\"","Michael approached the tree. The closer he came, the stronger the soul fluctuations became. Even his own soul felt strangely refreshed.","He placed one hand against the black trunk.","\"I’ll take the entire thing.\"","There was absolutely no reason to harvest only portions. The Mausoleum possessed more than enough space to transplant it. If he could keep it alive, it might continuously produce useful resources in the future.","Michael’s consciousness connected to the Mausoleum. He quickly selected an environment possessing high concentrations of dark energy. The ground inside the Mausoleum shifted, and a large pit appeared.","Michael smiled.","\"Perfect.\"","He crouched beside the Nether Soul Tree and extended his mana underground, carefully surrounding the roots.","He was just about to tear the surrounding earth free when he suddenly stopped.","\"...\"","Michael’s expression became serious.","\"Something’s here.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, a face appeared inches from his own.","\"...!\"","Michael’s heart nearly jumped out of his throat.","It was the face of a woman. Beautiful. Unnaturally so.","Long black hair drifting around her head as though submerged underwater. Dark lashes framed a pair of completely silver eyes without visible pupils. Her features were delicate enough to appear almost artificial, yet the faint smile on her lips made the sight infinitely more unsettling.","More importantly, there had been absolutely nothing there a moment ago. Now her face was so close that their noses were barely separated.","Michael instinctively jerked backward. At the exact same moment,","\"Ghost!\"","Isabella screamed.","If an undead could be scared by its own kind, there was little need to elaborate on Michael’s feeling.","What made his heart beat faster was the aura he sensed from the ghost.","It was a demigod."]},{"number":1187,"title":"Chapter 1187: You’re The Strangest","paragraphs":["RUN!","The moment Michael confirmed the aura, Wisdom State activated instantly. His Law surged through his body while the surrounding space subtly distorted.","At the same time, Michael’s connection to Isabella tightened. One thought was all he needed. One thought and he would grab Isabella, tear open space, and get the hell out of there.","He was already preparing to do exactly that.","Then Michael stopped himself.","\"...\"","His heart continued pounding violently inside his chest. Every instinct screamed at him not to remain casually standing before a Demigod. This wasn’t one of his enhanced undead temporarily reaching that level through his abilities. This was a true Demigod. An existence that had naturally crossed that threshold.","His fingers twitched. The spatial fluctuation surrounding him remained ready. If anything changed, anything at all, he would leave immediately.","Yet Michael forced himself to remain where he was. This was because something was missing.","Now that he had cleared his mind, he realized he didn’t sense a bit of danger. There was none.","The pressure radiating from the ghost was terrifying. Even while restrained, it felt like an enormous ocean surrounding a small island. Every strand of spiritual energy drifting from her translucent body seemed capable of crushing him.","But there was no killing intent. She was powerful. Extremely powerful. But she did not intend to attack him. At least, not yet.","Michael slowly exhaled. His body remained tense, and Wisdom State stayed active right away. But he didn’t teleport.","The ghost continued floating before him. Her silver eyes moved across his face curiously. Then she glanced toward the subtle spatial distortions surrounding him.","Her lips curved upward.","\"You were going to run.\"","Michael’s eyelid twitched.","\"No.\"","The woman’s smile widened.","\"You were.\"","\"...\"","Michael said nothing.","Isabella stood several metres behind Michael, completely frozen. Her violet soul flames had contracted into tiny points. Unlike Michael, she possessed none of his extraordinary resistance to spiritual pressure. Even though the ghost wasn’t deliberately suppressing her, simply standing near such an existence was enough to make Isabella’s bones tremble.","Michael subtly extended his aura around her, shielding her from the worst of it. Only then did Isabella seem capable of moving again.","\"Senior...\"","Her voice was barely audible.","Michael raised one hand.","\"Don’t.\"","She immediately went silent.","His eyes never left the ghost.","The woman tilted her head.","\"Senior?\"","Her silver gaze shifted toward Isabella. Then back toward Michael.","Her voice did not actually travel through the air. It wasn’t spoken language. It was closer to will communicating directly with will. It was the same method Michael and Isabella had used to speak with each other, but the Demigod had intruded on it, allowing her to understand the word Isabella had used.","Michael’s expression changed slightly. That was rather impolite.","Of course he only dared to think this, not say it.","The ghost seemed completely unconcerned and drifted closer. Michael’s body instinctively tensed again, but he didn’t move.","She slowly circled him. Her silver eyes examined him from head to toe as though she had encountered something she couldn’t understand.","Michael followed her movements with his perception.","\"What?\"","The ghost stopped beside him. Then continued floating until she was behind him.","Michael immediately felt a cold pressure against his back.","\"...\"","She leaned against him. One translucent arm rested lightly over his shoulder while a pale finger reached around and pressed against his cheek.","Michael’s eyelid twitched.","The contact was strange. She had no true physical body, yet he could still feel a faint chill wherever she touched him.","Her intention flowed into his mind again.","\"But you don’t look like me.\"","Michael paused.","The ghost tilted his face slightly with her finger.","\"So why does that little one call you Senior?\"","Isabella’s violet flames flickered violently. Little one?","Michael glanced toward her.","The Skeleton Chief had lived for more than fifty years in the Netherworld. Being called a little one by someone who looked like a young woman was admittedly strange. Then again, the being behind him was a Demigod. Age couldn’t be judged by appearance.","Michael sent back his intention.","\"It is a form of respectful address.\"","The ghost became still.","\"Respect?\"","\"Toward someone believed to be older, stronger, or more experienced.\"","She looked toward Isabella. Then back at Michael.","\"She thinks you’re older?\"","\"...Probably.\"","The ghost’s finger remained against his cheek.","\"But you aren’t old.\"","Michael’s eyebrow rose.","\"You can tell?\"","\"Yes.\"","The answer came instantly.","Michael became slightly more alert. Thanks to his strength, many tended to overestimate his age. Though there were a few ways to verify one’s age, the most accurate one was soul age.","Was it that this ghost could bypass his natural defenses and catch a glimpse of his soul?","As expected of a Demigod.","The ghost suddenly moved around him again until she floated directly in front of his face, though this time she left more than a few inches between them.","\"You are young.\"","Michael said nothing.","The ghost continued to study him.","\"So young but so strong.\"","Her gaze drifted toward the energy naturally gathering around Michael.","\"Strange too. Your nature is not from this place, but even among those I’ve seen come here, you’re the strangest by far.\"","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Others?\"","The ghost tilted her head.","\"Others like me?\"","He clarified through his will.","\"Others who weren’t born in this place.\"","Understanding immediately reached her.","The ghost nodded.","\"Yes.\"","Michael’s interest sharpened.","\"Many?\"","\"Some.\"","\"Humans?\"","She paused. Then shook her head.","\"Some looked like you. Some did not.\"","Her silver eyes drifted upward as though searching through old memories.","\"Some were tall.\"","Her hand rose above Michael’s head.","\"Some were small.\"","It dropped close to the ground.","\"Some had more arms. Some had tails. Some had scales. Some had skin like stone. Some were bright. Some were...\"","Michael listened silently. That wasn’t particularly surprising. The Netherworld clearly wasn’t connected to a singular realm. Anyone capable and daring could enter.","The ghost’s gaze returned to him.","\"But you are the strangest.\""]},{"number":1188,"title":"Chapter 1188: Leanring More About Death Heir","paragraphs":["The ghost floated closer. Michael’s muscles tightened slightly as he stopped himself from making a move. If it weren’t for the sliver of danger he couldn’t sense from her, he would have run away long ago.","She stopped directly before him and stared into his eyes.","\"You aren’t the strongest I’ve seen.\"","Michael wasn’t offended. That was obvious. She herself was stronger than him. And if she had existed long enough to encounter numerous outsiders, she had probably seen things far beyond his understanding.","\"But...\"","Her silver eyes narrowed.","\"Why do you feel close?\"","Michael froze.","The ghost leaned nearer.","\"Very close.\"","Her face approached his again. Michael resisted the instinct to move backward as her cheek brushed against his.","\"...\"","Michael remained completely still.","The ghost finally pulled away. Her expression became confused.","\"But we aren’t the same.\"","She looked down at herself. Then at him.","One spiritual being. One living human. They were completely different existences.","The confusion in her will was genuine.","Michael didn’t respond. It wasn’t because he lacked an answer. He was afraid that if he opened his mouth, he wouldn’t be able to contain his joy and would start laughing out loud.","His heart started racing again. But this time, not from fear, but from excitement. His eyes gradually brightened.","It’s the class!","Death’s Heir. There was almost no other explanation.","When Michael had first transitioned into the class, the description had stated that he possessed near absolute dominance over undead creatures. At the time, Michael had understood how absurd those words were. But only theoretically.","Since then, he had repeatedly witnessed pieces of what they actually meant. Weak undead were the simplest examples. Even Rank Four creatures. The moment they entered his influence, resistance practically ceased to exist. They obeyed him naturally. Some even worshipped him.","The effect remained incredibly strong even against Epic-grade undead. The Bone Hounds had proven that. Even when a creature possessed a higher Rank than Michael, it had still been unable to truly resist his authority.","There were differences in attitude, differences in how much individuality remained, but obedience itself remained.","Until Rank Five.","That was the only point where Michael had ever felt the absolute nature of Death’s Heir begin to loosen. He remembered clearly what happened when his undead were temporarily boosted into that realm. They still obeyed him and still recognized him. They would never attack him, and their instinct to protect him had remained. But something changed.","The unquestioning obedience became slack. If Michael gave an instruction, they might interpret it, choosing how far they wanted to obey it and deciding the method themselves. Their thoughts became far more independent.","The command still mattered. Michael still mattered. But they were no longer loyal subjects moving exactly according to his wishes. And that had happened with undead already contracted to him. Creatures whose souls were directly connected to his own.","Michael had never encountered a wild Rank Five undead before. Until now.","His gaze locked onto the ghost. This was his first opportunity to experience Death’s Heir’s authority against a naturally existing undead at the Demigod level.","And the result was fascinating.","She wasn’t kneeling. She wasn’t obeying him. She wasn’t even treating him as someone above her.","Yet she felt something. Closeness. An inexplicable familiarity strong enough that she felt no different from family.","Michael’s thoughts accelerated. Perhaps at this level, Death’s Heir couldn’t impose direct dominance on a wild undead. But the authority wasn’t gone. It was still influencing something fundamental.","Is it her instincts, or her perception of me? Maybe both.","Perhaps when I advanced it would be different.","The ghost floated around him once more.","\"I don’t understand.\"","Michael finally spoke through his will.","\"Neither do I.\"","That wasn’t entirely true. He understood more than she did.","Her silver eyes fixed on him.","\"You’re lying.\"","Michael’s expression stiffened before he offered a strained smile. At this point he was sure this ghost had some extremely strong senses.","Michael’s smile remained for a moment before he decided not to push the subject. The ghost didn’t seem particularly bothered by the lie either. She simply floated around him again, silver eyes studying him with that same intense curiosity.","Michael, meanwhile, had become much more confident. Not careless, though. The creature in front of him was still a genuine Demigod. If his interpretation of Death’s Heir was wrong, or if something suddenly changed, she could probably reduce him to nothing before he had time to regret it.","But the strange familiarity she felt toward him was real. More importantly, he still couldn’t sense hostility from her.","Michael glanced toward the Nether Soul Tree. He hesitated briefly.","\"Is that tree your treasure?\"","The ghost followed his gaze.","\"The tree?\"","\"Yes.\"","She stared at it for several seconds. Then shook her head.","\"No.\"","Michael’s eyes brightened.","What he didn’t know was that the ghost hadn’t interpreted the question in the way he intended. She understood what a treasure was. She had seen treasures before. Objects filled with power. Things fought over.","But this tree? She had simply found it growing here long ago. Sometimes she stayed near it. Sometimes she left for years before returning. It produced pleasant energy, and she liked resting beside it. Calling it a treasure had never crossed her mind. To her, it was like her home.","So naturally, she answered no.","Michael, unaware of the reasoning behind her response, became cautiously optimistic.","\"If it isn’t your treasure...\"","He pointed toward the tree.","\"Can I take it?\"","Suddenly, an enormous pressure descended upon the ravine.","BOOM!","Michael’s pupils contracted. The ground beneath him cracked. Isabella collapsed to one knee with a violent clatter of bones.","Michael’s Wisdom State surged to its absolute limit as his mana instinctively erupted around his body. His heart slammed against his chest. For the briefest instant, it felt as though the entire world had become heavy.","Shit!","*","A/N: Thank you for the continued support, dear readers!!! Cast those golden tickets you’re hiding away to support a poor author!","Semi announcement: I believe many readers might have noticed I posted a new novel. Please rest assured that this will not affect this novel’s update rate, as the other work is more of a passion project and a way to prevent writer’s block. In any case, based on previous habits, it’s pretty obvious EMUL is always my priority.","Thanks for reading!"]},{"number":1189,"title":"Chapter 1189: Very Resourceful Netherworld","paragraphs":["Michael’s spatial energy instantly gathered, and he was just about to run when the pressure disappeared completely, as if it had never existed.","\"...\"","Silence.","Michael remained frozen. His heartbeat had gone from relatively calm to insane in less than a second.","The ghost floated exactly where she had been before. Her expression hadn’t changed. She didn’t look angry, and there was still no killing intent.","Michael stared at her, cautiously.","His mouth slowly opened.","\"...So that’s a no?\"","The ghost nodded, then shook her head violently.","Michael’s eyelid twitched. He slowly released the spatial power gathered around him.","His heart, however, refused to calm down. That brief pressure had reminded him that though the ghost didn’t seem like she wanted to harm him, what exactly did harm mean to her?","This was a problem. Michael had unconsciously been judging her intentions through his own standards.","No killing intent meant she didn’t intend to kill him. No hostility meant she didn’t consider him an enemy. But neither of those things meant she couldn’t harm him.","A child might squeeze an insect without wanting to kill it. A giant might shove someone aside without considering the possibility that the person would break every bone in their body.","And this ghost.","Michael looked at her again. She had already shown that her understanding of ordinary boundaries was questionable at best. She entered other people’s spiritual communication without permission. Appeared directly inches from his face. Touched him whenever she felt curious.","Michael swallowed.","This woman is dangerous. Not necessarily malicious, but definitely dangerous.","Isabella slowly stood behind him. Several cracks now ran across portions of her bones.","Michael glanced back.","\"You alright?\"","\"Yes, Senior.\"","Michael looked at the damaged ribs.","\"...Sure.\"","The ghost also looked toward Isabella. Then tilted her head.","She then floated toward the Nether Soul Tree and wrapped both arms around its trunk. Her body partially sank through the bark.","\"Mine.\"","Michael stared.","\"You said it wasn’t your treasure.\"","\"It isn’t.\"","\"Then why can’t I take it?\"","\"Because it’s mine.\"","Michael closed his eyes. Of course.","He had asked the wrong question. The tree wasn’t her treasure. It was simply hers. There was apparently an important distinction in her mind.","Michael opened his eyes again.","\"Fine.\"","He wasn’t stupid enough to fight a Demigod over a Three-Star Epic tree. Valuable or not, his life was worth considerably more.","The ghost seemed satisfied.","Michael took one step away from the tree. Then stopped. His gaze sharpened slightly.","Actually, there was another possibility.","\"If I can’t take it...\"","The ghost looked at him.","Michael carefully continued.","\"Can I have part of it?\"","Her silver eyes blinked.","\"Part?\"","\"A branch.\"","The ghost looked at the tree. Then at Michael. Then back at the tree. For several seconds, she remained silent.","Michael kept his spatial escape ready.","Finally, she raised one pale hand. A thin black branch separated from the tree without any visible force. It floated toward Michael.","He caught it instinctively.","\"...\"","Michael stared at the branch. Then at the ghost.","She smiled.","\"You can have that.\"","Michael’s expression immediately softened.","\"Thank you.\"","Maybe communicating with her wasn’t impossible after all. He simply needed to be very, very specific.","Michael carefully stored the branch inside the Mausoleum.","\"That should be enough.\"","He had already gathered more than enough materials for the resurrection ritual. There was no reason to tempt fate over one tree when a Demigod had made her position very clear.","Michael turned toward Isabella.","\"Let’s go.\"","\"Yes, Senior.\"","Isabella moved closer immediately.","Michael was just about to open a spatial passage when he paused.","\"...\"","His eyes slowly shifted back toward the ghost. She was still floating beside the Nether Soul Tree, one arm wrapped loosely around the trunk while watching him.","Michael hesitated. He had already confirmed she was a Demigod. That should have been enough.","And yet, he was curious. Very curious.","He knew her rank. But what about her grade? What exactly was she? A ghost was merely the broadest possible description. The weaker spectral undead Michael had collected varied greatly despite appearing similar from the outside. Some were ordinary ghosts, while others possessed more specialized races.","This creature had naturally reached Demigod. Her race grade couldn’t possibly be ordinary.","Michael’s fingers twitched. Using Detect on something considerably stronger than himself wasn’t always harmless. Most weaker beings wouldn’t even notice. But powerful creatures could sometimes sense inspection. And with this ghost’s absurd perception, there was almost no chance she wouldn’t.","Michael glanced at Isabella.","\"Come closer.\"","Isabella immediately stepped beside him. Michael subtly placed a hand on her shoulder.","Wisdom State, which he had allowed to weaken slightly, surged again. Mana gathered silently around both himself and Isabella. His thoughts accelerated. Michael prepared several escape routes simultaneously. If the ghost reacted badly, he wasn’t staying around to explain himself.","The ghost tilted her head.","\"What are you doing?\"","Michael gave her a harmless smile.","\"Nothing.\"","Her silver eyes narrowed. Michael ignored that.","Detect.","For the briefest moment, nothing happened. Then the familiar translucent panel appeared.","Michael’s eyes widened.","[Netherborn Soul Saint]","[Grade: Epic ★★★]","Netherborn Soul Saint?","That race name sounded almost holy. Not something he would have associated with a ghost. More importantly, there was something about the word Netherborn that immediately caught his attention.","Born of the Netherworld itself?","Also she’s three stars?!","Michael’s gaze sharpened, his eyes lingering on the grade.","It was extremely high.","A Demigod with an Epic Three-Star race. Michael’s excitement rose again. This wasn’t simply some powerful ghost that had survived long enough to reach Rank Five. Her very existence was special.","Then the ghost’s face suddenly appeared directly beside the panel.","\"...\"","Michael nearly jumped again. She was floating inches from him.","\"When you look at me like that...\"","Her silver eyes stared directly into his.","\"It feels strange.\"","Michael immediately dismissed Detect.","\"Sorry.\"","The ghost touched her chest.","\"You looked deeper.\"","Michael’s heartbeat sped up.","*","A/N: Thank you for the continued support dear readers!"]},{"number":1190,"title":"Chapter 1190: Tricking A Demigod [1]","paragraphs":["She had noticed. Of course she had.","Michael’s grip on Isabella’s shoulder tightened slightly. The spatial power he had prepared remained ready.","The ghost studied him. Then, nothing happened. She simply leaned closer.","\"What did you see?\"","Michael paused. That question surprised him.","\"You know I saw something?\"","\"Yes.\"","Michael relaxed slightly. At this point, he was infinitely grateful for the class he had chosen to transition into back then. If he had chosen any other class back then, regardless of how powerful it was, his reckless actions now would have gotten him killed ten times over.","Perhaps only the Shadow Slave or Grave Warden class would have differed slightly.","Michael remained silent for several moments. He had originally intended to leave. After all, his resurrection materials were already sufficient, and staying near a Demigod any longer than necessary was asking for trouble.","But now that he knew more about this ghost, suddenly, she looked extremely attractive. Not in the physical sense, of course. He only had one person in his heart, and his orientation was perfectly ordinary for a human. He would only see another human that way.","She looked extremely attractive in value. He wanted her. He really wanted her.","A wild Demigod undead with a Three-Star Epic race. If he could somehow bring her into his legion, his overall strength would rise enormously. And that was before considering the other Demigod corpse he intended to resurrect.","Two Demigods. Michael’s heart accelerated just thinking about it. Most top-tier middle realms would consider two Demigods an overwhelming foundation.","With both under him, many of his current worries would disappear almost instantly. Even the Federation would have to treat such power seriously. More importantly, protecting his family would become easier.","Unfortunately, Michael looked at the ghost and immediately remembered the pressure from moments ago. There was one significant problem. He couldn’t force her. Not even remotely.","Death’s Heir clearly influenced her, but she was still a genuine Rank Five existence. Michael lacked the strength to enforce his will upon her. He couldn’t beat her into submission, nor could he even force her to sit down and negotiate with him as an equal.","This left only one option remaining.","Michael’s expression gradually became thoughtful.","I have to trick her.","The thought appeared naturally. He almost dismissed it, but stopped and reconsidered it properly.","The ghost was not stupid. Far from it. Her intelligence clearly wasn’t inferior to his own, but looking past that, at some of her other characteristics, this overpowered ghost felt a bit... naive.","Michael still didn’t know whether that was simply her natural personality or whether Death’s Heir was making her unusually trusting toward him. Either way, there was no harm in testing it.","At worst, she refused. At slightly worse, well, Michael glanced toward the shattered ground. She had misunderstood him and nearly crushed him already.","In any case, his spatial escape remained prepared. This time he was so prepared he didn’t even need to think of teleporting away, and instead had to force himself not to teleport. The moment his mind went blank, or he stopped thinking about it even accidentally, he would be out of here.","It’s worth the risk.","Michael loosened his grip on Isabella’s shoulder slightly and turned fully toward the ghost. She was still watching him curiously.","Michael chose his words carefully.","\"Have you ever wanted to see the outside world?\"","The ghost blinked in confusion.","\"Outside?\"","\"Outside the Netherworld.\"","Her silver eyes became still. Michael immediately noticed the shift in her attention. *Good.*","He continued.","\"You said you’ve seen outsiders before.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Do you know they come here from other worlds?\"","The ghost nodded.","Michael gestured vaguely upward.","\"Have you ever wondered where they came from?\"","She didn’t answer immediately. Her gaze drifted toward the dark sky beyond the ravine. For several seconds, Michael sensed something unfamiliar pass through her will.","Curiosity. A deeper kind than before.","\"I have.\"","Michael’s lips almost curved upward, but he quickly suppressed it.","\"Have you ever gone there?\"","The ghost shook her head.","\"No.\"","\"Why?\"","She seemed confused by the question.","\"Why would I?\"","Michael paused. Right. Someone had to first possess the concept of wanting to travel before asking why they hadn’t.","He quickly adjusted.","\"Because there are things outside the Netherworld that don’t exist here.\"","Her attention returned to him.","\"What things?\"","Michael almost smiled. This was what he wanted to see. While he might not succeed, the ghost entertaining him showed there was still a chance.","\"Too many to explain.\"","The ghost floated closer.","\"Explain.\"","\"Living cities.\"","She stared.","\"Cities?\"","\"Places where millions of beings gather together.\"","Her silver eyes widened slightly.","\"Millions?\"","\"Sometimes more. There are so many things to see there than here.\"","Michael continued before she could interrupt.","\"Don’t you want a change of scenery?\"","\"To see different races. Food.....\"","The ghost tilted her head.","\"Food?\"","Michael looked at her translucent body.","\"...Maybe that one isn’t relevant.\"","Isabella’s soul flames flickered behind him. He felt a stinging gaze at his back, but ignored it. He knew he had gotten carried away.","\"Are there really places like that outside?\" the ghost asked.","The ghost’s silver eyes grew increasingly focused. Michael could feel her curiosity building. He could understand it a little. The Netherworld might be unimaginably vast, yet if she had spent most of her existence wandering through regions like this, the novelty of the material world alone would be enormous.","\"Can I really see it?\" the ghost asked.","Michael’s heart began beating faster. This was going far better than expected. Yet he forced himself to remain cautious. A single mistake could still ruin everything.","He slowly smiled.","\"Of course.\"","Then added the most important part.","\"If you want.\"","The ghost stared at him. Michael stared back. For once, neither communicated through will.","Then the ghost’s silver eyes curved slightly.","\"I want to see.\"","Michael’s smile deepened. However, before his happiness could settle, the ghost poured cold water on him.","\"But I don’t want to do anything for you.\""]},{"number":1191,"title":"Chapter 1191: Tricking A Demigod [2]","paragraphs":["Michael’s smile stiffened.","\"...\"","For several seconds, he simply stared at the ghost. She stared back innocently.","\"I don’t want to do anything for you,\" she repeated.","Michael’s expression slowly twisted. What use would there be in bringing a Demigod outside if she refused to help him? Worse, with her personality, she might not even agree to a contract.","Michael had only wanted to bring her into his sphere because of the value she represented. A Three-Star Epic Demigod. Even if she wasn’t directly under his control, having such an existence nearby would be an enormous deterrent.","But if she refused to cooperate in anything, she could even become a walking disaster he had personally released into Aurora.","Michael glanced at the shattered ground nearby.","Also, just because she liked him didn’t mean she would treat everyone else the same way. In fact, she probably wouldn’t. Death’s Heir was almost certainly responsible for the strange closeness she felt toward him. Ordinary people wouldn’t possess that protection.","If someone annoyed her. Or misunderstood her. Or simply touched something she considered hers. Michael could already imagine the result.","Absolutely not.","There was no way he was taking her to Aurora without some form of guarantee.","Of course, none of those thoughts appeared on his face. Michael wasn’t ready to give up yet. He had gotten this far. There had to be something he could use.","The ghost floated lazily before him, completely unaware that Michael was desperately searching for a way to seduce, cough, persuade her into becoming an ally.","Michael thought rapidly. Then his eyes brightened.","\"What if...\"","The ghost tilted her head.","\"...I had something you wanted?\"","Michael watched carefully. The ghost’s silver eyes drifted slightly as she appeared to genuinely consider the question. Several seconds passed.","Then she shook her head.","\"I don’t want anything.\"","Michael’s expression almost collapsed.","\"Nothing?\"","\"Nothing.\"","\"You’ve never wanted anything?\"","The ghost thought again.","\"No.\"","Michael stared at her. That answer wasn’t arrogance. He could feel it clearly through their shared intentions. She genuinely believed she desired nothing.","And perhaps that made sense. She didn’t need food. She didn’t need shelter. She possessed overwhelming strength. The Netherworld itself nourished her. She had no society forcing material desires onto her. She didn’t seem to care about status, most likely because she was the status itself. She barely understood ownership beyond instinctively claiming things she liked.","What exactly was someone like that supposed to want?","But as crazy as it sounds, Michael felt he had something a Demigod of any kind would desire.","What was the most addictive thing in the universe?","Desire.","Michael had gradually come to understand that it didn’t matter whether someone was ordinary or extraordinary.","Poor or wealthy.","Unknown or worshipped.","Mortal or god.","Everyone desired something.","A starving man desired food.","A poor man might desire wealth. A wealthy merchant might desire greater influence.","A ruler with an entire kingdom could still desire another piece of land.","A warrior desired strength. A scholar desired knowledge.","Someone surrounded by enemies desired safety. Someone trapped by responsibility desired freedom.","Someone approaching the end of their lifespan desired another hundred years.","Even those who possessed almost everything could still find something beyond their reach, and the moment they did, desire would emerge.","It didn’t necessarily have to be grand.","Recognition. Love. Curiosity. A rare object. A new experience. Something another person possessed. Something they had never even known existed until it was placed before them.","That was the interesting thing about desire. A person couldn’t desire what they couldn’t imagine.","Perhaps the ghost genuinely believed she wanted nothing. Michael believed her. But that didn’t mean she was incapable of desire. Perhaps she had simply never encountered anything capable of making her want more.","Michael slowly inhaled. Then he summoned an item from his storage.","A crystalline object appeared above his palm. It was translucent, almost colorless, yet countless specks of light continuously moved inside it like tiny stars.","The moment it appeared, Isabella’s violet soul flames shifted toward it. The ghost’s silver eyes did the same.","A translucent panel floated within his vision.","[Evolution Essence Crystal]","[Grade: Extraordinary]","[Effect: When used by an Extraordinary-grade creature, it can raise the creature’s racial grade to Three-Star Extraordinary, the peak of the Extraordinary Grade.]","Reading the description alone, one would naturally assume the Evolution Essence Crystal could only be used by monsters. That wasn’t entirely true. The information displayed by the system merely described its most direct and efficient use.","Michael had been able to produce Evolution Essence Crystals through his talent for months now. Naturally, he hadn’t spent all that time simply stockpiling them without experimenting.","He had discovered several things. For one, Evolution Essence Crystals weren’t exclusively monster consumable resources. Michael had already confirmed that they could potentially be incorporated into the creation of equipment.","He hadn’t explored that path deeply since he wasn’t a craftsman, but the possibility existed.","Ordinary beings could theoretically absorb their essence as well. Humans. Elves. Other intelligent races. However, the result was completely different from what happened when a monster used one.","For ordinary beings, the energy wouldn’t conveniently increase their racial grade.","Instead, the essence would interact with their body according to numerous factors Michael still didn’t completely understand.","Bloodline. Physique. Race. And probably several other things.","Most importantly, a large portion of the crystal’s power would simply be wasted. Michael suspected that someone sufficiently knowledgeable might eventually develop a method to properly utilize it, but that was a problem for another day.","What mattered now was something else he had discovered. An Evolution Essence Crystal didn’t suddenly become useless because a creature’s grade surpassed the crystal’s own.","The system description had initially given Michael the wrong impression.","If an Extraordinary-grade monster used an Extraordinary Evolution Essence Crystal, the system would assist with the process.","The creature could directly absorb the crystal and, provided it fulfilled the necessary conditions, its racial grade would rise. Simple and efficient.","But if a Rare-grade creature absorbed an Extraordinary Evolution Essence Crystal? Or an Epic-grade creature?"]},{"number":1192,"title":"Chapter 1192: Supernatural Grade Drug","paragraphs":["The essence didn’t simply disappear. It still worked. Just differently. The system no longer conveniently converted everything into a direct racial advancement.","Instead, the creature absorbed the raw evolutionary essence itself. How useful that essence became depended entirely on the creature.","For something already far beyond the crystal’s grade, a single Extraordinary Evolution Essence Crystal obviously wouldn’t accomplish much. It was like pouring a cup of water into a lake. The water still entered the lake. There simply wasn’t enough of it to noticeably raise the water level.","And that was exactly what Michael wanted. He wasn’t trying to evolve the ghost with an Extraordinary-grade crystal.","That would be ridiculous. He only wanted her to experience what was inside it.","Michael’s gaze shifted from the crystal to the ghost. Her silver eyes remained fixed upon his hand. Michael’s heartbeat accelerated slightly.","This was probably one of the most reckless experiments he had ever attempted. He was about to introduce an energy provided by his talent into the body of a Demigod he had met less than an hour ago.","However, as crazy as it sounded, Michael trusted undead more than he trusted other intelligent beings.","At least they wouldn’t scheme against him in secret. If they had malice toward him, it would be pure and open.","Michael’s connection with the surrounding space tightened. His hand remained on Isabella. One wrong reaction, or one fluctuation of hostility, and he was gone.","Michael looked directly into the ghost’s silver eyes.","\"Don’t resist.\"","\"Why?\"","\"I promise you, you’ll like this.\"","The ghost stared at him for a moment. Then nodded.","\"Okay.\"","Michael almost questioned whether she should really trust someone that easily. Then he remembered Death’s Heir.","Right. Probably my fault.","Michael slowly tightened his fingers.","Crack.","A fracture appeared across the Evolution Essence Crystal. The ghost’s eyes immediately moved toward it.","Crack!","More fractures spread. The light trapped within the crystal intensified until the entire thing resembled a tiny star resting within Michael’s palm.","Then Michael crushed it.","Shatter!","The crystal collapsed into countless fragments. But before they could fall, the fragments dissolved. A strange translucent essence emerged from them.","It didn’t resemble ordinary mana. The energy was almost colorless, possessing only a faint silver-white tint, yet Michael could feel the peculiar vitality contained within it. That was the closest description Michael could give it.","Unfortunately, perhaps only when he ascended to a higher rank could he understand what this energy truly was.","Michael controlled the essence carefully.","\"Here.\"","The stream of evolutionary energy floated toward the ghost.","Michael watched her expression. The ghost watched the energy. For the first time, she seemed slightly cautious. Her silver eyes narrowed as the essence approached her translucent fingers.","Michael’s eyes brightened. The evolutionary essence flowed through her hand. Then her arm. Then gradually spread throughout her spiritual body.","The effect was immediate. The ghost froze. Her silver eyes widened.","\"...\"","Michael’s heartbeat accelerated. He could sense it. The Extraordinary-grade essence was laughably small compared to the terrifying amount of energy contained within her.","It entered her existence and practically disappeared. There was no advancement or visible strengthening. Not even a measurable increase in her aura.","Exactly as Michael expected.","if she isn’t stupid, she should have felt it by now.","The ghost remained frozen for several seconds. Then her expression drastically changed. Though ghosts, as part of the undead family, were even more expressive than a race like vampires, Michael hadn’t expected to see this level of expressiveness from her.","Greed.","It was raw. Almost frighteningly pure.","Michael’s heart skipped. At the same time, the ghost’s aura surged out of control.","BOOM!","The ravine shook violently. Countless cracks spread through the surrounding cliffs. The air distorted beneath the weight of Demigod-level pressure. It wasn’t directed at Michael.","It was simply the ghost losing control for a brief moment under the sudden force of what she had felt.","Unfortunately, that distinction meant absolutely nothing to Michael.","The moment her aura erupted, he disappeared. Space folded. Michael and Isabella vanished from the ravine.","The next instant, they appeared several kilometres away in the air. Michael didn’t stop. His Law surged again. He was already preparing another teleportation.","But just before space folded again, an intention reached him from behind.","\"Please don’t run.\"","Michael froze in midair. His expression became extremely cautious.","Isabella remained clutched beside him. Neither turned around immediately.","Michael’s perception expanded. The ghost was approaching. Fast.","Michael’s mana gathered again. Then she stopped, a hundred metres away.","Michael finally turned. The ghost floated there almost as if she had somehow understood that approaching too closely might send him running again.","Her silver eyes were still unusually bright. The excitement had not disappeared. But her aura was now completely restrained.","Michael narrowed his eyes.","\"What do you want?\"","The ghost’s expression became slightly troubled. Then her gaze dropped toward Michael’s hands.","\"That thing.\"","Michael immediately understood.","\"The crystal?\"","She nodded rapidly.","\"I want more.\"","Michael didn’t respond.","The ghost seemed to think. Then she raised both hands and began gesturing awkwardly.","\"A lot.\"","Michael’s eyebrow rose.","\"How much?\"","The ghost paused. Clearly, numbers were not something she used often. She spread her fingers. Then repeated the gesture.","Again. Again. Again.","Michael stared blankly.","The ghost frowned. Then tried communicating through intent instead. The meaning that reached Michael was extremely crude.","Michael’s expression slowly became strange.","\"Are you asking for...\"","He mentally translated the vague quantity.","\"...tens of thousands?\"","The ghost’s eyes brightened.","\"Yes.\"","Michael nearly choked.","Why doesn’t she just say she wants to rob me instead?","A single crystal of the level he had given her cost 30,000 Evolution Points to make. Don’t even talk about 10,000; he couldn’t even afford a thousand, which would be about 30 million Evolution Points.","With that much, he could evolve thirty of her to Legendary grade.","However, it wasn’t like Michael couldn’t understand her. He had expected this.","Compared to intelligent races, monsters, regardless of kind, craved evolution more purely than anything else.","Months ago, Michael had experimented with a Rare-grade monster using a Common-grade Evolution Essence Crystal, and the result was no different from what he was seeing now.","Yes.","If used right, Michael could make his Evolution Essence Crystals no different from an addictive drug for supernatural creatures.","*","A/N: Vote to support novel!!!"]},{"number":1193,"title":"Chapter 1193: Deal","paragraphs":["Michael had expected the crystal to work. He simply hadn’t expected it to work this well.","The ghost’s reaction had been far more intense than anything he anticipated, but no matter how excessive her reaction had been, it had given Michael exactly what he needed.","A chance.","Michael stared at the ghost hovering a hundred metres away.","\"Tens of thousands is impossible.\"","Michael continued before she could react.","\"I can’t give you that many, but if you’re willing to come with me, I can continue giving you those crystals.\"","The ghost tilted her head.","\"How many?\"","Michael’s eyelid twitched.","Straight to the important question.","He appreciated that, at least.","\"Not tens of thousands.\"","The ghost frowned.","Michael raised a hand.","\"Listen first.\"","She became quiet.","Michael carefully organized his thoughts.","\"I won’t ask you to constantly work for me.\"","The ghost’s silver eyes remained fixed on him.","\"You can go where you want inside the places I allow you to stay.\"","\"You can explore the outside world.\"","\"You won’t need to fight every day.\"","Michael paused.","\"But occasionally, I’ll need your help.\"","The ghost immediately seemed less interested.","Michael continued before she could reject him.","\"And whenever I ask for your help...\"","He raised one finger.","\"...I’ll pay you.\"","The ghost froze.","\"Pay?\"","\"With those crystals.\"","Her silver eyes brightened instantly.","Michael smiled faintly.","\"You do something for me, and I give you a corresponding amount of those crystals.\"","The ghost drifted slightly closer before remembering herself and stopping.","\"What things?\"","\"Different things.\"","Michael began counting on his fingers.","\"If I ask you to protect someone, you’ll be paid.\"","\"If I ask you to fight someone, you’ll be paid.\"","\"If I need you to accompany me somewhere dangerous, you’ll be paid.\"","\"If I ask you to guard a place for some time, you’ll be paid.\"","\"The harder the task...\"","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"...the more crystals you receive.\"","The ghost stared at him. For once, she didn’t immediately respond.","Michael could feel her thoughts moving through the faint connection between their wills. Knowing she was seriously considering it, he didn’t interrupt. There was no reason to pressure her. Michael had already presented the offer. Now she needed to convince herself.","Isabella remained beside him, silent throughout the exchange. Her violet soul flames occasionally shifted between Michael and the Demigod ghost. Michael could only imagine what she thought of the situation.","A Rank Four living being was negotiating employment terms with a Demigod undead using strange crystals as payment. Even to Michael, the situation sounded ridiculous when phrased that way.","Oh wait, he wasn’t actually Rank Four yet.","Tsk.","The ghost finally looked down at her hands. Then toward the direction of the ravine where the Nether Soul Tree remained. Then back toward Michael.","\"If I don’t want to do something?\"","Michael had expected that question.","\"You can refuse.\"","The ghost’s eyes immediately brightened.","Michael raised another finger.","\"But then you won’t get paid for it.\"","She became still again.","Michael almost laughed. He could practically see the internal calculation happening.","Freedom, or crystals.","The ghost remained silent.","Michael added calmly, \"I’m not asking you to become my slave.\"","That wasn’t entirely what he wanted, but telling a Demigod that would be idiotic.","\"I want cooperation.\"","\"You help me when I need it.\"","\"I give you something you want.\"","\"Both sides benefit.\"","The ghost slowly floated in a small circle. Michael continued watching without interfering.","Several seconds passed. Then nearly a minute. For someone who had answered most questions immediately until now, the amount of thought she was putting into this told Michael she was genuinely interested.","Eventually, her silver eyes returned to him.","\"How many for fighting?\"","Michael nearly smiled. That was not a rejection. Far from it.","\"Depends on who you’re fighting.\"","\"Someone like you?\"","Michael’s expression stiffened.","\"...Why is that your first example?\"","The ghost looked confused.","\"You said fighting.\"","\"Right.\"","Michael rubbed his forehead.","\"For someone around my strength, very few.\"","The ghost frowned.","\"How few?\"","Michael thought for a moment.","\"One.\"","Her silver eyes widened.","\"One?\"","Michael smiled.","\"There’s barely anybody on my level in the universe I can’t beat.\"","He wasn’t lying. He was someone who ranked high on a leaderboard meant for the rank above him. If there was any Rank Three being who could defeat him, he would eat grass with Lucky.","The ghost’s attention shifted.","\"What about someone like me?\"","Michael’s expression became serious. That was a much better question.","Michael considered the cost. Then he answered.","\"A lot.\"","The ghost leaned forward.","\"How much?\"","Michael smiled.","\"We’ll negotiate when that happens.\"","She frowned again. Michael didn’t budge. There was no chance he was establishing a fixed price for Demigod combat before understanding how difficult producing enough crystals for her would actually become. He still had thousands of undead he had to evolve, and so many more things to do.","The ghost studied him for several seconds. Then nodded.","\"Okay.\"","\"...Okay?\"","\"I’ll go.\"","His heart jumped.","That easy?","Michael didn’t allow the excitement to show. He immediately continued.","\"There are conditions.\"","Michael almost felt guilty. Almost.","\"One: you cannot harm anyone I specifically tell you not to harm.\"","She stared at him.","\"You cannot destroy things simply because they annoy you.\"","Her head tilted.","\"And if you’re uncertain whether something is allowed...\"","Michael pointed toward himself.","\"Ask me.\"","The ghost thought about this. Then nodded.","Michael added another condition.","\"You also cannot leave the place I bring you to without telling me first.\"","That received a longer pause.","\"Why?\"","\"Because the outside world is different from here.\"","Michael gestured toward Isabella.","\"Most beings there are far weaker than you.\"","\"If you release your aura like you did earlier in the middle of a city...\"","He paused.","\"A lot of people could die.\"","The ghost’s silver eyes shifted toward Isabella’s damaged body.","\"...Oh.\"","\"Exactly.\"","Michael’s voice became firmer.","\"If you want to explore, I’ll take you.\"","\"But until you understand the outside world properly, you should stay where I tell you.\"","The ghost became quiet again.","Michael waited. This condition mattered more than everything else. He wasn’t bringing an uncontrolled Demigod into Aurora simply because she promised to fight for crystals.","Eventually, the ghost nodded.","\"Okay.\"","Michael’s expression finally softened.","\"Good.\"","His heart was pounding again. Not from fear this time.","Two Demigods.","The thought surfaced once more. One he would revive. And another he had somehow hired with Evolution Essence Crystals.","Michael almost laughed. His talent was becoming increasingly absurd."]},{"number":1194,"title":"Chapter 1194: Panel [1]","paragraphs":["Just as Michael had suspected, evolution mattered enormously to monsters. In fact, the stronger a monster became, the deeper that instinct could grow.","For the ghost, the feeling brought by the Evolution Essence Crystal was almost unfamiliar. There had only been a few moments throughout her existence when she had experienced something remotely similar.","The earliest stretched so far back that even she could barely remember it clearly. Back when she had first formed within the Netherworld. Back when her consciousness had been little more than scattered impulses drifting through dense soul energy.","The Nether Soul Tree had already been there, and its energy continuously washed across the surrounding region. And because the ghost had remained close to it for most of her existence, that energy had become so ordinary that she barely noticed it anymore.","Warmth. Comfort. Familiarity. Those were the only meanings she associated with the tree. She had never understood that the constant nourishment it provided had quietly influenced her growth for countless years.","The ghost did not know that the reason she had eventually developed into a Three-Star Epic Netherborn Soul Saint was inseparably connected to that tree.","To her, their relationship had always been much simpler. The tree was hers. She stayed near it because she liked it. That was all. Even now, she did not understand the deeper connection between them.","But Michael’s crystal was different. Completely different.","The moment that strange essence entered her spiritual body, something buried extraordinarily deep within her existence had awakened. Strength itself had never particularly interested her. She was already powerful enough that most things she encountered couldn’t threaten her.","What she felt was much more fundamental. An instinct to evolve. To become more. It wasn’t something she consciously chose to desire. Her very existence hungered for it.","The amount contained in the crystal had been insignificant. So insignificant that the actual improvement to her body could barely be described as measurable. But she had a feeling that if she could absorb and accumulate many of them, a qualitative change would happen.","It was why she had agreed. She didn’t want to serve Michael. What she liked doing was sleeping.","Though she also wondered about the outside world, she felt it would limit her sleep time, but this time she had to make the decision. She simply wanted more of that energy.","Michael knew none of this. At the moment, his attention was focused entirely elsewhere.","A translucent formation of mana floated before him. Lines of light intertwined in increasingly complicated patterns while Michael silently modified the contract spell, adjusting it from the master-and-servant version he had originally only used.","He had considered tricking her. After all, the ordinary version of the contract would have given him considerably more control than what he had verbally promised.","If he worded things carefully enough and rushed her through the process, there was a genuine chance she might sign it without fully understanding every restriction, but he felt this was too risky.","Not because he believed she would definitely discover the deception immediately. She might not. The problem was what happened if she discovered it later.","This wasn’t some Rank Two monster he could simply suppress if negotiations failed. This was a Demigod. More importantly, she already possessed enough intelligence to understand betrayal.","If she ever realized Michael had deliberately manipulated the terms after pretending to offer her freedom, everything he had accomplished today would become meaningless. All of it could disappear.","And then Michael would leave the Netherworld with nothing except one branch and an extremely angry Demigod who knew exactly what he looked like.","That sounded unnecessarily stupid.","Also, he didn’t really like feeling like a scumbag. He preferred being a tyrant more, if he had to.","For now, honesty was simply the more profitable option.","Michael studied the completed spell. It was nowhere near as restrictive as he would have preferred. But it was fair. It was one of employer and employee, edging toward equals but still putting him a bit on the higher ground.","Michael looked toward her.","\"One more thing.\"","The ghost’s attention shifted toward the glowing formation.","\"What is that?\"","\"A contract.\"","She floated closer.","Michael immediately raised a hand.","She stopped and continued looking at the formation.","The ghost looked at him.","\"You aren’t going to trick me?\"","Michael’s expression froze for the briefest moment.","\"...Why would you ask that?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","Michael stared at her. Then sighed. Her perception really was ridiculous.","\"...Can we focus on the contract?\"","Isabella’s violet flames flickered violently beside him. Michael ignored her.","The ghost did not appear offended. Instead, she returned her attention to the spell and carefully inspected it.","Michael allowed her as much time as necessary.","Several minutes passed.","Finally, the ghost looked toward him.","\"Let’s do it.\"","Michael raised his hand.","\"Then place your will here.\"","The ghost extended one translucent finger toward the center of the formation. Her spiritual energy entered it. The entire contract instantly erupted with silver light.","Michael felt the connection form. Not the overwhelming master-servant bond he possessed with his undead. Something much weaker.","Michael stared at the ghost as the final strands of light disappeared into both of them. Then he finally allowed himself to smile and called upon the status panel of the ghost.","[Name: ???]","[Race: Netherborn Soul Saint]","[Grade: Epic ★★★]","[Level: 112]","[Type: Spiritual Undead]","[Trait: Soul Saint Physique, Netherworld’s Child]","[Skills: Soul Frost, White Netherfire, Mirror Soul, Divine Incarnation Possession...]","[Domain Law Technique: Ice Wheel]","Michael’s heart began beating faster the moment his gaze reached the fourth line.","[Level: 112]","\"...\"","Level One Hundred and Twelve.","This was the first time Michael had ever been able to see the exact level of a being beyond Level One Hundred. Until now, Rank Five had always been somewhat abstract to him.","Michael suppressed his excitement and quickly continued reading.","After a quick glance, two things stood out to him. One was a skill, and the other was the Domain Law Technique.","Unfortunately, no information opened for the latter, but Michael guessed it was probably something only Rank Five beings could have, given he had never seen it in any of his Rank Four undead’s status panels before.","Fortunately, the skill description could be seen, and its details were quite interesting.","[Divine Incarnation Possession]","[Description: The Netherborn Soul Saint may enter a compatible living or spiritual vessel and establish a parasitic symbiosis with the host. Rather than simply suppressing or replacing the original consciousness, the user may merge portions of their existence with the possessed target]","[While Possession is active, the host may temporarily share properties belonging to the Netherborn Soul Saint, including portions of its race traits, spiritual nature, elemental affinities, resistances, senses, skills, and physical characteristics]","[The depth of synchronization depends on compatibility, the amount of soul power invested, and the willingness or resistance of the host]","[At higher synchronization, the possessed vessel may reproduce characteristics of the original body to an extreme degree, effectively functioning as a secondary incarnation of the Netherborn Soul Saint]","*","A/N: Vote to support novel!!!"]},{"number":1195,"title":"Chapter 1195: Panel [2]","paragraphs":["Michael read the description of the skill and could understand the general idea easily enough.","Possession-type abilities were hardly rare among ghosts. In fact, depending on the species, possessing living creatures could practically be considered one of their defining abilities.","Some ghosts used possession simply to move through the material world. Others used it to feed on vitality. Certain malicious spirits could even slowly corrupt a host until nothing remained except an empty body under their control.","So the foundation of Divine Incarnation Possession wasn’t particularly difficult to understand. What made this version unusual was everything built on top of it.","Perhaps it was because of her race, or because she had reached the Demigod realm. Or maybe it was a combination of both. Whatever the case, this was clearly no ordinary possession skill.","The possessed target didn’t merely become a puppet. They could actually begin inheriting properties from the ghost herself.","Michael’s expression became thoughtful.","If the amount of power transferred depended on how much of herself the ghost invested into the host, then Divine Incarnation Possession wasn’t merely a utility or infiltration skill.","It was an enhancement skill. And potentially an absurd one.","Michael immediately looked toward the ghost.","\"How much stronger can you make someone with this?\"","She tilted her head in confusion.","\"When you enter someone.\"","Understanding appeared in her silver eyes.","\"Oh.\"","She floated closer.","\"A lot.\"","Michael’s eyelid twitched.","\"How much is ’a lot’?\"","The ghost became thoughtful.","Michael waited.","The ghost’s silver eyes moved across his body. Her expression gradually changed.","\"You...\"","She moved closer.","Michael remained still.","\"You can hold a lot.\"","His heartbeat increased.","\"How much?\"","The ghost thought. Then answered simply.","\"Most.\"","Michael froze.","\"...Most of what?\"","\"Me.\"","Silence.","Michael’s mind immediately began calculating.","Most of a Demigod.","If Divine Incarnation Possession could allow him to temporarily carry most of her properties and strength, his current combat ability was already absurd for Rank Three.","He could already compete with the foundation of an outside-world Level 100 mage, and could battle a physical-based supernatural of Level 90 for a period of time.","If he then layered the properties of a Level 112 Three-Star Epic Demigod over himself, Michael swallowed.","\"That sounds disgusting.\"","The ghost tilted her head.","\"Disgusting?\"","\"In a good way.\"","She seemed even more confused. Michael ignored her.","Michael’s expression soon became strange.","Could she possess one of his undead?","The idea immediately opened another rabbit hole, but before his thoughts could run too far, he forced himself to return to the more obvious possibility.","Himself.","The ghost had already said he could contain most of her. That statement had been sitting in the back of his mind ever since she said it.","Michael stared at her for several seconds. Curiosity gradually defeated his reluctance.","\"...What happens if you possess me? Will it harm me?\"","The ghost became thoughtful.","Michael’s expression turned serious.","\"Think carefully.\"","He wasn’t about to experiment with a Demigod possession ability based on one of her usual vague answers.","The ghost floated closer and stared at him. Her silver gaze moved across his body before sinking deeper.","Michael felt that familiar sensation of something brushing across his soul. His instincts immediately tightened, but he remained still.","Several seconds passed.","\"No.\"","Michael’s eyes narrowed.","\"No what?\"","\"You won’t break.\"","\"That’s reassuring.\"","She nodded as though she had given an excellent answer.","Michael rubbed his forehead.","\"I mean afterward.\"","The ghost tilted her head.","\"After?\"","\"Will there be damage to my soul?\"","\"No.\"","\"My body?\"","\"No.\"","\"My mind?\"","She paused.","Michael’s eyes sharpened.","\"No.\"","\"Then why did you take so long to answer?\"","\"I was thinking.\"","\"...Right.\"","Michael continued.","\"Could you accidentally take over my body?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"...\"","Michael immediately went silent.","The ghost added, \"But I won’t.\"","Michael stared at her.","\"I promise.\"","There was no hesitation behind the intention.","Michael remembered the contract. She couldn’t deliberately harm him. More importantly, Death’s Heir already created a strange natural closeness between them.","Even if something went wrong, Michael suspected his class would make complete hostile possession extremely difficult.","Even now, he felt nothing but great goodwill from her toward him after signing the contract.","Michael sighed.","\"Fine.\"","The ghost’s silver eyes brightened.","\"Do it.\"","She immediately floated toward him.","\"Wait.\"","She stopped.","\"This counts as work.\"","Michael froze.","The ghost stared at him. Michael stared back.","\"...One crystal.\"","\"Two.\"","Michael’s eyebrow twitched.","\"One.\"","\"Two.\"","\"One.\"","The ghost floated closer.","\"Two.\"","Michael stared at her for several seconds. Then sighed.","\"Fine. Two.\"","Her expression immediately became satisfied.","\"Now.\"","\"...Now?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"After.\"","The ghost’s eyes narrowed.","\"Now.\"","\"After the test.\"","\"Why?\"","\"Because I’m not paying you before you do anything.\"","The ghost thought about it. Then nodded.","\"Okay.\"","Michael took a slow breath.","\"Isabella.\"","\"Yes, Senior?\"","\"If anything strange happens...\"","He paused. Then realized how useless that sentence was.","What exactly was Isabella supposed to do against a Demigod?","\"...Just move away.\"","Isabella remained silent for a moment.","\"Yes, Senior.\"","Michael relaxed his body.","\"Alright.\"","He looked directly at the ghost.","\"Start, please.\"","The ghost floated toward him. This time, Michael didn’t resist.","Her translucent hand pressed against his chest.","It was cold, like the sensation of standing beneath winter rain.","Then her fingers sank through him.","Michael’s pupils contracted.","The rest of her hand followed. Then her arm. The ghost continued drifting forward until half of her body overlapped with his.","Michael immediately felt something touch his soul. His instincts exploded.","For a fraction of a second, Michael nearly teleported away. Then he forcefully stopped himself and let the ghost continue to possess him.","BOOM!","Michael’s aura changed.","Isabella, who had distanced herself, staggered backward. Her violet soul flames widened.","\"Senior?!\"","Michael didn’t answer. He couldn’t. He was too busy processing what had happened.","His black hair began turning silver from the roots. Frost spread across his skin in thin crystalline patterns. His pupils disappeared. Both eyes became completely silver.","At the same time, faint translucent mist drifted from his body."]},{"number":1196,"title":"Chapter 1196: Panel [3]","paragraphs":["The change wasn’t merely visual. Michael could feel it crawling through him, an icy vastness pouring into every corner of his being, as though his own mind had been stretched to make room for something far larger than himself.","His thoughts moved strangely, sharper in some places and disturbingly foreign in others, like borrowing a room in his own house that had quietly been redecorated by someone else.","Beneath the cold, there was an unmistakable sense of scale, of touching something that dwarfed his ordinary self entirely.","Michael looked down at his hands. They were still flesh. Yet they didn’t entirely feel physical anymore.","He could feel the material world. But also something layered beneath it.","Michael slowly raised one hand. His fingers became translucent. Then solid again.","\"...Spiritualization.\"","The ghost’s voice reached him from inside his mind.","\"Yes.\"","Michael’s heart began pounding. He clenched his fist, and mana erupted.","BOOM!","The ground shook.","Michael immediately restrained himself. Quickly, he summoned his status panel.","[Class]: Death’s Heir","[Attributes]","Strength: 2158.75 (+432)","Agility: 2400.71 (+1293)","Constitution: 2574.92 (+689)","Intelligence: 2620.92 (+3632)","Attribute Points: 517","\"Mama Mia!\"","Michael’s gaze remained fixed on Intelligence, the stat with the biggest increase.","Three thousand six hundred and thirty-two.","That wasn’t a minor increase. That wasn’t even something Michael could reasonably call an enhancement anymore. His Intelligence had more than doubled.","Michael slowly flexed his fingers. His current reserves had swollen to a ridiculous degree.","Michael had always possessed far more mana than most people at his level because of his constitution, class, and accumulated enhancements. But now, he could no longer properly compare himself to Rank Four beings.","Michael slowly raised one hand. A mass of energy gathered above his palm.","Michael dispersed it a few seconds later. His heart began beating faster.","At this point, could his mana reserves compete with a Demigod?","Michael’s breathing gradually slowed.","\"The quantity...\"","His silver eyes narrowed.","\"...might already be comparable.\"","And the quality?","Michael suspected it might actually be higher than that of many ordinary Demigods.","The ghost wasn’t some Common or Rare-grade creature. She was Epic Three-Star. And Michael’s own foundation was anything but ordinary.","The combination between them wasn’t simply one plus one.","Michael clenched his fist. Frost silently spread across the air around it. The surrounding space became unnaturally still. Even the black earth beneath him developed a thin silver-white coating.","Michael’s eyes gradually brightened.","\"If mana quantity and quality aren’t the issue...\"","Then what still separated him from a genuine Demigod?","Michael’s gaze shifted toward the ghost’s status information still lingering within his mind.","[Domain Law Technique: Ice Wheel]","\"...it can only be this.\"","His excitement paused. The Domain Law Technique. It was still the one thing he couldn’t properly inspect.","Michael had never seen such an entry on any Rank Four status panel. That strongly suggested it belonged specifically to Rank Five.","Maybe this was the defining difference.","A Demigod didn’t merely possess more mana or a stronger body. They possessed something fundamentally different in their relationship with Laws.","Michael rubbed his chin. A thought appeared in his mind.","\"...Hey.\"","\"What?\"","Divine Incarnation Possession allowed the host to share the properties of the original. The description had explicitly stated that at deeper synchronization, the host could reproduce characteristics of the original existence to an extreme degree.","Thanks to his class and the bribe he had offered, the harmony between them was already about as high as it could be right now.","\"Hey, can you lend me your wheel?\"","\"The wheel?\"","\"Yes.\"","The answer came after a brief hesitation.","\"You can try.\"","Michael’s smile slowly widened.","\"Let’s try it.\"","Michael felt something enormous move inside their shared soul. It wasn’t mana. Not exactly. Something deeper. It was more of a structure. Some sort of concept.","Michael’s expression became serious.","\"So this is...\"","The ghost’s intention touched his.","\"Don’t resist.\"","Michael almost laughed at the irony. Those had been his exact words to her earlier.","\"Fine.\"","He relaxed.","The next instant, everything changed.","Behind Michael, space cracked, and a circle appeared.","No. It was a wheel.","It started small. Barely larger than Michael’s head. Then it expanded.","Ten metres.","Fifty.","One hundred.","In seconds, an enormous silver-white wheel hovered behind Michael. Its surface was divided into countless concentric rings. Each ring rotated independently. Some clockwise. Others counterclockwise.","Majestic symbols Michael couldn’t understand appeared across their surfaces, glowing with cold blue light.","At the center of the wheel rested an empty circle resembling a pupil.","BOOM!","The world changed.","The black plain disappeared beneath silver frost instantly. Every exposed surface within kilometres became covered in pale crystalline ice.","Michael’s eyes widened as he felt a power stronger than anything he had ever experienced course through him.","It was different from the possession itself. If merging with the ghost had felt like carrying an ocean inside a cup, activating the wheel felt like the cup had briefly become the ocean’s outlet, a narrow channel through which an entire Law flowed freely.","His body ached faintly under the pressure. Every heartbeat sent a fresh wave of that authority through his veins, cold and absolute, until his own pulse began to feel like it was keeping time with something far bigger than himself.","Michael slowly stretched out one hand. The silver-white wheel behind him rotated.","Krrrrrrrr...","The sound echoed through the surrounding regions.","Frost spread farther across the plain. But Michael immediately noticed something strange. The temperature wasn’t the important part. It wasn’t even particularly difficult for someone at his level to resist ordinary cold.","What Ice Wheel produced was fundamentally different.","The ice carried Law. Every flake of frost that appeared around him was saturated with an authority that made ordinary elemental ice feel like frozen water in comparison.","Michael clenched his fingers. A small shard of ice condensed above his palm. The shard was barely the length of his finger. Yet the moment it appeared, the space around it distorted faintly.","*","A/N: Cast those power stones and golden tickets dear readers!"]},{"number":1197,"title":"Chapter 1197: Power Of The One Above","paragraphs":["\"...This power...\"","Michael had never felt anything like it before.","The ghost’s understanding continuously flowed through their synchronization, allowing Michael to grasp fragments of what he was currently using.","\"Ice Wheel isn’t simply a Law technique...\"","His silver eyes narrowed.","\"It’s a Domain Law Technique.\"","The distinction was enormous.","Michael had encountered domains before. At Rank Four, after one’s comprehension of Laws reached a sufficient level, a supernatural could gradually construct a Law Domain. Within that domain, their authority over the Laws they cultivated became vastly stronger.","Certain techniques could even only be activated while the domain was deployed.","Domain Skills.","They were essentially techniques that borrowed the complete structure of a Law Domain to function. Outside that domain, they simply couldn’t be used at all.","However, it seemed Rank Five was different.","Michael’s gaze lifted toward the massive Ice Wheel. At Rank Five, the Domain no longer remained merely a field created around the user. It evolved and transformed into a miniature world. A Law World.","Once that happened, a Demigod no longer needed to completely deploy their inner world every time they wanted to use certain Domain Skills. They could extract portions of its authority directly into reality.","In a sense, they were the world. Now it all made sense. Why the female Demigod could control a sea of blood. It was probably the effect of a Domain Law Technique.","Michael’s eyes shone.","\"So this wheel... is basically part of her world brought outside.\"","The ghost’s voice echoed through his mind.","\"Yes.\"","Michael suddenly understood why he had never seen anything like it from a Rank Four. It wasn’t simply because they lacked sufficient power. They fundamentally lacked the structure required to sustain such a technique.","Ice Wheel required a Law World. Without one, there was nothing to draw from. Yet Divine Incarnation Possession had temporarily allowed Michael to bypass that restriction.","He didn’t possess a Law World, but she did. And through their synchronization, he could borrow enough of its foundation to manifest Ice Wheel.","\"Ridiculous.\"","Michael grinned.","The first function of Ice Wheel was Amplification. Extreme amplification.","The second function was locking, essentially making it impossible to use the void for anything.","There was still something else inside Ice Wheel. He could feel it. A third function.","Unlike the first two, which were distributed throughout the structure, this one felt concentrated. Dangerously concentrated.","At the very center of the wheel.","Michael focused on it.","Immediately, his soul screamed, and his expression changed.","The Ice Wheel stopped rotating.","For a brief moment, Michael caught the faintest glimpse of something inside the central pupil. Then the connection disappeared.","Michael staggered slightly.","\"...\"","The ghost immediately reduced her synchronization.","\"You can’t.\"","Michael breathed out slowly.","\"No kidding.\"","Even with their current compatibility, he couldn’t properly comprehend the third function. Not because she refused to show him. His current existence simply couldn’t contain the complete information.","That realization made Michael’s expression serious.","Even when he could partially manifest a Rank Five Domain Law Technique, the third ability remained beyond him. That meant it wasn’t merely another application of Ice Wheel.","It was probably the technique’s true killing move. The trump card. One that might even drain the original body.","Michael stared at the enormous Ice Wheel for several seconds longer.","The temptation to continue probing the third function was strong. But after the reaction from his soul just now, even he knew when curiosity had crossed into stupidity.","\"At least I know it exists.\"","For now, that was enough.","His attention shifted back toward the first function. Amplification. Unlike the mysterious third ability, this one was something he could actually test properly.","Michael slowly lowered his gaze toward his hand.","\"I wonder...\"","There was one spell he had been casually studying whenever he had free time. Nothing particularly impressive. At least, it hadn’t been impressive when he first learned it.","Ice Spear.","A relatively straightforward intermediate ice spell.","Condense ice-element mana. Compress it. Shape it into a spear. Launch it. Simple.","Michael had originally learned it mostly because his elemental affinities had continued expanding, and he wanted at least a basic offensive spell for each element he could use.","Compared to his necromancy, Laws, undead, and other absurd abilities, Ice Spear had barely received any attention.","Michael’s silver eyes narrowed.","\"What happens if I go all out?\"","He raised his right hand. Immediately, the entire atmosphere changed.","Whoosh!","The surrounding ice-element energy rushed toward Michael. The Ice Wheel rotated once.","KRRRRRR...","A deep vibration spread through the frozen world. Every speck of frost suspended in the air trembled. The pale snowfall reversed direction. Instead of falling toward the ground, countless flakes rose toward Michael’s hand.","A small point of blue-white light appeared above his palm. Then compression began.","Michael’s expression changed almost immediately.","\"...Oh.\"","This was already beyond anything he had expected. The amount of mana gathering was absurd.","Under normal circumstances, Ice Spear had a natural limit. After enough mana was poured into the spell, maintaining the structure became increasingly difficult. Eventually, the spell would collapse before additional energy could be added.","But Ice Wheel was supporting it. Every time the spell formation approached instability, the surrounding Law authority reinforced it.","Michael added more mana. The glowing point expanded.","One metre.","Three metres.","Five.","The rough shape of a spear slowly appeared. Except calling it a spear was becoming increasingly ridiculous. It was already more than ten metres long.","Michael continued pouring mana into it. His newly enhanced reserves began dropping.","Ten percent.","Fifteen.","Twenty.","The spear compressed rather than expanding. Its enormous size shrank. Ten metres became eight. Eight became six. Yet the energy contained inside continued increasing.","The surrounding space began producing faint cracking sounds.","Isabella stared from the distance. Her violet soul flames widened. She had already moved several kilometres away when Michael first manifested Ice Wheel.","Without hesitation, she turned around and started running, her body a blur across the landscape.","Michael’s expression became increasingly serious.","Forty percent.","Fifty percent.","Sixty percent."]},{"number":1198,"title":"Chapter 1198: Progress","paragraphs":["Michael’s mana continued disappearing. For the first time since the possession began, he started feeling a strain. His mana pathways were carrying an amount of energy far beyond what they normally handled.","Fortunately, the ghost’s spiritual properties were reinforcing him from within. Without Divine Incarnation Possession, Michael suspected his body would already be screaming.","Seventy percent.","The Ice Wheel accelerated.","KRRRRRRRRR...","The concentric rings spun faster. The entire frozen region began feeding the spell.","Michael’s silver hair whipped violently around him. His robes, reinforced with his mana, snapped against the wind.","The spear shrank again.","Three metres.","Then two.","At this point, it looked almost elegant. A narrow silver-white lance floated above Michael’s palm.","Beautiful and terrifying.","Michael swallowed.","\"This thing...\"","His instincts were warning him.","Eighty percent.","The world around the spear began distorting. Thin black lines appeared intermittently around its edge.","These were not cracks in the ice, but cracks in space.","Michael’s eyes widened slightly. Ice Wheel had already locked the surrounding space. Yet the sheer concentration of energy contained inside the spear was beginning to forcefully deform even that reinforced environment.","Ninety percent.","Michael’s arms started trembling.","The ghost finally spoke.","\"You should stop.\"","With a Demigod directly telling him to stop, Michael didn’t need more convincing. It definitely wasn’t because he was afraid of killing himself.","Michael’s attention returned to the spell. He needed a target. His perception swept across the frozen landscape before locking onto a distant mountain.","The mountain stood nearly thirty kilometres away. Several kilometres tall.","Michael raised his arm. The spear aligned itself. He tightened his fingers.","The Ice Wheel behind him rotated once, then stopped.","Complete silence descended.","Michael released the spell.","\"Go.\"","There was no explosion. No thunder nor dramatic flash. The spear simply disappeared.","Michael’s pupils contracted. He hadn’t even seen it move.","A fraction of a second later, the distant mountain vanished.","For one impossible instant, the entire upper half of the mountain simply ceased to exist. Then reality caught up.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!","The Netherworld shook.","A colossal white pillar erupted from the mountain’s location and pierced into the dark-grey sky.","The shockwave arrived several seconds later. Michael’s robes snapped backward. The frozen ground beneath him peeled away in enormous layers. Kilometres of black stone fractured simultaneously.","The surrounding dead mountains trembled. Several distant peaks collapsed.","Then came the cold.","A wave of silver-white frost exploded outward from the impact point.","Ten kilometres.","Twenty.","Thirty.","The landscape froze instantly. Massive formations of ice rose from the ground like crystalline mountains. The remaining half of the original peak disappeared beneath a growing glacier.","Michael stared.","\"...What the hell?\"","The destruction continued. The initial impact had pierced through the mountain. But the Ice Wheel’s Law amplification had caused the spell to keep propagating afterward.","Everything in the spear’s path had been frozen at a conceptual level.","Before Michael could even process what was happening, the silver-white wheel behind him flickered.","His vision blurred. The strength that had filled every corner of his body only moments ago vanished frighteningly quickly.","\"...Ah.\"","Michael’s body tilted forward. The possession had allowed him to temporarily contain an absurd amount of power, but he had just emptied almost all of that borrowed foundation into a single attack.","His body lost strength. The world spun. Michael started falling from the sky.","Before gravity could properly claim him, however, a strange coldness separated from his body.","Whoosh.","The ghost emerged from his back.","The silver in Michael’s hair rapidly retreated until it returned to black. The frost patterns covering his skin disappeared, and his eyes returned to normal.","At the same time, the enormous Ice Wheel shattered into countless silver fragments that dissolved into the Netherworld.","Michael continued falling, but before he could touch the ground, he stopped. His body hung awkwardly in the air.","\"...?\"","The ghost floated beside him. Compared to before, her translucent body appeared noticeably dimmer. The silver glow beneath her skin had faded, and even her long black hair seemed slightly less substantial.","Apparently, lending Michael that much of herself hadn’t been free.","Michael slowly straightened himself with the aid of the invisible force.","\"Thanks.\"","The ghost looked at him.","\"You owe me. Pay me.\"","Michael shook his head with a wary laugh.","\"Right.\"","He wasn’t going to argue, especially when the payment was something he had already agreed to.","\"Two crystals.\"","\"Yes.\"","Michael opened his hand. Two Evolution Essence Crystals appeared above his palm.","The ghost immediately floated closer.","Michael tightened his fingers.","Crack.","Both crystals fractured simultaneously. Spiderweb-like lines spread across their surfaces before the two crystals shattered. They dissolved into two streams of pale essence.","Michael guided both streams toward her.","\"There.\"","The essence entered her spiritual body.","Whoosh.","Her entire figure trembled. The evolutionary energy spread throughout her translucent form before disappearing into depths Michael couldn’t perceive.","Again, the amount was insignificant compared to the sheer scale of her existence. Yet unlike the first time, there was at least a change now.","The dimness caused by Divine Incarnation Possession gradually faded. Her outline became clearer. The silver glow beneath her translucent skin strengthened.","Michael’s eyes narrowed.","\"So it actually helps recovery too?\"","Now that he thought of it, it wasn’t actually surprising. However, this was indeed a wasteful method.","However, Michael’s attention was soon taken by something else.","The moment his connection with the ghost ended, several panels appeared in front of him, informing him that a change had appeared in his rank advancement quest. This was the second time in three days, but the first time hadn’t made Michael happy.","However, this time there was a pleasant surprise.","[Rank Advancement Quest]","Comprehend A Domain [2.5% Progress]","A Death’s Heir is the future sovereign. Even young, every supreme has been stated to be special. Be Renowned.","[Influence Levels: Realmic, Multi-Realmic, Sectoric, Grand Sectoric, Galactic, Multi-Galactic, Cluster Sovereign, Supercluster Sovereign, Cosmic, Universal]","[Current Influence Level: Grand Sectoric]","[Progress: Complete]","Own an entity on the level of your Personal Influence. Not less than three levels below. [0% Progress]","Have Five Hundred Rank 4 Subjects [Progress: 1968/500]","Time Limit: 4 Years, 9 Months."]},{"number":1199,"title":"Chapter 1199: A Big Push After Three Months","paragraphs":["Compared to when the Rank Advancement Quest had first appeared, there were already several changes.","Some were pleasant. Others, not so much.","His gaze naturally fell toward the bottom.","[Time Limit: 4 Years, 9 Months.]","Michael’s lips twitched.","\"Three months already.\"","When the quest had originally appeared, he had been given five years. Now three months were gone.","It wasn’t exactly surprising. Time had to pass. No matter how absurd his talent became or how quickly his strength increased, Michael couldn’t exactly negotiate with the passage of time. Still, seeing the number decrease made the deadline feel slightly more real.","However, that wasn’t what truly caught his attention.","Michael’s eyes moved upward.","[Comprehend A Domain: 2.5% Progress]","Finally, the first requirement had moved.","Michael immediately understood why.","\"Ice Wheel.\"","There was practically no other explanation. Until today, the progress on this requirement had remained stubbornly at zero despite everything Michael had tried.","And it wasn’t because his comprehension was poor. Far from it. After undergoing so many evolutions, enhancements, transformations, and improvements to his soul, Michael’s comprehension had already reached an almost unreasonable level. Among ordinary geniuses, he would already stand near the peak.","Even among the monstrous talents produced by powerful realms and ancient factions, Michael suspected there wouldn’t be many who could surpass him. Perhaps only those freaks who appeared once in hundreds of thousands or even millions of years could clearly leave him behind.","Yet despite possessing comprehension at that level, this task had always remained at zero percent. The problem had never been him. The problem was the requirement itself.","\"Comprehend a Domain.\"","Domains weren’t something Rank Three beings were supposed to possess in the first place.","Even among Rank Four supernaturals, not everyone deliberately constructed their Domain immediately after advancement. For many, the process happened naturally. After entering Rank Four, their understanding of the Law would gradually deepen.","Eventually, the Law Seed would begin influencing the space around them. Then, after sufficient accumulation, comprehension, and interaction with their Law, the foundation of a Domain would naturally emerge.","In other words, the quest was asking Michael to comprehend something that many Rank Four beings only began touching after reaching Rank Four.","The Origin Will really expected too much from him.","Michael had tried several shortcuts before. His undead possessed Domains. Some had extremely powerful ones.","Michael had them release their Domains directly in front of him, entered, studied, observed the Law fluctuations, even let himself be suppressed to feel the effects from an enemy’s perspective and still got nothing.","Not even 0.1%.","Michael had also attempted using his Law of Echoed Existence to copy the domains, but that had failed as well.","He could copy many abilities from his undead and could reproduce their techniques, even borrowing portions of their unique properties. But a Domain wasn’t merely an ability.","It was the external manifestation of a supernatural’s Law foundation, but even Michael’s own Law Seed remained incomplete. Without first comprehending his Law Seed to completion, there was no complete foundation from which a Domain could emerge.","Cases like Beginning, who could form a partial foundation domain, were rare, and much of this was due to the unique properties of his Law, not its comprehension. It was also a domain he might be able to copy, but nothing was better than using this one.","Trying to directly copy someone else’s Domain was essentially like attempting to copy the roof of a building when he hadn’t finished constructing the walls beneath it.","The structure simply had nowhere to exist. But Michael could see a new path now, thanks to Ice Wheel, the ghost’s Domain Law Technique.","Through Divine Incarnation Possession, Michael hadn’t merely observed another person’s Domain. For a short period of time, he had actually carried the foundation of a Demigod’s Law World within himself. He had felt how the ghost’s Law World interacted with reality.","He had experienced how an established Domain could amplify elemental authority, suppress space, reinforce techniques, and alter the surrounding environment according to the user’s Law.","More importantly, for those few moments, Michael hadn’t been standing inside someone else’s Domain as an outsider. He had been the one controlling it. Even if the foundation had been borrowed, and even if Ice Wheel truly belonged to the ghost, the experience itself had been his.","Two and a half percent might seem small. But considering everything he had tried previously had produced absolutely nothing, this was enormous.","Michael’s gaze instinctively shifted toward the ghost. She was currently hovering nearby, happily absorbing the remnants of evolutionary essence from the two crystals he had given her.","She was truly the most expressive undead he had seen outside Jester, Lucky, and Lily.","The ghost noticed his stare almost immediately. Her silver eyes turned toward him.","\"What?\"","Michael’s expression gradually became strange.","\"...You might be more useful than I thought.\"","The ghost blinked in confusion.","\"More crystals?\"","Michael’s expression immediately flattened.","\"That’s not what I meant.\"","\"Oh.\"","Her interest disappeared almost instantly.","Michael ignored her as several thoughts raced through his mind.","If one brief manifestation of Ice Wheel had given him 2.5% progress, then what would happen if he repeatedly used it and studied its structure properly?","He also had a certain incense that could boost his comprehension that he had yet to use. What would happen if he combined both?","At this point, Michael knew that for the next five years, he was going to spend more time in the Origin Battlefield for the sake of his advancement.","Michael’s heartbeat accelerated.","Perhaps the requirement that had originally seemed the most impossible had just become the easiest one to brute-force.","But this was the only good news he had regarding his rank advancement task.","Thanks to a certain announcement, Michael’s Influence had jumped from Multi-Realmic to Grand Sectoric. At this level, it only proved his name had reached the higher-ups of hundreds of realms.","*","A/N: Sorry for the late update dear readers! Thank you for the continued support!"]},{"number":1200,"title":"Chapter 1200: Jester","paragraphs":["Fortunately, it hadn’t touched Galactic yet, since that would mean he went from someone that powerful individuals within a realm might take interest in, to an esteemed figure known across many realms.","Whether that would be a good thing or not was not something Michael wanted to find out.","After his last advancement task, this was the first one where Michael felt that doing what he could achieve was good enough. There was no need to be hell-bent on surpassing all limits.","The Origin Will indeed knew what it meant when it said it would only give him the highest task it could. But the good part was that it would also give him the highest rewards it could. Of course, the bad part was that failure would be just as costly.","In any case, thanks to a certain announcement, his other most difficult task outside of creating a Domain had just gotten harder.","[Own an entity on the level of your Personal Influence. Not less than three levels below]","Before today, this was the second requirement stuck at zero percent.","After three months since the task appeared, Michael had a few ideas of what it could mean. One of his best bets was that making one of his undead just as famous as him would work, and among all his undead, only Jester was suitable.","In the current Aurora, Michael might not have had the most followers, but he was undoubtedly the one teenager in the whole realm that people recognized as the greatest representation of the supernatural world.","This had all started with his college exams, when his performance drew initial attention. Then Jester and his sister, thanks to streaming, went further in making sure he stayed relevant even without doing anything.","Much of this had to do with Jester, who, with his appearance mirroring Michael’s, drew great attention, especially from the opposite gender.","Michael couldn’t count the amount of thirst traps he had seen of himself. It didn’t matter that the actual subject was Jester with his younger appearance; that was still his face.","Jester’s frequent appearances had helped keep Michael in the public consciousness even while Michael himself spent most of his time away from ordinary society.","Then three months ago, everything changed.","Brightgate City.","The incident had been impossible to hide. Too many people had seen what happened. And even more surprising, too many had recorded it.","Putting aside why people had their phones out in a time of danger, it didn’t matter whether Michael himself was seen clearly or not. Everyone knew he was the one who had saved the city.","At first, most videos focused on the immediate disaster. But as public interest grew, people began digging deeper. Old footage resurfaced. Videos recorded back in Woodstone City after the demonic supernatural attack began circulating again. Some showed Michael’s undead moving through ruined streets.","Michael wasn’t even the strongest supernatural involved in the attacks happening across Aurora during that period. Other cities had experienced incidents involving far more supernaturals. Some battles had even involved individuals vastly stronger than Michael was at the time.","Yet strangely enough, Michael benefited the most from the public attention.","The reason wasn’t particularly complicated. The Federation had begun gradually exposing ordinary citizens to the existence of the supernatural world, but there were still limits to how much information they could safely release.","Most truly powerful supernaturals remained hidden. Their identities weren’t public, and their battles weren’t livestreamed. Their organizations weren’t something ordinary citizens could simply search online.","Michael was different. He was visible. Young. And more importantly, spectacular. A teenager commanding undead creatures was almost perfectly designed to capture public attention.","To ordinary people who had spent their entire lives imagining what powerful supernaturals might look like, Michael was probably the closest thing available to the image they already carried in their minds.","Cool. Dangerous. Mysterious. Powerful. And just familiar enough to feel real.","And the effect wasn’t limited to him. His family had been dragged into it as well. His sister had accumulated a surprisingly large following online. Aunt Mia had one too.","Thankfully, the situation hadn’t become unbearable. Jester remained near them frequently, and both the Academy and Federation had quietly stationed additional personnel around the family. It was enough that anyone stupid enough to approach them with malicious intentions would have an extremely unpleasant day without affecting their daily life.","Michael had initially worried his growing fame would completely destroy their ordinary lives.","Fortunately, that hadn’t happened. At least not totally.","Aside from Lily, whose childhood could never be the same, Aunt Mia had even benefited from it.","Her restaurant had become famous.","People travelled from other cities simply because they heard it belonged to Michael’s aunt. Aunt Mia had since expanded, now possessing restaurants in multiple cities, something Michael still found slightly amusing whenever he thought about it.","Life really was strange.","However, even with all this change, the progress of this requirement remained unchanged.","Fortunately, three months of failure had given Michael time to develop several theories.","The first was simple. Jester might actually qualify in terms of popularity, but the Origin Will might not recognize him because almost nobody knew he belonged to Michael.","Ordinary people knew Jester existed. They knew he resembled Michael. Some even suspected there was a blood connection between them, but very few knew the truth. Jester was Michael’s undead. To the public, he was simply another person closely associated with Michael.","If the requirement specifically demanded that Michael \"own\" the entity, perhaps that relationship needed to be recognized by others. Influence was fundamentally social. If nobody knew something belonged to him, then perhaps its influence couldn’t properly be counted as part of his own foundation.","It would be like secretly owning a powerful company while the entire universe believed it belonged to someone else. Technically, it was his. But publicly, its influence had no connection to him.","If that interpretation was correct, then Michael might simply need to reveal Jester’s identity as one of his undead."]}]);
